UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Become skilled in analysing and explaining ideas and their consequences.</p><p>Are you passionate about understanding what connects and disrupts communities, the nation, and the world? Do you appreciate the power of narratives in the past and present that shape the future? Forge global citizenship and a meaningful career path by choosing from a range of major and minor study areas in the arts, humanities and languages.</p> <p>This degree program develops your love of reading, evaluating and writing into career-based skills for critiquing, curating, exhibiting, communicating and shaping knowledge about the place of people in the world. Explore ideas, theories and records of human interaction and more-than-human relationships with nature and artificial intelligence. Gain advanced skills in history, literature, language, politics, society and culture.</p> <p> <strong> Top 150 ? </strong> in the world for Education </p> <p> <strong> World top 250 ? </strong> for Sociology </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>You will enjoy flexible pathways, develop in-demand skills and gain broad career outcomes.</p><p>Employment options for Bachelor of Arts graduates are varied. Employability will be strengthened by your chosen areas of specialisation.</p><p>Professional outcomes</p><ul><li>Local, state and commonwealth public service</li><li>Non-government organisations</li><li>Higher education</li><li>Museums, libraries and archives</li><li>Arts and cultural organisations</li></ul><h4>Course overview</h4><p>Your core arts courses include practice-based projects and optional internships that further develop skills across digital literacy, problem-solving, innovative thinking and work-readiness.</p><p>Additionally, you can focus your studies through optional learning pathways:</p><ul><li>Entrepreneurial stream - work readiness and specified WIL courses</li><li>Online stream - online and part-time study</li><li>Global stream - languages acquisition, global and cultural awareness, international mobility, ie. student exchange</li><li>Innovator stream - digital learning and topics of inquiry.</li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Minors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>HASS1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS1000">BA Futures</a></li><li><strong>HASS2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS2000">BA Practice</a></li><li><strong>HASS3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3000">BA Project</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40096">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARTS3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS3020">Professional Career Ready Studio</a></li><li><strong>HASS3010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3010">Professional Career Ready Placement</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40096">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">English and Writing</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ENGL1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL1000">Introduction to English Literature</a></li><li><strong>ENGL1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL1040">Australian Stories</a></li><li><strong>ENGL1201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL1201">Creative Writing: Introduction</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2000">Literary Theory and Practice</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2005">Mind and Monstrosity: Victorian Novel</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2011">Children''s Literature</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2101">Writing Short Fiction</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2102">Creative Writing: Life Writing</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2104</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2104">Creative Writing: Writing Sci-Fi and Fantasy</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3012">Crime Fiction: Mutations of a Genre</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3302</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3302">The Novel Writing Toolkit</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3304</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3304">Creative Writing: Fiction, Medicine, Psychology</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3665</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3665">Young Adult Literature: Storying the World through Young Adult Voices</a></li><li><em>19 additional courses are part of "English and Writing" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40096">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"English and Writing"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40096">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">French Studies</a></p><p><strong>French Studies (Beginner Sequence) </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>FREN1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN1100">French Language and Culture Beginners 1 (A0 to A1.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN1200">French Language and Culture Beginners 2 (A1.1 to A1.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN2610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2610">French Language and Culture Elementary 1 (A1.2 to A2.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN2620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2620">French Language and Culture Elementary 2 (A2.1 to A2.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3610">French Language and Culture Intermediate 1 (A2.2 to B1.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3620">French Language and Culture Intermediate 2 (B1.1 to B1.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3702</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3702">Extended French through Translation</a></li><li><strong>HUMA2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUMA2001">Global Experiences</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "French Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40096">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>French Studies (Intermediate Sequence) </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>FREN2610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2610">French Language and Culture Elementary 1 (A1.2 to A2.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN2620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2620">French Language and Culture Elementary 2 (A2.1 to A2.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3610">French Language and Culture Intermediate 1 (A2.2 to B1.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3620">French Language and Culture Intermediate 2 (B1.1 to B1.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3702</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3702">Extended French through Translation</a></li><li><strong>HUMA2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUMA2001">Global Experiences</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "French Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40096">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"French Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40096">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Global Indigenous Studies</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1110">Blak Australia</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1370</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1370">Community Engagement: Respect and Reciprocity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1390</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1390">Blak Rights and the Fight for Justice</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1420</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1420">Yarning, Media and Futures</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2022</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2022">Aboriginal Cultural Practices</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2243</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2243">Indigenous People and Sustainable Environments</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2245">Aboriginal People and Law</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2330</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2330">Aboriginal Knowledge Systems</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3024">Blak Advocacy: Empowerment and Solidarity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3080">Indigenous Research</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3251</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3251">Global Indigenous Comparative Studies</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3380</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3380">Global Indigenous Human Rights</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3500">Aboriginal Education, Relationships and Responsibilities</a></li><li><em>5 additional courses are part of "Global Indigenous Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40096">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Global Indigenous Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40096">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">History</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>HIST1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1001">Europe and the World</a></li><li><strong>HIST1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1002">The United States from Civil War to Superpower</a></li><li><strong>HIST1051</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1051">The Australian Experience</a></li><li><strong>HIST1052</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1052">Origin of Controversies</a></li><li><strong>HIST2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2002">Fact or Fiction Reading the Past</a></li><li><strong>HIST2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2006">Australian Underworlds: Histories of Crime in Australia</a></li><li><strong>HIST2253</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2253">Bodies and Brains: Histories of Illness, Disability and Disease</a></li><li><strong>HIST2611</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2611">The Russian Revolution: From the Tsars to Putin</a></li><li><strong>HIST2650</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2650">War and Trauma</a></li><li><strong>HIST3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3008">Global Perspectives on the First World War</a></li><li><strong>HIST3152</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3152">The History of Racism</a></li><li><strong>HIST3201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3201">Power in the Asia Pacific: Conflict and Alliances</a></li><li><strong>HIST3621</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3621">Maps and Dreams: Aboriginal-Colonial Relationships in Australian History</a></li><li><strong>HIST3641</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3641">The Rise of Fascism: From the March on Rome to Hitler s Seizure of Power</a></li><li><strong>HIST3642</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3642">The Downfall of Fascism: The Third Reich, War and Genocide</a></li><li><em>14 additional courses are part of "History" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40096">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"History"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40096">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Geography and the Environment</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this minor.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3006">Surviving the Anthropocene: Sustainability in the 21st Century</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2080">Cities and Regions</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3090">Society and Space</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the list for a major (10 units at 1000 level, 10 units at 2000 level and 20 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1003">Environmental Values and Ethics</a></li><li><strong>ENVS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1004">Social Development and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2002">Environmental Legislation and Planning</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2008">The Sustainable Society</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3001">Integrated Impact Assessment</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3008">Work Integrated Learning in the Environmental and Development Sectors</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1030">Global Poverty and Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2130">Geographies of Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3300">Rethinking Development</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2065">Environment and Society</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Geography and the Environment"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40096">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Relations</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcas