UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Forge your own path</p><p>When you study a Bachelor of Arts/Bachelor of Laws (Honours) you unlock exciting and diverse career paths tailored to your passions. Choose from hundreds of courses in the arts and humanities, and graduate with strong legal expertise that elevates your potential across a wide range of sectors.</p> <p>Pursue a traditional career in the legal field, or make your mark across government, NGOs, business, and community organisations – there are opportunities in almost every sector.</p><p>In this combined degree, you’ll complete all courses required for the Bachelor of Arts degree in the first 3 years of study. In the final two years, students complete the requirements of the Bachelor of Laws (Honours).</p> <p> <strong> World top 300 ? </strong> for Law </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Career opportunities span a wide range of sectors including</p><ul><li>legal sector</li><li>local, state and commonwealth public service</li><li>non-government organisations</li><li>higher education</li><li>media and communications</li><li>arts and cultural organisations</li></ul> <p>90.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Law and Paralegal Studies</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You will develop skills to provide professional advice based on specialised knowledge of the law and its application to different situations.</p><p>You will study core law courses as well as arts study areas:</p><ul><li>the legal system</li><li>criminal law and procedure</li><li>international law</li><li>history</li><li>English and writing</li><li>psychology studies</li><li>information technology</li></ul>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-arts">Bachelor of Arts</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-laws-honours">Bachelor of Laws (Honours) Combined</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Minors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses - Law</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>LAWS1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1010">Legal System and Method I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1011">Legal System and Method II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1020">Torts I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1021</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1021">Torts II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS2030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS2030">Criminal Law and Procedure</a></li><li><strong>LAWS3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS3040">Contracts I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS3041</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS3041">Contracts II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4001">Constitutional Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4002">Administrative Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4003">Civil Dispute Resolution</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4004">Evidence</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4005">Company Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4007</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4007">Professional Conduct</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4010">Equity and Trusts</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4011">Property</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4012">Public International Law</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses - Law"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Core Courses - Arts</a></p><p><strong>Students must complete all the core courses.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>HASS1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS1000">BA Futures</a></li><li><strong>HASS2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS2000">BA Practice</a></li><li><strong>HASS3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3000">BA Project</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses - Arts"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARTS3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS3020">Professional Career Ready Studio</a></li><li><strong>HASS3010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3010">Professional Career Ready Placement</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Course List - Law</a></p><p><strong>Students must choose 80 units from the course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>LAWS5036</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS5036">International Clinical Legal Externship</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6016</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6016">Taxation Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6017</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6017">Family Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6020">Environmental Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6021</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6021">Advanced Criminal Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6024">Employment Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6038</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6038">Law and Economics of Climate Change</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6043</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6043">Advanced Legal Research Project</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6087</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6087">Internet Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6090">Health Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6091</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6091">Special Interest Topic</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6094</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6094">Indigenous Peoples, Issues and the Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6096</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6096">Child Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6097</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6097">Competitive Mooting</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6099</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6099">Sport and the Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6151</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6151">Gender and the Law</a></li><li><em>35 additional courses are part of "Course List - Law" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Course List - Law"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</p>Arts Major<p><a href="#">English and Writing</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ENGL1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL1000">Introduction to English Literature</a></li><li><strong>ENGL1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL1040">Australian Stories</a></li><li><strong>ENGL1201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL1201">Creative Writing: Introduction</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2000">Literary Theory and Practice</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2005">Mind and Monstrosity: Victorian Novel</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2011">Children''s Literature</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2101">Writing Short Fiction</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2102">Creative Writing: Life Writing</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2104</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2104">Creative Writing: Writing Sci-Fi and Fantasy</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3012">Crime Fiction: Mutations of a Genre</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3302</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3302">The Novel Writing Toolkit</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3304</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3304">Creative Writing: Fiction, Medicine, Psychology</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3665</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3665">Young Adult Literature: Storying the World through Young Adult Voices</a></li><li><em>19 additional courses are part of "English and Writing" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"English and Writing"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">French Studies</a></p><p><strong>French Studies (Beginner Sequence) </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>FREN1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN1100">French Language and Culture Beginners 1 (A0 to A1.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN1200">French Language and Culture Beginners 2 (A1.1 to A1.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN2610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2610">French Language and Culture Elementary 1 (A1.2 to A2.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN2620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2620">French Language and Culture Elementary 2 (A2.1 to A2.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3610">French Language and Culture Intermediate 1 (A2.2 to B1.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3620">French Language and Culture Intermediate 2 (B1.1 to B1.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3702</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3702">Extended French through Translation</a></li><li><strong>HUMA2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUMA2001">Global Experiences</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "French Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>French Studies (Intermediate Sequence) </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>FREN2610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2610">French Language and Culture Elementary 1 (A1.2 to A2.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN2620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2620">French Language and Culture Elementary 2 (A2.1 to A2.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3610">French Language and Culture Intermediate 1 (A2.2 to B1.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3620">French Language and Culture Intermediate 2 (B1.1 to B1.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3702</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3702">Extended French through Translation</a></li><li><strong>HUMA2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUMA2001">Global Experiences</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "French Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"French Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Global Indigenous Studies</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1110">Blak Australia</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1370</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1370">Community Engagement: Respect and Reciprocity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1390</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1390">Blak Rights and the Fight for Justice</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1420</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1420">Yarning, Media and Futures</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2022</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2022">Aboriginal Cultural Practices</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2243</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2243">Indigenous People and Sustainable Environments</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2245">Aboriginal People and Law</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2330</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2330">Aboriginal Knowledge Systems</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3024">Blak Advocacy: Empowerment and Solidarity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3080">Indigenous Research</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3251</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3251">Global Indigenous Comparative Studies</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3380</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3380">Global Indigenous Human Rights</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3500">Aboriginal Education, Relationships and Responsibilities</a></li><li><em>5 additional courses are part of "Global Indigenous Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Global Indigenous Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">History</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>HIST1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1001">Europe and the World</a></li><li><strong>HIST1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1002">The United States from Civil War to Superpower</a></li><li><strong>HIST1051</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1051">The Australian Experience</a></li><li><strong>HIST1052</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1052">Origin of Controversies</a></li><li><strong>HIST2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2002">Fact or Fiction Reading the Past</a></li><li><strong>HIST2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2006">Australian Underworlds: Histories of Crime in Australia</a></li><li><strong>HIST2253</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2253">Bodies and Brains: Histories of Illness, Disability and Disease</a></li><li><strong>HIST2611</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2611">The Russian Revolution: From the Tsars to Putin</a></li><li><strong>HIST2650</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2650">War and Trauma</a></li><li><strong>HIST3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3008">Global Perspectives on the First World War</a></li><li><strong>HIST3152</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3152">The History of Racism</a></li><li><strong>HIST3201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3201">Power in the Asia Pacific: Conflict and Alliances</a></li><li><strong>HIST3621</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3621">Maps and Dreams: Aboriginal-Colonial Relationships in Australian History</a></li><li><strong>HIST3641</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3641">The Rise of Fascism: From the March on Rome to Hitler s Seizure of Power</a></li><li><strong>HIST3642</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3642">The Downfall of Fascism: The Third Reich, War and Genocide</a></li><li><em>14 additional courses are part of "History" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"History"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Geography and the Environment</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this minor.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3006">Surviving the Anthropocene: Sustainability in the 21st Century</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2080">Cities and Regions</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3090">Society and Space</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the list for a major (10 units at 1000 level, 10 units at 2000 level and 20 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1003">Environmental Values and Ethics</a></li><li><strong>ENVS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1004">Social Development and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2002">Environmental Legislation and Planning</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2008">The Sustainable Society</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3001">Integrated Impact Assessment</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3008">Work Integrated Learning in the Environmental and Development Sectors</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1030">Global Poverty and Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2130">Geographies of Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3300">Rethinking Development</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2065">Environment and Society</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Geography and the Environment"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40150">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Relations</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2002">Business and the Politics of Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a></li><li><strong>IREL2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2004">Diplomacy, Trade and Politics</a></li><li><strong>IREL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3001">Public Diplomacy and Social Media</a></li><li><strong>IREL3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3002">Global Data Governance for Just and Sustainable Futures</a></li><li><strong>IREL3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3003">International Relations in a Changing World Order</a></li><li><strong>IREL3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3004">Indigenising International Politics, Policy and the Economy</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="