UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Open doors to almost any sector imaginable</p><p>When you study this combined degree you’ll develop a core understanding of the world around us and how it works. Pursue your passions, and learn from leading researchers who’ll guide you through a tailored program – specifically designed to give you the skills that employers are seeking.</p> <p>Forge your own path by choosing from 20 majors and minors and 100s of courses in the arts and humanities. Then round out your experience with scientific expertise that underpins technology, environmental management, business, research, and health.</p><p>This highly flexible combined degree can open doors across also every sector imaginable.</p> <p> <strong> 88.4% of students ? </strong> were happy with facilities and resources </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>This combined degree emphasises problem-solving, teamwork and critical thinking, graduates are therefore sought after across a range of sectors. You will enjoy flexible pathways, develop in-demand skills and gain broad career outcomes.</p> <p>Employment options for graduates are varied. Employability will be strengthened by your chosen areas of specialisation.</p><p>Career opportunities span almost every industry and sector. See individual degree pages for more information.</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You''ll develop highly sought-after and transferable skills in problem-solving, communication, independent thinking and work readiness. Your core courses for this combined degree will teach you how to deliver innovative solutions for real-world problems.</p>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-arts">Bachelor of Arts</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-science">Bachelor of Science</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Minors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>HASS1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS1000">BA Futures</a></li><li><strong>HASS2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS2000">BA Practice</a></li><li><strong>HASS3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3000">BA Project</a></li><li><strong>INFT1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT1004">Introduction to Programming</a></li><li><strong>SCIE1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE1002">Multidisciplinary Laboratories</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40168">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Mathematics Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following Mathematics Course List. Please note that some disciplines require a minimum level of mathematical knowledge. MATH1002 or higher is required for a Chemistry Major. MATH1110 or higher is required for Physics or Mathematics Majors.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>MATH1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1001">Preparatory Studies in Mathematics</a></li><li><strong>MATH1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1002">Foundational Studies in Mathematics</a></li><li><strong>MATH1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1110">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 1</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Mathematics Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40168">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Statistics Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following Statistics course list. The course you choose should align with your prior knowledge of statistics and mathematics. For detailed information about each course, please refer to the course handbook. If you are pursuing a major in Physics or Mathematics, it is recommended to complete STAT1300.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>STAT1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1070">Statistics for the Sciences</a></li><li><strong>STAT1300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1300">Fundamentals of Statistics</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Statistics Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40168">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready Placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following Course List.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARTS3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS3020">Professional Career Ready Studio</a></li><li><strong>HASS3010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3010">Professional Career Ready Placement</a></li><li><strong>SCIE3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE3002">WIL for the Sciences</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready Placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40168">handbook</a>.</p>Arts Majors<p><a href="#">English and Writing</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ENGL1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL1000">Introduction to English Literature</a></li><li><strong>ENGL1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL1040">Australian Stories</a></li><li><strong>ENGL1201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL1201">Creative Writing: Introduction</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2000">Literary Theory and Practice</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2005">Mind and Monstrosity: Victorian Novel</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2011">Children''s Literature</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2101">Writing Short Fiction</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2102">Creative Writing: Life Writing</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2104</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2104">Creative Writing: Writing Sci-Fi and Fantasy</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3012">Crime Fiction: Mutations of a Genre</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3302</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3302">The Novel Writing Toolkit</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3304</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3304">Creative Writing: Fiction, Medicine, Psychology</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3665</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3665">Young Adult Literature: Storying the World through Young Adult Voices</a></li><li><em>19 additional courses are part of "English and Writing" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40168">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"English and Writing"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40168">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">French Studies</a></p><p><strong>French Studies (Beginner Sequence) </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>FREN1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN1100">French Language and Culture Beginners 1 (A0 to A1.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN1200">French Language and Culture Beginners 2 (A1.1 to A1.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN2610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2610">French Language and Culture Elementary 1 (A1.2 to A2.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN2620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2620">French Language and Culture Elementary 2 (A2.1 to A2.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3610">French Language and Culture Intermediate 1 (A2.2 to B1.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3620">French Language and Culture Intermediate 2 (B1.1 to B1.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3702</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3702">Extended French through Translation</a></li><li><strong>HUMA2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUMA2001">Global Experiences</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "French Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40168">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>French Studies (Intermediate Sequence) </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>FREN2610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2610">French Language and Culture Elementary 1 (A1.2 to A2.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN2620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2620">French Language and Culture Elementary 2 (A2.1 to A2.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3610">French Language and Culture Intermediate 1 (A2.2 to B1.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3620">French Language and Culture Intermediate 2 (B1.1 to B1.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3702</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3702">Extended French through Translation</a></li><li><strong>HUMA2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUMA2001">Global Experiences</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "French Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40168">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"French Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40168">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Global Indigenous Studies</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1110">Blak Australia</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1370</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1370">Community Engagement: Respect and Reciprocity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1390</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1390">Blak Rights and the Fight for Justice</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1420</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1420">Yarning, Media and Futures</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2022</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2022">Aboriginal Cultural Practices</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2243</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2243">Indigenous People and Sustainable Environments</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2245">Aboriginal People and Law</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2330</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2330">Aboriginal Knowledge Systems</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3024">Blak Advocacy: Empowerment and Solidarity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3080">Indigenous Research</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3251</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3251">Global Indigenous Comparative Studies</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3380</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3380">Global Indigenous Human Rights</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3500">Aboriginal Education, Relationships and Responsibilities</a></li><li><em>5 additional courses are part of "Global Indigenous Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40168">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Global Indigenous Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40168">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">History</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>HIST1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1001">Europe and the World</a></li><li><strong>HIST1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1002">The United States from Civil War to Superpower</a></li><li><strong>HIST1051</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1051">The Australian Experience</a></li><li><strong>HIST1052</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1052">Origin of Controversies</a></li><li><strong>HIST2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2002">Fact or Fiction Reading the Past</a></li><li><strong>HIST2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2006">Australian Underworlds: Histories of Crime in Australia</a></li><li><strong>HIST2253</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2253">Bodies and Brains: Histories of Illness, Disability and Disease</a></li><li><strong>HIST2611</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2611">The Russian Revolution: From the Tsars to Putin</a></li><li><strong>HIST2650</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2650">War and Trauma</a></li><li><strong>HIST3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3008">Global Perspectives on the First World War</a></li><li><strong>HIST3152</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3152">The History of Racism</a></