UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Learn business locally. Do business globally</p><p>This program gives students a broad understanding of the Australian and global business environments. Choose to complete two Business majors, or pair a Business major with a Commerce major, and graduate as a competitive candidate in just three years.</p> <p>You will graduate with skills and attributes valued by employers in disciplines.</p><p><strong>You can major in:</strong></p><ul><li>Human resource management</li><li>Leadership and management</li><li>Entrepreneurship and innovation</li><li>Marketing</li><li>Industrial relations</li><li>International business.</li></ul> <p> <strong> World top 100 ? </strong> for Hospitality and Tourism Management </p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <p> <strong> World top 150 ? </strong> for Business Administration </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>On completion of this degree, you’ll be able to work in roles such as:</p><ul><li>Brand Manager</li><li>Digital Marketing Coordinator</li><li>Human Resource Manager</li><li>Entrepreneur</li><li>Foreign Correspondent</li><li>Foreign Affairs and Trade Officer</li><li>Business Relationship Manager</li><li>Public Service</li><li>Policy and Research Development Officer</li><li>International Exchange Coordinator</li></ul> <p>91.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2023 - Undergraduate Business and Management</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You will establish a firm understanding of the contemporary business environment and undertake studies in a range of disciplines. You will have the opportunity to select your courses from six business-related majors, with the option to major in up to two areas or minor in up to two areas with one major. You will also have the option to select your second major from the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-commerce">Bachelor of Commerce</a> majors.</p><p><strong>You will develop skills in the following areas:</strong></p><ul><li>innovation</li><li>management</li><li>diplomacy and conflict negotiation</li><li>marketing</li><li>business decision making</li><li>accounting</li><li>business analytics</li><li>teamwork</li><li>critical thinking and problem solving</li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Minors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ACCT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT1001">Fundamentals of Accounting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>BUSN1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN1010">Analytics in Business</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN1001">Fundamentals of Finance</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>INOV1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV1001">Design Thinking: Creativity in Action</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BUSN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3002">Industry Placement</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BUSN3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3004">Career-Ready Industry Led Project Lab</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BUSN3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3500">International Work Placement in Business</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Business Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ACCT3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3005">Business Analysis and Valuation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BUSN1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN1002">Business Communications</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BUSN2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN2001">Ethical Principles for Responsible Business</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON1111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON1111">Economics for Business Decisions</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>LEGL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LEGL1001">Foundations of Law</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Business Course List" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Business Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p>Business Majors<p><a href="#">Innovation and Entrepreneurship</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of the major.</p><ul><li><strong>INOV2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2001">Entrepreneurial MakerSpace</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2002">Social Entrepreneurship for Impact</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2003">Data Analytics in Digital Entrepreneurship</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2004">Prompt Engineering for Innovation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3001">Global Networking and Negotiation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3002">Traction and Growth</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3003">Venture Funding</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3004">Acceleration for Student Entrepreneurs (I2N)</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Innovation and Entrepreneurship"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Marketing</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MKTG2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2001">Digital and Social Media Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2010">Marketing Research and Data-Driven Insights</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2060">International Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2101">Consumer Decision Making</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3000">Strategic Marketing Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3003">Creating and Managing Brands</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3004">Advertising and Image Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3040">Services Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Marketing"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Leadership and Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2005">Leadership Models and Practices</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2006">Management in Environmental Turbulence</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2008">Digital Business Applications</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT2009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2009">Organisational Behaviour</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3011">Leading Organisational Change</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3012">Business Strategy</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3013</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3013">Innovation Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3014</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3014">Managing Inclusion, Diversity and Equity in Organisations</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Leadership and Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Resource Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>HRER2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2001">Managing Talent</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2002">Introduction to Employment Relations</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2003">Dynamics of People and Work in Organisations</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2004">HR Analytics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3001">Future of Work</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3002">Negotiation and Conflict Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3003">Strategic HR</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3004">Human Capital Development</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Resource Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Relations</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2002">Business and the Politics of Globalisation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2004">Diplomacy, Trade and Politics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3001">Public Diplomacy and Social Media</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3002">Global Data Governance for Just and Sustainable Futures</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3003">International Relations in a Changing World Order</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3004">Indigenising International Politics, Policy and the Economy</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Business</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IBUS2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2001">Cross-Cultural Management and Negotiations</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2003">International Trade Logistics in a Digital Age</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2004">Managing International Business</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2005">Corporate Social Responsibility for Global Business</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3000">International Business Strategy</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3001">International Human Resource Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3004">International Business Alliances</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3005">International Business in Emerging Markets</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Business"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p>Commerce Majors<p><a href="#">Accounting</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>ACCT2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT2001">Accounting Practice and Reporting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT2002">Management Accounting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT2003">Financial Accounting and Reporting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3001">Auditing and Assurance</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3002">Accounting for Corporate Entities</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3003">Taxation</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3004">Accounting Information Systems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>LEGL2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LEGL2010">Australian Business and Company Law</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Accounting"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Economics</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>ECON2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2001">Microeconomics for Business</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2002">Intermediate Macroeconomics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON2111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2111"> Econometrics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON2112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2112"> Health Economics and Finance</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3006">Environmental Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3009">Urban and Regional Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3111">Behavioural Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3112">International Economics and Payment Infrastructure</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Economics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Finance</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>FINN2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2001">Financial Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2002">Debt Securities and Bank Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2003">Financial Technologies and Innovations</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2004">International Finance</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3001">Financial Modelling</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3002">Investment Analysis and Portfolio Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3003">Derivative Securities</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3004">Alternative Investments</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Finance"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p>Business Minors<p><a href="#">Innovation and Entrepreneurship</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 40 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this minor.</p><ul><li><strong>INOV2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2001">Entrepreneurial MakerSpace</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2004">Prompt Engineering for Innovation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3002">Traction and Growth</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3004">Acceleration for Student Entrepreneurs (I2N)</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Innovation and Entrepreneurship"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Marketing</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 40 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this minor.</p><ul><li><strong>MKTG2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2001">Digital and Social Media Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2101">Consumer Decision Making</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3003">Creating and Managing Brands</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3004">Advertising and Image Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Marketing"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Leadership and Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 40 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this minor.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2005">Leadership Models and Practices</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT2009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2009">Organisational Behaviour</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3011">Leading Organisational Change</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3013</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3013">Innovation Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Leadership and Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Resource Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 40 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this minor.</p><ul><li><strong>HRER2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2001">Managing Talent</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2002">Introduction to Employment Relations</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3001">Future of Work</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3002">Negotiation and Conflict Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Resource Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Relations</a></p><p><strong>International Relations </strong>Complete 40 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this minor.</p><ul><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2002">Business and the Politics of Globalisation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3001">Public Diplomacy and Social Media</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3002">Global Data Governance for Just and Sustainable Futures</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Business</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 40 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this minor</p><ul><li><strong>IBUS2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2001">Cross-Cultural Management and Negotiations</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2004">Managing International Business</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3001">International Human Resource Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3004">International Business Alliances</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Business"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 80 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50034">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Business</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=50034&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=NCLE&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience The power of Work Integrated Learning 2:20 <p>Thinking of completing or hosting a career-ready placement opportunity? Hear firsthand from Alumnus Martin and Enigma Managing Director Pete about the opportunities available to you.</p> Career-ready placements <p>You will complete 140 hours of supervised placement that enable you to apply knowledge developed throughout your studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support your career readiness.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle City campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Studying at Central Coast campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/central-coast/living-on-the-central-coast"> Living on the Central Coast <p>The Central Coast offers a relaxed and convenient lifestyle with access to beautiful beaches and national parks. Our campuses have industry-leading facilities all within beautiful bushland.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Student highlights <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2026/sukontha-thongkao"> <p>Student</p> Learning, leading, and connecting <p>Business student, Sukontha, is turning her people skills into purpose through human resources, leadership, and real-world experience.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2026/saying-yes-to-opportunity-makenzies-journey-through-law-and-business"> <p>Student</p> Saying Yes to Opportunity: Makenzie’s Journey Through Law and Business <p>Makenzie is turning opportunity into real-world experience across business and law.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2024/jiaqian-ling"> <p>Student</p> Transforming Travel: From tourist to tourism management and marketing <p>Taking any opportunities that came her way, Jiaqian was able to develop a range of skills that gave her the confidence to determine what she wanted her future to look like in Tourism Management</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2024/le-nguyn-hoang-thong"> <p>Student</p> Chasing childhood dreams of becoming an Entrepreneur <p>Le Nguyen Hoang Thong, well known amongst peers as ‘Timmy’, decided to pursue a Bachelor of Business at the University of Newcastle, double majoring in Leadership, Management and Marketing to fulfil his childhood dream of becoming an Entrepreneur.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2024/kayla-business-and-management"> <p>Student</p> Growing as an individual through tertiary study <p>After spending some time in the workforce, Kayla recognised the need for formal qualifications to further her career. With a keen interest in social media marketing, she decided to pursue a Bachelor of Business at the University of Newcastle, with a major in marketing.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2022/ruofei-li"> <p>Student</p> Discovering a passion for marketing in international study <p>Ruofei Li (Roffy) began her career in Newcastle and discovered a passion which has carried her into a dream role. Find out about how Newcastle helped shape her journey here.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Real-world experience - Bachelor of Business student Will at Fresh Marketing 1:00 <p>As part of his degree, Bachelor of Business graduate Will interned with Newcastle-based boutique marketing agency Fresh Marketing. He gained hands-on campaign experience and made valuable industry contacts – giving him a leg up in a competitive industry.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/482202"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p><a href="https://www.psb-academy.edu.sg/the-university-of-newcastle-australia/bachelor-of-business">Apply via PSB</a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=50034">Apply online</a><a href="https://www.psb-academy.edu.sg/the-university-of-newcastle-australia/bachelor-of-business">Apply via PSB</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-business-laws-honours">Bachelor of Business / Bachelor of Laws (Honours)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 87.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 37,400</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 5 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 12 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="undergraduate-certificate-in-innovation-and-entrepreneurship">Undergraduate Certificate in Innovation and Entrepreneurship<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 60.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> undefined</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 0.5 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 3 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-commerce">Bachelor of Commerce<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,565</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/business-and-management">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://www.ahri.com.au"></a><p>The Bachelor of Business (HRM major) is accredited by the Australian Human Resource Management Institute (AHRI) https://www.ahri.com.au/</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>You will complete 140 hours of supervised placement that enable you to apply knowledge developed throughout your studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support your career readiness.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
