UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Make your mark on the global economy</p><p>Business and commerce are the foundations of our global economy. And there are countless opportunities to forge a solid career in these fields when you combine the Bachelor of Business with the Bachelor of Commerce.</p> <p>Through courses in your chosen majors, you will gain insight into the interplay between the financial, legal, political and economic systems and how these factors influence the contemporary business environment, both in Australian and global contexts.</p><p>Industry placements will build your workplace confidence and prepare you for the real world beyond your studies.</p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <p> <strong> World top 100 ? </strong> for Hospitality and Tourism Management </p> <p> <strong> World top 150 ? </strong> for Business Administration </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Embedding commerce and business into a combined degree program with practical experiences in diverse industries makes you extremely employable in both the public and private sectors.</p> <p>Depending on your chosen areas of study, careers might include:</p><ul><li>business development executive</li><li>data and business analyst</li><li>market research analyst</li><li>government advisor</li><li>marketing manager</li><li>entrepreneur</li></ul> <p>91.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Business and Management</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You will establish a firm understanding of the contemporary business environment and undertake studies in a range of disciplines. You''ll have the opportunity to double-major, selecting one major from each of the business and commerce programs.</p><p><strong>You will develop skills in the following areas:</strong></p><ul><li>accounting</li><li>management</li><li>law</li><li>marketing</li><li>microeconomics</li><li>finance</li><li>business decision making</li></ul>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-business">Bachelor of Business (from 2025)</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-commerce">Bachelor of Commerce (from 2025)</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ACCT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT1001">Fundamentals of Accounting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>BUSN1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN1010">Analytics in Business</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ECON1111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON1111">Economics for Business Decisions</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN1001">Fundamentals of Finance</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>INOV1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV1001">Design Thinking: Creativity in Action</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50066">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BUSN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3002">Industry Placement</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BUSN3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3004">Career-Ready Industry Led Project Lab</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BUSN3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3500">International Work Placement in Business</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50066">handbook</a>.</p>Business Majors<p><a href="#">Innovation and Entrepreneurship</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of the major.</p><ul><li><strong>INOV2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2001">Entrepreneurial MakerSpace</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2002">Social Entrepreneurship for Impact</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2003">Data Analytics in Digital Entrepreneurship</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2004">Prompt Engineering for Innovation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3001">Global Networking and Negotiation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3002">Traction and Growth</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3003">Venture Funding</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3004">Acceleration for Student Entrepreneurs (I2N)</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Innovation and Entrepreneurship"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50066">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Marketing</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MKTG2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2001">Digital and Social Media Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2010">Marketing Research and Data-Driven Insights</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2060">International Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2101">Consumer Decision Making</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3000">Strategic Marketing Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3003">Creating and Managing Brands</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3004">Advertising and Image Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3040">Services Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Marketing"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50066">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Leadership and Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2005">Leadership Models and Practices</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2006">Management in Environmental Turbulence</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2008">Digital Business Applications</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT2009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2009">Organisational Behaviour</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3011">Leading Organisational Change</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3012">Business Strategy</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3013</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3013">Innovation Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3014</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3014">Managing Inclusion, Diversity and Equity in Organisations</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Leadership and Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50066">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Resource Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>HRER2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2001">Managing Talent</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2002">Introduction to Employment Relations</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2003">Dynamics of People and Work in Organisations</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2004">HR Analytics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3001">Future of Work</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3002">Negotiation and Conflict Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3003">Strategic HR</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3004">Human Capital Development</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Resource Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50066">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Relations</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2002">Business and the Politics of Globalisation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2004">Diplomacy, Trade and Politics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3001">Public Diplomacy and Social Media</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3002">Global Data Governance for Just and Sustainable Futures</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3003">International Relations in a Changing World Order</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3004">Indigenising International Politics, Policy and the Economy</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50066">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Business</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IBUS2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2001">Cross-Cultural Management and Negotiations</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2003">International Trade Logistics in a Digital Age</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2004">Managing International Business</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2005">Corporate Social Responsibility for Global Business</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3000">International Business Strategy</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3001">International Human Resource Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3004">International Business Alliances</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3005">International Business in Emerging Markets</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Business"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50066">handbook</a>.</p>Commerce Majors<p><a href="#">Accounting</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>ACCT2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT2001">Accounting Practice and Reporting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT2002">Management Accounting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT2003">Financial Accounting and Reporting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3001">Auditing and Assurance</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3002">Accounting for Corporate Entities</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3003">Taxation</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3004">Accounting Information Systems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>LEGL2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LEGL2010">Australian Business and Company Law</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Accounting"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50066">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Economics</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>ECON2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2001">Microeconomics for Business</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2002">Intermediate Macroeconomics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON2111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2111"> Econometrics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON2112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2112"> Health Economics and Finance</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3006">Environmental Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3009">Urban and Regional Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3111">Behavioural Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3112">International Economics and Payment Infrastructure</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Economics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50066">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Finance</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>FINN2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2001">Financial Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2002">Debt Securities and Bank Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2003">Financial Technologies and Innovations</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2004">International Finance</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3001">Financial Modelling</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3002">Investment Analysis and Portfolio Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3003">Derivative Securities</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3004">Alternative Investments</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Finance"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50066">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 80 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50066">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50066">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Business / Bachelor of Commerce</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=50066&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=NCLE&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Career-ready placement at KPMG 1:27 <p>Hear from international student Heidi, who completed her career-ready placement with KPMG Newcastle.</p> Career-ready placements <p>Students will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within their third year of study that will enable them to apply knowledge developed throughout their studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support career readiness. The professional experience placement course provides an opportunity to undertake workplace experience in the desired career field, including business analysis, consulting, project management, marketing, and business development.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle City campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Studying at Central Coast campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/central-coast/living-on-the-central-coast"> Living on the Central Coast <p>The Central Coast offers a relaxed and convenient lifestyle with access to beautiful beaches and national parks. Our campuses have industry-leading facilities all within beautiful bushland.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase The power of Work Integrated Learning 2:20 <p>Thinking of completing or hosting a Work Integrated Learning opportunity? Hear firsthand from Alumnus Martin and Enigma Managing Director Pete about the opportunities available to you.</p> Real-world experience - Bachelor of Business student Will at Fresh Marketing 1:00 <p>As part of his degree, Bachelor of Business graduate Will interned with Newcastle-based boutique marketing agency Fresh Marketing. He gained hands-on campaign experience and made valuable industry contacts – giving him a leg up in a competitive industry.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/482205"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=50066">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-business">Bachelor of Business<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,540</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-laws-honours">Bachelor of Laws (Honours) Combined<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 87.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> undefined</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 5 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 12 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-commerce">Bachelor of Commerce<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,565</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/business-and-management">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://www.ahri.com.au"></a><p>The Bachelor of Business (HRM major) is accredited by the Australian Human Resource Management Institute (AHRI) https://www.ahri.com.au/</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Students will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within their third year of study that will enable them to apply knowledge developed throughout their studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support career readiness. The professional experience placement course provides an opportunity to undertake workplace experience in the desired career field, including business analysis, consulting, project management, marketing, and business development.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
