UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Make your mark on the global economy</p><p>Business and commerce are the foundations of our global economy. And there are countless opportunities to forge a solid career in these fields when you combine the Bachelor of Business with the Bachelor of Commerce.</p> <p>Through courses in your chosen major, you will gain insight into the interplay between the financial, legal, political and economic systems and how these factors influence the contemporary business environment, both in Australian and global contexts.</p><p>Industry placements will build your workplace confidence and prepare you for the real world beyond your studies.</p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <p> <strong> World top 100 ? </strong> for Hospitality and Tourism Management </p> <p> <strong> World top 150 ? </strong> for Business Administration </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Embedding commerce and business into a combined degree program with practical experiences in diverse industries makes you extremely employable in both the public and private sectors.</p> <p>Depending on your chosen areas of study, careers might include:</p><ul><li>business development executive</li><li>data and business analyst</li><li>market research analyst</li><li>government advisor</li><li>marketing manager</li><li>entrepreneur</li></ul> <p>89.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2021-2023 - Undergraduate Business and Management</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You will establish a firm understanding of the contemporary business environment and undertake studies in a range of disciplines. You''ll have the opportunity to select your courses from seven business and commerce related majors.</p><p><strong>You will develop skills in the following areas:</strong></p><ul><li>accounting</li><li>management</li><li>law</li><li>marketing</li><li>microeconomics</li><li>finance</li><li>business decision making</li></ul>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-business-pre-2025">Bachelor of Business (pre 2025)</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-commerce-pre-2025">Bachelor of Commerce (pre 2025)</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>LEGL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LEGL1001">Foundations of Law</a></li><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a></li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><strong>STAT1060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1060">Business Decision Making</a></li><li><em>5 additional courses are part of "Core Courses" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement Course List</a></p><ul><li><strong>BUSN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3002">Industry Placement</a></li><li><strong>BUSN3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3500">International Work Placement in Business</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p>Business Majors<p><a href="#">Entrepreneurship and Innovation</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>LEGL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LEGL1001">Foundations of Law</a></li><li><em>4 additional courses are part of "Entrepreneurship and Innovation" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 30 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 2000 level and a minimum of 20 units at the 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2006">Management in Environmental Turbulence</a></li><li><em>5 additional courses are part of "Entrepreneurship and Innovation" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Entrepreneurship and Innovation"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Resource Management</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><em>5 additional courses are part of "Human Resource Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 20 units from the following course list.</p><p>5 courses are part of "Human Resource Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Resource Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Business</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfill the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IBUS2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2001">Cross-Cultural Management and Negotiations</a></li><li><strong>IBUS2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2003">International Trade Logistics in a Digital Age</a></li><li><strong>IBUS3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3000">International Business Strategy</a></li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "International Business" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 30 units from the following course list.</p><p>7 courses are part of "International Business" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Business"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Leadership and Management</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfill the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><strong>MNGT2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2005">Leadership Models and Practices</a></li><li><strong>MNGT3011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3011">Leading Organisational Change</a></li><li><strong>MNGT3012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3012">Business Strategy</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 2000 level and a minimum of 20 units at the 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2006">Management in Environmental Turbulence</a></li><li><em>9 additional courses are part of "Leadership and Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Leadership and Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Marketing</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfill the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a></li><li><strong>MKTG2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2010">Marketing Research and Data-Driven Insights</a></li><li><strong>MKTG2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2101">Consumer Decision Making</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3000">Strategic Marketing Management</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>MKTG3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3003">Creating and Managing Brands</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3004">Advertising and Image Management</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3040">Services Marketing</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Marketing" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Marketing"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Politics and International Relations</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>LEGL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LEGL1001">Foundations of Law</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Politics and International Relations" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 50 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level, 10 units at 2000 level, and 30 units at 3000 level).</p><p>9 courses are part of "Politics and International Relations" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Politics and International Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Sports Management</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfill the requirements of this major</p><ul><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a></li><li><em>4 additional courses are part of "Sports Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list</p><p>1 courses are part of "Sports Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p><strong>Directed Courses </strong>Choose 20 units from the following course list. Note: Students can only count one of BUSN3001, BUSN3002, BUSN3500 or BUSN3600 towards the major. They may choose the other courses as electives.</p><ul><li><strong>BUSN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3002">Industry Placement</a></li><li><strong>BUSN3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3500">International Work Placement in Business</a></li><li><strong>EDUC4015</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4015">Sociology of Health and Physical Education, Sport and Physical Activity</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3040">Services Marketing</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Sports Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Sports Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Tourism and Event Management</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete all Compulsory courses for the major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><em>4 additional courses are part of "Tourism and Event Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 30 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 2000 level and a minimum of 20 units at the 3000 level).</p><p>4 courses are part of "Tourism and Event Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Tourism and Event Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p>Commerce Majors<p><a href="#">Accounting</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory</strong></p><p>8 courses are part of "Accounting" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Accounting"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Economics</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ECON2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2001">Microeconomics for Business</a></li><li><strong>ECON2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2002">Intermediate Macroeconomics</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Economics" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 30 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>ECON3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3006">Environmental Economics</a></li><li><strong>ECON3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3009">Urban and Regional Economics</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Economics" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Economics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Finance</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory</strong></p><p>5 courses are part of "Finance" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Students must complete 30 units from the following course list.</p><p>6 courses are part of "Finance" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Finance"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 90 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40035">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Business / Bachelor of Commerce</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=40035&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=NCLE&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a> </p> Student experience Career-ready placement at KPMG 1:27 <p>Hear from international student Heidi, who completed her career-ready placement with KPMG Newcastle.</p> Career-ready placements <p>Students will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within their third year of study that will enable them to apply knowledge developed throughout their studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support career readiness. The professional experience placement course provides an opportunity to undertake workplace experience in the desired career field, including business analysis, consulting, project management, marketing, and business development.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle City campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase The power of Work Integrated Learning 2:20 <p>Thinking of completing or hosting a Work Integrated Learning opportunity? Hear firsthand from Alumnus Martin and Enigma Managing Director Pete about the opportunities available to you.</p> Real-world experience - Bachelor of Business student Will at Fresh Marketing 1:00 <p>As part of his degree, Bachelor of Business graduate Will interned with Newcastle-based boutique marketing agency Fresh Marketing. He gained hands-on campaign experience and made valuable industry contacts – giving him a leg up in a competitive industry.</p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-laws-honours">Bachelor of Laws (Honours) Combined<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 87.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> undefined</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 5 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 12 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-commerce-pre-2025">Bachelor of Commerce<p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-business-pre-2025">Bachelor of Business<p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/business-and-management">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://www.accaglobal.com/gb/en.html"></a><p>Exemptions may apply for the Association of Chartered Certified Accountants (ACCA) for students who complete the Bachelor of Commerce (Accounting major).Please visit: http://www.accaglobal.com/an/en.html</p><a href="https://www.ahri.com.au"></a><p>The Bachelor of Business (HRM major) is accredited by the Australian Human Resource Management Institute (AHRI) https://www.ahri.com.au/</p><a href="https://www.aiaworldwide.com/"></a><p>Exemptions from selected examinations may be awarded to University of Newcastle graduates who have completed the Bachelor of Commerce degree program with a focus on Accounting. For specific information regarding exemptions please refer to the AIA Database at: http://www.aiaworldwide.com</p><a href="https://www.cpaaustralia.com.au/"></a><p>Students must complete the units set out in the CPA and CA Australia and New Zealand accreditation requirements in order to meet the academic requirements for Associate membership of CPA Australia and enrolment in the CPA Program, and for enrolment in the Chartered Accountants Program of CA Australia and New Zealand. For further information see the document in the Additional Information section or go to CPA Australia at https://www.cpaaustralia.com.au/ or CA Australia and New Zealand at https://www.charteredaccountantsanz.com/Students can find lists of Accredited courses at:https://apps.cpaaustralia.com.au/search-accredited-search/</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Students will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within their third year of study that will enable them to apply knowledge developed throughout their studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support career readiness. The professional experience placement course provides an opportunity to undertake workplace experience in the desired career field, including business analysis, consulting, project management, marketing, and business development.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
