UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Become a business law expert</p><p>Combining the Bachelor of Business with a Bachelor of Laws (Combined) will open you up to a myriad of career opportunities. Not only will you gain a broad understanding of Australian and global business environments, but you will also develop a strong legal understanding and the ability to apply logical reasoning which can be used within various business settings.</p> <p>You will have hands-on experience with opportunities to work on real cases, while gaining essential courtroom experience. This degree is a combined program meaning you will gain two qualifications in only five years of study.</p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <p> <strong> World top 300 ? </strong> for Law </p> <p> <strong> World top 150 ? </strong> for Business Administration </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Undertaking studies in law not only prepares graduates for a career in the legal profession but a huge variety of other roles in sectors ranging from government and business to media and the arts.</p> <p>On completion of this degree, you’ll be able to work in roles such as:</p><ul><li>business development manager</li><li>corporate/commercial lawyer</li><li>in-house counsel</li><li>policy/compliance officer</li><li>financial analyst</li><li>human resources manager</li></ul> <p>91.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Business and Management</p> <p>90.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Law and Paralegal Studies</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Within the combined degree program, students study a combination of Bachelor of Business and Bachelor of Laws (Honours) courses over a period of five years full-time. On completion of the first three years students will have completed all the courses required for the Bachelor of Business degree. In the final two years of the combined degree program students complete the requirements for the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) and may enrol in these two years on a less than full time basis.</p><p>Students completing this combined degree program become specialists in Business and meet the academic requirements to practice law in NSW. However, students wishing to practice law must also complete postgraduate professional training approved by the Legal Profession Admission Board. Alternatively, students completing this degree may apply for entry to the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) /Diploma of Legal Practice Program - see separate handbook entry - which allows immediate admission to legal practice on graduation.</p><p>Domestic students who commence full time in Semester 2 should expect to complete the program in a minimum 5.5 years.</p>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-business">Bachelor of Business (from 2025)</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-laws-honours">Bachelor of Laws (Honours) Combined</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ACCT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT1001">Fundamentals of Accounting</a></li><li><strong>BUSN1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN1010">Analytics in Business</a></li><li><strong>FINN1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN1001">Fundamentals of Finance</a></li><li><strong>INOV1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV1001">Design Thinking: Creativity in Action</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1010">Legal System and Method I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1011">Legal System and Method II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1020">Torts I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1021</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1021">Torts II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS2030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS2030">Criminal Law and Procedure</a></li><li><strong>LAWS3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS3040">Contracts I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS3041</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS3041">Contracts II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4001">Constitutional Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4002">Administrative Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4003">Civil Dispute Resolution</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4004">Evidence</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4005">Company Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4007</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4007">Professional Conduct</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4010">Equity and Trusts</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4011">Property</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4012">Public International Law</a></li><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a></li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BUSN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3002">Industry Placement</a></li><li><strong>BUSN3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3004">Career-Ready Industry Led Project Lab</a></li><li><strong>BUSN3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3500">International Work Placement in Business</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Business Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ACCT3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3005">Business Analysis and Valuation</a></li><li><strong>BUSN2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN2001">Ethical Principles for Responsible Business</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Business Course List" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50036">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Business Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Law Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 80 units from the following courses across Years 4 and 5.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>LAWS5036</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS5036">International Clinical Legal Externship</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6016</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6016">Taxation Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6017</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6017">Family Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6020">Environmental Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6021</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6021">Advanced Criminal Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6024">Employment Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6038</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6038">Law and Economics of Climate Change</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6043</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6043">Advanced Legal Research Project</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6087</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6087">Internet Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6090">Health Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6091</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6091">Special Interest Topic</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6094</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6094">Indigenous Peoples, Issues and the Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6096</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6096">Child Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6097</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6097">Competitive Mooting</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6099</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6099">Sport and the Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6102">Alternative Dispute Resolution</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6151</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6151">Gender and the Law</a></li><li><em>35 additional courses are part of "Law Course List" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50036">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Law Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50036">handbook</a>.</p>Business Major<p><a href="#">Innovation and Entrepreneurship</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of the major.</p><ul><li><strong>INOV2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2001">Entrepreneurial MakerSpace</a></li><li><strong>INOV2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2002">Social Entrepreneurship for Impact</a></li><li><strong>INOV2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2003">Data Analytics in Digital Entrepreneurship</a></li><li><strong>INOV2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2004">Prompt Engineering for Innovation</a></li><li><strong>INOV3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3001">Global Networking and Negotiation</a></li><li><strong>INOV3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3002">Traction and Growth</a></li><li><strong>INOV3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3003">Venture Funding</a></li><li><strong>INOV3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3004">Acceleration for Student Entrepreneurs (I2N)</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Innovation and Entrepreneurship"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Marketing</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MKTG2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2001">Digital and Social Media Marketing</a></li><li><strong>MKTG2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2010">Marketing Research and Data-Driven Insights</a></li><li><strong>MKTG2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2060">International Marketing</a></li><li><strong>MKTG2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2101">Consumer Decision Making</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3000">Strategic Marketing Management</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3003">Creating and Managing Brands</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3004">Advertising and Image Management</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3040">Services Marketing</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Marketing"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Leadership and Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2005">Leadership Models and Practices</a></li><li><strong>MNGT2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2006">Management in Environmental Turbulence</a></li><li><strong>MNGT2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2008">Digital Business Applications</a></li><li><strong>MNGT2009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2009">Organisational Behaviour</a></li><li><strong>MNGT3011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3011">Leading Organisational Change</a></li><li><strong>MNGT3012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3012">Business Strategy</a></li><li><strong>MNGT3013</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3013">Innovation Management</a></li><li><strong>MNGT3014</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3014">Managing Inclusion, Diversity and Equity in Organisations</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Leadership and Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Resource Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>HRER2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2001">Managing Talent</a></li><li><strong>HRER2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2002">Introduction to Employment Relations</a></li><li><strong>HRER2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2003">Dynamics of People and Work in Organisations</a></li><li><strong>HRER2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2004">HR Analytics</a></li><li><strong>HRER3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3001">Future of Work</a></li><li><strong>HRER3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3002">Negotiation and Conflict Management</a></li><li><strong>HRER3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3003">Strategic HR</a></li><li><strong>HRER3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3004">Human Capital Development</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Resource Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Relations</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2002">Business and the Politics of Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a></li><li><strong>IREL2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2004">Diplomacy, Trade and Politics</a></li><li><strong>IREL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3001">Public Diplomacy and Social Media</a></li><li><strong>IREL3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3002">Global Data Governance for Just and Sustainable Futures</a></li><li><strong>IREL3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3003">International Relations in a Changing World Order</a></li><li><strong>IREL3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3004">Indigenising International Politics, Policy and the Economy</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Business</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IBUS2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2001">Cross-Cultural Management and Negotiations</a></li><li><strong>IBUS2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2003">International Trade Logistics in a Digital Age</a></li><li><strong>IBUS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2004">Managing International Business</a></li><li><strong>IBUS2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2005">Corporate Social Responsibility for Global Business</a></li><li><strong>IBUS3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3000">International Business Strategy</a></li><li><strong>IBUS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3001">International Human Resource Management</a></li><li><strong>IBUS3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3004">International Business Alliances</a></li><li><strong>IBUS3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3005">International Business in Emerging Markets</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Business"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50036">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50036">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Business / Bachelor of Laws (Honours)</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=50036&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=NCLE&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience The power of career-ready placements 2:20 <p>Thinking of completing or hosting a career-ready placement opportunity? Hear firsthand from Alumnus Martin and Enigma Managing Director Pete about the opportunities available to you.</p> Career-ready placements <p>Law students complete the first 105 hours of required supervised clinical legal experience under the supervision of solicitors from our School. School staff also assist to arrange external placements to make up the remaining 180 hours required to qualify to practise as a lawyer. The Bachelor of Business integrates opportunities for you to gain national and international workplace experience.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle City campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Real-world experience - Bachelor of Business student Will at Fresh Marketing 1:00 <p>As part of his degree, Bachelor of Business graduate Will interned with Newcastle-based boutique marketing agency Fresh Marketing. He gained hands-on campaign experience and made valuable industry contacts – giving him a leg up in a competitive industry.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/483100"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=50036">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-business">Bachelor of Business<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,540</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-laws-honours">Bachelor of Laws (Honours) Combined<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 87.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> undefined</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 5 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 12 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-commerce">Bachelor of Commerce<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,565</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/business-and-management">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://www.ahri.com.au"></a><p>The Bachelor of Business (HRM major) is accredited by the Australian Human Resource Management Institute (AHRI) https://www.ahri.com.au/</p><a href="https://lpab.nsw.gov.au/"></a><p>Our LLB (Hons) is accredited by the Legal Profession Admission Board (LPAB) of New South Wales. It provides you with all the academic study necessary to apply to practice as a lawyer in Australia, subject to completing an accredited practical legal training program (including the required number of hours of supervised legal work experience) and satisfying the LPAB’s ‘fit and proper person’ test. For more details see the LPAB’s ‘Guide for Applicants’, or for specific inquiries please contact the LPAB.If you would like to complete an accredited program of practical legal training and supervised legal work experience while you complete your academic legal studies under the LLB (Hons), then you may enrol in, from the fourth year of LLB (Hons) studies, our combined LLB (Hons)/ Diploma of Legal Practice.</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Law students complete the first 105 hours of required supervised clinical legal experience under the supervision of solicitors from our School. School staff also assist to arrange external placements to make up the remaining 180 hours required to qualify to practise as a lawyer. The Bachelor of Business integrates opportunities for you to gain national and international workplace experience.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
