UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Become a business law expert</p><p>Combining the Bachelor of Business with a Bachelor of Laws (Combined) will open you up to a myriad of career opportunities. Not only will you gain a broad understanding of Australian and global business environments, but you will also develop a strong legal understanding and the ability to apply logical reasoning which can be used within various business settings.</p> <p>You will have hands-on experience with opportunities to work on real cases, while gaining essential courtroom experience. This degree is a combined program meaning you will gain two qualifications in only five years of study.</p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <p> <strong> World top 300 ? </strong> for Law </p> <p> <strong> World top 150 ? </strong> for Business Administration </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Undertaking studies in law not only prepares graduates for a career in the legal profession but a huge variety of other roles in sectors ranging from government and business to media and the arts.</p> <p>On completion of this degree, you’ll be able to work in roles such as:</p><ul><li>business development manager</li><li>corporate/commercial lawyer</li><li>in-house counsel</li><li>policy/compliance officer</li><li>financial analyst</li><li>human resources manager</li></ul> <p>89.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2021-2023 - Undergraduate Business and Management</p> <p>89.6% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2021-2023 - Undergraduate Law and Paralegal Studies</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Within the combined degree program, students study a combination of Bachelor of Business and Bachelor of Laws (Honours) courses over a period of five years full-time. On completion of the first three years students will have completed all the courses required for the Bachelor of Business degree. In the final two years of the combined degree program students complete the requirements for the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) and may enrol in these two years on a less than full time basis.</p><p>Students completing this combined degree program become specialists in Business and meet the academic requirements to practice law in NSW. However, students wishing to practice law must also complete postgraduate professional training approved by the Legal Profession Admission Board. Alternatively, students completing this degree may apply for entry to the Bachelor of Laws (Honours) /Diploma of Legal Practice Program - see separate handbook entry - which allows immediate admission to legal practice on graduation.</p><p>Domestic students who commence full time in Semester 2 should expect to complete the program in a minimum 5.5 years.</p>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-business-pre-2025">Bachelor of Business (pre 2025)</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-laws-honours">Bachelor of Laws (Honours) Combined</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses - Business</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a></li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><strong>STAT1060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1060">Business Decision Making</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Core Courses - Business" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses - Business"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Core Courses - Law</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>LAWS1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1010">Legal System and Method I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1011">Legal System and Method II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1020">Torts I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1021</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1021">Torts II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS2030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS2030">Criminal Law and Procedure</a></li><li><strong>LAWS3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS3040">Contracts I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS3041</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS3041">Contracts II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4001">Constitutional Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4002">Administrative Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4003">Civil Dispute Resolution</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4004">Evidence</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4005">Company Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4007</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4007">Professional Conduct</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4010">Equity and Trusts</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4011">Property</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4012">Public International Law</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses - Law"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Law Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 80 units from the following course list across Years 4 and 5.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>LAWS5036</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS5036">International Clinical Legal Externship</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6016</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6016">Taxation Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6017</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6017">Family Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6020">Environmental Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6021</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6021">Advanced Criminal Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6024">Employment Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6038</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6038">Law and Economics of Climate Change</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6043</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6043">Advanced Legal Research Project</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6087</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6087">Internet Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6090">Health Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6091</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6091">Special Interest Topic</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6094</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6094">Indigenous Peoples, Issues and the Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6096</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6096">Child Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6097</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6097">Competitive Mooting</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6099</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6099">Sport and the Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6102">Alternative Dispute Resolution</a></li><li><em>31 additional courses are part of "Law Course List" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Law Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BUSN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3002">Industry Placement</a></li><li><strong>BUSN3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3500">International Work Placement in Business</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p>Business Majors<p><a href="#">Entrepreneurship and Innovation</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Please note combined Law students receive an exemption for LEGL1001 in the Business degree.</p><p>4 courses are part of "Entrepreneurship and Innovation" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 30 units from the following courses (with a minimum of 10 units at the 2000 level and a minimum of 20 units at the 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2006">Management in Environmental Turbulence</a></li><li><em>5 additional courses are part of "Entrepreneurship and Innovation" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Entrepreneurship and Innovation"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Resource Management</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory</strong></p><ul><li><strong>LAWS6024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6024">Employment Law</a></li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><em>4 additional courses are part of "Human Resource Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 20 units from the following course list.</p><p>5 courses are part of "Human Resource Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Resource Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Business</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfill the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IBUS2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2001">Cross-Cultural Management and Negotiations</a></li><li><strong>IBUS2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2003">International Trade Logistics in a Digital Age</a></li><li><strong>IBUS3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3000">International Business Strategy</a></li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "International Business" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 30 units from the following course list.</p><p>7 courses are part of "International Business" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Business"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Leadership and Management</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfill the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><strong>MNGT2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2005">Leadership Models and Practices</a></li><li><strong>MNGT3011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3011">Leading Organisational Change</a></li><li><strong>MNGT3012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3012">Business Strategy</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 2000 level and a minimum of 20 units at the 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2006">Management in Environmental Turbulence</a></li><li><em>9 additional courses are part of "Leadership and Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Leadership and Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Marketing</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfill the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a></li><li><strong>MKTG2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2010">Marketing Research and Data-Driven Insights</a></li><li><strong>MKTG2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2101">Consumer Decision Making</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3000">Strategic Marketing Management</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>MKTG3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3003">Creating and Managing Brands</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3004">Advertising and Image Management</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3040">Services Marketing</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Marketing" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Marketing"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Politics and International Relations</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Please note combined Law students receive an exemption for LEGL1001 in the Business degree.</p><p>2 courses are part of "Politics and International Relations" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 50 units from the following courses (10 units at 1000 level, 10 units at 2000 level, and 30 units at 3000 level).</p><p>8 courses are part of "Politics and International Relations" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Politics and International Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Tourism and Event Management</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete all Compulsory courses for the major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><em>4 additional courses are part of "Tourism and Event Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 30 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 2000 level and a minimum of 20 units at the 3000 level).</p><p>4 courses are part of "Tourism and Event Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Tourism and Event Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 20 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40036">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Business / Bachelor of Laws (Honours)</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=40036&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=NCLE&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a> </p> Student experience The power of career-ready placements 2:20 <p>Thinking of completing or hosting a career-ready placement opportunity? Hear firsthand from Alumnus Martin and Enigma Managing Director Pete about the opportunities available to you.</p> Career-ready placements <p>Law students complete the first 105 hours of required supervised clinical legal experience under the supervision of solicitors from our School. School staff also assist to arrange external placements to make up the remaining 180 hours required to qualify to practise as a lawyer. The Bachelor of Business integrates opportunities for you to gain national and international workplace experience.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle City campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Real-world experience - Bachelor of Business student Will at Fresh Marketing 1:00 <p>As part of his degree, Bachelor of Business graduate Will interned with Newcastle-based boutique marketing agency Fresh Marketing. He gained hands-on campaign experience and made valuable industry contacts – giving him a leg up in a competitive industry.</p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-business-pre-2025">Bachelor of Business<p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-arts">Bachelor of Arts<p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-laws-honours">Bachelor of Laws (Honours) Combined<p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/business-and-management">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Law students complete the first 105 hours of required supervised clinical legal experience under the supervision of solicitors from our School. School staff also assist to arrange external placements to make up the remaining 180 hours required to qualify to practise as a lawyer. The Bachelor of Business integrates opportunities for you to gain national and international workplace experience.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
