UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Learn business locally. Do business globally</p><p>This program gives students a broad understanding of Australian and global business environments. You will graduate with skills and attributes valued by employers in disciplines.</p> <p><strong>These include:</strong></p><ul><li>human resource management</li><li>leadership</li><li>tourism/event management</li><li>entrepreneurship and innovation</li><li>politics</li><li>marketing</li><li>industrial relations and international business.</li></ul> <p> <strong> World top 100 ? </strong> for Hospitality and Tourism Management </p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <p> <strong> World top 150 ? </strong> for Business Administration </p> <p>89.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2021-2023 - Undergraduate Business and Management</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You will establish a firm understanding of the contemporary business environment and undertake studies in a range of disciplines. You''ll have the opportunity to select your courses from seven business-related majors.</p><p><strong>You will develop skills in the following areas:</strong></p><ul><li>accounting</li><li>management</li><li>law</li><li>marketing</li><li>microeconomics</li><li>finance</li><li>business decision making</li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>LEGL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LEGL1001">Foundations of Law</a></li><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a></li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><strong>STAT1060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1060">Business Decision Making</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Core Courses" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BUSN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3002">Industry Placement</a></li><li><strong>BUSN3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3500">International Work Placement in Business</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</p>Major<p><a href="#">Entrepreneurship and Innovation</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>LEGL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LEGL1001">Foundations of Law</a></li><li><em>4 additional courses are part of "Entrepreneurship and Innovation" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 30 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 2000 level and a minimum of 20 units at the 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2006">Management in Environmental Turbulence</a></li><li><em>5 additional courses are part of "Entrepreneurship and Innovation" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Entrepreneurship and Innovation"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Resource Management</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><em>5 additional courses are part of "Human Resource Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 20 units from the following course list.</p><p>5 courses are part of "Human Resource Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Resource Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Business</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfill the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IBUS2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2001">Cross-Cultural Management and Negotiations</a></li><li><strong>IBUS2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2003">International Trade Logistics in a Digital Age</a></li><li><strong>IBUS3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3000">International Business Strategy</a></li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "International Business" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 30 units from the following course list.</p><p>7 courses are part of "International Business" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Business"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Leadership and Management</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfill the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><strong>MNGT2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2005">Leadership Models and Practices</a></li><li><strong>MNGT3011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3011">Leading Organisational Change</a></li><li><strong>MNGT3012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3012">Business Strategy</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 2000 level and a minimum of 20 units at the 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2006">Management in Environmental Turbulence</a></li><li><em>9 additional courses are part of "Leadership and Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Leadership and Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Marketing</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfill the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a></li><li><strong>MKTG2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2010">Marketing Research and Data-Driven Insights</a></li><li><strong>MKTG2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2101">Consumer Decision Making</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3000">Strategic Marketing Management</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>MKTG3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3003">Creating and Managing Brands</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3004">Advertising and Image Management</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3040">Services Marketing</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Marketing" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Marketing"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Politics and International Relations</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>LEGL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LEGL1001">Foundations of Law</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Politics and International Relations" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 50 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level, 10 units at 2000 level, and 30 units at 3000 level).</p><p>9 courses are part of "Politics and International Relations" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Politics and International Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Tourism and Event Management</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete all Compulsory courses for the major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><em>4 additional courses are part of "Tourism and Event Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 30 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 2000 level and a minimum of 20 units at the 3000 level).</p><p>4 courses are part of "Tourism and Event Management" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Tourism and Event Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 90 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40027">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Business</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=40027&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=PSBC&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a> </p> Student experience The power of Work Integrated Learning 2:20 <p>Thinking of completing or hosting a career-ready placement opportunity? Hear firsthand from Alumnus Martin and Enigma Managing Director Pete about the opportunities available to you.</p> Career-ready placements <p>You will complete 140 hours of supervised placement that enable you to apply knowledge developed throughout your studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support your career readiness.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Student showcase Student highlights <!-- None --> Real-world experience - Bachelor of Business student Will at Fresh Marketing 1:00 <p>As part of his degree, Bachelor of Business graduate Will interned with Newcastle-based boutique marketing agency Fresh Marketing. He gained hands-on campaign experience and made valuable industry contacts – giving him a leg up in a competitive industry.</p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-business-laws-honours-pre-2025">Bachelor of Business / Bachelor of Laws (Honours)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 82.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 38,070</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 5 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 12 years</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-commerce-pre-2025">Bachelor of Commerce<ul><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 39,665</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> PSB Singapore</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-business-commerce-pre-2025">Bachelor of Business / Bachelor of Commerce<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 62.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 39,485</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/business-and-management">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>You will complete 140 hours of supervised placement that enable you to apply knowledge developed throughout your studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support your career readiness.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
