UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Work with some of the most unique and diverse coasts and marine ecosystems in the world</p><p>Learn from experts in marine, coastal and ecological fields, giving you practical skills to make a difference to our world. Our coastal and marine environments face issues like climate change, pollution and urbanisation. By understanding these ecological, physical, conservation, societal and management issues, we can help find solutions to these problems.</p> <p>You will engage in contemporary issues in the marine environment from day one. Our program features skills-based courses and extensive fieldwork opportunities and integrates subjects like biology, ecology, earth science and management of the coastal zone into your program.</p> <p> <strong> World top 200 ? </strong> for Environmental Sciences </p> <p> <strong> 88.4% of students ? </strong> were happy with facilities and resources </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Our skills-orientated courses provide students with strong expertise in conducting fieldwork using both traditional and novel techniques. and to analyse and interpret resultant data.</p><p>Our graduates are fully aware of the need for such data to be used for informing management approaches, and the expectations by the scientific and broader community to communicate those results in different forms.</p> <p>The flexible structure of this degree allows students to pursue careers that span all sectors of the marine and coastal workforce.</p><p><strong>Professional Outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>Environmental/Marine Consultant</li><li>Aquatic Ecologist</li><li>Scientific Officer</li><li>Catchment Management Officer</li><li>Environmental Education Officer</li><li>Fisheries Research Scientist/Technician/Officer</li><li>Aquaculture Research Scientist/Technician</li><li>Environment and Sustainability Coordinator</li><li>Land and Sea Ranger</li><li>Marine Policy Analyst</li><li>Marine Resource Manager</li><li>Ecotourism Coordinator</li></ul> <p>88.5% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Science &amp; Mathematics</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You will experience relevant field-based scenarios and engage with managers and policymakers from industry, government and the not-for-profit sectors. This will enable students to progress into a career that spans all sectors of the coastal and marine space. Courses that you will study could include:</p><ul><li>chemistry</li><li>food science</li><li>plant biology</li><li>sustainability</li><li>environmental science</li><li>animal biology</li><li>biodiversity and conservation</li><li>coastal processes</li><li>geography</li><li>sustainable tourism</li><li>indigenous environmental and community practice</li><li>communication</li><li>education</li><li>politics and policy</li></ul><p>Your fundamental marine science skills can be complemented by up to two minors, from a traditional science or non-traditional areas such as social science or communication.</p> <p>Core</p><p>Minors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ENVS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2004">Ecology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2320</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2320">Experimental Design and Analysis in Ecology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3008">Work Integrated Learning in the Environmental and Development Sectors</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS2161</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2161">Spatial Science</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3220">Coastal Environments and Processes</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI1000">Our Oceans</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>MARI2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI2300">Marine Biology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI3300">Integrated Coastal Ecosystems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI3500">Sustainable Fisheries and Aquaculture</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCIE1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE1002">Multidisciplinary Laboratories</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCIE2223</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE2223">Weather and Waves</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40210">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Mathematics Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following Mathematics course list. Which course you should complete will depend on your previous mathematical background, please refer to each course handbook for more information.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>MATH1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1001">Preparatory Studies in Mathematics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1002">Foundational Studies in Mathematics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1110">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 1</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Mathematics Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40210">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Statistics Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following Statistics course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>STAT1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1020">Statistical Reasoning and Literacy</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>STAT1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1070">Statistics for the Sciences</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Statistics Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40210">handbook</a>.</p>Minors<p><a href="#">Animal Biology</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses. NOTE: BIOL1002 is common across both biology and some environmental science minors in the Bachelor of Coastal and Marine Science. For those who complete a double minor where BIOL1002 appears in both minors, please complete an additional 2000 level BIOL course to ensure there is no course overlap.</p><ul><li><strong>BIOL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1001">Molecules, Cells and Organisms</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1002">Organisms to Ecosystems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL2050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2050">Molecular Genetics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL3020">Animal Physiology, Reproduction and Development</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Animal Biology"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40210">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Biodiversity and Conservation</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses.</p><ul><li><strong>BIOL1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1002">Organisms to Ecosystems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2005">Management of Australian Flora</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2006">Ecology and Management of Wildlife</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 10 units from the following directed courses.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3003">Conservation Biology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3005">Animal Behaviour</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Biodiversity and Conservation"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40210">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Cell and Molecular Biology</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses. NOTE: BIOL1002 is common across both biology and some environmental science minors in the Bachelor of Coastal and Marine Science. For those who complete a double minor where BIOL1002 appears in both minors, please complete an additional 2000 level BIOL course to ensure there is no course overlap.</p><ul><li><strong>BIOL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1001">Molecules, Cells and Organisms</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1002">Organisms to Ecosystems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL2050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2050">Molecular Genetics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL3090">Molecular Biology</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Cell and Molecular Biology"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40210">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Chemistry</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses.</p><ul><li><strong>CHEM1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1010">Introductory Chemistry I</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>CHEM1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1020">Introductory Chemistry II</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM2110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM2110">Applied Analytical Chemistry</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM2310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM2310">Organic Chemistry</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Chemistry"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40210">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Coastal and Surface Processes</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses.</p><ul><li><strong>GEOS1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS1050">Earth: Natural Hazards</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS2050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2050">Catchments and Climate</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2080">Earth''s Dynamic Surface</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3250</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3250">Advanced Spatial Science</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Coastal and Surface Processes"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40210">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Communication</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>1000 Level Directed Courses - Complete 20 units from the following directed courses.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>CMNS1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1100">Media, Culture and Narrative</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>CMNS1234</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1234">Media and Communication Concepts</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>2000 Level Directed Courses - Complete 20 units from the following directed courses.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2000">Digital Media Engagement</a> (Newcastle, Singapore