UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>More than just numbers. Study a commerce degree.</p><p>The Bachelor of Commerce is a practical and flexible degree, with core courses designed to give you a thorough overview of business and commerce environments.</p><p>Choose to major in two Commerce areas (e.g. Accounting and Finance), or opt for your second major in Business area (e.g. Marketing), to graduate a competitive candidate, in just three years.</p> <p>When you study a commerce degree, you will be equipped to make a smooth transition from the classroom to the boardroom, by acquiring practical skills that employers value, such as problem-solving and critical-thinking.</p><p>A sense of global citizenship is imparted through international case studies and cross-cultural analysis. Through courses in your chosen major, you will gain insight into the interlinkages between financial, legal, political and economic systems and how these factors influence the contemporary business environment, both in Australian and global context.</p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <p> <strong> AACSB &amp; EQUIS ? </strong> accredited business school <!-- no link --> </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Commerce graduates go on to exciting, stimulating and lucrative careers in the fields of accounting, auditing, consulting, stockbroking, business analysis and academia.</p> <p>Commerce graduates go on to exciting, stimulating and lucrative careers in the fields of accounting, auditing, consulting, stockbroking, business analysis and academia.</p><p>These opportunities can be pursued in a wide range of business, government departments and not-for-profit organisations.</p><p>On completion of this degree, you’ll be able to work in roles such as:</p><ul><li>Financial/Management Accountant</li><li>Auditor</li><li>Tax agent</li><li>Stockbroker/ Stock Trader</li><li>Financial Analyst</li><li>Mortgage Broker</li><li>Treasurer</li><li>Policy consultant</li><li>Data consultant</li><li>Development Economist</li></ul> <p>91.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Business and Management</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>We maintain strong relationships with employers and professional associations to ensure that the courses and majors offered in our degree maintain real-world relevance.</p><p>This degree gives you a strong grounding in business and economic principles, and you will learn core business development skills before selecting your major. You will also have the option to double major, or major and double minor in Accounting, Economics, or Finance. You will also have the option to select your second major from the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-business">Bachelor of Business</a> majors.</p><p><strong>You will develop skills in the following areas:</strong></p><ul><li>accounting</li><li>management</li><li>law</li><li>marketing</li><li>microeconomics</li><li>finance</li><li>business decision making</li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Minors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ACCT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT1001">Fundamentals of Accounting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>BUSN1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN1010">Analytics in Business</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ECON1111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON1111">Economics for Business Decisions</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN1001">Fundamentals of Finance</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>INOV1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV1001">Design Thinking: Creativity in Action</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BUSN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3002">Industry Placement</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BUSN3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3004">Career-Ready Industry Led Project Lab</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BUSN3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3500">International Work Placement in Business</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Commerce Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BUSN1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN1002">Business Communications</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BUSN2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN2001">Ethical Principles for Responsible Business</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IBUS2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2005">Corporate Social Responsibility for Global Business</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>LEGL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LEGL1001">Foundations of Law</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Commerce Course List" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Commerce Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p>Commerce Majors<p><a href="#">Accounting</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>ACCT2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT2001">Accounting Practice and Reporting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT2002">Management Accounting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT2003">Financial Accounting and Reporting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3001">Auditing and Assurance</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3002">Accounting for Corporate Entities</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3003">Taxation</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3004">Accounting Information Systems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>LEGL2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LEGL2010">Australian Business and Company Law</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Accounting"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Economics</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>ECON2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2001">Microeconomics for Business</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2002">Intermediate Macroeconomics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON2111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2111"> Econometrics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON2112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2112"> Health Economics and Finance</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3006">Environmental Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3009">Urban and Regional Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3111">Behavioural Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3112">International Economics and Payment Infrastructure</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Economics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Finance</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>FINN2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2001">Financial Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2002">Debt Securities and Bank Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2003">Financial Technologies and Innovations</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2004">International Finance</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3001">Financial Modelling</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3002">Investment Analysis and Portfolio Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3003">Derivative Securities</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3004">Alternative Investments</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Finance"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p>Business Majors<p><a href="#">Innovation and Entrepreneurship</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of the major.</p><ul><li><strong>INOV2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2001">Entrepreneurial MakerSpace</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2002">Social Entrepreneurship for Impact</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2003">Data Analytics in Digital Entrepreneurship</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2004">Prompt Engineering for Innovation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3001">Global Networking and Negotiation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3002">Traction and Growth</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3003">Venture Funding</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3004">Acceleration for Student Entrepreneurs (I2N)</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Innovation and Entrepreneurship"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Marketing</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MKTG2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2001">Digital and Social Media Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2010">Marketing Research and Data-Driven Insights</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2060">International Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2101">Consumer Decision Making</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3000">Strategic Marketing Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3003">Creating and Managing Brands</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3004">Advertising and Image Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3040">Services Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Marketing"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Leadership and Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2005">Leadership Models and Practices</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><s