trong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2003">Dynamics of People and Work in Organisations</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2004">HR Analytics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3001">Future of Work</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3002">Negotiation and Conflict Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3003">Strategic HR</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3004">Human Capital Development</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Resource Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Relations</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2002">Business and the Politics of Globalisation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2004">Diplomacy, Trade and Politics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3001">Public Diplomacy and Social Media</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3002">Global Data Governance for Just and Sustainable Futures</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3003">International Relations in a Changing World Order</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3004">Indigenising International Politics, Policy and the Economy</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Business</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IBUS2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2001">Cross-Cultural Management and Negotiations</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2003">International Trade Logistics in a Digital Age</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2004">Managing International Business</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2005">Corporate Social Responsibility for Global Business</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3000">International Business Strategy</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3001">International Human Resource Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3004">International Business Alliances</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3005">International Business in Emerging Markets</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Business"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p>Commerce Minors<p><a href="#">Accounting</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 40 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this minor.</p><ul><li><strong>ACCT2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT2001">Accounting Practice and Reporting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT2002">Management Accounting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3001">Auditing and Assurance</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>ACCT3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3004">Accounting Information Systems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Accounting"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Economics</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 40 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this minor.</p><ul><li><strong>ECON2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2001">Microeconomics for Business</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2002">Intermediate Macroeconomics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3006">Environmental Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3111">Behavioural Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Economics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Finance</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 40 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this minor.</p><ul><li><strong>FINN2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2001">Financial Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2003">Financial Technologies and Innovations</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3002">Investment Analysis and Portfolio Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3004">Alternative Investments</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Finance"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 80 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50037">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Commerce</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=50037&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=NCLE&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience From China to Newcastle: Zoe’s Business Journey 2:21 <p>Moving from China to Australia to study is a big step. For Zoe, it marked the beginning of a new chapter filled with change, opportunity and new experiences.</p> Meet Holly, Bachelor of Commerce Student 1:40 <p>Hear how studying a Bachelor in Commerce is giving Holly the tools to follow her passions in building financial literacy in her community through work-integrated learning experiences like the Greater Bank Finance Academy.</p> Career-ready placements at KPMG 1:44 <p>Hear from international student Heidi, who has done her career-ready placement with KPMG Newcastle.</p> Career-ready placements <p>Students will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within their third year of study that will enable them to apply knowledge developed throughout their studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support career readiness. The professional experience placement course provides an opportunity to undertake workplace experience in the desired career field, including business analysis, consulting, project management, marketing, and business development.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle City campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Studying at Central Coast campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/central-coast/living-on-the-central-coast"> Living on the Central Coast <p>The Central Coast offers a relaxed and convenient lifestyle with access to beautiful beaches and national parks. Our campuses have industry-leading facilities all within beautiful bushland.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Student Highlights <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2026/building-confidence-far-from-home"> <p>Student</p> Building confidence far from home <p>From China to Newcastle, one student is building independence, confidence, and a future in business.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2024/getting-down-to-business-with-a-future-investment"> <p>Student</p> Getting down to business with a future investment <p>Holly McKelligot began university hoping for a career in marketing, but soon found herself drawn in other directions.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2023/teck-hao-ng-jeffrey"> <p>Student</p> Jeffrey''s path as an international Commerce student in Newcastle <p>Jeffrey''s growth, resilience, and determination to make the most of his university experience while pursuing his career aspirations.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2023/natasha-put-her-dream-out-to-the-universe-and-it-came-true"> <p>Student</p> Natasha put her dream out to the universe. And it came true. <p>Dreams do come true, hear it first hand from Natasha.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2019/william-li"> <p>Student</p> Life changing experience in Newcastle <p>William Li is a Chinese international student studying a Bachelor of Commerce at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Meet Jeffrey, a Bachelor of Commerce student from Malaysia 1:23 <p>Jeffrey talks about his experience studying a Bachelor of Commerce at the University of Newcastle.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/482301"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p><a href="https://www.psb-academy.edu.sg/the-university-of-newcastle-australia/bachelor-of-commerce">Apply via PSB</a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=50037">Apply online</a><a href="https://www.psb-academy.edu.sg/the-university-of-newcastle-australia/bachelor-of-commerce">Apply via PSB</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-business-commerce">Bachelor of Business / Bachelor of Commerce<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,510</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-commerce-business-analytics">Bachelor of Commerce / Bachelor of Business Analytics<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,965</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-business">Bachelor of Business<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,540</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/business-and-management">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Students will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within their third year of study that will enable them to apply knowledge developed throughout their studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support career readiness. The professional experience placement course provides an opportunity to undertake workplace experience in the desired career field, including business analysis, consulting, project management, marketing, and business development.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
