UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Are you driven by data?</p><p>The quality, quantity and diversity of data available to businesses and the world over has never been greater. With many organisations relying on the expertise of business analysts to inform decision-making and strategic direction. As a result, career opportunities in this area have boomed.</p> <p>The Bachelor of Commerce/Bachelor of Business Analytics is a practical and flexible degree, with core courses designed to give you a thorough overview of business and commerce environments along with key analysis insights.</p><p>You will be equipped to make a smooth transition from the classroom to the boardroom, by acquiring skills that employers value.</p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <p> <strong> World top 150 ? </strong> for Business Administration </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>You could use your skills to inform strategic business direction or financial and economic trends in jobs such as:</p><ul><li>Commercial Analyst</li><li>eCommerce Specialist</li><li>Data Analyst</li><li>Business Analyst</li><li>Digital Solutions Developer</li><li>Financial Manager</li></ul> <p>91.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Business and Management</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>This combined degree program provides students with the opportunity to increase the depth and breadth of their study in relevant disciplines within Commerce and Business Analytics whilst completing two awards over four years of full-time study or part-time equivalent.</p><p>A combined degree program enhances the academic and professional qualities gained in each separate degree. At the same time, it recognises the increasing need for students to graduate with multidisciplinary skills.</p>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-commerce">Bachelor of Commerce (from 2025)</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-business-analytics">Bachelor of Business Analytics</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ACCT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT1001">Fundamentals of Accounting</a></li><li><strong>ACCT1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT1002">Business Acumen Fundamentals</a></li><li><strong>BUSA1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSA1001">Introduction to Business Information Systems</a></li><li><strong>BUSA2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSA2001">Big Data Analytics</a></li><li><strong>BUSA2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSA2002">Data Visualisation for Decision Makers in Business</a></li><li><strong>BUSA3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSA3001">Artificial Intelligence in Business</a></li><li><strong>BUSA3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSA3003">Business Process Modelling</a></li><li><strong>BUSN1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN1010">Analytics in Business</a></li><li><strong>EBUS3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EBUS3040">Business Intelligence in Practice</a></li><li><strong>ECON1111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON1111">Economics for Business Decisions</a></li><li><strong>ECON2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2003">Predictive Modelling in Business</a></li><li><strong>FINN1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN1001">Fundamentals of Finance</a></li><li><strong>INOV1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV1001">Design Thinking: Creativity in Action</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50039">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BUSN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3002">Industry Placement</a></li><li><strong>BUSN3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3004">Career-Ready Industry Led Project Lab</a></li><li><strong>BUSN3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3500">International Work Placement in Business</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50039">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 90 units from the list below, with a minimum of 10 units at the 2000 level.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BUSA3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSA3005">Cybersecurity for Business</a></li><li><strong>BUSA3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSA3006">Digital Ecosystems and Transformation</a></li><li><strong>BUSA3007</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSA3007">Data Governance Using Blockchain for Business</a></li><li><strong>BUSN1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN1002">Business Communications</a></li><li><strong>BUSN2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN2001">Ethical Principles for Responsible Business</a></li><li><strong>FINN2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2003">Financial Technologies and Innovations</a></li><li><strong>HRER2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2004">HR Analytics</a></li><li><strong>IBUS2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2005">Corporate Social Responsibility for Global Business</a></li><li><strong>INFT1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT1004">Introduction to Programming</a></li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a></li><li><strong>LEGL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LEGL1001">Foundations of Law</a></li><li><strong>MNGT2009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2009">Organisational Behaviour</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Course List" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50039">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50039">handbook</a>.</p>Commerce Major<p><a href="#">Accounting</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>ACCT2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT2001">Accounting Practice and Reporting</a></li><li><strong>ACCT2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT2002">Management Accounting</a></li><li><strong>ACCT2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT2003">Financial Accounting and Reporting</a></li><li><strong>ACCT3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3001">Auditing and Assurance</a></li><li><strong>ACCT3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3002">Accounting for Corporate Entities</a></li><li><strong>ACCT3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3003">Taxation</a></li><li><strong>ACCT3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT3004">Accounting Information Systems</a></li><li><strong>LEGL2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LEGL2010">Australian Business and Company Law</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Accounting"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50039">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Economics</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>ECON2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2001">Microeconomics for Business</a></li><li><strong>ECON2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2002">Intermediate Macroeconomics</a></li><li><strong>ECON2111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2111"> Econometrics</a></li><li><strong>ECON2112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2112"> Health Economics and Finance</a></li><li><strong>ECON3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3006">Environmental Economics</a></li><li><strong>ECON3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3009">Urban and Regional Economics</a></li><li><strong>ECON3111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3111">Behavioural Economics</a></li><li><strong>ECON3112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3112">International Economics and Payment Infrastructure</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Economics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50039">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Finance</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>FINN2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2001">Financial Management</a></li><li><strong>FINN2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2002">Debt Securities and Bank Management</a></li><li><strong>FINN2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2003">Financial Technologies and Innovations</a></li><li><strong>FINN2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN2004">International Finance</a></li><li><strong>FINN3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3001">Financial Modelling</a></li><li><strong>FINN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3002">Investment Analysis and Portfolio Management</a></li><li><strong>FINN3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3003">Derivative Securities</a></li><li><strong>FINN3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN3004">Alternative Investments</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Finance"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50039">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50039">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50039">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Commerce / Bachelor of Business Analytics</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=50039&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=NCLE&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Work Integrated Learning at KPMG 1:43 <p>Hear from international student Heidi, who completed her career-ready placement with KPMG Newcastle.</p> Career-ready placements <p>Students will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within their third year of study that will enable them to apply knowledge developed throughout their studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support career readiness. The professional experience placement course provides an opportunity to undertake workplace experience in the desired career field, including business analysis, consulting, project management, marketing, and business development.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle City campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/482303"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=50039">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-business-analytics">Bachelor of Business Analytics<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 41,110</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-commerce">Bachelor of Commerce<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,565</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-business-commerce">Bachelor of Business / Bachelor of Commerce<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,510</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/business-and-management">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Students will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within their third year of study that will enable them to apply knowledge developed throughout their studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support career readiness. The professional experience placement course provides an opportunity to undertake workplace experience in the desired career field, including business analysis, consulting, project management, marketing, and business development.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
