UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Develop the skills to equip you to work in diverse media industries.</p><p>Learn to push your creative boundaries. Embrace the changes occurring across today’s complex communication landscape. Choose your major area/s of study and develop work-ready skills, including critical thinking, writing, and producing creative and factual content.</p> <p>Course options prepare you to create content for many forms of media. These include social, radio, podcasting, broadcast, streaming, and news platforms. You can tailor your skills for specific areas of interest, including drama and documentary, gaming and lifestyle, strategic communications, public relations and corporate communications.</p><p>Communication integrates practical experience, critical analysis, and creative thinking with industry opportunities. You’ll be ready to take on a range of exciting careers.</p> <p> <strong> Cutting-edge facilities ? </strong> so you graduate work-ready <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/school/humanities-creative-industries-social-sciences/study-with-hciss/facilities">Find out more</a> </p> <p> <strong> Professional placement </strong> and practical opportunities </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Communication prepares you to work across a wide range of sectors and industries. It also opens pathways for further study and research.</p> <p>Employment outcomes span exciting, dynamic and growing fields across industries around the world such as media, journalism, public relations, advertising and marketing.</p><p>On completion of this degree, you’ll be able to work in roles such as:</p><ul><li>media consultant/PR consultant</li><li>festival/events coordinator</li><li>interactive media designer/developer</li><li>foreign affairs and trade officer</li><li>media production editor</li><li>campaign manager</li></ul> <p>91.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>This degree provides a solid foundation and in-depth understanding of communication theory and practice. Depending on your chosen major/s, you could study courses in various sectors of media production and theory including:</p><ul><li>cultural studies</li><li>magazine and broadcast journalism</li><li>media interviewing</li><li>media production</li><li>photomedia</li><li>professional writing</li><li>public relations practice</li><li>screenwriting</li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1100">Media, Culture and Narrative</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1234</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1234">Media and Communication Concepts</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2000">Digital Media Engagement</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2510</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2510">Global Media Industries</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2600">Audience Participation and Interaction</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3310">Communication and Creativity</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Core Courses" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following courses. Please note: Students studying at PSB Singapore must enrol in CIND3000.</strong></p><p>2 courses are part of "Career-ready placement Course List" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</p>COMM Majors<p><a href="#">Media Arts Production</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following 20 units of compulsory courses.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 60 units from the following course list; 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2016</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2016">Interactive Storytelling</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2035</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2035">Cinematography</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2130">Sound Production</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2180</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2180">Screenwriting</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2900">Documentary Filmmaking</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3440</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3440">Short Film Production</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3999</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3999">Advanced Media Production</a></li><li><em>4 additional courses are part of "Media Arts Production" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Media Arts Production"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">News Media</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following 20 units of compulsory courses.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 60 units from the following course list; 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2280</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2280">Feature Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2320</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2320">News Media</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2700">Create Your Own Business</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3150</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3150">Podcasting</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3333</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3333">Multiplatform Journalism</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3470</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3470">Data Visualisation in Journalism</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3666</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3666">Contemporary Journalism</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "News Media" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"News Media"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Public Relations</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following 20 units of compulsory courses.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 60 units from the following course list; 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2140</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2140">Principles of Public Relations</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2530</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2530">Organisational Communication</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2700">Create Your Own Business</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3520</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3520">Political Communication</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3540</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3540">Public Relations Campaigns</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3737</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3737">Social Media Listening and Monitoring</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Public Relations" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Public Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Media Studies</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the following course list; 20 units at 1000 level , 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>SCRN1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN1000">Media Literacy</a></li><li><strong>SCRN1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN1200">Film and Television Studies</a></li><li><strong>SCRN2100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN2100">Popular Music and Culture</a></li><li><strong>SCRN2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN2200">Popular Culture and Society</a></li><li><strong>SCRN3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN3000">Social Media and Digital Culture</a></li><li><strong>SCRN3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN3100">Peak TV: Texts, Industry, Culture</a></li><li><strong>SCRN3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN3300">Contemporary Cinema: Style, Culture, Story</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1010">Society and Culture: an Introduction to Sociology</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Media Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Media Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</p>SOCI Majors<p><a href="#">Animation and Interaction</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory course.</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1031</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1031">Visual Abstraction</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 70 units from the following course list (with a maximum of 10 units at the 1000 level and a minimum of 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1331</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1331">Character Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN1600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1600">Interaction Design (IxD) Fundamentals</a></li><li><strong>DESN1801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1801">Animation Thinking</a></li><li><strong>DESN2610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2610">User Interface (UI) Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN2801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2801">Animation Process</a></li><li><strong>DESN2804</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2804">Motion Graphic Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3600">Physical Experience (PxD) Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3801">Production Studio</a></li><li><strong>DESN3802</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3802">Environment Design</a></li><li><em>4 additional courses are part of "Animation and Interaction" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Animation and Interaction"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Creative Arts</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory course.</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1031</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1031">Visual Abstraction</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 70 units from the following course list (with a maximum of 10 units at the 1000 level and a minimum of 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>DESN2211</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2211">Visual Narrative</a></li><li><em>10 additional courses are part of "Creative Arts" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Creative Arts"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Graphic Design and Illustration</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory course.</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1031</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1031">Visual Abstraction</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 70 units from the following course list (with a maximum of 10 units at the 1000 level and a minimum of 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1101">Typography</a></li><li><strong>DESN1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1200">Drawing Foundations</a></li><li><strong>DESN1600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1600">Interaction Design (IxD) Fundamentals</a></li><li><strong>DESN2011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2011">Design Futures</a></li><li><strong>DESN2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2060">Scientific Illustration</a></li><li><strong>DESN2221</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2221">Graphic Brand Identities and Spaces</a></li><li><strong>DESN3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3040">Commercial Illustration</a></li><li><strong>DESN3321</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3321">Publication Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3411</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3411">Studio: Professional Portfolio</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Graphic Design and Illustration" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Graphic Design and Illustration"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 80 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11496">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Communication (Singapore)</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=11496&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=PSBC&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience JJ and Oli''s Bachelor of Media and Communication story 2:54 <p>Check out JJ and Oli''s study journey into a Bachelor of Media and Communication. Using state of the art equipment allows students to gain real experience and become career ready.</p> Blue Heeler Film Festival 1:46 <p>Hear from our students about their work career-ready placement at the Blue Heeler Film Festival.</p> Career-ready placements <p>You will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within your third year of study. Workplace experience is undertaken in your desired career field, including media, journalism, public relations, advertising, marketing, theatre production, musical ensembles, performing arts and visual communications.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Student showcase <a href="/media/viewer?media=904117"></a><a href="/media/viewer?media=904118"></a> <p>Staff gather to see our state of the art production studios </p> <p>UON students work in dedicated production studios to enrich their learning </p> Behind the scenes of a university ad 2:38 <p>See behind the scenes of ''The Courier'' advertisement concept created entirely by staff and students within Creative Industries at the University of Newcastle. Students studying Media Production conceptualised, coordinated and filmed the recruitment ad as a Work Integrated Learning project.</p> Q Building Virtual Campus Tour 2:07 <p>Located in Honeysuckle, Q Building is part of our city precinct providing state-of-the-art facilities for the School of Humanities, Creative Industries and Social Sciences (HCISS) and the Integrated Innovation Network (I2N) Hub.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="https://www5.uac.edu.au/uacug/">Apply via UAC</a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.5</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions">Apply now</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-education-secondary">Bachelor of Education (Secondary)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 41,150</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-business">Bachelor of Business<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,540</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-visual-communication-design">Bachelor of Visual Communication Design<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 43,065</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/creative-industries-and-communication">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>You will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within your third year of study. Workplace experience is undertaken in your desired career field, including media, journalism, public relations, advertising, marketing, theatre production, musical ensembles, performing arts and visual communications.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
