UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Design the systems and algorithms behind today’s most advanced technologies.</p><p>Computer science gives you the technical foundation behind modern digital systems. From artificial intelligence and cyber security to software development, you’ll learn how complex systems are designed, built and improved.</p><p>You’ll develop strong skills in algorithms, data structures and system design while building the problem-solving capability employers value in a rapidly evolving digital economy.</p> <p>Choose to specialise in Artificial Intelligence, Cyber Security or Software Development. Whether you want to design intelligent systems, protect digital infrastructure or create innovative software solutions, you’ll graduate ready to contribute to one of Australia’s fastest-growing technology workforces.</p><p>Students enrolled in this degree are encouraged to apply for the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/college/engineering-science-environment/data-and-digital-recruitment-program">Data and Digital Cadet Programs,</a> delivered on campus in collaboration with The Australian Public Service (APS).</p><p>Through this program, you can gain valuable industry experience while completing your studies. APS supports you while you obtain your degree, offering a study allowance each semester. Upon program completion, successful students will be offered an ongoing full-time job with the organisation.</p> <p> <strong> 15.6% projected employment growth ? </strong> for the Computer System Design and Related Services industry by 2029 </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Computer Science is a high-growth industry with many opportunities. There are roles that haven’t even been invented yet! Opportunities exist all over the world, industries from IT to business, health, education, manufacturing, defence and more.</p> <p><strong>Some typical roles include:</strong></p><ul><li>Full Stack Developer</li><li>Computer Software Program Manager</li><li>Games Developer</li><li>Business Intelligence Director</li><li>Cyber Security Advisor</li><li>Security Architect.</li></ul><p><strong>Emerging roles include:</strong></p><ul><li>Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning Engineer</li><li>Information Security Analyst</li><li>Process Automation Specialist</li><li>Digital Transformation Specialist.</li></ul><p>Open doors to Australia’s fastest-growing jobs. <a href="https://ia.acs.org.au/article/2026/ai-jobs-are-the-fastest-growing-in-australia.html">Artificial intelligence jobs are the fastest growing in the country. </a>Strong foundations in computer science, maths and data, plus practical coding and teamwork skills put you in line for these roles and build a career-proofing pathway across industries.</p> <p>86.3% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Computing and Information Systems.</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Students can specialise in their degree by choosing one of three majors. Each major provides a special suite of courses to develop in-demand technical skills for high-growth careers.</p><p><strong>The available majors include:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Artificial Intelligence</strong> – gain the skills to design intelligent systems and work with data-driven technologies shaping the future.</li><li><strong>Cyber Security</strong> – learn to protect systems and data, tackling the growing challenges of digital security.</li><li><strong>Software Development</strong> - build practical coding and problem-solving expertise to create innovative software solutions.</li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>COMP1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP1010">Computing Fundamentals</a></li><li><strong>COMP1140</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP1140">Database and Information Management</a></li><li><strong>COMP2230</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP2230">Algorithms</a></li><li><strong>COMP2240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP2240">Operating Systems</a></li><li><strong>COMP2270</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP2270">Theory of Computation</a></li><li><strong>COMP3851A</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3851A">Computing and Information Sciences Work Integrated Learning Part A</a></li><li><strong>COMP3851B</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3851B">Computing and Information Sciences Work Integrated Learning Part B</a></li><li><strong>INFT3800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT3800">Professional Practice in IT</a></li><li><strong>MATH1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1110">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 1</a></li><li><strong>MATH1510</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1510">Discrete Mathematics</a></li><li><strong>SENG1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG1050">Web Technologies</a></li><li><strong>SENG1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG1110">Object Oriented Programming</a></li><li><strong>SENG1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG1120">Data Structures</a></li><li><strong>SENG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG2130">Systems Analysis and Design</a></li><li><strong>SENG2250</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG2250">System and Network Security</a></li><li><strong>SENG4500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG4500">Network and Distributed Computing</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40103">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Software Development</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses. Core courses SENG1050 and SENG2130 count towards the requirements for this major.</p><ul><li><strong>INFT3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT3100">ICT Project Management</a></li><li><strong>SENG1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG1050">Web Technologies</a></li><li><strong>SENG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG2130">Systems Analysis and Design</a></li><li><strong>SENG2260</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG2260">Human-Computer Interaction</a></li><li><strong>SENG3320</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG3320">Software Verification and Validation</a></li><li><strong>SENG4430</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG4430">Software Quality</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 20 units from the following course list. Students in the B Data Science/B Computer Science combined program complete INFT2150 and COMP3260 as part of their core courses, and must choose 20 units from the remaining options.</p><ul><li><strong>COMP3260</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3260">Data Security</a></li><li><strong>COMP3350</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3350">Advanced Database</a></li><li><strong>INFT2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT2060">Applied Artificial Intelligence</a></li><li><strong>INFT2150</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT2150">ICT Business Analysis</a></li><li><strong>INFT3060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT3060">Cloud Computing</a></li><li><strong>INFT3950</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT3950">Games Design</a></li><li><strong>SENG2050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG2050">Web Engineering</a></li><li><strong>SENG4400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG4400">Enterprise Software Architectures</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Software Development" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40103">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Software Development"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40103">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Cyber Security</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses. Core courses COMP2240 and SENG2250 count towards the requirements for this major. Students in the B Data Science/B Computer Science combined program will also count core course COMP3260 towards this major.</p><ul><li><strong>COMP2240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP2240">Operating Systems</a></li><li><strong>COMP3260</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3260">Data Security</a></li><li><strong>COMP3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3500">Security Attacks: Analysis and Mitigation Strategies</a></li><li><strong>COMP3600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3600">Cyber Security Governance, Risk, and Compliance</a></li><li><strong>INFT2031</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT2031">Systems and Network Administration</a></li><li><strong>SENG2250</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG2250">System and Network Security</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 20 units from the following course list. Students in the B Data Science/B Computer Science combined program complete COMP3330 and COMP3340 as part of their core courses, and must choose 20 units from the remaining options.</p><ul><li><strong>COMP3330</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3330">Machine Intelligence</a></li><li><strong>COMP3340</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3340">Data Engineering and Mining</a></li><li><strong>COMP3350</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3350">Advanced Database</a></li><li><strong>INFT1060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT1060">Cybersecurity Fundamentals</a></li><li><strong>INFT2051</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT2051">Mobile Application Programming</a></li><li><strong>INFT3050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT3050">Web Programming</a></li><li><strong>INFT3060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT3060">Cloud Computing</a></li><li><strong>INFT3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT3100">ICT Project Management</a></li><li><strong>SENG3320</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG3320">Software Verification and Validation</a></li><li><strong>SENG4430</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG4430">Software Quality</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Cyber Security"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40103">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Artificial Intelligence</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses. Core courses MATH1510 and COMP2230 count towards the requirements for this major. Students in the B Data Science/B Computer Science combined program will also count core courses MATH1120 and COMP3330 towards this major.</p><ul><li><strong>COMP2230</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP2230">Algorithms</a></li><li><strong>COMP3330</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3330">Machine Intelligence</a></li><li><strong>MATH1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1120">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 2</a></li><li><strong>MATH1510</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1510">Discrete Mathematics</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Artificial Intelligence" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40103">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 20 units from the following course list. Students in the B Data Science/B Computer Science combined program complete STAT2020 and COMP3340 as part of their core courses, and must choose 20 units from the remaining options.</p><ul><li><strong>COMP3340</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3340">Data Engineering and Mining</a></li><li><strong>COMP3350</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3350">Advanced Database</a></li><li><strong>INFT2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT2060">Applied Artificial Intelligence</a></li><li><strong>INFT3060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT3060">Cloud Computing</a></li><li><strong>MATH2340</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2340">Linearity and Continuity 1</a></li><li><strong>MECH2360</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MECH2360">Dynamics of Machines</a></li><li><strong>STAT2020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2020">Predictive Analytics</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Artificial Intelligence"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40103">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 20 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40103">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40103">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Computer Science</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=40103&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience FIFA hopeful robots 2:27 <p>Ysobel leads the NUBots, programming soccer playing robots to compete in the RoboCup Championships.</p> Career-ready placements <p>Final year students work on a project related to computer science and information technology. The work is undertaken in an organisation or as an innovative proposal for an entrepreneurial prototype.</p><p>Students undertake between 200 and 250 hours of career-ready placement with an organisation involved in computer science or information technology.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Lana''s Bachelor of Computer Science story 2:16 <p>Learn about Lana''s experience studying a Bachelor of Computer Science at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Video</p> Ribhab''s Bachelor of Computer Science story 1:25 <p>Learn about Ribhab''s journey to study a Bachelor of Computer Science at the University of Newcastle.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/482400"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=40103">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-computer-systems-engineering-honours">Bachelor of Computer Systems Engineering (Honours)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 77.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 45,690</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-information-technology">Bachelor of Information Technology<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 67.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 43,940</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, PSB Singapore</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-electrical-and-electronic-engineering-honours">Bachelor of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (Honours)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 77.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 46,575</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/computing-maths-and-technology">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://www.acs.org.au/"></a><p>The Bachelor of Computer Science major in Software Development and major in Cyber Security are accredited by the Australian Computer Society (ACS). The new major in Artificial Intelligence is not accredited by the Australian Computer Society.</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Final year students work on a project related to computer science and information technology. The work is undertaken in an organisation or as an innovative proposal for an entrepreneurial prototype.</p><p>Students undertake between 200 and 250 hours of career-ready placement with an organisation involved in computer science or information technology.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
