UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Design the world around you</p><p>Architecture is more than art and technology. At the University of Newcastle, learn to design spaces that shape communities.</p> <p>From day one, you’ll work in a collaborative studio with 24/7 access. You’ll create and develop your ideas alongside your peers. Through hands-on, project-based learning, you’ll tackle real-world challenges and build strong design portfolio.</p><p>You’ll explore how architecture responds to climate challenges and supports diverse communities. You’ll learn to design with purpose, with a strong focus on sustainability and respect for Country.</p><p>Graduate ready to make an impact. Combine creativity, technical skills and a commitment to shaping better futures through architecture.</p> <p> <strong> World top 200 ? </strong> for Architecture and the Built Environment </p> <p> <strong> Ranked 1 ? </strong> in NSW for learning resources </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>After completing this degree, graduates may pursue careers in private architectural practice or fields like government, international aid, infrastructure planning, research, journalism, architectural criticism, restoration, and conservation.</p> <p>Students wishing to qualify as professional architects can further their studies by enrolling in the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-architecture">Master of Architecture program.</a></p><p><strong>With this degree, graduates are prepared for roles such as:</strong></p><ul><li>technician</li><li>drafter</li><li>project manager</li><li>designer</li><li>town planner</li><li>infrastructure planner</li></ul> <p>86.8% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024, Undergraduate Architecture &amp; Building.</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p><strong>Spend more time in the studio! </strong>More than half of your design courses are spent in the architecture studio.</p><p><strong>In your courses you’ll learn about:</strong></p><ul><li>the architectural site as a landscape</li><li>construction and detailing of buildings</li><li>sustainable design practices</li><li>communication in the built environment</li><li>construction technology and ecology</li><li>making conceptual and realistic models in our workshop</li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARBE1101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE1101">Construction Technology</a></li><li><strong>ARBE1102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE1102">Construction Ecology</a></li><li><strong>ARBE1103</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE1103">Digital Communication in the Built Environment</a></li><li><strong>ARBE1104</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE1104">History and Theory in the Built Environment 1</a></li><li><strong>ARBE1106</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE1106">Country Led Practice in the Built Environment</a></li><li><strong>ARBE1201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE1201">Visual Communication in the Built Environment</a></li><li><strong>ARBE1220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE1220">Architecture Studio 2</a></li><li><strong>ARBE1222</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE1222">Architecture Studio 1</a></li><li><strong>ARBE2203</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE2203">History and Theory in the Built Environment 2</a></li><li><strong>ARBE2220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE2220">Architecture Studio 3</a></li><li><strong>ARBE2222</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE2222">Architecture Studio 4</a></li><li><strong>ARBE3030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE3030">Work Integrated Learning in the Built Environment</a></li><li><strong>ARBE3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE3100">Advanced Construction Technology</a></li><li><strong>ARBE3101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE3101">Performance and Sustainability of the Built Environment</a></li><li><strong>ARBE3200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE3200">History and Theory in the Built Environment 3</a></li><li><strong>ARBE3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE3220">Architecture Studio 5</a></li><li><strong>ARBE3221</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARBE3221">Architecture Studio 6</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10028">handbook</a>.</p>Elective<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10028">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10028">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Design (Architecture)</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=10028&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience EJE Architecture - Supporting our Architecture graduates 1:56 <p>Hear from Anthony and Holly at EJE Architecture as they discuss how architecture graduates from the University of Newcastle are helping push their business forward.</p> Career-ready placements <p>From 2023, students will complete 140 hours of placement experiences or activities through the course ARBE3030 Work Integrated Learning in the Built Environment. .</p><p>Our students also engage in live projects and exhibit their work publicly at our graduate exhibition, which is an opportunity to showcase work to industry and the local community.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Student highlights <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2026/sage-mclean"> <p>Student</p> Turning creativity into a career in architecture <p>While studying architecture, Sage is already gaining hands-on industry experience and building creative and practical skills for a future career in design.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2026/sarah-hurley"> <p>Student</p> Sarah Hurley <p>Balancing study, work and family life, Sarah is building a new career in architecture while developing practical skills and strong academic results.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2026/mackenzie-mcdermott"> <p>Student</p> Designing with a global perspective <p>From studio projects to international study, Mackenzie is developing a global perspective on architecture and how design can respond to place, culture and community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2026/john-young"> <p>Student</p> From industry experience to architectural design <p>After a career in construction and design, John is applying real-world experience to his architecture studies, developing practical skills and tackling complex design challenges.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2026/harry-troup"> <p>Student</p> Studio culture and community shaping a career in architecture <p>While studying architecture, Harry is building industry experience and connections through studio culture, shaping his pathway into professional practice.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2024/kate-architecture"> <p>Student</p> Pursuing your passions, at any age <p>Architectural design is more than just creating buildings; it‘s about shaping communities and transforming lives.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="/media/viewer?media=901822"></a><a href="/media/viewer?media=902048"></a><a href="/media/viewer?media=902049"></a><a href="/media/viewer?media=902050"></a><a href="/media/viewer?media=902053"></a><a href="/media/viewer?media=902056"></a><a href="/media/viewer?media=902059"></a><a href="/media/viewer?media=902062"></a> Meet Syahmina, a Bachelor of Design (Architecture) student from Malaysia 1:36 <p>Syahmina talks about her experience studying a Bachelor of Design (Architecture at the University of Newcastle.</p> Tour of the School of Architecture 2:03 <p>Take a look around the facilities available for School of Architecture students at the University of Newcastle.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/482500"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=10028">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-civil-engineering-honours">Bachelor of Civil Engineering (Honours)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 77.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 46,695</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-visual-communication-design">Bachelor of Visual Communication Design<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 43,065</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-business">Bachelor of Business<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,540</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <a href="/study/architecture-and-construction">Explore study area</a> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://www.lam.gov.my/boards-of-architects-malaysia"></a><p>The Bachelor of Design Architecture program has been validated by the Lembaga Arkitek Malaysia (Board of Architects Malaysia) as equivalent to / exempt from their Part I examination.This program is recognised by the Board of Architects Malaysia. Students are required to complete the Master of Architecture in order to be eligible for registration by the Board of Architects Malaysia.</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>From 2023, students will complete 140 hours of placement experiences or activities through the course ARBE3030 Work Integrated Learning in the Built Environment. .</p><p>Our students also engage in live projects and exhibit their work publicly at our graduate exhibition, which is an opportunity to showcase work to industry and the local community.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
