UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>A focus on equality in contemporary business environments</p><p>Equal opportunity for all continues to be one of the highest priorities in our society. How can this be achieved across business, government, research and economics? These key areas will be explored through this combined degree program. Gain a deeper understanding into how you might apply this to the business landscape to make a difference in the world.</p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <p> <strong> World top 150 ? </strong> for Geography </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Skills, abilities and knowledge learnt in this combined program are highly sought after by a broad range of employers. You could go on to work in the public or private sector, with NGOs or charities or work in a consultancy or advisory role.</p> <p><strong>Professional outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>International Aid/Development</li><li>Urban and Regional Planning</li><li>Advocacy and Policy Development Work</li><li>Research</li><li>Business Advisor</li><li>Foreign Affairs and Trade Officer</li></ul> <p>91.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Business and Management</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Specialise your studies by choosing a major from each degree program.</p>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-development-studies">Bachelor of Development Studies</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-business-pre-2025">Bachelor of Business (pre 2025)</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1110">Blak Australia</a></li><li><strong>ACCT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT1001">Fundamentals of Accounting</a></li><li><strong>BUSN1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN1010">Analytics in Business</a></li><li><strong>ECON1111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON1111">Economics for Business Decisions</a></li><li><strong>ENVS1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1003">Environmental Values and Ethics</a></li><li><strong>FINN1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN1001">Fundamentals of Finance</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1030">Global Poverty and Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2130">Geographies of Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3300">Rethinking Development</a></li><li><strong>INOV1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV1001">Design Thinking: Creativity in Action</a></li><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a></li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1010">Society and Culture: an Introduction to Sociology</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40101">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">1000 Level Development Studies Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1370</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1370">Community Engagement: Respect and Reciprocity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1390</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1390">Blak Rights and the Fight for Justice</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1420</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1420">Yarning, Media and Futures</a></li><li><strong>ENVS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1004">Social Development and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1020">What is Anthropology</a></li><li><strong>THHE1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE1001">Introduction to Global Tourism</a></li><li><strong>THHE1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE1002">Sustainable Tourism Systems</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"1000 Level Development Studies Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40101">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">2000 Level Development Studies Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR2022</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2022">Aboriginal Cultural Practices</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2002">Environmental Legislation and Planning</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2008">The Sustainable Society</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2080">Cities and Regions</a></li><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2400">Future Societies: Beyond Capitalist Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"2000 Level Development Studies Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40101">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready Placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BUSN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3002">Industry Placement</a></li><li><strong>BUSN3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3500">International Work Placement in Business</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3008">Work Integrated Learning in the Environmental and Development Sectors</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready Placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40101">handbook</a>.</p>Development Studies Major<p><a href="#">Cultures and Citizenship</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory course.</p><ul><li><stron