UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Push for equality for all</p><p>This combined degree program is embedded with Indigenous culture, knowledge and practices. Examine inequity in education, health and business and social contexts. Contribute to the push for equal rights - both locally and globally.</p> <p>You will gain an understanding of uneven development, decolonisation, identity cultures, and representation. You''ll graduate an active global citizen, ready to create innovative solutions to pressing issues.</p><p>A partner in the program, The Wollotuka Institute is committed to the advancement of Indigenous education at a local, national and international level.</p> <p> <strong> World top 150 ? </strong> for Geography </p> <p> <strong> 88% of students ? </strong> were happy with facilities and resources – above the national average </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>This program opens doors for jobs in a range of areas in both Indigenous and non-Indigenous organisations in a global context.</p><p>Skills, abilities and knowledge learnt in the combined program are highly sought after by a broad range of employers, including international aid organisations, consulting firms and local, state and federal government departments.</p> <p><strong>Professional Outcomes</strong></p><ul><li>Global Development Worker</li><li>Organisational Cultural Diversity Practitioner</li><li>Cultural Heritage Conservationist</li><li>Policy and Research Officer</li><li>International Aid/Development</li><li>Advocacy and Policy Development Work</li></ul> <p>82.9% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Humanities, Culture and Social Sciences</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Specialise your studies by choosing a major from each degree program.</p>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-development-studies">Bachelor of Development Studies</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-global-indigenous-studies">Bachelor of Global Indigenous Studies</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1001">Critical Indigenous Studies</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1110">Blak Australia</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2001">Business Innovation and Entrepreneurship</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3001">Professional Practice and Entrepreneurship</a></li><li><strong>ECON1111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON1111">Economics for Business Decisions</a></li><li><strong>ENVS1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1003">Environmental Values and Ethics</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1030">Global Poverty and Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2130">Geographies of Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3300">Rethinking Development</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1010">Society and Culture: an Introduction to Sociology</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40179">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready Placement Course Options</a></p><p><strong>Choose 20 units from either: ABOR3999 (20 units); or ENVS3008 (10 units) plus 10-unit 2000/3000 level Development Studies Course List.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR3999</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3999">Aboriginal Professional Experience</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3008">Work Integrated Learning in the Environmental and Development Sectors</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready Placement Course Options"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40179">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">1000 Level Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 20 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1370</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1370">Community Engagement: Respect and Reciprocity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1390</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1390">Blak Rights and the Fight for Justice</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1420</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1420">Yarning, Media and Futures</a></li><li><strong>ENVS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1004">Social Development and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1020">What is Anthropology</a></li><li><strong>THHE1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE1001">Introduction to Global Tourism</a></li><li><strong>THHE1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE1002">Sustainable Tourism Systems</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"1000 Level Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40179">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">2000 Level Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 20 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR2022</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2022">Aboriginal Cultural Practices</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2002">Environmental Legislation and Planning</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2008">The Sustainable Society</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2080">Cities and Regions</a></li><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2400">Future Societies: Beyond Capitalist Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"2000 Level Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40179">handbook</a>.</p>Development Studies Majors<p><a href="#">Cultures and Citizenship</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory course.</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR3024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3024">Blak Advocacy: Empowerment and Solidarity</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 70 units including a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1370</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1370">Community Engagement: Respect and Reciprocity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2022</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2022">Aboriginal Cultural Practices</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3251</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3251">Global Indigenous Comparative Studies</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3380</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3380">Global Indigenous Human Rights</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3090">Society and Space</a></li><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2002">Business and the Politics of Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>IREL3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3004">Indigenising International Politics, Policy and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>SCIE3600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE3600">International Study Experience</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1020">What is Anthropology</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3220">Youth Culture and Risk</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3666</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3666">Consumption, Technology and Everyday Life</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3780</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3780">Leading Social Change: Applying Critical Theories in Critical Times</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3790</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3790">Mobilities, Migration and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3850</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3850">Rage Against the Machine: Indigenous Activism, Ways of Life and the Future</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2300">Ethics for the Social Sciences</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a></li><li><strong>THHE2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE2002">Tourism and Intercultural Encounters</a></li><li><em>9 additional courses are part of "Cultures and Citizenship" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40179">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Cultures and Citizenship"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40179">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Environmental Sustainability</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory course.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3006">Surviving the Anthropocene: Sustainability in the 21st Century</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 70 units including a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR2243</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2243">Indigenous People and Sustainable Environments</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2245">Aboriginal People and Law</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3024</s