UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Work towards a more equitable and sustainable future</p><p>Development, poverty, inequality and environmental sustainability are some of the most important issues in the world today. Study the causes and consequences of unequal development. Assess policy options for a more equitable and sustainable future. Broaden your understanding with legal expertise.</p> <p>This program is the only development studies program in Australia to include economics and Aboriginal studies as core courses.</p><p>Pursue a career in the legal field, or make your mark across research, government, NGOs, business, and community organisations.</p> <p> <strong> World top 300 ? </strong> for Law </p> <p> <strong> World top 150 ? </strong> for Geography </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Work across international aid organisations, consulting firms and local, state and federal government departments and more.</p> <p>Not everyone uses their degree in the same way and the transferable skills gained through university study may allow graduates to pursue a range of careers that might not be directly linked to their study.</p><p><strong>Professional outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>International Aid/Development</li><li>Urban and Regional Planning</li><li>Community Development</li><li>Environmental Lawyer</li><li>Advocacy and Policy Development Work</li><li>Research</li></ul> <p>90.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Law</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>This combined program provides opportunities to study the causes and consequences of unequal development and assess policy options for a more equitable and sustainable future, while studying the complementary skills in Law.</p><p>Learn and develop skills by studying courses in various aspects of law including:</p><ul><li>Criminal law and procedure</li><li>Evidence</li><li>Equity and trusts</li><li>Administrative law</li><li>Property law</li><li>Contract law</li></ul>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-development-studies">Bachelor of Development Studies</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-laws-honours">Bachelor of Laws (Honours) Combined</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1110">Blak Australia</a></li><li><strong>ECON1111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON1111">Economics for Business Decisions</a></li><li><strong>ENVS1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1003">Environmental Values and Ethics</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3008">Work Integrated Learning in the Environmental and Development Sectors</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1030">Global Poverty and Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2130">Geographies of Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3300">Rethinking Development</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1010">Legal System and Method I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1011">Legal System and Method II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1020">Torts I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1021</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1021">Torts II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS2030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS2030">Criminal Law and Procedure</a></li><li><strong>LAWS3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS3040">Contracts I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS3041</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS3041">Contracts II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4001">Constitutional Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4002">Administrative Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4003">Civil Dispute Resolution</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4004">Evidence</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4005">Company Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4007</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4007">Professional Conduct</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4010">Equity and Trusts</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4011">Property</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4012">Public International Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6020">Environmental Law</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1010">Society and Culture: an Introduction to Sociology</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Core" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40130">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40130">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Laws Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 60 units from the list to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>LAWS5036</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS5036">International Clinical Legal Externship</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6016</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6016">Taxation Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6017</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6017">Family Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6020">Environmental Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6021</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6021">Advanced Criminal Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6024">Employment Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6038</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6038">Law and Economics of Climate Change</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6043</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6043">Advanced Legal Research Project</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6087</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6087">Internet Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6090">Health Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6091</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6091">Special Interest Topic</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6094</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6094">Indigenous Peoples, Issues and the Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6096</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6096">Child Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6097</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6097">Competitive Mooting</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6099</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6099">Sport and the Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6102">Alternative Dispute Resolution</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6151</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6151">Gender and the Law</a></li><li><em>34 additional courses are part of "Laws Course List" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40130">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Laws Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40130">handbook</a>.</p>Development Studies Majors<p><a href="#">Cultures and Citizenship</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory course.</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR3024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3024">Blak Advocacy: Empowerment and Solidarity</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 70 units including a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1370</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1370">Community Engagement: Respect and Reciprocity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2022</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2022">Aboriginal Cultural Practices</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3251</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3251">Global Indigenous Comparative Studies</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3380</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3380">Global Indigenous Human Rights</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3090">Society and Space</a></li><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2002">Business and the Politics of Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>IREL3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3004">Indigenising International Politics, Policy and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>SCIE3600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE3600">International Study Experience</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1020">What is Anthropology</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3220">Youth Culture and Risk</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3666</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3666">Consumption, Technology and Everyday Life</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3780</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3780">Leading Social Change: Applying Critical Theories in Critical Times</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3790</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3790">Mobilities, Migration and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3850</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3850">Rage Against the Machine: Indigenous Activism, Ways of Life and the Future</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2300">Ethics for the Social Sciences</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a></li><li><strong>THHE2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE2002">Tourism and Intercultural Encounters</a></li><li><em>9 additional courses are part of "Cultures and Citizenship" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40130">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Cultures and Citizenship"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40130">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Environmental Sustainability</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory course.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3006">Surviving the Anthropocene: Sustainability in the 21st Century</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 70 units including a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR2243</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2243">Indigenous People and Sustainable Environments</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2245">Aboriginal People and Law</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3024">Blak Advocacy: Empowerment and Solidarity</a></li><li><strong>ECON3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3006">Environmental Economics</a></li><li><strong>ENVS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1004">Social Development and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2002">Environmental Legislation and Planning</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2008">The Sustainable Society</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3001">Integrated Impact Assessment</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2080">Cities and Regions</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3090">Society and Space</a></li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a></li><li><strong>SCIE3600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE3600">International Study Experience</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2065">Environment and Society</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3790</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3790">Mobilities, Migration and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>THHE3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE3001">Managing and Marketing Destinations</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Environmental Sustainability" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40130">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Environmental Sustainability"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40130">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Urban and Regional Development</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory course.</p><ul><li><strong>GEOG3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3090">Society and Space</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 70 units including a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2245">Aboriginal People and Law</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3024">Blak Advocacy: Empowerment and Solidarity</a></li><li><strong>ECON3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3006">Environmental Economics</a></li><li><strong>ECON3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3009">Urban and Regional Economics</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2002">Environmental Legislation and Planning</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2008">The Sustainable Society</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3001">Integrated Impact Assessment</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3006">Surviving the Anthropocene: Sustainability in the 21st Century</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2080">Cities and Regions</a></li><li><strong>GEOS2161</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2161">Spatial Science</a></li><li><strong>GEOS3250</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3250">Advanced Spatial Science</a></li><li><strong>HUSE3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUSE3006">Social Policy and Planning in Regional Contexts</a></li><li><strong>SCIE3600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE3600">International Study Experience</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2065">Environment and Society</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a></li><li><strong>THHE3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE3002">Strategy for Tourism Futures and Innovation</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Urban and Regional Development" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40130">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Urban and Regional Development"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40130">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Geopolitics and Economic Development</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory course.</p><ul><li><strong>IREL3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3003">International Relations in a Changing World Order</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Students must complete 70 units from the following course list, including 30 units of ECON courses and a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>ECON2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2002">Intermediate Macroeconomics</a></li><li><strong>ECON2112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2112"> Health Economics and Finance</a></li><li><strong>ECON3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3009">Urban and Regional Economics</a></li><li><strong>ECON3111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3111">Behavioural Economics</a></li><li><strong>ECON3112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3112">International Economics and Payment Infrastructure</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a></li><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2002">Business and the Politics of Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a></li><li><strong>IREL2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2004">Diplomacy, Trade and Politics</a></li><li><strong>IREL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3001">Public Diplomacy and Social Media</a></li><li><strong>IREL3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3002">Global Data Governance for Just and Sustainable Futures</a></li><li><strong>IREL3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3004">Indigenising International Politics, Policy and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>THHE3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE3002">Strategy for Tourism Futures and Innovation</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Geopolitics and Economic Development" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40130">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Geopolitics and Economic Development"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40130">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40130">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Development Studies / Bachelor of Laws (Honours)</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=40130&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=NCLE&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Meet Kirra, Bachelor of Development Studies student 1:41 <p>Meet University of Newcastle student, Kirra and find out why she chose to study a Bachelor of Development Studies. From international travel opportunities to industry work experience, this degree is preparing Kirra for the real world.</p> Career-ready placements <p>You will complete the first 105 hours of your required supervised clinical legal experience under the supervision of solicitors from our School – either in the legal centre itself or as part of our “Law on the Beach” program. School staff also assist to arrange external placements to make up the remaining 180 professional training hours required to qualify to practise as a lawyer.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Studying at Newcastle City campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Law on the Beach 1:50 <p>Law on the Beach is a free legal advice clinic for members of the local community, held in the relaxed setting of Merewether Surf Club each January and February. Allowing our students to work on real-world cases alongside their studies with Newcastle Legal Centre lawyers, the clinics make seeking legal advice more approachable, particularly for young people.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/483100"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=40130">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-psychological-science">Bachelor of Psychological Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 67.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 45,070</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-social-science">Bachelor of Social Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 37,200</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-arts">Bachelor of Arts<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 36,450</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Online</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/humanities-and-social-sciences">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://lpab.nsw.gov.au/"></a><p>Our LLB (Hons) is accredited by the Legal Profession Admission Board (LPAB) of New South Wales. It provides you with all the academic study necessary to apply to practice as a lawyer in Australia, subject to completing an accredited practical legal training program (including the required number of hours of supervised legal work experience) and satisfying the LPAB’s ‘fit and proper person’ test. For more details see the LPAB’s ‘Guide for Applicants’, or for specific inquiries please contact the LPAB.If you would like to complete an accredited program of practical legal training and supervised legal work experience while you complete your academic legal studies under the LLB (Hons), then you may enrol in, from the fourth year of LLB (Hons) studies, our combined LLB (Hons)/ Diploma of Legal Practice.</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>You will complete the first 105 hours of your required supervised clinical legal experience under the supervision of solicitors from our School – either in the legal centre itself or as part of our “Law on the Beach” program. School staff also assist to arrange external placements to make up the remaining 180 professional training hours required to qualify to practise as a lawyer.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
