UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Use your voice for those who need to be heard</p><p>The combined degree will equip you with the capabilities needed to develop and present clear and effective narratives and arguments across written, visual, oral and multimedia form – allowing you to speak up and record the stories of those who need to be heard</p> <p>You will build experience in different forms of media that can be used in various industries – making a real difference to communities locally and around the world.</p><p>This program is the only development studies program in Australia to include economics and Aboriginal studies as core courses.</p> <p> <strong> Cutting-edge facilities ? </strong> so you graduate work-ready <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/school/humanities-creative-industries-social-sciences/study-with-hciss/facilities">Find out more</a> </p> <p> <strong> Professional placement </strong> and practical opportunities </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Skills, abilities and knowledge learnt in this combined degree are highly sought after by a broad range of employers, including international aid organisations, consulting firms and local, state and federal government departments.</p> <p><strong>Professional outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>International aid/development</li><li>Urban and regional planning</li><li>Advocacy and policy development work</li><li>Media consultant/PR consultant</li><li>Foreign affairs and trade officer</li><li>Campaign manager</li></ul> <p>95.7% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2021-2023 - Undergraduate Communications</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Specialise your studies by choosing a major from each degree program.</p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1110">Blak Australia</a></li><li><strong>ARTS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS1004">Creative Collaborations</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1100">Media, Culture and Narrative</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1234</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1234">Media and Communication Concepts</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2000">Digital Media Engagement</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2510</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2510">Global Media Industries</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2600">Audience Participation and Interaction</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3310">Communication and Creativity</a></li><li><strong>ECON1111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON1111">Economics for Business Decisions</a></li><li><strong>ENVS1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1003">Environmental Values and Ethics</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1030">Global Poverty and Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2130">Geographies of Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3300">Rethinking Development</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1010">Society and Culture: an Introduction to Sociology</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement course list</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following Career-ready placement course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARTS3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS3020">Professional Career Ready Studio</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3008">Work Integrated Learning in the Environmental and Development Sectors</a></li><li><strong>HASS3010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3010">Professional Career Ready Placement</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement course list"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</p>Development Studies Major<p><a href="#">Cultures and Citizenship</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory course.</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR3024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3024">Blak Advocacy: Empowerment and Solidarity</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 70 units including a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1370</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1370">Community Engagement: Respect and Reciprocity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2022</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2022">Aboriginal Cultural Practices</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3251</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3251">Global Indigenous Comparative Studies</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3380</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3380">Global Indigenous Human Rights</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3090">Society and Space</a></li><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2002">Business and the Politics of Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>IREL3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3004">Indigenising International Politics, Policy and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>SCIE3600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE3600">International Study Experience</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1020">What is Anthropology</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3220">Youth Culture and Risk</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3666</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3666">Consumption, Technology and Everyday Life</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3780</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3780">Leading Social Change: Applying Critical Theories in Critical Times</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3790</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3790">Mobilities, Migration and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3850</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3850">Rage Against the Machine: Indigenous Activism, Ways of Life and the Future</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2300">Ethics for the Social Sciences</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a></li><li><strong>THHE2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE2002">Tourism and Intercultural Encounters</a></li><li><em>9 additional courses are part of "Cultures and Citizenship" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Cultures and Citizenship"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Environmental Sustainability</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory course.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3006">Surviving the Anthropocene: Sustainability in the 21st Century</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 70 units including a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR2243</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2243">Indigenous People and Sustainable Environments</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2245">Aboriginal People and Law</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3024">Blak Advocacy: Empowerment and Solidarity</a></li><li><strong>ECON3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3006">Environmental Economics</a></li><li><strong>ENVS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1004">Social Development and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2002">Environmental Legislation and Planning</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2008">The Sustainable Society</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3001">Integrated Impact Assessment</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2080">Cities and Regions</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3090">Society and Space</a></li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a></li><li><strong>SCIE3600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE3600">International Study Experience</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2065">Environment and Society</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3790</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3790">Mobilities, Migration and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>THHE3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE3001">Managing and Marketing Destinations</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Environmental Sustainability" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Environmental Sustainability"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Geopolitics and Economic Development</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory course.</p><ul><li><strong>IREL3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3003">International Relations in a Changing World Order</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Students must complete 70 units from the following course list, including 30 units of ECON courses and a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>ECON2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2002">Intermediate Macroeconomics</a></li><li><strong>ECON2112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2112"> Health Economics and Finance</a></li><li><strong>ECON3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3009">Urban and Regional Economics</a></li><li><strong>ECON3111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3111">Behavioural Economics</a></li><li><strong>ECON3112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3112">International Economics and Payment Infrastructure</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a></li><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2002">Business and the Politics of Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a></li><li><strong>IREL2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2004">Diplomacy, Trade and Politics</a></li><li><strong>IREL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3001">Public Diplomacy and Social Media</a></li><li><strong>IREL3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3002">Global Data Governance for Just and Sustainable Futures</a></li><li><strong>IREL3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3004">Indigenising International Politics, Policy and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>THHE3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE3002">Strategy for Tourism Futures and Innovation</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Geopolitics and Economic Development" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Geopolitics and Economic Development"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Urban and Regional Development</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory course.</p><ul><li><strong>GEOG3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3090">Society and Space</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 70 units including a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2245">Aboriginal People and Law</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3024">Blak Advocacy: Empowerment and Solidarity</a></li><li><strong>ECON3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3006">Environmental Economics</a></li><li><strong>ECON3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3009">Urban and Regional Economics</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2002">Environmental Legislation and Planning</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2008">The Sustainable Society</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3001">Integrated Impact Assessment</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3006">Surviving the Anthropocene: Sustainability in the 21st Century</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2080">Cities and Regions</a></li><li><strong>GEOS2161</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2161">Spatial Science</a></li><li><strong>GEOS3250</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3250">Advanced Spatial Science</a></li><li><strong>HUSE3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUSE3006">Social Policy and Planning in Regional Contexts</a></li><li><strong>SCIE3600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE3600">International Study Experience</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2065">Environment and Society</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a></li><li><strong>THHE3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE3002">Strategy for Tourism Futures and Innovation</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Urban and Regional Development" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Urban and Regional Development"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</p>Media and Communication Major<p><a href="#">Media Production</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following 20 units of compulsory courses</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 60 units from the following directed course list; 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2016</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2016">Interactive Storytelling</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2035</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2035">Cinematography</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2130">Sound Production</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2180</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2180">Screenwriting</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2700">Create Your Own Business</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2900">Documentary Filmmaking</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3440</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3440">Short Film Production</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3801">Media Production Project</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3999</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3999">Advanced Media Production</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Media Production" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Media Production"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">News Media</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following 20 units of compulsory courses</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 60 units from the following directed course list; 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2280</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2280">Feature Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2320</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2320">News Media</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2470</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2470">Data Storytelling</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3150</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3150">Podcasting</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3333</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3333">Multiplatform Journalism</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3666</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3666">Contemporary Journalism</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3802</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3802">Public Relations and News Media Project</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"News Media"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Public Relations</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following 20 units of compulsory courses</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 60 units from the following directed course list; 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2140</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2140">Principles of Public Relations</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2212</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2212">Activism and Social Change</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2530</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2530">Organisational Communication</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3520</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3520">Political Communication</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3540</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3540">Public Relations Campaigns</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3737</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3737">Social Media Listening and Monitoring</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3802</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3802">Public Relations and News Media Project</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Public Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50006">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Development Studies / Bachelor of Media and Communication</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=50006&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Meet Kirra, Bachelor of Development Studies student 1:41 <p>Meet Kirra and find out why she chose to study a Bachelor of Development Studies.</p> Career-ready placements <p>Every major has a course available that includes a 140-hour placement with relevant industry partners in government, not-for-profit organisations, or private businesses. </p><p>Students may also undertake international placement, available by enrolling in international study. </p><p>Fieldwork, in places like the sacred Aboriginal Baiame Cave, provides the chance to develop research skills.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Behind the scenes of a university ad 2:38 <p>See behind the scenes of ''The Courier'' advertisement concept created entirely by staff and students within Creative Industries at the University of Newcastle. Students studying Media Production conceptualised, coordinated and filmed the recruitment ad as a Work Integrated Learning project.</p> Q Building Virtual Campus Tour 2:07 <p>Located in Honeysuckle, Q Building is part of our city precinct providing state-of-the-art facilities for the School of Humanities, Creative Industries and Social Sciences (HCISS) and the Integrated Innovation Network (I2N) Hub.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/482557"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.5</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=50006">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-arts">Bachelor of Arts<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 36,450</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Online</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-development-studies">Bachelor of Development Studies<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 67.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 46,965</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-media-and-communication">Bachelor of Media and Communication<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 38,815</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/creative-industries-and-communication">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Every major has a course available that includes a 140-hour placement with relevant industry partners in government, not-for-profit organisations, or private businesses. </p><p>Students may also undertake international placement, available by enrolling in international study. </p><p>Fieldwork, in places like the sacred Aboriginal Baiame Cave, provides the chance to develop research skills.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
