UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Find solutions to global challenges</p><p>Development, poverty, inequality and environmental sustainability are some of the most important issues in the world today. Study the causes and consequences of unequal development. Assess policy options for a more equitable and sustainable future.</p> <p>This program is the only development studies program in Australia to include economics and Aboriginal studies as core courses.</p><p>Through social science, analyse, challenge and gain an insight into global theories. Cover life cycle, gender, class, race, work and social justice. Gain an understanding of global inequality development with a grounding in social science theory and practice.</p> <p> <strong> World top 150 ? </strong> for Geography </p> <p> <strong> 88% of students ? </strong> were happy with facilities and resources – above the national average </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Work across international aid organisations, consulting firms and local, state and federal government departments and more.</p> <p>Not everyone uses their degree in the same way and the transferable skills gained through university study may allow graduates to pursue a range of careers that might not be directly linked to their study.</p><p><strong>Professional outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>International Aid/Development</li><li>Urban and Regional Planning</li><li>Community Development</li><li>Environmental Management</li><li>Advocacy and Policy Development Work</li><li>Research</li></ul> <p>82.9% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Humanities, Culture and Social Sciences</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Specialise your studies by choosing a major from each degree program.</p>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-development-studies">Bachelor of Development Studies</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-social-science">Bachelor of Social Science</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1110">Blak Australia</a></li><li><strong>ECON1111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON1111">Economics for Business Decisions</a></li><li><strong>ENVS1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1003">Environmental Values and Ethics</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1030">Global Poverty and Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2130">Geographies of Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3300">Rethinking Development</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1010">Society and Culture: an Introduction to Sociology</a></li><li><strong>SOCS1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS1100">Professional Skills and Key Debates in Social Sciences</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2200">Social Analysis: Theorising Social Problems</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2300">Ethics for the Social Sciences</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a></li><li><strong>SOCS3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS3100">Policy Development, Program Management and Evaluation</a></li><li><strong>SOCS3200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS3200">Qualitative Social Inquiry: Applied Research Project</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40095">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">1000 Level Development Studies Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following Development Studies course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1370</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1370">Community Engagement: Respect and Reciprocity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1390</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1390">Blak Rights and the Fight for Justice</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1420</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1420">Yarning, Media and Futures</a></li><li><strong>ENVS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1004">Social Development and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1020">What is Anthropology</a></li><li><strong>THHE1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE1001">Introduction to Global Tourism</a></li><li><strong>THHE1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE1002">Sustainable Tourism Systems</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"1000 Level Development Studies Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40095">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">2000 Level Dev Studies Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following Development Studies course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR2022</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2022">Aboriginal Cultural Practices</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2002">Environmental Legislation and Planning</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2008">The Sustainable Society</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2080">Cities and Regions</a></li><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2400">Future Societies: Beyond Capitalist Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"2000 Level Dev Studies Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40095">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready Placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARTS3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS3020">Professional Career Ready Studio</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3008">Work Integrated Learning in the Environmental and Development Sectors</a></li><li><strong>HASS3010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3010">Professional Career Ready Placement</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready Placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40095">handbook</a>.</p>Social Science Majors<p><a href="#">Criminology</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Students must complete all courses to fulfill the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>CRIM1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM1010">Introduction to Criminology</a></li><li><strong>CRIM1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM1020">Victimology</a></li><li><strong>CRIM2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM2001">Criminal Justice in Practice</a></li><li><strong>CRIM2030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM2030">Criminology in the Legal Context</a></li><li><strong>CRIM3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM3020">Crime, Power and the State</a></li><li><strong>CRIM3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM3040">Forensic Evidence</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 20 units at the 3000 level from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>CRIM3051</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM3051">Cybercrime: Tools, Tactics and Traps</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3220">Youth Culture and Risk</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Criminology" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40095">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Criminology"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40095">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">History</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>AHIS1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS1000">Ancient Greece</a></li><li><strong>AHIS2110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS2110">Sparta</a></li><li><strong>AHIS3510</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS3510">Greek Society</a></li><li><strong>AHIS3663</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS3663">Folklore and Fairy Tale in Antiquity</a></li><li><strong>HIST1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1001">Europe and the World</a></li><li><strong>HIST1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1002">The United States from Civil War to Superpower</a></li><li><strong>HIST1051</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1051">The Australian Experience</a></li><li><strong>HIST1052</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1052">Origin of Controversies</a></li><li><strong>HIST2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2002">Fact or Fiction Reading the Past</a></li><li><strong>HIST2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2006">Australian Underworlds: Histories of Crime in Australia</a></li><li><strong>HIST2253</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2253">Bodies and Brains: Histories of Illness, Disability and Disease</a></li><li><strong>HIST2611</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2611">The Russian Revolution: From the Tsars to Putin</a></li><li><strong>HIST2650</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2650">War and Trauma</a></li><li><strong>HIST3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3008">Global Perspectives on the First World War</a></li><li><strong>HIST3152</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3152">The History of Racism</a></li><li><strong>HIST3201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3201">Power in the Asia Pacific: Conflict and Alliances</a></li><li><strong>HIST3621</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3621">Maps and Dreams: Aboriginal-Colonial Relationships in Australian History</a></li><li><strong>HIST3641</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3641">The Rise of Fascism: From the March on Rome to Hitler s Seizure of Power</a></li><li><strong>HIST3642</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3642">The Downfall of Fascism: The Third Reich, War and Genocide</a></li><li><em>18 additional courses are part of "History" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40095">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"History"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40095">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Resource Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>HRER2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2001">Managing Talent</a></li><li><strong>HRER2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastl