UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Make a difference. Study a dual teaching qualification degree in early childhood and primary education.</p><p>Teachers and education professionals play a key role in scaffolding and shaping young minds. Start a rewarding career working with children with the Bachelor of Education (Early Childhood and Primary).</p> <p><strong>Graduates qualify to work across a wide age range:</strong></p><ul><li>Preschool and early childhood (birth – 5 years): Play a meaningful role in guiding children’s holistic development during the crucial stage of early years.</li><li>Primary school (kinder – year 6): Teach across the full scale of children’s intellectual, physical and social development.</li></ul><p>Study in our state-of-the-art technologies. SimTeach, SimCave and SimSchool immerse students in virtual reality and hands-on experiences. These technologies prepare Education students to teach in diverse contexts and students in the 21st century. Our technology and pedagogical practices reflect our commitment to equity, excellence and indigenous knowledge, through shared experiences, indigenous storytelling and reflective practice.</p> <p> <strong> Top 150 ? </strong> in the world for Education </p> <p> <strong> Top 1% ? </strong> university in the world <!-- no link --> </p> <p> <strong> Commonwealth Prac Payment available ? </strong> to eligible students while completing mandatory placement <a href="https://www.education.gov.au/higher-education/commonwealth-prac-payment">Find out more</a> </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>While most study Education to become teachers, your qualification opens doors to careers in related industries, including leadership and professional roles in research and policy development.</p> <p>Professional outcomes</p><p>On completion of this degree, you’ll be able to work in roles such as:</p><ul><li>Early Childhood Teacher</li><li>Early Childhood Centre Director</li><li>K-6 Primary Teacher</li><li>Specialist Teacher in Primary School</li><li>Community Educator</li><li>Education Policy Analyst</li><li>Curriculum Developer or Evaluator.</li></ul> <p>$85,000 median starting salary.</p> <p>NSW Government, 2023</p> <p>92.9% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Education</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>In this degree program focused on teaching children from birth to 12 years, you will explore a diverse range of subjects designed to prepare you for a rewarding career in early childhood and primary education.</p> <p><strong>Your studies will include:</strong></p><ul><li>The psychology behind how children learn and how effective teaching supports their development</li><li>Children''s learning, development, and wellbeing from birth through to age 12</li><li>The role of families and communities in children''s lives</li><li>Curriculum planning and educational programming for children aged 0–5 years</li><li>Supporting children''s early language, literacy, and numeracy development</li><li>Aboriginal education and culturally responsive teaching practices</li><li>Key educational policies and contemporary issues in teaching</li><li>Positive behaviour guidance and classroom management strategies</li><li>Inclusive education for children with diverse learning needs</li><li>Ethical practice and professional codes of conduct for educators.</li></ul><p>This comprehensive curriculum will equip you with the knowledge and practical skills to support young children’s learning and development across various settings.</p><p><em>Please note: Depending on your chosen teaching areas, you may need to attend classes at multiple campuses (e.g., Callaghan, Newcastle City, Gosford) or online. While core courses are offered at your chosen location, some discipline-specific courses may only be available at other locations.</em></p> <p>Core</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3500">Aboriginal Education, Relationships and Responsibilities</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1048</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1048">Becoming a Teacher: Primary and Early Childhood Context</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1055</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1055">Foundations of Child Development</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1070">Foundation of Creative Arts for Early Childhood and Primary Teachers</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1103</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1103">Schooling, Society and Inequality</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2066</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2066">Teaching, Learning and Play in Early Childhood</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2102">Educational Psychology: Learners and the Learning Process</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2186</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2186">Quality Teaching and Student Learning K-6</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2200">The Future of Teaching and Learning</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>EDUC2744</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2744">K-6 Science and Technology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2746</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2746">K-6 Society and Environment</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2747</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2747">K-6 PDHPE</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2748</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2748">K-6 Literacy 1</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2749</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2749">K-6 Numeracy</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3055</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3055">Pedagogies of Numeracy from Birth to 12 Years</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3065">Culture, Diversity and Inclusion in Early Childhood and Primary School Settings</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3066</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3066">Early Childhood Education and Care: Children''s places</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3075</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3075">Multiliteracies, Communication and the Young Child</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3103</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3103">Inclusive Education in Early Childhood and Primary Settings</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>EDUC3745</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3745">K-6 Creative Arts</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4025</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4025">Leadership, Advocacy and Administration in EC Settings</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>EDUC4035</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4035">Inquiry into Early Childhood Philosophy and Practices</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>EDUC4147</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4147">Early Childhood/Primary Professional Experience</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4175</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4175">Pedagogies of Reading and Writing: Birth to 12 Years</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>EDUC4182</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4182">Research as Practice</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HIST1051</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1051">The Australian Experience</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>LING1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING1000">Foundations of Language - Primary and Early Childhood contexts</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1900">Elementary Mathematics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PUBH1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PUBH1020">Foundations of Early Childhood Health and Well-Being</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCIM1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIM1040">Foundations of Science and Technology</a> (Online)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50093">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50093">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Education (Early Childhood and Primary)</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=50093&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience <p> Hear from our teachers 1:20 </p> Career-ready placements <p>As you move through your degree you will complete at least three professional experience placements. This equates to approximately 90 days supervised professional experience in relevant school settings. Students also benefit from ongoing volunteer placement opportunities, a strong alumni network and an engaging online platform.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements/study-area/education">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Studying at Central Coast campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/central-coast/living-on-the-central-coast"> Living on the Central Coast <p>The Central Coast offers a relaxed and convenient lifestyle with access to beautiful beaches and national parks. Our campuses have industry-leading facilities all within beautiful bushland.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Immersive, state of the art technology in the School of Education 2:10 <p>SimTeach, SimCave and SimSchool immerse students in both virtual reality and hands on experiences. These technologies prepare students for diverse contexts and diverse students. Our technologies are used to reflect our commitment to equity, excellence, indigenous knowledges, through shared experiences, indigenous storytelling and reflective practice. They will transform the next generation of teachers, education leaders and scholars.</p> School of Education - SimCave 0:53 <p>SimCave is a 360° immersive environment that provides student teachers with the best of immersive learning experiences and the potential to use new digital media for deeper, creative and cultural learning.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/484751"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.5</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 7.0 (R,W), 8.0 (L,S)</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=50093">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-nursing">Bachelor of Nursing<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 70.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 44,210</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-education-primary">Bachelor of Education (Primary)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 41,160</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-education-secondary">Bachelor of Education (Secondary)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 41,150</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <a href="/study/education">Explore study area</a> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://www.acecqa.gov.au/about-us"></a><p>Graduates of this program will be recognised as having Australian Childrens Education Care Quality Authority (ACECQA) approved early childhood education and care qualification as Early Childhood Teachers (under the National Quality Framework (NQF)). Early childhood teachers can pursue careers as teachers in different early childhood settings, such as kindergarten, day care or preschool.</p><a href="https://educationstandards.nsw.edu.au/wps/portal/nesa/teacher-accreditation/meeting-requirements/who-needs-accreditation"></a><p>Graduates of this accredited initial teacher education program will be eligible for registration with the New South Wales Education Standards Authority (NESA), and can pursue careers as teachers or educators in both the NSW Department of Education and Communities, Catholic Education and Independent school systems; and in public and private sectors both nationally and internationally.</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>As you move through your degree you will complete at least three professional experience placements. This equates to approximately 90 days supervised professional experience in relevant school settings. Students also benefit from ongoing volunteer placement opportunities, a strong alumni network and an engaging online platform.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements/study-area/education">Learn more</a> </p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 208,
