UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Inspire young minds. Study primary education.</p><p>Primary school (kinder – year 6) is the critical period where children cultivate life-long skills. Discover how you can empower the next generation and influence positive change.</p> <p>Study in our state-of-the-art technologies: SimTeach, SimCave and SimSchool. These immerse students in both virtual reality and hands-on experiences and prepare students for diverse contexts and diverse students. Our technologies are used to reflect our commitment to equity, excellence and indigenous knowledge, through shared experiences, indigenous storytelling and reflective practice.</p> <p> <strong> Top 150 ? </strong> in the world for Education </p> <p> <strong> Top 1% ? </strong> university in the world <!-- no link --> </p> <p> <strong> Commonwealth Prac Payment available ? </strong> to eligible students while completing mandatory placement <a href="https://www.education.gov.au/higher-education/commonwealth-prac-payment">Find out more</a> </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Diversify your skills and career pathways by qualifying for both teaching and non-teaching roles. Work with diverse families and children in various educational settings.</p> <p><strong>Professional outcomes</strong></p><p>On completion of this degree, you’ll be able to work in roles such as:</p><ul><li>Primary School Teacher</li><li>Specialist Teacher in Primary School</li><li>English as a Second Language Teacher</li><li>Community Educator</li><li>Education Policy Analyst</li><li>Curriculum Developer or Evaluator</li></ul> <p>$85,000 median starting salary.</p> <p>NSW Government, 2023</p> <p>92.3% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Education</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p><strong>Key study areas include:</strong></p><ul><li>Foundations of primary education</li><li>How to teach K-6 curriculum</li><li>Language and literacy development</li><li>Psychology of learning and teaching</li><li>Behaviour management</li></ul><p><strong>Study a discipline depth in any of the following areas:</strong></p><ul><li>Human society and its environment</li><li>Creative arts</li><li>English</li><li>Personal development, health and physical education</li><li>Mathematics</li><li>Science and technology</li><li>Special education</li></ul> <p>Students of this degree graduate with the skills, knowledge and influence to nurture capable, confident and well-adjusted individuals. The University of Newcastle Primary Education graduates enjoy diverse careers as specialist teachers, leaders and education professionals across related sectors in Australia and around the world.</p><p><em>Please note: Depending on your chosen teaching areas, you may need to attend classes at multiple campuses (e.g., Callaghan, Newcastle City, Gosford) or online. While core courses are offered at your chosen location, some discipline-specific courses may only be available at other locations.</em></p> <p>Core</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3500">Aboriginal Education, Relationships and Responsibilities</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1048</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1048">Becoming a Teacher: Primary and Early Childhood Context</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1050">K-6 Pedagogies</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1070">Foundation of Creative Arts for Early Childhood and Primary Teachers</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1103</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1103">Schooling, Society and Inequality</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2102">Educational Psychology: Learners and the Learning Process</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2186</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2186">Quality Teaching and Student Learning K-6</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2200">The Future of Teaching and Learning</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>EDUC2744</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2744">K-6 Science and Technology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2746</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2746">K-6 Society and Environment</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2747</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2747">K-6 PDHPE</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2748</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2748">K-6 Literacy 1</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2749</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2749">K-6 Numeracy</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3026</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3026">Inclusive and Special Education</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3055</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3055">Pedagogies of Numeracy from Birth to 12 Years</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3186</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3186">Quality Teaching, Equity and Diversity K-6</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3745</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3745">K-6 Creative Arts</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3748</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3748">K-6 Literacy 2</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4748</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4748">Advanced Literacy Studies</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4750</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4750">K-6 Curriculum Contexts: Integration and Inclusion</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HIST1051</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1051">The Australian Experience</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>LING1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING1000">Foundations of Language - Primary and Early Childhood contexts</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1900">Elementary Mathematics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PUBH1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PUBH1030">Foundation Studies in K-6 PDHPE</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCIM1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIM1040">Foundations of Science and Technology</a> (Online)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50092">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Internship Course List</a></p><p><strong>Students undertaking an internship in a special education setting must complete EDUC4167. All other students must complete EDUC4187</strong></p><ul><li><strong>EDUC4167</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4167">Special Education Internship</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4187</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4187">Quality Teaching and Professional Practice K-6</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Internship Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50092">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Discipline Depth Study Areas</a></p><p><strong>Creative Arts</strong></p><p><em>Choose 40 units from the following course list with no more than 20 units at the 1000 level and a minimum of 20 units of EDUC courses.</em></p><ul><li><strong>EDUC1751</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1751">Knowledge and Communication Technologies</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>EDUC2081</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2081">Creativity in practice: drama pedagogies for imaginative learning</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3810</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3810">Teaching Science with The Creative Arts</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4810</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4810">Media Arts Learning in Primary School: An Integrated Approach</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Human Society and its Environment</strong></p><p><em>Choose 40 units from the following course list with no more than 20 units at the 1000 level and a minimum of 20 units of EDUC courses.</em></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1420</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1420">Yarning, Media and Futures</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHIN1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHIN1110">Chinese Language and culture Beginners 1 (A0 to A1.1) for students with other language backgrounds</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHIN1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHIN1120">Chinese Language and Culture Beginners 2 (A1.1 to A1.2) for students with other language backgrounds</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2143</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2143">Junior Languages Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3800">Intercultural Understanding for Educators</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>EDUC3801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3801">Global Education Pedagogies</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3802</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3802">Applied Learning in Diverse Contexts</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4800">Education in Global Perspective: Issues for Australian teachers</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>ENVS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1004">Social Development and the Environment</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>FREN1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN1100">French Language and Culture Beginners 1 (A0 to A1.1)</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>FREN1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN1200">French Language and Culture Beginners 2 (A1.1 to A1.2)</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HIST1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1001">Europe and the World</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>HUMA2070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUMA2070">Auslan Language and Culture Beginners 1</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>JAPN1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/JAPN1110">Japanese Language and Culture Beginners 1 (A0 to A1.1)</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>JAPN1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/JAPN1120">Japanese Language and Culture Beginners 2 (A1.1 to A1.2)</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>PHIL1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHIL1040">World Religions</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1020">What is Anthropology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA2065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2065">Environment and Society</a> (Online)</li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Discipline Depth Study Areas" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50092">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Personal Development, Health and Physical Ed</strong></p><p><em>Choose 40 units from the following course list with no more than 20 units at the 1000 level and a minimum of 20 units of EDUC courses.</em></p><ul><li><strong>EDUC1014</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1014">PE Studies 1: Motor Development and Skill Acquisition</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1058</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1058">Lifetime Physical Activities</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2057</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2057">PE Studies 3: Performance Activities</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3514</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3514">Primary Kinetics 1</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4016</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4016">Physical Education, Physical Activity and Health Research in Primary Schools</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4017</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4017">The Daughters and Dads program: Optimising children''s physical activity and well-being</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HLSC2240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC2240">Nutrition in Childhood</a> (Online)</li></ul><p><strong>Mathematics</strong></p><p><em>Choose 40 units from the following course list with no more than 20 units at the 1000 level and a minimum of 20 units of EDUC courses.</em></p><ul><li><strong>EDUC1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1090">Junior Mathematics Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4016</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4016">Physical Education, Physical Activity and Health Research in Primary Schools</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH3910</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3910">Mathematics With a View to Teaching</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH3920</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3920">Thinking and Working Mathematically</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Science and Technology</strong></p><p><em>Choose 40 units from the following course list with no more than 20 units at the 1000 level and a minimum of 20 units of EDUC courses.</em></p><ul><li><strong>BIOL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1001">Molecules, Cells and Organisms</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1002">Organisms to Ecosystems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1010">Introductory Chemistry I</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>CHEM1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1020">Introductory Chemistry II</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1751</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1751">Knowledge and Communication Technologies</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>EDUC3801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3801">Global Education Pedagogies</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3810</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3810">Teaching Science with The Creative Arts</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1001">Environmental Science Concepts and Methods</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS1040">Earth: Our Dynamic Planet</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI1000">Our Oceans</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>PHYS1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHYS1200">Introductory Physics for the Life Sciences</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PHYS2100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHYS2100">Introduction to Astronomy</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PHYS2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHYS2300">Climate and Energy</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1010">Psychology Introduction 1</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li></ul><p><strong>Special Education</strong></p><p><em>Choose 40 units from the following course list. Students undertaking Special Education Discipline Depth must complete EDUC4167 Special Education Internship.</em></p><ul><li><strong>EDUC4002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4002">Meet Spec. Needs in Diverse Social and Educ. Context</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4063</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4063">Planning for Teaching in Special Education</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4064</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4064">Assessing and Addressing Learning Difficulties</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4065">Supporting Behaviour Change</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Discipline Depth Study Areas"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50092">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50092">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Education (Primary)</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=50092&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience <p> Hear from our teachers 1:20 </p> Career-ready placements <p>There are 3 placements in primary school settings totalling 90 days for domestic and international students. As these are professional placements, international students should have a professional level of spoken and written English. New Colombo Plan Mobility Program – experience teaching in bilingual classrooms in Asia with funding available.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements/study-area/education">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Studying at Central Coast campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/central-coast/living-on-the-central-coast"> Living on the Central Coast <p>The Central Coast offers a relaxed and convenient lifestyle with access to beautiful beaches and national parks. Our campuses have industry-leading facilities all within beautiful bushland.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Student highlights <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2026/charlotte-vinen"> <p>Student</p> Turning a passion for teaching into practice <p>From a Fiji study tour to placement at Newcastle’s McDonald Jones Stadium, Charlotte brings her love of teaching to life through hands-on learning and real-world impact.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2023/grace-riley"> <p>Student</p> Grace Riley <p>Hear how Grace’s practical placements reinforced her passion for teaching.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2023/harrison-sheperd"> <p>Student</p> Cultural connections in Education <p>Harrison, a proud Wiradjuri man, found his passion for Education on his gap year. Now, he is a New Colombo Plan Scholarship recipient and expanding his skills and knowledge in Fiji.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2023/isabella-wightman"> <p>Student</p> Isabella Wightman <p>Teaching really does make a difference in students'' lives. Discover how important this is to Isabella.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Immersive, state of the art technology in the School of Education 2:10 <p>SimTeach, SimCave and SimSchool immerse students in both virtual reality and hands on experiences. These technologies prepare students for diverse contexts and diverse students. Our technologies are used to reflect our commitment to equity, excellence, indigenous knowledges, through shared experiences, indigenous storytelling and reflective practice. They will transform the next generation of teachers, education leaders and scholars.</p> School of Education - SimCave 0:53 <p>SimCave is a 360° immersive environment that provides student teachers with the best of immersive learning experiences and the potential to use new digital media for deeper, creative and cultural learning.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/484753"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.5</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 7.0 (R,W), 8.0 (L,S)</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=50092">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-nursing">Bachelor of Nursing<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 70.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 44,210</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-education-early-childhood-and-primary">Bachelor of Education (Early Childhood and Primary)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 41,130</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-education-secondary">Bachelor of Education (Secondary)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 41,150</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <a href="/study/education">Explore study area</a> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://educationstandards.nsw.edu.au/wps/portal/nesa/teacher-accreditation/meeting-requirements/who-needs-accreditation"></a><p>Graduates of this accredited initial teacher education program will be eligible for registration with the New South Wales Education Standards Authority (NESA), and can pursue careers as teachers or educators in both the NSW Department of Education and Communities, Catholic Education and Independent school systems; and in public and private sectors both nationally and internationally.</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>There are 3 placements in primary school settings totalling 90 days for domestic and international students. As these are professional placements, international students should have a professional level of spoken and written English. New Colombo Plan Mobility Program – experience teaching in bilingual classrooms in Asia with funding available.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements/study-area/education">Learn more</a> </p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 208,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 164640,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td>Successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the Higher School Certificate (HSC)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must meet the University''s English proficiency requirement</li><li>IELTS overall minimum 7.5</li><li>IELTS section minimum 7.0 for Reading and Writing, 8.0 for Listening and Speaking</li><li>Refer to the English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy for further information</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-education-primary',
