UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Empower young minds. Study secondary education.</p><p>Secondary teachers nurture, teach and empower students at a critical period of their development. You will learn how to inspire high school students to make the most of their education and ignite their passion in a particular subject area.</p> <p>Combine your passion for education with your chosen areas of interest. Choose your teaching specialisations from a range of NESA Accredited Teaching Areas. Gain in-depth knowledge, expertise, confidence, and the skills to be an exceptional teacher.</p><p>Study in our state-of-the-art technologies. SimTeach, SimCave and SimSchool immerse students in both virtual reality and hands on experiences. These technologies prepare students for diverse contexts and diverse students. Our technologies are used to reflect our commitment to equity, excellence and indigenous knowledges, through shared experiences, indigenous storytelling and reflective practice.</p> <p> <strong> Top 150 ? </strong> in the world for Education </p> <p> <strong> Top 1% ? </strong> university in the world <!-- no link --> </p> <p> <strong> Commonwealth Prac Payment available ? </strong> to eligible students while completing mandatory placement <a href="https://www.education.gov.au/higher-education/commonwealth-prac-payment">Find out more</a> </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Diversify your skills and career pathways by qualifying for both teaching and non-teaching roles. Work with diverse families and children in various educational settings.</p> <p><strong>Professional outcomes</strong></p><p>On completion of this degree, you’ll be able to work in roles such as:</p><ul><li>High School Teacher (in subject-specific areas)</li><li>Specialist Teacher in Primary School</li><li>English as a Second Language Teacher</li><li>Community Educator</li><li>Education Policy Analyst</li><li>Curriculum Developer or Evaluator</li></ul> <p>$85,000 median starting salary.</p> <p>NSW Government, 2023</p> <p>92.3% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Education</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Specialise and diversify with up to three teaching areas – choose from 29 teaching areas and increase your knowledge, expertise and career pathways..</p> <ul><li>Complete one first teaching area; and</li><li>Choose to complete another first teaching area, or one or two additional teaching area/s;</li><li>Extended studies are also an option in some majors where you only want to qualify in the single area: Health and Physical Education, and Mathematics.</li></ul><p>To focus your studies and gain flexibility in your degree, you may qualify in teaching areas from within or across different school learning areas: English/Drama, Human Society &amp; Its Environment, Health &amp; Physical Education, Languages, Mathematics, Science, Technologies &amp; Applied Studies.</p><p><em>Please note: Depending on your chosen teaching areas, you may need to attend classes at multiple campuses (e.g., Callaghan, Newcastle City, Gosford) or online. While core courses are offered at your chosen location, some discipline-specific courses may only be available at other locations.</em></p> <p>Core</p><p>Teaching Areas</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3500">Aboriginal Education, Relationships and Responsibilities</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1038</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1038">Foundations of Secondary Education</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1101">Curriculum, Assessment and Pedagogy</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1103</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1103">Schooling, Society and Inequality</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2102">Educational Psychology: Learners and the Learning Process</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2151</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2151">Multiliteracies</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2181</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2181">Managing the Learning Environment</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2196</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2196">Quality Teaching and Student Learning 7-12</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2200">The Future of Teaching and Learning</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>EDUC3026</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3026">Inclusive and Special Education</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3196</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3196">Quality Teaching, Equity and Diversity 7-12</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4181</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4181">Ethical Teaching in Classrooms</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Internship Course List</a></p><p><strong>Students undertaking an internship in a Special Education setting, must complete EDUC4167. All other students must complete EDUC4197.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>EDUC4167</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4167">Special Education Internship</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4197</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4197">Quality Teaching and Professional Practice 7-12</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Internship Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p>First Teaching Areas<p><a href="#">Aboriginal Studies</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for a first teaching area, complete the courses listed below.</p><ul><li><strong>EDUC2036</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2036">Junior History Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4991</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4991">Senior Social Sciences Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>To fulfil the requirements for a first teaching area, choose 60 units from the following list (with a maximum of 20 units at the 1000 level and a minimum of 20 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1110">Blak Australia</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>ABOR1370</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1370">Community Engagement: Respect and Reciprocity</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>ABOR1390</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1390">Blak Rights and the Fight for Justice</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>ABOR1420</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1420">Yarning, Media and Futures</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ABOR2243</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2243">Indigenous People and Sustainable Environments</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>ABOR2245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2245">Aboriginal People and Law</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ABOR2330</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2330">Aboriginal Knowledge Systems</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>ABOR3024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3024">Blak Advocacy: Empowerment and Solidarity</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>ABOR3080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3080">Indigenous Research</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>ABOR3251</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3251">Global Indigenous Comparative Studies</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>ABOR3380</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3380">Global Indigenous Human Rights</a> (Online)</li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Aboriginal Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Aboriginal Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Ancient History</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for a first teaching area, complete the courses listed below.</p><ul><li><strong>EDUC2036</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2036">Junior History Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4136</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4136">Senior History Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HIST3621</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3621">Maps and Dreams: Aboriginal-Colonial Relationships in Australian History</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>To fulfil the requirements for a first teaching area choose 50 units from the following list (with a maximum of 20 units at the 1000 level and a minimum of 20 units at the 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>AHIS1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS1000">Ancient Greece</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>AHIS1080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS1080">The Byzantine Empire: From Constantine to Iconoclasm (306-726)</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>AHIS2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS2010">Pompeii: Rediscovering the Past</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>AHIS2110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS2110">Sparta</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>AHIS3510</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS3510">Greek Society</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>AHIS3663</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS3663">Folklore and Fairy Tale in Antiquity</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><em>9 additional courses are part of "Ancient History" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Ancient History"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Biology</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for a first teaching area, complete the courses listed below.</p><ul><li><strong>EDUC2052</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2052">Junior Science Curriculum Methods</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3052</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3052">Senior Science Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3157</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3157">History, Nature and Practice of Science</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>To fulfil the requirements for a first teaching area, choose 40 units from the the following course list (with a maxiumum of 20 units at the 1000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>BIOL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1001">Molecules, Cells and Organisms</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1002">Organisms to Ecosystems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1003">Professional Skills for Biological Sciences 1</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2001">Molecular Laboratory Skills for Biological Sciences</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2002">Laboratory Skills in Biological Systems</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2010">Biochemistry</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL2050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2050">Molecular Genetics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL2090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2090">Microbial Biology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL2220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2220">Plant Adaptation to Climate Change</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL3001">Advanced Laboratory Skills in Biological Sciences</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL3020">Animal Physiology, Reproduction and Development</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL3090">Molecular Biology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL3100">Microbiology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI2300">Marine Biology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI3410</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI3410">Coral Reef Biology, Ecology and Sustainability</a> (Central Coast)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Biology"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Business Studies</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for a first teaching area, complete the courses listed below.</p><ul><li><strong>EDUC2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2060">Junior Geography and Commerce Curriculum Methods</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4991</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4991">Senior Social Sciences Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List A </strong>To fulfil the course requirements for a first teaching area, complete 10 units from the Course List A listed below.</p><ul><li><strong>ACCT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT1001">Fundamentals of Accounting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FINN1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN1001">Fundamentals of Finance</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List B </strong>To fulfil the course list requirements for a first teaching area, choose 40 units from Course List B (with a minimum of 20 units at the 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ECON2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2001">Microeconomics for Business</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON2002">Intermediate Macroeconomics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ECON3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3009">Urban and Regional Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2001">Managing Talent</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2004">Prompt Engineering for Innovation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3001">Global Networking and Negotiation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3002">Traction and Growth</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MKTG2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2001">Digital and Social Media Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2005">Leadership Models and Practices</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2006">Management in Environmental Turbulence</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3011">Leading Organisational Change</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Business Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Business Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Chemistry</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for a first teaching area, complete the courses listed below.</p><ul><li><strong>EDUC2052</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2052">Junior Science Curriculum Methods</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3052</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3052">Senior Science Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3157</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3157">History, Nature and Practice of Science</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>To fulfil the requirements for a first teaching area, choose 40 units from the following list (with a maximum of 20 units at the 1000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>CHEM1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1010">Introductory Chemistry I</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>CHEM1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1020">Introductory Chemistry II</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM2110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM2110">Applied Analytical Chemistry</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM2210</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM2210">Materials Chemistry</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM2310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM2310">Organic Chemistry</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM2410</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM2410">Physical Chemistry</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM3110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM3110">Instrumental Chemical Analysis</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM3210</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM3210">Functional Materials</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM3310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM3310">Molecular Organic Synthesis</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM3410</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM3410">Energy and Materials</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM3550</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM3550">Medicinal and Biological Chemistry</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM3580</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM3580">Colloids, Interfaces and Soft Matter</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Chemistry" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Chemistry"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Design and Technology</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for a first teaching area, complete the courses listed below.</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1011">Visual Culture</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>DESN1031</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1031">Visual Abstraction</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>DESN2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2002">Design Thinking and Innovation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>DESN2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2003">Visual Process</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2145</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2145">Junior Technology Curriculum Methods</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4245">Senior Technology 4 Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>To fulfil the requirements for a first teaching area, choose 20 units from the following list.</p><ul><li><strong>EDUC3036</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3036">Technology Teaching Studies 5: Food Technology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3037</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3037">Technology Teaching Studies 6: Textile Technology</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>EDUC3516</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3516">Specialist Studies in Technology Timber</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3517</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3517">Specialist Studies in Metal Technology</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Design and Technology"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Drama</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for a first teaching area, complete the courses listed below.</p><ul><li><strong>CAPA2410</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA2410">Australian Theatre and Performance</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2136</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2136">Junior Drama Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4036</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4036">Senior Drama Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>To fulfil the requirements for a first teaching area, choose 50 units from the following list (with a maximum of 20 units at the 1000 level and a minimum of 20 units at the 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>CAPA1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA1001">Creative and Performing Arts 1</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CAPA1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA1030">Acting and Performance 1</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CAPA2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA2001">Creative and Performing Arts 2</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CAPA3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA3001">Creative and Performing Arts 3</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MUSI3461</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI3461">Creative Practice Lab</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Drama" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Drama"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Earth and Environmental Science</a></