om the following list (with a maximum of 10 units at the 1000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1003">Environmental Values and Ethics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1004">Social Development and the Environment</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2002">Environmental Legislation and Planning</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2008">The Sustainable Society</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOG1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1030">Global Poverty and Development</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOG2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2080">Cities and Regions</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2130">Geographies of Development</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SOCA2065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2065">Environment and Society</a> (Online)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List B (Physical Geography) </strong>To fulfil the course list requirements for a first teaching area, choose 20 units from the following list (with a maximum of 10 units at the 1000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>GEOS1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS1040">Earth: Our Dynamic Planet</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS1050">Earth: Natural Hazards</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS2050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2050">Catchments and Climate</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2060">Earth''s Critical Zone</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2080">Earth''s Dynamic Surface</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS2161</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2161">Spatial Science</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List C </strong>To fulfil the course list requirements for a first teaching area, choose 20 units from the following list.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3001">Integrated Impact Assessment</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3006">Surviving the Anthropocene: Sustainability in the 21st Century</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOG3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3090">Society and Space</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOG3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3300">Rethinking Development</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3220">Coastal Environments and Processes</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3250</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3250">Advanced Spatial Science</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3340</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3340">Climate Change and Resource Management</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Geography"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Health and Physical Education</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for a first teaching area, complete the courses listed below.</p><ul><li><strong>EDUC1014</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1014">PE Studies 1: Motor Development and Skill Acquisition</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1016</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1016">PE Studies 2: Court and Striking Games</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1058</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1058">Lifetime Physical Activities</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC1203</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1203">Junior HPE Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2057</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2057">PE Studies 3: Performance Activities</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC2058</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2058">PE Studies 4: Invasion Games</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3203</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3203">Senior HPE Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4015</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4015">Sociology of Health and Physical Education, Sport and Physical Activity</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HUBS2520</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS2520">Sports Science 1</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PUBH2040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PUBH2040">Health Studies 1</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PUBH3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PUBH3040">Health Studies 3</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>HPE Extended Studies </strong>Students undertaking the Health and Physical Education first teaching area (FTA) have the option of completing the HPE Extended Studies. HPE Extended Studies option is only available to students undertaking the HPE FTA.</p><ul><li><strong>EDUC3514</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3514">Primary Kinetics 1</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4016</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4016">Physical Education, Physical Activity and Health Research in Primary Schools</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4017</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4017">The Daughters and Dads program: Optimising children''s physical activity and well-being</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Health and Physical Education" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Health and Physical Education"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Industrial Technology Graphics and Multimedia</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for a first teaching area, complete the courses listed below.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>EDUC2145</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2145">Junior Technology Curriculum Methods</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4245">Senior Technology 4 Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List A </strong>Choose 10 units from the following list for a first teaching area.</p><ul><li><strong>ARBE1201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newca