2145</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2145">Junior Technology Curriculum Methods</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4245">Senior Technology 4 Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI1000">Our Oceans</a> (Online)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>To fulfil the requirements for a first teaching area, choose 40 units from the following list (minimum 20 units at the 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2004">Ecology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3220">Coastal Environments and Processes</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI2300">Marine Biology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI3300">Integrated Coastal Ecosystems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI3410</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI3410">Coral Reef Biology, Ecology and Sustainability</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>MARI3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI3500">Sustainable Fisheries and Aquaculture</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCIE2223</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE2223">Weather and Waves</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Marine Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Mathematics</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for a first teaching area, complete the courses listed below. Students who do not meet the enrolment requisite for MATH1110 must take MATH1002 Foundational Studies in Mathematics. For these students MATH1002 will count for 10 units of electives.</p><ul><li><strong>EDUC1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC1090">Junior Mathematics Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC3090">Senior Mathematics Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1110">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 1</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1120">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 2</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH2310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2310">Calculus of Science and Engineering</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH2800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2800">Ordinary Differential Equations and Applied Linear Algebra</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH3910</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3910">Mathematics With a View to Teaching</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH3920</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3920">Thinking and Working Mathematically</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Extended Studies in Mathematics </strong>Extended Studies in Mathematics – Complete up to 40 units as electives, or up to 60 units in place of an additional teaching area.</p><ul><li><strong>MATH1510</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1510">Discrete Mathematics</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MATH1800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1800">Mathematical Modelling</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH3120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3120">Algebra</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH3170</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3170">Number Theory</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH3820</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3820">Numerical Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>STAT1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1070">Statistics for the Sciences</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>STAT1300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1300">Fundamentals of Statistics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>STAT3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3100">Systems Thinking for an Integrated Workforce</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>STAT6001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT6001">Data Wrangling and Visualisation</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Mathematics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Modern History</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for a first teaching area, complete the courses listed below.</p><ul><li><strong>EDUC2036</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2036">Junior History Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4136</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4136">Senior History Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HIST3621</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3621">Maps and Dreams: Aboriginal-Colonial Relations