ances</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HIST3641</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3641">The Rise of Fascism: From the March on Rome to Hitler s Seizure of Power</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>HIST3642</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3642">The Downfall of Fascism: The Third Reich, War and Genocide</a> (Online)</li><li><em>12 additional courses are part of "Modern History" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List B </strong>To fulfil the course list requirements for an additional teaching area, choose 10 units from the following list.</p><ul><li><strong>AHIS1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS1000">Ancient Greece</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>AHIS1080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS1080">The Byzantine Empire: From Constantine to Iconoclasm (306-726)</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>AHIS2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS2010">Pompeii: Rediscovering the Past</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>AHIS2110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS2110">Sparta</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>AHIS3510</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS3510">Greek Society</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>AHIS3663</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS3663">Folklore and Fairy Tale in Antiquity</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><em>9 additional courses are part of "Modern History" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Modern History"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Society and Culture</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for an additional teaching area, complete the course listed below.</p><ul><li><strong>EDUC2036</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2036">Junior History Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4991</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4991">Senior Social Sciences Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 30 units from the following list for an additional teaching area (with a maximum of 20 units at the 1000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCRN1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN1000">Media Literacy</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>SCRN1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN1200">Film and Television Studies</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>SCRN2100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN2100">Popular Music and Culture</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SCRN2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN2200">Popular Culture and Society</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SCRN2500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN2500">Science Fiction and Fantasy on Screen</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SCRN3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN3000">Social Media and Digital Culture</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SCRN3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN3100">Peak TV: Texts, Industry, Culture</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1010">Society and Culture: an Introduction to Sociology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1020">What is Anthropology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1200">Sociology of Health and Illness</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA2065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2065">Environment and Society</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA2700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2700">Gender, Religion and Power</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA3178</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3178">Health, ''Wellness'' and Power: The Social Contexts of Expert Knowledge</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3220">Youth Culture and Risk</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA3780</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3780">Leading Social Change: Applying Critical Theories in Critical Times</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA3850</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3850">Rage Against the Machine: Indigenous Activism, Ways of Life and the Future</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCS2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2200">Social Analysis: Theorising Social Problems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>SOCS2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2300">Ethics for the Social Sciences</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SOCS3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS3100">Policy Development, Program Management and Evaluation</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><em>7 additional courses are part of "Society and Culture" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Society and Culture"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Software Design and Development</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for an additional teaching area, complete the courses listed below.</p><ul><li><strong>EDUC2145</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2145">Junior Technology Curriculum Methods</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4245">Senior Technology 4 Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INFT1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT1004">Introduction to Programming</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SENG1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG1110">Object Oriented Programming</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 20 units from the following list for an additional teaching area.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2016</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2016">Interactive Storytelling</a> (Singapore)</li><li><strong>EBUS3050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EBUS3050">Systems Design for the Digital Economy</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>INFT2051</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT2051">Mobile Application Programming</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>INFT3050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT3050">Web Programming</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>INFT3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT3100">ICT Project Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>INFT3950</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT3950">Games Design</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>SENG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG2130">Systems Analysis and Design</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Software Design and Development" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Software Design and Development"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Special Education</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory Courses </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for anadditional teaching area, complete the courses listed below. To qualify as a Special Education teacher EDUC4167 Special Education Internship must be completed.</p><ul><li><strong>EDUC4002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4002">Meet Spec. Needs in Diverse Social and Educ. Context</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4063</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4063">Planning for Teaching in Special Education</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4064</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4064">Assessing and Addressing Learning Difficulties</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4065">Supporting Behaviour Change</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Special Education"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Studies of Religion</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>To fulfil the compulsory course requirements for an additional teaching area, complete the courses listed below.</p><ul><li><strong>EDUC2036</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC2036">Junior History Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EDUC4991</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EDUC4991">Senior Social Sciences Curriculum Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PHIL1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHIL1040">World Religions</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 30 units from the following list for an additional teaching area (with a maximum of 10 units at 1000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>PHIL1042</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHIL1042">Religion, Science and Popular Beliefs</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>PHIL2040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHIL2040">Philosophy of Relationships</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>PHIL2041</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHIL2041">Democracy and Diversity</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA2700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2700">Gender, Religion and Power</a> (Online)</li><li><em>4 additional courses are part of "Studies of Religion" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Studies of Religion"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50091">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Education (Secondary)</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=50091&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience <p> Hear from our teachers 1:20 </p> Career-ready placements <p>As you move through your degree you will complete at least three professional experience placements. This equates to approximately 90 days supervised professional experience in relevant school settings. Students also benefit from ongoing volunteer placement opportunities, a strong alumni network and an engaging online platform.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements/study-area/education">Learn more on placement requirements</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Studying at Central Coast campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/central-coast/living-on-the-central-coast"> Living on the Central Coast <p>The Central Coast offers a relaxed and convenient lifestyle with access to beautiful beaches and national parks. Our campuses have industry-leading facilities all within beautiful bushland.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Immersive, state of the art technology in the School of Education 2:10 <p>Immersive, state of the art technology in the School of Education</p> School of Education - SimCave 0:53 <p>SimCave is a 360° immersive environment that provides student teachers with the best of immersive learning experiences and the potential to use new digital media for deeper, creative and cultural learning.</p> Pathways Stories - Iglal 1:46 <p>Hear about pathways graduate Iglal Kodi''s journey to becoming a teacher.</p> Meet Paris, Bachelor of Education (Secondary) Student 1:34 <p>Want to be a secondary teacher? Hear about Paris'' experience in interactive learning environments, from University of Newcastle SimTeach facilities to placement teach Year 8 on the Central Coast.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/484755"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.5</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 7.0 (R,W), 8.0 (L,S)</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=50091">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-education-primary">Bachelor of Education (Primary)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 41,160</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="undergraduate-certificate-in-sport-and-movement-leadership">Undergraduate Certificate in Sport and Movement Leadership<p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-exercise-and-sport-science">Bachelor of Exercise and Sport Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 72.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 44,000</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <a href="/study/education">Explore study area</a> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://educationstandards.nsw.edu.au/wps/portal/nesa/teacher-accreditation/meeting-requirements/who-needs-accreditation"></a><p>Graduates of this accredited initial teacher education program will be eligible for registration with the New South Wales Education Standards Authority (NESA), and can pursue careers as teachers or educators in both the NSW Department of Education and Communities, Catholic Education and Independent school systems; and in public and private sectors both nationally and internationally.</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>As you move through your degree you will complete at least three professional experience placements. This equates to approximately 90 days supervised professional experience in relevant school settings. Students also benefit from ongoing volunteer placement opportunities, a strong alumni network and an engaging online platform.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements/study-area/education">Learn more on placement requirements</a> </p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 208,
