UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Saving the world. It’s a growth industry.</p><p>Do you have a passion for science and sustainability? Do you want to play a part in solving the environmental problems facing our society? Then the Bachelor of Environmental Science and Management at The University of Newcastle is for you.</p> <p>The University of Newcastle provides the opportunity to explore the science behind human-induced impacts. You''ll learn to understand and combat the critical issues placing a growing strain on the earth’s natural resources such as climate change, human impacts, and the biodiversity crisis. Gain experience in management-based skills to help protect our environment. Both now and into the future.</p><p>Our region offers vast environmental diversity and is perfect for gaining practical experience in the field. We are right on the doorstep of the Hunter Valley mining belt, the Hunter wetlands and the NSW coastline. Our partnership with industry allows you to take part in exciting work placements and research opportunities while you study.</p> <p> <strong> World top 150 ? </strong> for Geography </p> <p> <strong> World top 200 ? </strong> for Environmental Sciences </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Graduates of the Bachelor of Environmental Science and Management can go on to work in a diverse range of areas depending on their chosen majors and specialties.</p><p>You might work for government departments or councils, for non-government-organisations, or in private industry.</p> <p><strong>Professional outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>Conservation and Ecology</li><li>Environmental Consulting</li><li>Laboratory and Research Work</li><li>Urban and Regional Planning</li><li>Policy Development</li><li>Marine Biology</li></ul> <p>87% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024, Undergraduate Agriculture &amp; Environmental Studies.</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>The Bachelor of Environmental Science and Management offers four majors so you can tailor your degree to suit your interests and career objectives. Studying a major allows you to gain detailed skills and a strong understanding of key principles in your chosen environmental science speciality. Majors include:</p><ul><li>Climate science and natural hazards</li><li>Ecosystems and biodiversity</li><li>Marine science and management</li><li>Sustainability</li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BIOL1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1002">Organisms to Ecosystems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1001">Environmental Science Concepts and Methods</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1002">Physical and Chemical Environmental Systems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1003">Environmental Values and Ethics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2002">Environmental Legislation and Planning</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3001">Integrated Impact Assessment</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3002">Environmental Management Perspectives</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3008">Work Integrated Learning in the Environmental and Development Sectors</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS2161</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2161">Spatial Science</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCIE1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE1002">Multidisciplinary Laboratories</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11587">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Mathematics Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list. Which course you should complete will depend on your previous mathematical background, please refer to each course handbook for more information.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>MATH1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1001">Preparatory Studies in Mathematics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1002">Foundational Studies in Mathematics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1110">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 1</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Mathematics Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11587">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Statistics Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>STAT1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1020">Statistical Reasoning and Literacy</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>STAT1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1070">Statistics for the Sciences</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Statistics Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11587">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Marine Science and Management</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ENVS2320</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2320">Experimental Design and Analysis in Ecology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3220">Coastal Environments and Processes</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI1000">Our Oceans</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>MARI2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI2300">Marine Biology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI3300">Integrated Coastal Ecosystems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI3500">Sustainable Fisheries and Aquaculture</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>2000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2004">Ecology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2080">Earth''s Dynamic Surface</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCIE2223</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE2223">Weather and Waves</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>3000 level Course List </strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>ECON3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3006">Environmental Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3004">Ecotoxicology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3005">Animal Behaviour</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3009">Advanced Water Science and Resource Management</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3250</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3250">Advanced Spatial Science</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI3410</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI3410">Coral Reef Biology, Ecology and Sustainability</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>SCIE3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE3500">Research Integrated Learning</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Marine Science and Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11587">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Ecosystems and Biodiversity</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ENVS2320</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2320">Experimental Design and Analysis in Ecology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>1000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>BIOL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1001">Molecules, Cells and Organisms</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1010">Introductory Chemistry I</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>CHEM1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1020">Introductory Chemistry II</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS1040">Earth: Our Dynamic Planet</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>2000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 20 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>BIOL2090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2090">Microbial Biology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2004">Ecology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2005">Management of Australian Flora</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2006">Ecology and Management of Wildlife</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2009">Catchment and Water Resource Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>3000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 40 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>ECON3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3006">Environmental Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3003">Conservation Biology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3004">Ecotoxicology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3005">Animal Behaviour</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3009">Advanced Water Science and Resource Management</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3250</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3250">Advanced Spatial Science</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCIE3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE3500">Research Integrated Learning</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SRMT3060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SRMT3060">Vegetation Classification and Ecological Restoration</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Ecosystems and Biodiversity"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11587">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Climate Science and Natural Hazards</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory</strong></p><ul><li><strong>GEOS2050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2050">Catchments and Climate</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2060">Earth''s Critical Zone</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3050">Water Resilience: From Climate to Groundwater</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3250</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3250">Advanced Spatial Science</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3340</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3340">Climate Change and Resource Management</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>1000 level Course List </strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>GEOS1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS1040">Earth: Our Dynamic Planet</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS1050">Earth: Natural Hazards</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>2000 level Course List </strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS2009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2009">Catchment and Water Resource Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2320</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2320">Experimental Design and Analysis in Ecology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2080">Earth''s Dynamic Surface</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCIE2223</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE2223">Weather and Waves</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>3000 level Course List </strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3009">Advanced Water Science and Resource Management</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3220">Coastal Environments and Processes</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCIE3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE3500">Research Integrated Learning</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Climate Science and Natural Hazards"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11587">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Sustainability</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ENVS2320</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2320">Experimental Design and Analysis in Ecology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>1000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>BIOL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1001">Molecules, Cells and Organisms</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1004">Social Development and the Environment</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>2000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 20 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2004">Ecology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2005">Management of Australian Flora</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2006">Ecology and Management of Wildlife</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2008">The Sustainable Society</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2009">Catchment and Water Resource Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOG2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2080">Cities and Regions</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2130">Geographies of Development</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>3000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 40 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>ECON3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ECON3006">Environmental Economics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3003">Conservation Biology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3006">Surviving the Anthropocene: Sustainability in the 21st Century</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3009">Advanced Water Science and Resource Management</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOG3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3090">Society and Space</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3250</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3250">Advanced Spatial Science</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS3340</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3340">Climate Change and Resource Management</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI3500">Sustainable Fisheries and Aquaculture</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCIE3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE3500">Research Integrated Learning</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SRMT3060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SRMT3060">Vegetation Classification and Ecological Restoration</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Sustainability"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11587">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 40 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11587">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11587">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Environmental Science and Management</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=11587&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Unlocking secrets of the sea 4:11 <p>Our students teamed up with CSIRO and Geosciences Sydney Uni on the voyage of a lifetime, investigating the causes of submarine landslides that lead to tsunamis. .</p> Career-ready placements <p>Students will complete a 140-hour work placement in a private sector, government or community organisation. There is also the option to undertake overseas field courses.</p><p>Fieldwork is a strong focus of the program and is complemented by practical lab work using professional equipment.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Studying at Central Coast campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/central-coast/living-on-the-central-coast"> Living on the Central Coast <p>The Central Coast offers a relaxed and convenient lifestyle with access to beautiful beaches and national parks. Our campuses have industry-leading facilities all within beautiful bushland.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Why study a Bachelor of Environmental Science and Management? 1:29 <p>Meet Bachelor of Environmental Science and Management student Hanne and hear firsthand why she chose to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> Field Trip to Pacific Palms 3:37 <p>Meet and hear from a number of students who recently went on a field trip to Pacific Palms to learn more about coastal processes.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/482750"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=11587">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-coastal-and-marine-science">Bachelor of Coastal and Marine Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 67.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 46,285</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Central Coast</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-science">Bachelor of Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 67.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 42,840</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Central Coast</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/science-and-the-environment">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Students will complete a 140-hour work placement in a private sector, government or community organisation. There is also the option to undertake overseas field courses.</p><p>Fieldwork is a strong focus of the program and is complemented by practical lab work using professional equipment.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
