UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Become a leader in the business of sustainability</p><p>Do you have a passion for science and sustainability? Want to play a part in solving the environmental problems facing our society? This combined degree can help set you on a leadership path in this fast-growing industry.</p> <p>Learn to understand and combat the critical issues placing a growing strain on the earth’s natural resources such as climate change, human impacts, and the biodiversity crisis. Gain experience in management-based skills to help protect our environment. Both now and into the future.</p><p>When you combine these skills with a broad knowledge of local and global business environments, you expand your commercial and entrepreneurial opportunities in the environmental space – and maximise your employability when you graduate.</p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <p> <strong> World top 200 ? </strong> for Environmental Sciences </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Graduates of this combined degree go on to work in a diverse range of areas. You might work for government departments or councils, for non-government-organisations, or in private industry.</p> <p><strong>Professional outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>Conservation and Ecology</li><li>Environmental Consulting</li><li>Laboratory and Research Work</li><li>Urban and Regional Planning</li><li>Policy Development</li><li>Marine Biology</li></ul> <p>87% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Agriculture &amp; Environmental Studies</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Specialise your studies by choosing majors from each program:</p><p><strong>Business majors (60 units):</strong></p><ul><li>Innovation and Entrepreneurship</li><li>International Relations</li><li>Human Resource Management</li><li>International Business</li><li>Leadership and Management</li><li>Marketing</li></ul><p><strong>Environmental Science and Management majors (80 units):</strong></p><ul><li>Ecosystems and Biodiversity</li><li>Marine Science and Management</li><li>Climate Science and Natural Hazards</li><li>Sustainability</li></ul>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-environmental-science-and-management">Bachelor of Environmental Science and Management</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-business-pre-2025">Bachelor of Business (pre 2025)</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ACCT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT1001">Fundamentals of Accounting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>BIOL1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1002">Organisms to Ecosystems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1001">Environmental Science Concepts and Methods</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1002">Physical and Chemical Environmental Systems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1003">Environmental Values and Ethics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2002">Environmental Legislation and Planning</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3001">Integrated Impact Assessment</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3002">Environmental Management Perspectives</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>FINN1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN1001">Fundamentals of Finance</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>GEOS2161</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2161">Spatial Science</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV1001">Design Thinking: Creativity in Action</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>SCIE1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE1002">Multidisciplinary Laboratories</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40172">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Mathematics Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list. Which course you should complete will depend on your previous mathematical background, please refer to each course handbook for more information.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>MATH1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1001">Preparatory Studies in Mathematics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1002">Foundational Studies in Mathematics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1110">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 1</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Mathematics Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40172">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Statistics Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>STAT1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1020">Statistical Reasoning and Literacy</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>STAT1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1070">Statistics for the Sciences</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Statistics Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40172">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready Placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following courses.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BUSN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3002">Industry Placement</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BUSN3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3500">International Work Placement in Business</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3008">Work Integrated Learning in the Environmental and Development Sectors</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready Placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40172">handbook</a>.</p>Business Majors<p><a href="#">Innovation and Entrepreneurship</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of the major.</p><ul><li><strong>INOV2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2001">Entrepreneurial MakerSpace</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2002">Social Entrepreneurship for Impact</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2003">Data Analytics in Digital Entrepreneurship</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2004">Prompt Engineering for Innovation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3001">Global Networking and Negotiation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3002">Traction and Growth</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3003">Venture Funding</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3004">Acceleration for Student Entrepreneurs (I2N)</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Innovation and Entrepreneurship"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40172">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Leadership and Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2005">Leadership Models and Practices</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT2