UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Build your career in health and human performance.</p><p>Exercise is central to improving health, fitness and wellbeing, and enhancing performance in both recreational and elite sport. Exercise and Sport Science is a dynamic, science-led field that focuses on prescribing, delivering, and evaluating exercise to improve health, function, and performance.</p> <p>Exercise scientists work in a wide range of settings. These include professional sporting organisations, hospitals, rehabilitation clinics, community health services, fitness centres, research institutes, and private practice. From your first year, you’ll learn in state-of-the-art facilities and develop the practical skills needed to make a real-world impact. You’ll gain career-ready experience through placements and industry partnerships with clinics, hospitals, and professional sporting organisations, including connections with elite clubs such as the Newcastle Knights, Newcastle Jets, and Central Coast Mariners. You’ll also learn to collaborate effectively with exercise physiologists, physiotherapists, doctors, and other allied health professionals to support better health outcomes.</p><p>This degree provides a streamlined pathway into the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-of-exercise-physiology">Master of Exercise Physiology</a>, supporting your progression toward becoming an Accredited Exercise Physiologist.</p><p>Studying in a region with strong links to sport, health services, and community wellbeing means you’ll be well positioned to make a meaningful impact on health and performance at both individual and population levels. You can also broaden your career options by combining Exercise and Sport Science with <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-exercise-and-sport-science-business">Business</a> or <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-exercise-and-sport-science-psychological-science">Psychological Science</a>.</p><p><strong>Concurrent Enrolment</strong></p><p>Exercise and Sport Science students are encouraged to consider concurrent enrolment in the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-applied-data-science">Bachelor of Applied Data Science program.</a></p><p>The Bachelor of Applied Data Science equips Exercise and Sport Science students with data analysis and AI skills to optimise athlete performance, injury prevention, personalised training, and so on. It enhances career opportunities in sports analytics, health tech, and research-driven practice.</p><p>Complete both programs in only one extra year of study and graduate with two degrees, increasing your in-demand skills and employability in roles such as performance analysis, research and high-level sports coaching.</p> <p> <strong> World Top 150 ? </strong> for Sports-related subjects </p> <p> <strong> World top 46 ? </strong> for Sport Science </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Careers are available in a variety of public and private sectors including sporting and fitness organisations, and academia.</p> <p>With strong ties to various sporting centres such as Central Coast Mariners, Newcastle Knights, and Newcastle Jet, students can receive a dynamic placement before commencing their career.</p><p><strong>Professional outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>Exercise Scientist</li><li>Sport Scientist</li><li>Strength and Conditioning Coach</li><li>Exercise Rehabilitation Specialist</li><li>Health Promotion Officer</li><li>Community Recreation and Fitness Officer</li><li>Sports Development Manager</li><li>Sports Administrator</li><li>Research Scientist</li><li>Allied Health Assistant</li></ul> <p>89.7% of students rated learning resources positively.</p> <p>Student Experience Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Health Services</p> <p>86.4% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Health Services and Support</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>We offer a globally recognised Bachelor of Exercise and Sport Science program that encompasses all aspects of physical health delivered through a combination of online and face-to-face teaching.</p><p>Students will be able to undertake electives in alternative health areas (nutrition, anatomy, podiatry or psychology) as well as education, business or media to prepare themselves for professional or further postgraduate study opportunities.</p> <p>Core</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>EXSS1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS1040">Functional Anatomy for Exercise Science</a></li><li><strong>EXSS1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS1050">Fundamentals of Exercise and Sport Science Practice</a></li><li><strong>EXSS1060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS1060">Fundamentals of Exercise Prescription and Delivery</a></li><li><strong>EXSS1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS1070">Physical Activity and Exercise Across the Lifespan</a></li><li><strong>EXSS1080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS1080">Psychological, Nutritional and Injury Foundations for Exercise and Sport Science</a></li><li><strong>EXSS2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS2010">Exercise Physiology</a></li><li><strong>EXSS2020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS2020">Biomechanics</a></li><li><strong>EXSS2030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS2030">Sport, Exercise and Performance Psychology</a></li><li><strong>EXSS2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS2060">Motor Control</a></li><li><strong>EXSS2090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS2090">Performance and Data Analysis for Exercise and Sport Science</a></li><li><strong>EXSS2100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS2100">Exercise Prescription and Delivery</a></li><li><strong>EXSS3030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS3030">Nutrition for Health, Fitness and Sport</a></li><li><strong>EXSS3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS3040">Practicum in Exercise and Sports Science</a></li><li><strong>EXSS3050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS3050">Applied Exercise Physiology and Training</a></li><li><strong>EXSS3060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS3060">Advanced Biomechanics</a></li><li><strong>EXSS3070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS3070">Skill Acquisition and Development for Exercise and Sport Science</a></li><li><strong>EXSS3080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS3080">Behavioural Change for Physical Activity and Health</a></li><li><strong>HUBS1108</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1108">Fundamentals of Human Anatomy</a></li><li><strong>HUBS1401</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1401">Human Bioscience</a></li><li><strong>STAT1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1070">Statistics for the Sciences</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40257">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 40 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40257">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40257">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Exercise and Sport Science</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=40257&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Career-ready placement with the Central Coast Academy of Sport 1:48 <p>Hear from Mikaela, an Exercise and Sports Science student about what she has learnt throughout her career-ready placement experience at the Central Coast Academy of Sport.</p> Career-ready placements <p>Gain valuable experience through our 140-hour professional placement program. Start with 40 hours of internal placement to build confidence, before applying your skills and knowledge in clinics, gyms, hospitals, schools, aged care or professional sporting organisations such as the Central Coast Mariners, Newcastle Knights, and Newcastle Jets. Utilise state of the art facilities at our Callaghan campus, including high-quality laboratories, a high-performance gym, and performance testing equipment.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase <a href="/media/viewer?media=907126"></a> <p>ex_ss_prac_experience</p> Study a Bachelor of Exercise and Sport Science 3.28 <p>Find out why Wil Southcombe and Brooke Shoveller chose to study a Bachelor of Exercise and Sports Science at The University of Newcastle.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/482805"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=40257">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-exercise-and-sport-science-psychological-science">Bachelor of Exercise and Sport Science / Bachelor of Psychological Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 72.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> undefined</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4.5 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 11 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-physiotherapy-honours">Bachelor of Physiotherapy (Honours)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 96.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 46,380</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 6 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-exercise-and-sport-science-business">Bachelor of Exercise and Sport Science / Bachelor of Business<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 72.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> undefined</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/health-and-medicine">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Gain valuable experience through our 140-hour professional placement program. Start with 40 hours of internal placement to build confidence, before applying your skills and knowledge in clinics, gyms, hospitals, schools, aged care or professional sporting organisations such as the Central Coast Mariners, Newcastle Knights, and Newcastle Jets. Utilise state of the art facilities at our Callaghan campus, including high-quality laboratories, a high-performance gym, and performance testing equipment.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
