UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Food is an essential part of life</p><p>Society is constantly facing new challenges in food production while the demand for sustainable and healthy choices continues to grow. As novel ingredients, trends and challenges reshape our food landscape, we must continue to assess how they impact health. This field of study requires people driven by curiosity and with a passion for innovative thinking.</p> <p>Food and beverage processing is Australia''s largest manufacturing industry. This dynamic industry offers great opportunities for food and nutrition scientists to work in different areas. Examples include product development, food regulation, nutrition, quality assurance, food safety and research.</p><p>As a graduate of the Bachelor of Food Science and Human Nutrition, you could work with fresh or processed foods, developing new products, or analysing existing ones. Or you could work on ensuring that foods are nutritionally balanced, safe to eat, cost-effective, environmentally friendly, and desirable for consumers.</p> <p> <strong> Real world experience </strong> through our modern food innovation centre and sensory laboratory </p> <p> <strong> 88.4% of students ? </strong> were happy with facilities and resources </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Graduates of Food Science and Human Nutrition are in high demand. The industry is rapidly growing as society becomes savvier and the thirst for transparency and nutritional information grows.</p> <p>Technological advances and investment in scientific research also mean there is growing use of food, diet and functional food components to treat and prevent illness and disease.</p><p>Graduates can also undertake further study such as Honours or a Higher Degree by Research in Food Science. This program can also provide a pathway into Dietetics with additional study.</p><p><strong>Professional Outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>food scientist, technologist or chemist</li><li>food product development</li><li>food biotechnology</li><li>flavourist</li><li>nutrition education &amp; nutrition research</li><li>community health promotion</li></ul> <p>88.5% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024, Undergraduate Science &amp; Mathematics</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You will gain extensive practical experience from our well-equipped laboratories and our industry partners. Our bachelor program covers a wide range of topics, which prepare you for leading roles as a food and nutrition professional and give you a competitive edge in the job market.</p><p><strong>Core courses include:</strong></p><ul><li>biology and biochemistry</li><li>biomedical science</li><li>chemistry</li><li>essential nutrients</li><li>food analysis</li><li>food marketing and consumer behaviour</li><li>food product development</li><li>food safety, microbiology and immunology</li><li>food technologies</li><li>future food: technologies, issues and trends</li><li>nutrition in health and disease</li><li>plant and animal food products</li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BIOL2011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2011">Fundamentals of Biology and Biochemistry</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>CHEM1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1010">Introductory Chemistry I</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>CHEM1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1020">Introductory Chemistry II</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>FSHN1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN1010">Introduction to Food Science and Technology</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN1020">Introduction to Nutrition Science and Applications</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN2010">Essential Nutrients</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN2040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN2040">Animal Food Products</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN2050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN2050">Plant Food Products</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN2060">Food Marketing and Consumer Behaviour</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>FSHN2100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN2100">Microbiology, Food Safety and Immunology</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3020">Nutrition in Health and Disease</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN3030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3030">Future Food: Technologies, Issues and Trends</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN3210</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3210">Food Product Development</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN3230</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3230">Food Analysis</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3500">Professional Practice</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>MATH1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1001">Preparatory Studies in Mathematics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>STAT1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1070">Statistics for the Sciences</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11680">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Health and Wellbeing Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete a course pair from either [FSHN1030 and HUBS1401] or [HUBS1403 and HUBS1404].</strong></p><ul><li><strong>FSHN1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN1030">Introduction to the Nutritional, Physical and Psychological Aspects of Wellness</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>HUBS1401</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1401">Human Bioscience</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HUBS1403</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1403">Biomedical Science Part 1</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>HUBS1404</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1404">Biomedical Science Part 2</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Health and Wellbeing Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11680">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Area of Interest Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>FSHN3010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3010">Food Processing and Quality Management</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN3060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3060">Nutrition for the life cycle</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>FSHN3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3100">Research Methods</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Area of Interest Course List" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11680">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Area of Interest Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11680">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 40 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11680">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11680">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Food Science and Human Nutrition</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=11680&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CCSTC&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Creating meaningful opportunities for students 1:48 <p>At the University of Newcastle, we embed practical, hands-on learning in all our degrees. Check out how a career-ready placement provided real world experience and prepared Andrew for a career as a food scientist.</p> Career-ready placements <p>You will train in the food innovation centre, which includes commercial-grade kitchens and food analysis and sensory laboratories. Work through the product development process, initiating and testing product concepts as you would in the industry. </p><p>Students will also complete a minimum 140-hour career-ready placement through the FSHN3500 course.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Central Coast campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/central-coast/living-on-the-central-coast"> Living on the Central Coast <p>The Central Coast offers a relaxed and convenient lifestyle with access to beautiful beaches and national parks. Our campuses have industry-leading facilities all within beautiful bushland.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase <a href="/media/viewer?media=902027"></a><a href="/media/viewer?media=902028"></a><a href="/media/viewer?media=902029"></a> <p>B-Food-Sci-Human-Nutri-2018-Namra-IN-0205</p> <p>UON 2020 UG MKG CC Ourimbah</p> <p>UON Brand 2020 308</p> Study a Bachelor of Food Science and Human Nutrition 1:03 <p>Meet Dr Quan Vuong and students Audrey and Minh to hear first-hand why you should choose to study a Bachelor of Food Science and Human Nutrition at the University of Newcastle.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/482900"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=11680">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-psychological-science">Bachelor of Psychological Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 67.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 45,070</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-exercise-and-sport-science">Bachelor of Exercise and Sport Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 72.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 44,000</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-food-science-and-human-nutrition-business">Bachelor of Food Science and Human Nutrition / Bachelor of Business<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 67.00 (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 46,725</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Central Coast</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/science-and-the-environment">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>You will train in the food innovation centre, which includes commercial-grade kitchens and food analysis and sensory laboratories. Work through the product development process, initiating and testing product concepts as you would in the industry. </p><p>Students will also complete a minimum 140-hour career-ready placement through the FSHN3500 course.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
