UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Design your own career in the food industry</p><p>Match business skills with your passion for food and nutrition, and maximise your employability once you graduate.</p><p>With society facing new challenges in food production, and the demand for sustainable and healthy choices growing, there’s never been a better time to enter the food and nutrition industry.</p> <p>This combined degree allows you to pair in-depth scientific knowledge with business expertise across marketing, tourism, industrial relations and more.</p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <p> <strong> Real world experience </strong> through our modern food innovation centre and sensory laboratory </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>The food industry is rapidly growing as society becomes savvier and the thirst for transparency and nutritional information grows.</p> <p><strong>Professional outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>food scientist, technologist or chemist</li><li>food product development officer</li><li>food biotechnologist</li><li>flavourist</li><li>nutrition educator or researcher</li><li>community health promotions officer</li></ul> <p>91.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Business and Management</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You will gain extensive practical experience from our well-equipped laboratories and industry partners. Our bachelor program covers a wide range of topics, which prepare you for leading roles as a food and nutrition professional and give you a competitive edge in the job market.</p><p><strong>Core courses include:</strong></p><ul><li>biology and biochemistry</li><li>food marketing and consumer behaviour</li><li>food safety and microbiology</li><li>food technologies</li><li>nutrition in health and disease</li><li>accounting</li><li>management</li><li>finance</li></ul>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-food-science-and-human-nutrition">Bachelor of Food Science and Human Nutrition</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-business-pre-2025">Bachelor of Business (pre 2025)</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ACCT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT1001">Fundamentals of Accounting</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>BIOL2011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2011">Fundamentals of Biology and Biochemistry</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>BUSN1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN1010">Analytics in Business</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>CHEM1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1010">Introductory Chemistry I</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>CHEM1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1020">Introductory Chemistry II</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>FINN1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN1001">Fundamentals of Finance</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>FSHN1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN1010">Introduction to Food Science and Technology</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN1020">Introduction to Nutrition Science and Applications</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN2010">Essential Nutrients</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN2040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN2040">Animal Food Products</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN2050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN2050">Plant Food Products</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN2060">Food Marketing and Consumer Behaviour</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>FSHN2100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN2100">Microbiology, Food Safety and Immunology</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3020">Nutrition in Health and Disease</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN3030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3030">Future Food: Technologies, Issues and Trends</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN3210</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3210">Food Product Development</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN3230</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3230">Food Analysis</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>INOV1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV1001">Design Thinking: Creativity in Action</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>STAT1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1070">Statistics for the Sciences</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40102">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Health and Wellbeing Directed Course - Human Health and Wellbeing Directed Course L</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following courses.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>FSHN1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN1030">Introduction to the Nutritional, Physical and Psychological Aspects of Wellness</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>HUBS1401</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1401">Human Bioscience</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HUBS1403</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1403">Biomedical Science Part 1</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>HUBS1404</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1404">Biomedical Science Part 2</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Health and Wellbeing Directed Course - Human Health and Wellbeing Directed Course L"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40102">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready Placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following courses.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BUSN3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3002">Industry Placement</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BUSN3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN3500">International Work Placement in Business</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>FSHN3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3500">Professional Practice</a> (Central Coast)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready Placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40102">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Area of Interest Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>FSHN3010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3010">Food Processing and Quality Management</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>FSHN3060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3060">Nutrition for the life cycle</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>FSHN3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN3100">Research Methods</a> (Central Coast)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Area of Interest Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40102">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Innovation and Entrepreneurship</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of the major.</p><ul><li><strong>INOV2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2001">Entrepreneurial MakerSpace</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2002">Social Entrepreneurship for Impact</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2003">Data Analytics in Digital Entrepreneurship</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2004">Prompt Engineering for Innovation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3001">Global Networking and Negotiation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3002">Traction and Growth</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3003">Venture Funding</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>INOV3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3004">Acceleration for Student Entrepreneurs (I2N)</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Innovation and Entrepreneurship"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40102">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Marketing</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MKTG2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2001">Digital and Social Media Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2010">Marketing Research and Data-Driven Insights</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2060">International Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2101">Consumer Decision Making</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3000">Strategic Marketing Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3003">Creating and Managing Brands</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3004">Advertising and Image Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MKTG3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3040">Services Marketing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Marketing"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40102">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Leadership and Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2005">Leadership Models and Practices</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2006">Management in Environmental Turbulence</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2008">Digital Business Applications</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT2009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2009">Organisational Behaviour</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3011">Leading Organisational Change</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3012">Business Strategy</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3013</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3013">Innovation Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>MNGT3014</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3014">Managing Inclusion, Diversity and Equity in Organisations</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Leadership and Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40102">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Resource Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>HRER2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2001">Managing Talent</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2002">Introduction to Employment Relations</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2003">Dynamics of People and Work in Organisations</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2004">HR Analytics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3001">Future of Work</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3002">Negotiation and Conflict Management</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3003">Strategic HR</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HRER3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3004">Human Capital Development</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Resource Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40102">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Business</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IBUS2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2001">Cross-Cultural Management and Negotiations</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2003">International Trade Logistics in a Digital Age</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2004">Managing International Business</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2005">Corporate Social Responsibility for Global Business</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3000">International Business Strategy</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3001">International Human Resource Management</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3004">International Business Alliances</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>IBUS3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3005">International Business in Emerging Markets</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Business"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40102">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Relations</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2002">Business and the Politics of Globalisation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2004">Diplomacy, Trade and Politics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3001">Public Diplomacy and Social Media</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3002">Global Data Governance for Just and Sustainable Futures</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3003">International Relations in a Changing World Order</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3004">Indigenising International Politics, Policy and the Economy</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40102">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40102">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Food Science and Human Nutrition / Bachelor of Business</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=40102&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CCSTC&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Real-world experience - Bachelor of Business student Will at Fresh Marketing 1:00 <p>As part of his degree, Bachelor of Business graduate Will interned with Newcastle-based boutique marketing agency Fresh Marketing. He gained hands-on campaign experience and made valuable industry contacts – giving him a leg up in a competitive industry.</p> Career-ready placements <p>This combined degree integrates opportunities for you to gain national and international work experience and professional mentoring, building practical skills and work-ready graduates.</p><p>Students train in the food innovation centre, which includes commercial-grade kitchens and food analysis and sensory laboratories.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Central Coast campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/central-coast/living-on-the-central-coast"> Living on the Central Coast <p>The Central Coast offers a relaxed and convenient lifestyle with access to beautiful beaches and national parks. Our campuses have industry-leading facilities all within beautiful bushland.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Study a Bachelor of Food Science and Human Nutrition 1:03 <p>Meet Dr Quan Vuong and students Audrey and Minh to hear first-hand why you should choose to study a Bachelor of Food Science and Human Nutrition at the University of Newcastle.</p> Meet Emily, a Bachelor of Food Science and Human Nutrition / Bachelor of Business student 1:43 <p>Emily talks about her experience studying a Bachelor of Food Science and Human Nutrition / Bachelor of Business at the University of Newcastle.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/482910"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=40102">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-food-science-and-human-nutrition">Bachelor of Food Science and Human Nutrition<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 67.00 (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 45,060</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Central Coast</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-exercise-and-sport-science">Bachelor of Exercise and Sport Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 72.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 44,000</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-nutrition-and-dietetics-honours">Bachelor of Nutrition and Dietetics (Honours)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 77.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 45,070</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 6 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/business-and-management">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://www.ahri.com.au"></a><p>The Bachelor of Business (HRM major) is accredited by the Australian Human Resource Management Institute (AHRI) https://www.ahri.com.au/</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>This combined degree integrates opportunities for you to gain national and international work experience and professional mentoring, building practical skills and work-ready graduates.</p><p>Students train in the food innovation centre, which includes commercial-grade kitchens and food analysis and sensory laboratories.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
