UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Be the next big thing</p><p>Information technology (IT) is all about developing, building and maintaining software technology systems to meet the challenges faced by business and society. We train IT graduates to be technically savvy, creative and flexible.</p> <p>Our majors are designed to meet industry''s evolving IT needs. You can focus on business technology and design and manage large and complex software systems critical for big corporations and government. You’ll be equipped to develop cloud-computing solutions or specialise in IT security.</p><p>Why combine IT with business? Complete these two bachelor degrees in just four years. Compliment your technical skills with an understanding of local and global business environments. You''ll also cover entrepreneurism and the ability to commercialise IT innovations.</p><p>Learn how to manage people and finances, propose new business opportunities and market your product. Prepare yourself for a leadership role with this unique package of capabilities.</p> <p> <strong> 12 weeks </strong> of Industrial Experience </p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>IT and business graduates enjoy great employment prospects and go on to work in dynamic sectors at the forefront of discovery and innovation.</p> <p>You could work for organisations like Google, Amazon, Facebook or Apple.</p><p><strong>Professional Outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>Mobile App Designer</li><li>Software Developer</li><li>Games Designer</li><li>IT Analyst</li><li>IT Project Manager</li><li>Infrastructure Business Analyst</li></ul> <p>91.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Business and Management</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p><strong>Study one of three majors:</strong></p><ul><li>Business Technology</li><li>International Business</li><li>Leadership and Management</li></ul><p>You will study courses in web technologies, programming, databases and information management, systems analysis and design, and project management.</p><p>Develop your business skills in accounting, finance, microeconomics for business decisions, international business risk, and business analysis.</p><p>All students will complete the ICT Business Analyst major as part of the Bachelor of Information Technology.</p>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-information-technology">Bachelor of Information Technology</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-business">Bachelor of Business (from 2025)</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ACCT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ACCT1001">Fundamentals of Accounting</a></li><li><strong>COMP1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP1010">Computing Fundamentals</a></li><li><strong>COMP1140</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP1140">Database and Information Management</a></li><li><strong>COMP3851A</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3851A">Computing and Information Sciences Work Integrated Learning Part A</a></li><li><strong>COMP3851B</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3851B">Computing and Information Sciences Work Integrated Learning Part B</a></li><li><strong>FINN1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FINN1001">Fundamentals of Finance</a></li><li><strong>INFT1060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT1060">Cybersecurity Fundamentals</a></li><li><strong>INFT2031</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT2031">Systems and Network Administration</a></li><li><strong>INFT2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT2060">Applied Artificial Intelligence</a></li><li><strong>INFT3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT3100">ICT Project Management</a></li><li><strong>INFT3800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT3800">Professional Practice in IT</a></li><li><strong>INOV1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV1001">Design Thinking: Creativity in Action</a></li><li><strong>MKTG1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG1001">Foundations of Marketing</a></li><li><strong>MNGT1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT1001">Introduction to Management and Sustainability</a></li><li><strong>SENG1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG1050">Web Technologies</a></li><li><strong>SENG1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG1110">Object Oriented Programming</a></li><li><strong>SENG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG2130">Systems Analysis and Design</a></li><li><strong>SENG2260</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG2260">Human-Computer Interaction</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12238">handbook</a>.</p>ICT Major<p><a href="#">ICT Business Analyst</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following courses to fulfil the requirements of this major. 20 units of courses are counted from the core for this major - COMP3851A and COMP3851B.</p><ul><li><strong>BUSA2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSA2001">Big Data Analytics</a></li><li><strong>BUSA2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSA2002">Data Visualisation for Decision Makers in Business</a></li><li><strong>COMP3350</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3350">Advanced Database</a></li><li><strong>COMP3851A</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3851A">Computing and Information Sciences Work Integrated Learning Part A</a></li><li><strong>COMP3851B</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3851B">Computing and Information Sciences Work Integrated Learning Part B</a></li><li><strong>EBUS3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EBUS3040">Business Intelligence in Practice</a></li><li><strong>INFT1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT1004">Introduction to Programming</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 10 units from this course list</p><ul><li><strong>BUSN1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BUSN1010">Analytics in Business</a></li><li><strong>STAT1060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1060">Business Decision Making</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"ICT Business Analyst"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12238">handbook</a>.</p>Business Majors<p><a href="#">Innovation and Entrepreneurship</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of the major.</p><ul><li><strong>INOV2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2001">Entrepreneurial MakerSpace</a></li><li><strong>INOV2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2002">Social Entrepreneurship for Impact</a></li><li><strong>INOV2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2003">Data Analytics in Digital Entrepreneurship</a></li><li><strong>INOV2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV2004">Prompt Engineering for Innovation</a></li><li><strong>INOV3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3001">Global Networking and Negotiation</a></li><li><strong>INOV3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3002">Traction and Growth</a></li><li><strong>INOV3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3003">Venture Funding</a></li><li><strong>INOV3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INOV3004">Acceleration for Student Entrepreneurs (I2N)</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Innovation and Entrepreneurship"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12238">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Marketing</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MKTG2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2001">Digital and Social Media Marketing</a></li><li><strong>MKTG2010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2010">Marketing Research and Data-Driven Insights</a></li><li><strong>MKTG2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2060">International Marketing</a></li><li><strong>MKTG2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG2101">Consumer Decision Making</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3000">Strategic Marketing Management</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3003">Creating and Managing Brands</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3004">Advertising and Image Management</a></li><li><strong>MKTG3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MKTG3040">Services Marketing</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Marketing"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12238">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Leadership and Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>MNGT2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2005">Leadership Models and Practices</a></li><li><strong>MNGT2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2006">Management in Environmental Turbulence</a></li><li><strong>MNGT2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2008">Digital Business Applications</a></li><li><strong>MNGT2009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT2009">Organisational Behaviour</a></li><li><strong>MNGT3011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3011">Leading Organisational Change</a></li><li><strong>MNGT3012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3012">Business Strategy</a></li><li><strong>MNGT3013</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3013">Innovation Management</a></li><li><strong>MNGT3014</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MNGT3014">Managing Inclusion, Diversity and Equity in Organisations</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Leadership and Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12238">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Resource Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>HRER2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2001">Managing Talent</a></li><li><strong>HRER2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2002">Introduction to Employment Relations</a></li><li><strong>HRER2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2003">Dynamics of People and Work in Organisations</a></li><li><strong>HRER2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2004">HR Analytics</a></li><li><strong>HRER3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3001">Future of Work</a></li><li><strong>HRER3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3002">Negotiation and Conflict Management</a></li><li><strong>HRER3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3003">Strategic HR</a></li><li><strong>HRER3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3004">Human Capital Development</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Resource Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12238">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Business</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IBUS2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2001">Cross-Cultural Management and Negotiations</a></li><li><strong>IBUS2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2003">International Trade Logistics in a Digital Age</a></li><li><strong>IBUS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2004">Managing International Business</a></li><li><strong>IBUS2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS2005">Corporate Social Responsibility for Global Business</a></li><li><strong>IBUS3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3000">International Business Strategy</a></li><li><strong>IBUS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3001">International Human Resource Management</a></li><li><strong>IBUS3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3004">International Business Alliances</a></li><li><strong>IBUS3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IBUS3005">International Business in Emerging Markets</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Business"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12238">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Relations</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2002">Business and the Politics of Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a></li><li><strong>IREL2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2004">Diplomacy, Trade and Politics</a></li><li><strong>IREL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3001">Public Diplomacy and Social Media</a></li><li><strong>IREL3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3002">Global Data Governance for Just and Sustainable Futures</a></li><li><strong>IREL3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3003">International Relations in a Changing World Order</a></li><li><strong>IREL3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3004">Indigenising International Politics, Policy and the Economy</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12238">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12238">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Information Technology / Bachelor of Business</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=12238&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Creating meaningful opportunities for students 0:44 <p>At the University of Newcastle, we embed practical, hands-on learning in all our degrees. Check out just some of the opportunities our students have had to build their experience.</p> Career-ready placements <p>Students have the opportunity to undertake industry placement. This career-ready placement opportunity allows students to gain hands-on experience in the industry, creating graduates who are prepared for immediate and productive employment.</p><p>You will work with a team of students to complete a major IT project, with the opportunity to find and develop a project with an industry partner.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Meet Amanda, a Bachelor of Information Technology student from Philippines 1:39 <p>Find out why Amanda loves studying at the University of Newcastle.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/483050"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=12238">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-information-technology">Bachelor of Information Technology<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 67.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 43,940</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, PSB Singapore</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-business">Bachelor of Business<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,540</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-software-engineering-honours">Bachelor of Software Engineering (Honours)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 77.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 44,420</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/business-and-management">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://www.acs.org.au/"></a><p>The Bachelor Information Technology is accredited by the Australian Computer Society.</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Students have the opportunity to undertake industry placement. This career-ready placement opportunity allows students to gain hands-on experience in the industry, creating graduates who are prepared for immediate and productive employment.</p><p>You will work with a team of students to complete a major IT project, with the opportunity to find and develop a project with an industry partner.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
