UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Build the mathematics behind artificial intelligence and data.</p><p>Mathematics is the language of science and technology. It underpins many of the systems and innovations we rely on every day. In this program, you’ll develop essential skills in logic, mathematical modelling, experimental design and data analysis.</p><p>If you enjoy analysing problems and thinking critically, mathematics can open the door to a wide range of careers. As artificial intelligence and data-driven technologies continue to grow, organisations need people who can interpret data, build models and support complex decision-making.</p> <p>From AI and data to finance, energy and research, studying mathematics prepares you to step into some of the fastest growing and most future-focused roles across industries.</p> <p> <strong> 88.4% of students ? </strong> were happy with facilities and resources </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>This degree can take students to varied and ground-breaking places. Graduates work in a wide range of fields including communications, international finance and the futures market, the energy sector, and medical and health research.</p> <p>Current research is inventing new ways of using existing mathematics as well as creating new mathematics for the future. Analytical thinking and innovation, critical thinking and analysis, complex problem-solving, technology design and programming and reasoning, problem-solving and ideation are all embedded within this degree, and are skills that have been identified as being in demand and emerging according to the <a href="https://www.weforum.org/publications/the-future-of-jobs-report-2025/">World Economic Forum’s The Future of Jobs Report 2025.</a></p><p>With <a href="https://www.voced.edu.au/content/ngv%3A100325#:~:text=To%20fulfill%20the%20AI%20jobs,career%20retraining">industry experts predicting</a> up to 200,000 new AI-focused roles in Australia by 2030, you will be equipped as an adaptable graduate to take advantage of new opportunities and solve global challenges.</p><p><strong>Professional outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>data mining analyst</li><li>economic/social statistician</li><li>investment banker/stockbroker</li><li>sports statistician</li><li>meteorologist</li><li>data analyst and scientist</li></ul> <p>88.5% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024, Undergraduate Science &amp; Mathematics</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Current research is inventing new ways of using existing mathematics as well as creating new mathematics for the future. As part of your structured mathematics major, you will study courses in topic areas such as:</p><ul><li>statistics</li><li>differential equations</li><li>numerical methods</li><li>number theory</li><li>complex analysis</li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>MATH1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1110">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 1</a></li><li><strong>MATH1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1120">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 2</a></li><li><strong>MATH1800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1800">Mathematical Modelling</a></li><li><strong>MATH2310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2310">Calculus of Science and Engineering</a></li><li><strong>MATH2340</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2340">Linearity and Continuity 1</a></li><li><strong>MATH2350</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2350">Linearity and Continuity 2</a></li><li><strong>MATH3600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3600">Work Integrated Learning for Mathematical Sciences</a></li><li><strong>STAT1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1100">Data Communication and Modelling</a></li><li><strong>STAT1300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1300">Fundamentals of Statistics</a></li><li><strong>STAT2020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2020">Predictive Analytics</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10237">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Programming Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list. Students completing the Data Science or Computer Science Co Major, must complete SENG1110.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ENGG1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGG1003">Introduction to Engineering Programming with Python</a></li><li><strong>INFT1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT1004">Introduction to Programming</a></li><li><strong>SENG1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG1110">Object Oriented Programming</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Programming Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10237">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Pure and Applied Mathematics</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses.</p><ul><li><strong>MATH1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1120">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 2</a></li><li><strong>MATH1800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1800">Mathematical Modelling</a></li><li><strong>MATH2242</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2242">Complex Analysis</a></li><li><strong>MATH2800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2800">Ordinary Differential Equations and Applied Linear Algebra</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 40 units from the following directed courses.</p><ul><li><strong>MATH3120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3120">Algebra</a></li><li><strong>MATH3170</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3170">Number Theory</a></li><li><strong>MATH3205</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3205">Applied Fourier Analysis</a></li><li><strong>MATH3700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3700">Partial Differential Equations</a></li><li><strong>MATH3820</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3820">Numerical Methods</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Pure and Applied Mathematics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10237">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Statistics</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses</p><ul><li><strong>STAT1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1100">Data Communication and Modelling</a></li><li><strong>STAT1300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1300">Fundamentals of Statistics</a></li><li><strong>STAT2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2000">Applied Statistics and Research Methods</a></li><li><strong>STAT2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2300">Statistical Inference</a></li><li><strong>STAT3030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3030">Generalised Linear Models</a></li><li><strong>STAT3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3040">Time Series Forecasting</a></li><li><strong>STAT3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3100">Systems Thinking for an Integrated Workforce</a></li><li><strong>STAT3800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3800">Deterministic and Stochastic Optimisation</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Statistics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10237">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Studies in Mathematics and Statistics</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory Courses</strong></p><ul><li><strong>MATH1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1120">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 2</a></li><li><strong>MATH1800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1800">Mathematical Modelling</a></li></ul><p><strong>2000 Level Course List </strong>Completed 20 units from the 2000 level course list.</p><ul><li><strong>MATH2242</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2242">Complex Analysis</a></li><li><strong>MATH2800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2800">Ordinary Differential Equations and Applied Linear Algebra</a></li><li><strong>STAT2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2000">Applied Statistics and Research Methods</a></li><li><strong>STAT2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2300">Statistical Inference</a></li></ul><p><strong>3000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 40 units from the 3000 level course list.</p><ul><li><strong>MATH3120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3120">Algebra</a></li><li><strong>MATH3170</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3170">Number Theory</a></li><li><strong>MATH3205</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3205">Applied Fourier Analysis</a></li><li><strong>MATH3700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3700">Partial Differential Equations</a></li><li><strong>MATH3820</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3820">Numerical Methods</a></li><li><strong>STAT3030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3030">Generalised Linear Models</a></li><li><strong>STAT3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3040">Time Series Forecasting</a></li><li><strong>STAT3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3100">Systems Thinking for an Integrated Workforce</a></li><li><strong>STAT3800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3800">Deterministic and Stochastic Optimisation</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Studies in Mathematics and Statistics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10237">handbook</a>.</p>Co-majors (Optional)<p><a href="#">Climate Science</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses.</p><ul><li><strong>GEOS1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS1050">Earth: Natural Hazards</a></li><li><strong>GEOS2050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2050">Catchments and Climate</a></li><li><strong>GEOS2161</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2161">Spatial Science</a></li><li><strong>GEOS3250</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3250">Advanced Spatial Science</a></li><li><strong>GEOS3340</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3340">Climate Change and Resource Management</a></li><li><strong>PHYS2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHYS2300">Climate and Energy</a></li><li><strong>SCIE2223</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE2223">Weather and Waves</a></li><li><strong>STAT1300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1300">Fundamentals of Statistics</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Climate Science"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10237">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Computer Science</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory</strong></p><ul><li><strong>COMP2230</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP2230">Algorithms</a></li><li><strong>COMP2270</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP2270">Theory of Computation</a></li><li><strong>COMP3260</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3260">Data Security</a></li><li><strong>COMP3290</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3290">Compiler Design</a></li><li><strong>COMP3320</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3320">Computer Graphics</a></li><li><strong>MATH1510</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1510">Discrete Mathematics</a></li><li><strong>SENG1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG1110">Object Oriented Programming</a></li><li><strong>SENG1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG1120">Data Structures</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Computer Science"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10237">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Data Science</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses.</p><ul><li><strong>COMP1140</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP1140">Database and Information Management</a></li><li><strong>COMP2230</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP2230">Algorithms</a></li><li><strong>COMP3330</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3330">Machine Intelligence</a></li><li><strong>COMP3340</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/COMP3340">Data Engineering and Mining</a></li><li><strong>SENG1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG1110">Object Oriented Programming</a></li><li><strong>SENG1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SENG1120">Data Structures</a></li><li><strong>STAT2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2300">Statistical Inference</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>STAT3030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3030">Generalised Linear Models</a></li><li><strong>STAT3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3040">Time Series Forecasting</a></li><li><strong>STAT3800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3800">Deterministic and Stochastic Optimisation</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Data Science"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10237">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 70 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10237">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10237">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Mathematics</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=10237&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Creating meaningful opportunities for students 0:44 <p>At the University of Newcastle, we embed practical, hands-on learning in all our degrees. Check out just some of the opportunities our students have had to build their experience.</p> Career-ready placements <p>Through the program, you will complement your theoretical studies with tutorials and laboratories that apply theory to practical situations. In your final year, you will complete a capstone project, working with industry on a real-world project.</p><p>High achieving students can also apply for our Merit Pathway program. Students work on active research projects and are mentored by leading researchers.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/483200"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=10237">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-science">Bachelor of Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 67.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 42,840</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Central Coast</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-education-secondary">Bachelor of Education (Secondary)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 41,150</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-mathematics-advanced">Bachelor of Mathematics (Advanced)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 90.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 43,760</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/computing-maths-and-technology">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Through the program, you will complement your theoretical studies with tutorials and laboratories that apply theory to practical situations. In your final year, you will complete a capstone project, working with industry on a real-world project.</p><p>High achieving students can also apply for our Merit Pathway program. Students work on active research projects and are mentored by leading researchers.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
