UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Deepen your understanding of the world around you</p><p>Science is about asking new questions and uncovering the answers. It underpins technology, business, environmental management, research, health and the world around us. Mathematics is the language of science. It underpins most technological advances that we rely on every day. Without maths, interpreting the real world would not be possible.</p> <p>When you study this combined degree, you’ll deepen your understanding of complex concepts and diversify your potential across a wide range of industries and sectors.</p><p>Learn from leading researchers who will guide you through a tailored program, designed to give you the skills that employers are seeking. Graduate with the practical skills to make a difference in the world – and contribute new solutions to the many scientific challenges we face.</p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Most of the critical issues that face our society today require both science and mathematics to help find solutions. Because this combined degree emphasises problem-solving, teamwork and critical thinking, graduates are sought after across a range of sectors.</p> <p><strong>Professional outcomes might include:</strong></p><ul><li>microbiologist</li><li>neuroscientist</li><li>data mining analyst</li><li>economic/social statistician</li><li>researcher</li><li>statistician</li></ul> <p>88.5% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Science and Mathematics</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Your degree includes compulsory or optional courses in maths. To increase your chance of academic success, it is recommended that you select a course which matches your existing knowledge and understanding of maths concepts.</p>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-mathematics">Bachelor of Mathematics</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-science">Bachelor of Science</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>INFT1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT1004">Introduction to Programming</a></li><li><strong>MATH1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1110">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 1</a></li><li><strong>MATH1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1120">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 2</a></li><li><strong>MATH1800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1800">Mathematical Modelling</a></li><li><strong>MATH2310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2310">Calculus of Science and Engineering</a></li><li><strong>MATH2340</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2340">Linearity and Continuity 1</a></li><li><strong>MATH2350</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2350">Linearity and Continuity 2</a></li><li><strong>SCIE1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE1002">Multidisciplinary Laboratories</a></li><li><strong>STAT1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1100">Data Communication and Modelling</a></li><li><strong>STAT1300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1300">Fundamentals of Statistics</a></li><li><strong>STAT2020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2020">Predictive Analytics</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Work Integrated Learning</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>MATH3600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3600">Work Integrated Learning for Mathematical Sciences</a></li><li><strong>SCIE3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE3002">WIL for the Sciences</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Work Integrated Learning"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p>Mathematics Major<p><a href="#">Statistics</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses</p><ul><li><strong>STAT1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1100">Data Communication and Modelling</a></li><li><strong>STAT1300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1300">Fundamentals of Statistics</a></li><li><strong>STAT2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2000">Applied Statistics and Research Methods</a></li><li><strong>STAT2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2300">Statistical Inference</a></li><li><strong>STAT3030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3030">Generalised Linear Models</a></li><li><strong>STAT3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3040">Time Series Forecasting</a></li><li><strong>STAT3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3100">Systems Thinking for an Integrated Workforce</a></li><li><strong>STAT3800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3800">Deterministic and Stochastic Optimisation</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Statistics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Studies in Mathematics and Statistics</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory Courses</strong></p><ul><li><strong>MATH1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1120">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 2</a></li><li><strong>MATH1800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1800">Mathematical Modelling</a></li></ul><p><strong>2000 Level Course List </strong>Completed 20 units from the 2000 level course list.</p><ul><li><strong>MATH2242</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2242">Complex Analysis</a></li><li><strong>MATH2800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2800">Ordinary Differential Equations and Applied Linear Algebra</a></li><li><strong>STAT2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2000">Applied Statistics and Research Methods</a></li><li><strong>STAT2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2300">Statistical Inference</a></li></ul><p><strong>3000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 40 units from the 3000 level course list.</p><ul><li><strong>MATH3120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3120">Algebra</a></li><li><strong>MATH3170</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3170">Number Theory</a></li><li><strong>MATH3205</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3205">Applied Fourier Analysis</a></li><li><strong>MATH3700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3700">Partial Differential Equations</a></li><li><strong>MATH3820</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3820">Numerical Methods</a></li><li><strong>STAT3030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3030">Generalised Linear Models</a></li><li><strong>STAT3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3040">Time Series Forecasting</a></li><li><strong>STAT3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3100">Systems Thinking for an Integrated Workforce</a></li><li><strong>STAT3800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT3800">Deterministic and Stochastic Optimisation</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Studies in Mathematics and Statistics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Pure and Applied Mathematics</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses.</p><ul><li><strong>MATH1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1120">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 2</a></li><li><strong>MATH1800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1800">Mathematical Modelling</a></li><li><strong>MATH2242</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2242">Complex Analysis</a></li><li><strong>MATH2800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2800">Ordinary Differential Equations and Applied Linear Algebra</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 40 units from the following directed courses.</p><ul><li><strong>MATH3120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3120">Algebra</a></li><li><strong>MATH3170</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3170">Number Theory</a></li><li><strong>MATH3205</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3205">Applied Fourier Analysis</a></li><li><strong>MATH3700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3700">Partial Differential Equations</a></li><li><strong>MATH3820</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3820">Numerical Methods</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Pure and Applied Mathematics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p>Science Major<p><a href="#">Biodiversity and Conservation</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following Compulsory Courses.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1001">Environmental Science Concepts and Methods</a></li><li><strong>ENVS1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1003">Environmental Values and Ethics</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3003">Conservation Biology</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3004">Ecotoxicology</a></li></ul><p><strong>2000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 20 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2004">Ecology</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2005">Management of Australian Flora</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2006">Ecology and Management of Wildlife</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2009">Catchment and Water Resource Management</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2320</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2320">Experimental Design and Analysis in Ecology</a></li><li><strong>MARI2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI2300">Marine Biology</a></li></ul><p><strong>3000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 20 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3005">Animal Behaviour</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3009</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3009">Advanced Water Science and Resource Management</a></li><li><strong>MARI3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI3300">Integrated Coastal Ecosystems</a></li><li><strong>MARI3410</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI3410">Coral Reef Biology, Ecology and Sustainability</a></li><li><strong>SRMT3060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SRMT3060">Vegetation Classification and Ecological Restoration</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Biodiversity and Conservation"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Earth Science</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following Compulsory Courses.</p><ul><li><strong>GEOS1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS1040">Earth: Our Dynamic Planet</a></li><li><strong>GEOS1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS1050">Earth: Natural Hazards</a></li><li><strong>GEOS2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2080">Earth''s Dynamic Surface</a></li><li><strong>GEOS2161</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2161">Spatial Science</a></li><li><strong>GEOS3050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3050">Water Resilience: From Climate to Groundwater</a></li></ul><p><strong>2000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>GEOS2050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2050">Catchments and Climate</a></li><li><strong>GEOS2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2060">Earth''s Critical Zone</a></li><li><strong>SCIE2223</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE2223">Weather and Waves</a></li></ul><p><strong>3000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 20 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>GEOS3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3220">Coastal Environments and Processes</a></li><li><strong>GEOS3250</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3250">Advanced Spatial Science</a></li><li><strong>GEOS3340</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3340">Climate Change and Resource Management</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Earth Science"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Psychology</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following Compulsory Courses.</p><ul><li><strong>PSYC1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1010">Psychology Introduction 1</a></li><li><strong>PSYC1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1020">Psychology Introduction 2</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2300">Cognitive Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2400">Biological Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3000">Advanced Research Methods and Statistics in Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3800">Advanced Special Topics in Psychology 2</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 20 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3005">Animal Behaviour</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3006">Individual Differences and Assessment</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3301</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3301">Advanced Perception and Learning in Psychology</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Psychology"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Geography</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following Compulsory Courses.</p><ul><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a></li><li><strong>GEOS1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS1040">Earth: Our Dynamic Planet</a></li><li><strong>GEOS2161</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2161">Spatial Science</a></li><li><strong>GEOS3250</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3250">Advanced Spatial Science</a></li></ul><p><strong>2000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2002">Environmental Legislation and Planning</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2008">The Sustainable Society</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2080">Cities and Regions</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2130">Geographies of Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOS2050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2050">Catchments and Climate</a></li><li><strong>GEOS2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS2080">Earth''s Dynamic Surface</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a></li></ul><p><strong>3000 Level Course List </strong>Complete 30 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3001">Integrated Impact Assessment</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3006">Surviving the Anthropocene: Sustainability in the 21st Century</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3008">Work Integrated Learning in the Environmental and Development Sectors</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3090">Society and Space</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3300">Rethinking Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOS3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3220">Coastal Environments and Processes</a></li><li><strong>GEOS3340</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS3340">Climate Change and Resource Management</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Geography" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Geography"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Chemistry</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory</strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHEM1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1010">Introductory Chemistry I</a></li><li><strong>CHEM1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1020">Introductory Chemistry II</a></li><li><strong>CHEM2110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM2110">Applied Analytical Chemistry</a></li><li><strong>CHEM2410</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM2410">Physical Chemistry</a></li></ul><p>1 courses are part of "Chemistry" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Chemistry"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Biological Sciences</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory Courses </strong>Complete the following Compulsory Courses.</p><ul><li><strong>BIOL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1001">Molecules, Cells and Organisms</a></li><li><strong>BIOL1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1002">Organisms to Ecosystems</a></li><li><strong>BIOL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2001">Molecular Laboratory Skills for Biological Sciences</a></li><li><strong>BIOL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2002">Laboratory Skills in Biological Systems</a></li><li><strong>BIOL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL3001">Advanced Laboratory Skills in Biological Sciences</a></li></ul><p>1 courses are part of "Biological Sciences" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Biological Sciences"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Physics</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following Compulsory Courses to fulfill the requirements of the Major.</p><ul><li><strong>MATH1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1110">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 1</a></li><li><strong>MATH1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1120">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 2</a></li><li><strong>MATH2310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2310">Calculus of Science and Engineering</a></li><li><strong>PHYS1210</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHYS1210">Advanced Physics I</a></li><li><strong>PHYS1220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHYS1220">Advanced Physics II</a></li><li><strong>PHYS2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHYS2101">Quantum Science</a></li><li><strong>PHYS2203</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHYS2203">Advanced Mechanics</a></li><li><strong>PHYS2204</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHYS2204">Electromagnetism</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Physics" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</p><ul><li><strong>MATH2242</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH2242">Complex Analysis</a></li><li><strong>MATH3820</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH3820">Numerical Methods</a></li><li><strong>PHYS2102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHYS2102">Particles and Space</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Physics" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Physics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 60 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40170">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Mathematics / Bachelor of Science</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=40170&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Creating meaningful opportunities for students 0:44 <p>At the University of Newcastle, we embed practical, hands-on learning in all our degrees. Check out just some of the opportunities our students have had to build their experience.</p> Career-ready placements <p>Through the program, you will complement your theoretical studies with tutorials and laboratories that apply theory to practical situations. In your final year, you will complete a capstone project, working with industry on a real-world project.</p><p>High achieving students can also apply for our Merit Pathway program. Students work on active research projects and are mentored by leading researchers.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/483310"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=40170">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-chemical-engineering-honours">Bachelor of Chemical Engineering (Honours)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 77.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 46,645</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-mathematics">Bachelor of Mathematics<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 77.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 44,650</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-mathematics-advanced">Bachelor of Mathematics (Advanced)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 90.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 43,760</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/computing-maths-and-technology">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Through the program, you will complement your theoretical studies with tutorials and laboratories that apply theory to practical situations. In your final year, you will complete a capstone project, working with industry on a real-world project.</p><p>High achieving students can also apply for our Merit Pathway program. Students work on active research projects and are mentored by leading researchers.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
