UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Work in diverse media and communication industries.</p><p>Develop skills to produce ground-breaking, thought-provoking, and engaging work in today’s complex communication landscape.</p> <p>Course options prepare you to craft stories and create content tailored to different audiences and communication contexts. These include creating content and campaigns for social, radio, podcasting, broadcast, streaming and news platforms. You can tailor your skills for specific areas of interest, including:</p><ul><li>documentary and filmmaking</li><li>podcasting or multiplatform journalism</li><li>social media content creation</li><li>strategic communication campaigns</li><li>political or organisational communication</li><li>health or government communication.</li></ul><p>This program is a creative journey. Gain the skills, creativity and confidence to produce content, tell stories and engage with your audience. Connect with industry networks and thrive in a career in media and communication.</p> <p> <strong> Cutting-edge facilities ? </strong> so you graduate work-ready <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/school/humanities-creative-industries-social-sciences/study-with-hciss/facilities">Find out more</a> </p> <p> <strong> Professional placement </strong> and practical opportunities </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Media and Communication prepares you to work across a wide range of sectors and industries. It also opens pathways for further study and research.</p> <p>Employment outcomes span exciting, dynamic and growing fields across industries around the world such as media, journalism, public relations, advertising and marketing.</p><p>On completion of this degree, you’ll be able to work in roles such as:</p><ul><li>Media / PR / communication consultant</li><li>Foreign affairs and trade officer</li><li>Media production editor</li><li>Campaign manager</li><li>Film or television directors / producers</li><li>Camera operators</li><li>On-screen presenters</li><li>Political speechwriters</li><li>Radio program producers</li><li>Video producer / editor</li><li>Communication manager / coordinator</li><li>Social media manager / coordinator / specialist</li><li>PR / social media account managers</li><li>Public affairs consultant / advisor</li><li>Community relations manager / coordinator</li><li>Press journalists</li><li>Digital media bloggers</li><li>Radio journalists</li><li>Podcasters</li><li>Online journalists</li><li>Marketing communication manager / coordinator</li></ul> <p>93.5% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Communications</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>This degree provides a solid foundation and in-depth understanding of media and communication theory and practice. Depending on your chosen major/s, you could study courses in various sectors of media production, public relations, and news media, including:</p><ul><li>Magazine and broadcast journalism</li><li>Podcasting</li><li>Documentary and drama filmmaking</li><li>Public relations practice</li><li>Corporate communication</li><li>Content creation for social media</li><li>Screenwriting</li></ul><p><strong>The Bachelor of Media and Communication program requires students to successfully complete 240 units, which comprise of:</strong></p><ul><li>80 units of core courses</li><li>One 80 unit Media and Communication major, students may choose from: Media Production, News Media, or Public Relations</li><li>80 units of electives, <em>or</em> a second 80 unit major as part of a Double Major pathway</li></ul><p>For a full list of available major pathway options refer to the <a href="./?external-uuid=40d9c757-4443-4f96-aeb6-062e37fea13c#program-requirements">program requirements in the handbook</a>.</p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARTS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS1004">Creative Collaborations</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1100">Media, Culture and Narrative</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1234</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1234">Media and Communication Concepts</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2000">Digital Media Engagement</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2510</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2510">Global Media Industries</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2600">Audience Participation and Interaction</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3310">Communication and Creativity</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program. Please note: Students studying at PSB Singapore must enrol in ARTS3020.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARTS3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS3020">Professional Career Ready Studio</a></li><li><strong>HASS3010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3010">Professional Career Ready Placement</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">handbook</a>.</p>Media and Communication Majors<p><a href="#">Media Production</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following 20 units of compulsory courses</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 60 units from the following directed course list; 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2016</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2016">Interactive Storytelling</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2035</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2035">Cinematography</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2130">Sound Production</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2180</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2180">Screenwriting</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2700">Create Your Own Business</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2900">Documentary Filmmaking</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3440</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3440">Short Film Production</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3801">Media Production Project</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3999</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3999">Advanced Media Production</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Media Production" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Media Production"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">News Media</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following 20 units of compulsory courses</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 60 units from the following directed course list; 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2280</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2280">Feature Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2320</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2320">News Media</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2470</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2470">Data Storytelling</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3150</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3150">Podcasting</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3333</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3333">Multiplatform Journalism</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3666</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3666">Contemporary Journalism</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3802</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3802">Public Relations and News Media Project</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"News Media"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Public Relations</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following 20 units of compulsory courses</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 60 units from the following directed course list; 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2140</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2140">Principles of Public Relations</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2212</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2212">Activism and Social Change</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2530</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2530">Organisational Communication</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3520</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3520">Political Communication</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3540</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3540">Public Relations Campaigns</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3737</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3737">Social Media Listening and Monitoring</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3802</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3802">Public Relations and News Media Project</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Public Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">handbook</a>.</p>HCISS Majors<p><a href="#">Screen and Cultural Studies</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>SCRN1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN1000">Media Literacy</a></li><li><strong>SCRN1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN1200">Film and Television Studies</a></li><li><strong>SCRN2100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN2100">Popular Music and Culture</a></li><li><strong>SCRN2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN2200">Popular Culture and Society</a></li><li><strong>SCRN2500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN2500">Science Fiction and Fantasy on Screen</a></li><li><strong>SCRN3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN3000">Social Media and Digital Culture</a></li><li><strong>SCRN3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN3100">Peak TV: Texts, Industry, Culture</a></li><li><strong>SCRN3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN3300">Contemporary Cinema: Style, Culture, Story</a></li><li><em>6 additional courses are part of "Screen and Cultural Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Screen and Cultural Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Graphic Design</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses.</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1031</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1031">Visual Abstraction</a></li><li><strong>DESN3900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3900">Major Project</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 50 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 1000 level, 10 units at 2000 level and 20 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1101">Typography</a></li><li><strong>DESN1600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1600">Interaction Design (IxD) Fundamentals</a></li><li><strong>DESN1700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1700">Digital Photography</a></li><li><strong>DESN2011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2011">Design Futures</a></li><li><strong>DESN2221</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2221">Graphic Brand Identities and Spaces</a></li><li><strong>DESN2610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2610">User Interface (UI) Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN2700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2700">Commercial Studio Photography</a></li><li><strong>DESN2804</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2804">Motion Graphic Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3321</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3321">Publication Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3600">Physical Experience (PxD) Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3730</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3730">Transmedia Product and Campaign Design</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Graphic Design" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Graphic Design"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Animation and Illustration</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses.</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1031</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1031">Visual Abstraction</a></li><li><strong>DESN3900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3900">Major Project</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 50 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 1000 level, 10 units at 2000 level and 20 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1200">Drawing Foundations</a></li><li><strong>DESN1331</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1331">Character Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN1601</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1601">Materials and Making</a></li><li><strong>DESN1801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1801">Animation Thinking</a></li><li><strong>DESN2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2060">Scientific Illustration</a></li><li><strong>DESN2801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2801">Animation Process</a></li><li><strong>DESN2804</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2804">Motion Graphic Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3040">Commercial Illustration</a></li><li><strong>DESN3801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3801">Production Studio</a></li><li><strong>DESN3802</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3802">Environment Design</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Animation and Illustration" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Animation and Illustration"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 80 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Media and Communication</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=50003&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=NCLE&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience JJ and Oli''s Bachelor of Media and Communication story 2:54 <p>Check out JJ and Oli''s study journey into a Bachelor of Media and Communication. Using state of the art equipment allows students to gain real experience and become career ready.</p> Blue Heeler Film Festival 1:46 <p>Hear from our students about their work career-ready placement at the Blue Heeler Film Festival.</p> Career-ready placements <p>You will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within your third year of study. Workplace experience is undertaken in your desired career field, including media, journalism, public relations, advertising, marketing, theatre production, musical ensembles, performing arts and visual communications.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle City campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase <a href="/media/viewer?media=904117"></a><a href="/media/viewer?media=904118"></a> <p>Staff gather to see our state of the art production studios </p> <p>UON students work in dedicated production studios to enrich their learning </p> Behind the scenes of a university ad 2:38 <p>See behind the scenes of ''The Courier'' advertisement concept created entirely by staff and students within Creative Industries at the University of Newcastle. Students studying Media Production conceptualised, coordinated and filmed the recruitment ad as a Work Integrated Learning project.</p> Q Building Virtual Campus Tour 2:07 <p>Located in Honeysuckle, Q Building is part of our city precinct providing state-of-the-art facilities for the School of Humanities, Creative Industries and Social Sciences (HCISS) and the Integrated Innovation Network (I2N) Hub.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/483330"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.5</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=50003">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-business">Bachelor of Business<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,540</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-arts">Bachelor of Arts<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 36,450</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Online</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-education-secondary">Bachelor of Education (Secondary)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 41,150</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/creative-industries-and-communication">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>You will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within your third year of study. Workplace experience is undertaken in your desired career field, including media, journalism, public relations, advertising, marketing, theatre production, musical ensembles, performing arts and visual communications.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
