UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Be the scientist behind the fight against cancer.</p><p>Nuclear medicine graduates from the University of Newcastle are highly sought after and typically secure employment quickly. In a field where demand continues to grow, this is not a generalist imaging degree. It is a specialist pathway where diagnostics meets treatment, combining advanced medical imaging, radiopharmaceutical science, and patient-centred care.</p> <p>As a Nuclear Medicine Scientist, you won’t just image disease – you’ll help diagnose and treat cancer using radioactive substances. This will directly improve patient outcomes and give people the best possible chance of living full, healthy lives. You’ll learn how to perform advanced nuclear medicine scans using radiopharmaceuticals, working with specialised equipment to track how these substances move through the body. These techniques allow early detection of disease or injury, and in oncology settings, directly inform treatment decisions. You’ll gain hands-on experience with leading technologies through clinical placements and within our world-class, purpose-built health sciences precinct. This includes nuclear medicine image processing software, a CT laboratory, and the Southern Hemisphere’s largest University-based radiopharmacy laboratory.</p><p>When you graduate, you won’t just be qualified – you’ll be specialised. You’ll have the confidence, competence, and real-world experience required for professional practice as a Nuclear Medicine Scientist, ready to step directly into an essential role in healthcare.</p> <p> <strong> 40+ weeks </strong> clinical placement </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Nuclear Medicine is a highly specialised degree. Our graduates are very employable and highly regarded. Many of our graduates have advanced rapidly in their careers and are now in management roles in Australia and overseas.</p><p>As a graduate you will be qualified to register and work as Nuclear Medical Technologists. You’ll work closely with patients and allied health professionals to diagnose life-threatening diseases such as cancer and help monitor a patient’s health.</p> <p><strong>Some common roles for Nuclear Medicine graduates include:</strong></p><ul><li>Nuclear Medicine Technologist/Scientist</li><li>Sonographer</li><li>MRI technologist</li><li>Medical Imaging sales representative</li><li>Applications specialist</li><li>Radiopharmaceutical development and production</li><li>University lecturer/academic</li><li>Nuclear medicine researcher</li></ul><p>Some roles within nuclear medicine may require further qualifications or experience beyond the degree level.</p> <p>86.4% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024, Undergraduate Health Services and Support</p> <p>86.6% of students rated learning resources positively.</p> <p>Student Experience Survey 2022-2024, undergraduate Health Services</p> Is Nuclear Medicine right for you? <p><a href="https://uninewcastle.questionpro.com.au/a/TakeSurvey?tt=LLPvEnCa%2B5o%3D">Take this short quiz to find out</a></p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You will be able to enrol in a range of radiation science courses including:</p><ul><li>anatomy</li><li>molecular imaging</li><li>nuclear medicine instrumentation and radiopharmacy</li><li>nuclear medicine theory</li><li>patient care</li><li>physiology</li><li>psychology</li><li>research</li></ul> <p>Core</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>HLSC1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC1000">Transition to Health Sciences Education and Practice</a></li><li><strong>HLSC4120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC4120">Research Methodology and Design</a></li><li><strong>HUBS1105</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1105">Musculoskeletal Anatomy</a></li><li><strong>HUBS1401</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1401">Human Bioscience</a></li><li><strong>HUBS2103</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS2103">Neural and Visceral Anatomy</a></li><li><strong>HUBS2203</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS2203">Introductory Pharmacology</a></li><li><strong>INDH2490</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INDH2490">Foundations of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Health</a></li><li><strong>MRSC1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC1010">Medical Radiation Science 1A</a></li><li><strong>MRSC1330</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC1330">Nuclear Medicine Professional Practice 1B</a></li><li><strong>MRSC1350</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC1350">Nuclear Medicine Methods 1</a></li><li><strong>MRSC2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC2300">Nuclear Medicine Methods IIA</a></li><li><strong>MRSC2330</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC2330">Nuclear Medicine Professional Practice 2A</a></li><li><strong>MRSC2350</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC2350">Nuclear Medicine Methods IIB</a></li><li><strong>MRSC2380</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC2380">Nuclear Medicine Professional Practice 2B</a></li><li><strong>MRSC2560</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC2560">Medical Radiation Science Instrumentation 2B</a></li><li><strong>MRSC2600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC2600">Person-Centred Care in Medical Radiation Science</a></li><li><strong>MRSC3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC3020">MRS Cross-Sectional Imaging 1</a></li><li><strong>MRSC3080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC3080">MRS Cross-Sectional Imaging 2</a></li><li><strong>MRSC3305</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC3305">Nuclear Medicine Methods IIIA</a></li><li><strong>MRSC3330</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC3330">Nuclear Medicine Professional Practice 3A</a></li><li><strong>MRSC3355</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC3355">Nuclear Medicine Methods IIIB</a></li><li><strong>MRSC3380</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC3380">Nuclear Medicine Professional Practice 3B</a></li><li><strong>MRSC4040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC4040">MRS Image Interpretation</a></li><li><strong>MRSC4050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC4050">MRS Transition to Practice</a></li><li><strong>MRSC4340A</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC4340A">Nuclear Medicine Professional Practice 4A</a></li><li><strong>MRSC4340B</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC4340B">Nuclear Medicine Professional Practice 4B</a></li><li><strong>PHYS1250</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHYS1250">MRS Physics and Radiation Protection</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2505</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2505">Foundations of Psychology and Sociology for Health Professionals</a></li><li><strong>STAT1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1070">Statistics for the Sciences</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40011">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Graded Honours Stream</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units of electives, AND the following courses to fulfil the requirements of the Graded Honours stream.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>HLSC4310A</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC4310A">Research Project A</a></li><li><strong>HLSC4310B</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC4310B">Research Project B</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Graded Honours Stream"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40011">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Ungraded Honours Stream</a></p><p><strong>Complete MRSC4080 and 20 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the Ungraded Honours Stream.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>MRSC4080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MRSC4080">MRS Advanced and Future Practice</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Ungraded Honours Stream"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40011">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40011">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Medical Radiation Science (Honours) (Nuclear Medicine)</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=40011&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Health Education and Research Building 2:48 <p>Take a quick tour of the Health Education and Research Building, a purpose-built facility that delivers modern teaching and learning for our nursing, midwifery and allied health students, here at our Callaghan campus.</p> Work Integrated Learning <p>All nuclear medicine students complete 40+ weeks of professional practice during their degree. During your placement, you are mentored and supervised by qualified nuclear medicine professionals.</p><p>You may undertake placements in public and private hospitals and practices located in the Hunter Region, NSW, interstate or overseas.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Hear from our students and Program Convenor 2:13 <p>Use advanced imaging technology to improve lives. At the University of Newcastle, we prepare diagnostic radiography students for a dynamic career using advanced imaging technology. Develop essential clinical reasoning and patient management skills and learn how create medical images to diagnose and manage patient health, combining sophisticated technology and medical expertise to save and improve lives.</p> Compare our three medical radiation science programs 3:27 <p>Find out the difference between the Bachelor of Medical Radiation Science (Nuclear Medicine), Bachelor of Medical Radiation Science (Diagnostic Radiography) and Medical Radiation Science (Radiation Therapy) programs to see which degree interests you most.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/483365"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=40011">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-nursing">Bachelor of Nursing<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 70.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 44,210</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-medical-radiation-science-honours-radiation-therapy">Bachelor of Medical Radiation Science (Honours) (Radiation Therapy)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 87.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 43,250</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 6 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-biomedical-science">Bachelor of Biomedical Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 70.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 48,650</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, PSB Singapore</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <a href="/study/health-and-medicine">Explore study area</a> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 208,
