UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Take the leap – pursue your passion for the performing arts</p><p>A career in music and performing arts offers an exciting future within the evolving creative arts industries. This highly flexible combined degree allows you to enhance your skills, discover new opportunities, and fast track your creative career through practical and creative learning.</p> <p>You might develop skills in music theory technology, hone your creative passion and technical skills across performance, songwriting or production.</p><p>Forge your own path by choosing from 20 majors and minors and hundreds of courses in the arts and humanities.</p> <p> <strong> Cutting-edge facilities ? </strong> so you graduate work-ready <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/school/humanities-creative-industries-social-sciences/study-with-hciss/facilities">Find out more</a> </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>This combined program prepares you for a range of careers such as:</p><ul><li>Professional Musician</li><li>Performing Artist</li><li>Theatre Maker</li><li>Composer</li><li>Songwriter</li><li>Music Producer</li></ul> <p>93.5% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Communications</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You will complete a major in Music and Performing Arts, and a major in arts, with the option to complete an Arts minor or complement your degree with elective choices.</p><p><strong>Music and Performing Arts majors:</strong></p><ul><li>Performance</li><li>Songwriting and production</li><li>Performing arts</li></ul>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-music-and-performing-arts">Bachelor of Music and Performing Arts</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-arts">Bachelor of Arts</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Minors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Music and Performing Arts Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARTS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS1004">Creative Collaborations</a></li><li><strong>MUSI1705</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI1705">Foundations in Digital Media</a></li><li><strong>MUSI1731</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI1731">Sound, Music and Texture</a></li><li><strong>MUSI2181</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI2181">Music Culture and Identity</a></li><li><strong>MUSI2701</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI2701">Studio Sessions</a></li><li><strong>MUSI3102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI3102">Researching Australian Music and the Performing Arts</a></li><li><strong>MUSI3442</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI3442">Engaging in the Music Industry</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Music and Performing Arts Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Arts Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>HASS1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS1000">BA Futures</a></li><li><strong>HASS2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS2000">BA Practice</a></li><li><strong>HASS3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3000">BA Project</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Arts Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready Placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARTS3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS3020">Professional Career Ready Studio</a></li><li><strong>HASS3010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3010">Professional Career Ready Placement</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready Placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p>Performing Arts and Music Majors<p><a href="#">Performance</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the following list to fulfil the requirements of this major including 20 units at 1000 level, 20 units at 2000 level, and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>MUSI1260</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI1260">Introduction to Music Theory</a></li><li><strong>MUSI1461</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI1461">Collaborative Music Making 1</a></li><li><strong>MUSI1462</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI1462">Collaborative Music Making 2</a></li><li><strong>MUSI2421</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI2421">Ensemble Performance and Musicianship</a></li><li><strong>MUSI2461</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI2461">Collaborative Music Making 3</a></li><li><strong>MUSI2462</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI2462">Collaborative Music Making 4</a></li><li><strong>MUSI2731</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI2731">Chords, Harmonies and Progressions</a></li><li><strong>MUSI3121</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI3121">Music and Performing Arts Creative Project</a></li><li><strong>MUSI3461</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI3461">Creative Practice Lab</a></li><li><strong>MUSI3602</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI3602">Music Research Studies</a></li><li><strong>MUSI3620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI3620">Music and Health</a></li><li><em>5 additional courses are part of "Performance" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Performance"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Performing Arts</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the following list to fulfil the requirements of this major including 20 units at 1000 level, 20 units at 2000 level, and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>CAPA1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA1001">Creative and Performing Arts 1</a></li><li><strong>CAPA1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA1030">Acting and Performance 1</a></li><li><strong>CAPA2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA2001">Creative and Performing Arts 2</a></li><li><strong>CAPA2410</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA2410">Australian Theatre and Performance</a></li><li><strong>CAPA3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA3001">Creative and Performing Arts 3</a></li><li><strong>MUSI3121</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI3121">Music and Performing Arts Creative Project</a></li><li><strong>MUSI3461</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI3461">Creative Practice Lab</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Performing Arts" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Performing Arts"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Songwriting and Production</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the following list to fulfil the requirements of this major including 20 units at 1000 level, 20 units at 2000 level, and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>MUSI1561</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI1561">Creative Music Studio 1</a></li><li><strong>MUSI1562</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI1562">Creative Music Studio 2</a></li><li><strong>MUSI1901</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI1901">Songwriting</a></li><li><strong>MUSI2561</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI2561">Creative Music Studio 3</a></li><li><strong>MUSI2705</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI2705">Music Recording and Production Techniques</a></li><li><strong>MUSI3121</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI3121">Music and Performing Arts Creative Project</a></li><li><strong>MUSI3501</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI3501">Sonic Alchemy: Explorations in Sound and Visualisation</a></li><li><strong>MUSI3502</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI3502">Music for Games and VR</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Songwriting and Production" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Songwriting and Production"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p>Arts Majors<p><a href="#">English and Writing</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ENGL1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL1000">Introduction to English Literature</a></li><li><strong>ENGL1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL1040">Australian Stories</a></li><li><strong>ENGL1201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL1201">Creative Writing: Introduction</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2000">Literary Theory and Practice</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2005">Mind and Monstrosity: Victorian Novel</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2011">Children''s Literature</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2101">Writing Short Fiction</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2102">Creative Writing: Life Writing</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2104</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2104">Creative Writing: Writing Sci-Fi and Fantasy</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3012">Crime Fiction: Mutations of a Genre</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3302</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3302">The Novel Writing Toolkit</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3304</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3304">Creative Writing: Fiction, Medicine, Psychology</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3665</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3665">Young Adult Literature: Storying the World through Young Adult Voices</a></li><li><em>19 additional courses are part of "English and Writing" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"English and Writing"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">French Studies</a></p><p><strong>French Studies (Beginner Sequence) </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>FREN1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN1100">French Language and Culture Beginners 1 (A0 to A1.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN1200">French Language and Culture Beginners 2 (A1.1 to A1.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN2610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2610">French Language and Culture Elementary 1 (A1.2 to A2.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN2620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2620">French Language and Culture Elementary 2 (A2.1 to A2.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3610">French Language and Culture Intermediate 1 (A2.2 to B1.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3620">French Language and Culture Intermediate 2 (B1.1 to B1.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3702</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3702">Extended French through Translation</a></li><li><strong>HUMA2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUMA2001">Global Experiences</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "French Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p><strong>French Studies (Intermediate Sequence) </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>FREN2610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2610">French Language and Culture Elementary 1 (A1.2 to A2.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN2620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2620">French Language and Culture Elementary 2 (A2.1 to A2.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3610">French Language and Culture Intermediate 1 (A2.2 to B1.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3620">French Language and Culture Intermediate 2 (B1.1 to B1.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3702</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3702">Extended French through Translation</a></li><li><strong>HUMA2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUMA2001">Global Experiences</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "French Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"French Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Global Indigenous Studies</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1110">Blak Australia</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1370</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1370">Community Engagement: Respect and Reciprocity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1390</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1390">Blak Rights and the Fight for Justice</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1420</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1420">Yarning, Media and Futures</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2022</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2022">Aboriginal Cultural Practices</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2243</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2243">Indigenous People and Sustainable Environments</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2245">Aboriginal People and Law</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2330</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2330">Aboriginal Knowledge Systems</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3024">Blak Advocacy: Empowerment and Solidarity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3080">Indigenous Research</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3251</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3251">Global Indigenous Comparative Studies</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3380</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3380">Global Indigenous Human Rights</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3500">Aboriginal Education, Relationships and Responsibilities</a></li><li><em>5 additional courses are part of "Global Indigenous Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Global Indigenous Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">History</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>HIST1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1001">Europe and the World</a></li><li><strong>HIST1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1002">The United States from Civil War to Superpower</a></li><li><strong>HIST1051</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1051">The Australian Experience</a></li><li><strong>HIST1052</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1052">Origin of Controversies</a></li><li><strong>HIST2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2002">Fact or Fiction Reading the Past</a></li><li><strong>HIST2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2006">Australian Underworlds: Histories of Crime in Australia</a></li><li><strong>HIST2253</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2253">Bodies and Brains: Histories of Illness, Disability and Disease</a></li><li><strong>HIST2611</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2611">The Russian Revolution: From the Tsars to Putin</a></li><li><strong>HIST2650</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2650">War and Trauma</a></li><li><strong>HIST3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3008">Global Perspectives on the First World War</a></li><li><strong>HIST3152</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3152">The History of Racism</a></li><li><strong>HIST3201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3201">Power in the Asia Pacific: Conflict and Alliances</a></li><li><strong>HIST3621</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3621">Maps and Dreams: Aboriginal-Colonial Relationships in Australian History</a></li><li><strong>HIST3641</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3641">The Rise of Fascism: From the March on Rome to Hitler s Seizure of Power</a></li><li><strong>HIST3642</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3642">The Downfall of Fascism: The Third Reich, War and Genocide</a></li><li><em>14 additional courses are part of "History" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"History"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Geography and the Environment</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </stron