APN3501</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/JAPN3501">Japanese in Context 3 (A2.2 to B1.1)</a></li><li><strong>JAPN3502</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/JAPN3502">Japanese in Context 4 (B1.1 to B1.2)</a></li><li><em>4 additional courses are part of "Japanese Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Japanese Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Linguistics</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the list for a minor (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and at least 20 units at 2000 or 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>LING1111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING1111">How Languages Work: Linguistics and the Structure of Language</a></li><li><strong>LING1112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING1112">Languages in the World</a></li><li><strong>LING2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING2001">Indigenous languages of Australia and the Pacific</a></li><li><strong>LING2501</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING2501">Cross-cultural Communication</a></li><li><strong>LING2502</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING2502">Issues of Bilingualism and Bilingual Education</a></li><li><strong>LING3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3008">Introduction to Phonology and Morphology</a></li><li><strong>LING3110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3110">Language and Cognition</a></li><li><strong>LING3310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3310">Language and Meaning</a></li><li><strong>LING3350</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3350">Structure of English</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Linguistics" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Linguistics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Performing Arts</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the list for a minor (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 20 units at 2000 or 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>CAPA1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA1001">Creative and Performing Arts 1</a></li><li><strong>CAPA1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA1030">Acting and Performance 1</a></li><li><strong>CAPA2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA2001">Creative and Performing Arts 2</a></li><li><strong>CAPA2410</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA2410">Australian Theatre and Performance</a></li><li><strong>CAPA3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CAPA3001">Creative and Performing Arts 3</a></li><li><strong>MUSI3461</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MUSI3461">Creative Practice Lab</a></li><li><em>5 additional courses are part of "Performing Arts" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Performing Arts"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Psychology Studies</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this minor.</p><ul><li><strong>PSYC1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1010">Psychology Introduction 1</a></li><li><strong>PSYC1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1020">Psychology Introduction 2</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2500">Introduction to Mental Health and Mental Disorders</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 10 units from the list for a minor (at 2000 or 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>PSYC2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2300">Cognitive Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2400">Biological Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2505</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2505">Foundations of Psychology and Sociology for Health Professionals</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2800">Special Topics in Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3000">Advanced Research Methods and Statistics in Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3300">Advanced Cognitive Psychology: Theory and Applications</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3301</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3301">Advanced Perception and Learning in Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3800">Advanced Special Topics in Psychology 2</a></li><li><strong>STAT2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2000">Applied Statistics and Research Methods</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Psychology Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Psychology Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Screen and Cultural Studies</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the list for a minor (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and at least 20 units at 2000 or 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>SCRN1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN1000">Media Literacy</a></li><li><strong>SCRN1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN1200">Film and Television Studies</a></li><li><strong>SCRN2100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN2100">Popular Music and Culture</a></li><li><strong>SCRN2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN2200">Popular Culture and Society</a></li><li><strong>SCRN2500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN2500">Science Fiction and Fantasy on Screen</a></li><li><strong>SCRN3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN3000">Social Media and Digital Culture</a></li><li><strong>SCRN3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN3100">Peak TV: Texts, Industry, Culture</a></li><li><strong>SCRN3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN3300">Contemporary Cinema: Style, Culture, Story</a></li><li><em>6 additional courses are part of "Screen and Cultural Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Screen and Cultural Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Sociology and Anthropology</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this minor.</p><ul><li><strong>SOCA1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1010">Society and Culture: an Introduction to Sociology</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1020">What is Anthropology</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2200">Social Analysis: Theorising Social Problems</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 10 units from the list for a minor (at 2000 or 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>SCRN2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN2200">Popular Culture and Society</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2065">Environment and Society</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2400">Future Societies: Beyond Capitalist Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2700">Gender, Religion and Power</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3178</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3178">Health, ''Wellness'' and Power: The Social Contexts of Expert Knowledge</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3220">Youth Culture and Risk</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3666</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3666">Consumption, Technology and Everyday Life</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3780</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3780">Leading Social Change: Applying Critical Theories in Critical Times</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3790</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3790">Mobilities, Migration and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3850</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3850">Rage Against the Machine: Indigenous Activism, Ways of Life and the Future</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2300">Ethics for the Social Sciences</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a></li><li><strong>SOCS3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS3100">Policy Development, Program Management and Evaluation</a></li><li><em>6 additional courses are part of "Sociology and Anthropology" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Sociology and Anthropology"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Studies of Philosophy, Religion and Ethics</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the list for a minor (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and at least 20 units at 2000 or 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>PHIL1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHIL1040">World Religions</a></li><li><strong>PHIL1042</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHIL1042">Religion, Science and Popular Beliefs</a></li><li><strong>PHIL1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHIL1090">Ethics of Emerging Technologies</a></li><li><strong>PHIL2040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHIL2040">Philosophy of Relationships</a></li><li><strong>PHIL2041</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHIL2041">Democracy and Diversity</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2700">Gender, Religion and Power</a></li><li><em>4 additional courses are part of "Studies of Philosophy, Religion and Ethics" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Studies of Philosophy, Religion and Ethics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Violence Studies</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this minor (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and at least 20 units at 2000 level or 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a></li><li><strong>HIST2253</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2253">Bodies and Brains: Histories of Illness, Disability and Disease</a></li><li><strong>HIST2611</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2611">The Russian Revolution: From the Tsars to Putin</a></li><li><strong>HIST2650</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2650">War and Trauma</a></li><li><strong>HIST3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3008">Global Perspectives on the First World War</a></li><li><strong>HIST3621</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3621">Maps and Dreams: Aboriginal-Colonial Relationships in Australian History</a></li><li><strong>HIST3641</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3641">The Rise of Fascism: From the March on Rome to Hitler s Seizure of Power</a></li><li><strong>HIST3642</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3642">The Downfall of Fascism: The Third Reich, War and Genocide</a></li><li><strong>HUSE2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUSE2002">Child Protection Work</a></li><li><strong>HUSE2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUSE2005">Gendered Violence</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1050">Youth, Gender and Crime</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3850</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3850">Rage Against the Machine: Indigenous Activism, Ways of Life and the Future</a></li><li><em>8 additional courses are part of "Violence Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Violence Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Writing Studies</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this minor (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and at least 20 units at 2000 level or 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>ENGL1201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL1201">Creative Writing: Introduction</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2101">Writing Short Fiction</a></li><li><strong>ENGL2102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL2102">Creative Writing: Life Writing</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3302</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3302">The Novel Writing Toolkit</a></li><li><strong>ENGL3304</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENGL3304">Creative Writing: Fiction, Medicine, Psychology</a></li><li><em>4 additional courses are part of "Writing Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Writing Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 50 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40311">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Music and Performing Arts / Bachelor of Arts</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=40311&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=NCLE&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Creating meaningful opportunities for students 0:44 <p>At the University of Newcastle, we embed practical, hands-on learning in all our degrees. Check out just some of the opportunities our students have had to build their experience.</p> Career-ready placements <p>You will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within your third year of study that will enable you to apply knowledge developed throughout your studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support your career readiness. You will undertake workplace experience in your desired career field, including media, theatre production, musical ensembles, performing arts and visual communications.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle City campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Bachelor of Music and Performing Arts - Introduction and Audition Process 10:33 <p>Do you have questions about applying for the Bachelor of Music and Performing Arts at The University of Newcastle? Some of our academic staff provide an introduction to the degree and share some helpful tips for the application process</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/489813">Apply via UAC</a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=40311">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-education-secondary">Bachelor of Education (Secondary)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 41,150</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-media-and-communication">Bachelor of Media and Communication<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 38,815</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-arts">Bachelor of Arts<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 36,450</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Online</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/creative-industries-and-communication">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>You will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within your third year of study that will enable you to apply knowledge developed throughout your studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support your career readiness. You will undertake workplace experience in your desired career field, including media, theatre production, musical ensembles, performing arts and visual communications.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
