UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Become the nurse your community needs</p><p>Study nursing and gain the skills and experience to deliver high-quality care to individuals, families, and communities. At the University of Newcastle, you’ll study in a supportive environment, with guaranteed clinical placements and dedicated guidance to help you complete your 800 hours on time.</p> <p>Throughout your degree, you’ll learn in diverse and dynamic clinical environments. Your professional placements will take you into medical–surgical units, acute care settings, aged care facilities and rural health services. You’ll build confidence in our advanced on- campus simulation laboratories. These are designed to replicate real-world clinical scenarios in a safe and supportive setting.</p><p>You’ll study in one of Australia’s most diverse regional health districts. Strong employment prospects and less competition than metropolitan areas create a clear pathway to securing a meaningful career.</p><p>Whether you’re starting out or changing careers, the Bachelor of Nursing prepares you for a future-proof profession. We offer flexible study options, immersive learning experiences, and connections to health services across the Hunter New England and Central Coast regions. Graduate ready to meet the needs of your community and thrive in a career that truly matters.</p> <p> <strong> World top 100 ? </strong> for Nursing </p> <p> <strong> ANMAC ? </strong> accredited degree </p> <p> <strong> 800 hours </strong> of clinical placement for Bachelor of Nursing </p> <p> <strong> Commonwealth Prac Payment available ? </strong> to eligible students while completing mandatory placement <a href="https://www.education.gov.au/higher-education/commonwealth-prac-payment">Find out more</a> </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Graduates are eligible to apply for registration with the Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia and practice as Registered Nurses in Australia as well as in many overseas countries.</p> <p>On completion of this degree, you’ll be able to work as a Nurse in roles such as:</p><ul><li>Clinical nurse specialist</li><li>Clinical nurse consultant</li><li>Nurse educator</li><li>Nurse manager</li><li>Nurse researcher</li></ul> <p>90.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024, undergraduate Nursing &amp; Midwifery</p> <p>$68,900 median starting salary.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024, undergraduate Nursing and Midwifery</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You will have the opportunity to engage in a diverse range of health and medical courses that combine theoretical knowledge with practical experience. Learning is supported through hands-on training in clinical laboratories and a variety of professional placement settings. Your studies will cover key areas such as:</p><ul><li>Lifespan approach</li><li>Bioscience</li><li>Pharmacology</li><li>Older people</li><li>Community health</li><li>Acute care</li><li>Medical and surgical nursing</li><li>Mental health</li><li>Indigenous health</li><li>Health promotion and education</li><li>Child and adolescent health</li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>HUBS1406</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1406">Human Bioscience for Nursing and Midwifery</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HUBS1416</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1416">Advanced Human Bioscience</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HUBS2203</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS2203">Introductory Pharmacology</a> (Online, Singapore)</li><li><strong>INDH2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INDH2000">Foundations of Nursing Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>NURS1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS1001">Introduction to the Profession of Nursing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>NURS1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS1002">Essentials of Professional Communication</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>NURS1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS1003">Professional Experience 1</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>NURS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS1004">Evidence for Nursing Practice</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>NURS1005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS1005">Essentials of Caring for the Older Person</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>NURS1006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS1006">Professional Experience 2</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>NURS2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS2001">Essentials of Surgical Nursing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>NURS2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS2003">Professional Experience 3</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>NURS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS2004">Essentials of Medical Nursing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>NURS2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS2005">Essentials of Health Promotion</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>NURS2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS2006">Professional Experience 4</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>NURS2103</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS2103">Essentials of Mental Health Nursing</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>NURS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS3001">Essentials of Nursing the Deteriorating Person</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>NURS3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS3002">Essentials of Palliative Care</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>NURS3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS3003">Professional Experience 5</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>NURS3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS3004">Essentials of Chronic Illness and Disability</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>NURS3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS3005">Transition to Professional Nursing</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>NURS3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/NURS3006">Professional Experience 6</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40298">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40298">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40298">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Nursing</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=40298&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p>As a commencing student in this degree, you may be eligible for the new Tertiary Health Study Subsidy. You could secure up to $12,000 to support your health studies. To learn more and submit your application visit NSW Health.</p> <p><a href="https://www.health.nsw.gov.au/studysubsidies">NSW Health</a></p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Nursing at the Central Coast Clinical School 2:39 <p>Check out our facilities at the Central Coast Clinical School and hear from our Bachelor of Nursing students, Emma and Hannah.</p> Work Integrated Learning <p>Our Bachelor of Nursing students are required to complete 800 hours of clinical experience. During your clinical placements, you’ll gain valuable hands-on experience in a range of health facility locations across NSW.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Our industry partners Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Studying at Central Coast campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/central-coast/living-on-the-central-coast"> Living on the Central Coast <p>The Central Coast offers a relaxed and convenient lifestyle with access to beautiful beaches and national parks. Our campuses have industry-leading facilities all within beautiful bushland.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Student highlights <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2026/skye-walters"> <p>Student</p> Balancing family and dreams of a career in nursing <p>First-in-family student Skye is turning her passion for nursing into a career, balancing family life and university with purpose.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2024/martha-neema-bukulu"> <p>Student</p> Inspiring future generations through nursing excellence <p>Martha was immediately drawn to the institution''s reputation and offerings.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2024/krishna-prasad-paudel"> <p>Student</p> Clinical confidence meets coastal bliss <p>Driven by his passion for nursing, Krishna navigates Newcastle''s academic landscape, finding purpose in every clinical placement and coastal sunset.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2023/anusha-timalsina"> <p>Student</p> Studying as an international student in Nursing <p>Anusha, an international student from Nepal, reflects on some of the highlights from her Bachelor of Nursing. Achieving her career goal, she hopes to continue studying to support those who need it most.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2022/xiuli-weng"> <p>Student</p> Support services to succeed <p>Xiuli has been studying her Bachelor of Nursing while taking advantage of student support services offered to students for academic and personal benefit. Read how these services have helped her become more confident.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Excellence in caring 2:33 <p>Hear from our Head of School and Dean of Nursing and Midwifery, Professor Amanda Johnson, and meet Sindi Ford, Bachelor of Nursing student.</p> Meet Connar 2:20 Nursing Lab Tour, Callaghan Campus 1:17 How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p>School leavers may be eligible for admission under the <strong>School Based Traineeship (SBT)</strong> pathway.</p><p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry/entry-options/school-based-traineeship">Find out more</a></p> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/483600"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=40298">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-midwifery">Bachelor of Midwifery<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 82.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> undefined</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 6 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-podiatric-medicine">Bachelor of Podiatric Medicine<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 77.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 46,685</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 6 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Central Coast</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-occupational-therapy-honours">Bachelor of Occupational Therapy (Honours)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 90.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 43,885</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 6 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <a href="/study/health-and-medicine">Explore study area</a> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p>',
