UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Become a future ready pharmacist.</p><p>Pharmacy is more than dispensing medicines. Today’s pharmacists are frontline healthcare professionals with strong long-term career prospects. They play a vital role in improving medication safety, improving patient outcomes, and supporting community health.</p> <p>Throughout your studies, you’ll work directly with patients, healthcare teams, and communities. You’ll learn to counsel people on the safe and effective use of medicines, help manage chronic disease, provide advice on common health conditions, and contribute to preventative care.</p><p>Learning in a fully equipped demonstration pharmacy will help you build practical, hands-on skills in dispensing, preparing, and reviewing medicines, while also establishing a strong foundation in biomedical and pharmaceutical sciences. Extensive placements and hands‑on learning will ensure you are well prepared to make a meaningful contribution in real healthcare settings.</p><p>As a pharmacist, you’ll be equipped to adapt to evolving healthcare models, with skills that remain relevant as the profession continues to expand in scope and impact. You’ll contribute to a healthier society by educating and empowering people to use medicines safely and effectively, making a meaningful difference to patient care every day.</p> <p> <strong> 88.3% ? </strong> rated learning resources positively </p> <p> <strong> 82.70 ? </strong> rated teaching quality positively </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>As a qualified pharmacist, you can choose from a range of interesting and rewarding career options.</p> <p><strong>Professional outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>Researcher</li><li>Consultant/accredited pharmacist</li><li>Clinical research coordinator</li><li>Diabetes educator</li><li>GP pharmacist</li><li>Aged-care pharmacist</li></ul> <p>88.3% of students rated learning resources positively.</p> <p>Student Experience Survey 2022-2024, undergraduate Pharmacy</p> <p>100% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcome Survey, 2021-2023, undergraduate Pharmacy</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You''ll gain theoretical knowledge in biomedical, pharmaceutical sciences and pharmacotherapeutics. You will also have plenty of opportunities to develop your skills through hands-on professional placements. Areas of study include:</p><ul><li>Anatomy and physiology</li><li>Dosage design and formulation</li><li>Chemistry</li><li>Drug design and discovery</li><li>Mental health first aid</li><li>Pharmacotherapeutics</li><li>Pharmacy practice</li><li>Epidemiology</li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHEM1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1010">Introductory Chemistry I</a></li><li><strong>CHEM1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1020">Introductory Chemistry II</a></li><li><strong>HUBS1202</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1202">Human Genomics and Biomolecular Analysis</a></li><li><strong>HUBS1403</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1403">Biomedical Science Part 1</a></li><li><strong>HUBS1404</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1404">Biomedical Science Part 2</a></li><li><strong>HUBS2206</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS2206">Human Biochemistry and Cell Biology</a></li><li><strong>HUBS2407</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS2407">Experimental and Clinical Design in Medical Research</a></li><li><strong>HUBS2601</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS2601">Human Infection and Immunity</a></li><li><strong>PHAR1101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR1101">Introduction to Pharmacy and Formulation Sciences</a></li><li><strong>PHAR1201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR1201">Introduction to Formulation Sciences</a></li><li><strong>PHAR2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR2101">Dermatology and Topical Formulations</a></li><li><strong>PHAR2102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR2102">Cardiovascular and Renal Health</a></li><li><strong>PHAR2103</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR2103">Introductory Clinical Pharmacotherapy</a></li><li><strong>PHAR2202</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR2202">Drug Design and Analytical Methods</a></li><li><strong>PHAR2203</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR2203">Gastrointestinal Health and Solid Dosage Formulations</a></li><li><strong>PHAR2204</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR2204">Clinical Pharmacotherapy 1</a></li><li><strong>PHAR3101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR3101">Endocrinology and Injectable Dosage Formulations</a></li><li><strong>PHAR3102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR3102">Eyes, Ears, Nose and Throat Health, Respiratory Health and Related Formulations</a></li><li><strong>PHAR3103</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR3103">Mental and Neurological Health</a></li><li><strong>PHAR3104</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR3104">Clinical Pharmacotherapy 2</a></li><li><strong>PHAR3201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR3201">Genitourinary and Reproductive Health and Dosage Formulations</a></li><li><strong>PHAR3202</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR3202">Rheumatology and Pain Management</a></li><li><strong>PHAR3203</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR3203">Clinical Pharmacotherapy 3</a></li><li><strong>PHAR4101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR4101">Cancer, Critical Care and Palliation</a></li><li><strong>PHAR4102A</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR4102A">Transition to Professional Practice in Pharmacy (Part A)</a></li><li><strong>PHAR4102B</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR4102B">Transition to Professional Practice in Pharmacy (Part B)</a></li><li><strong>PHAR4104A</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR4104A">Pharmacy Projects (Part A)</a></li><li><strong>PHAR4104B</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR4104B">Pharmacy Projects (Part B)</a></li><li><strong>PHAR4201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR4201">Pharmacogenomics and Health Technology Assessment</a></li><li><strong>PHAR4204</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHAR4204">Clinical Leadership in Health Care</a></li><li><strong>STAT1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1070">Statistics for the Sciences</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12328">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12328">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12328">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Pharmacy (Honours)</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=12328&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p>As a commencing student in this degree, you may be eligible for the new Tertiary Health Study Subsidy. You could secure up to $12,000 to support your health studies. To learn more and submit your application visit NSW Health.</p> <p><a href="https://www.health.nsw.gov.au/studysubsidies">NSW Health</a></p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Creating meaningful opportunities for students 0:44 <p>At the University of Newcastle, we embed practical, hands-on learning in all our degrees. Check out just some of the opportunities our students have had to build their experience.</p> Career-ready placements <p>All University of Newcastle pharmacy students complete more than 420 hours of professional practice during their degree, starting in their first year. During your placement, you are mentored and supervised by qualified pharmacy educators.</p><p>You can undertake your placement in a variety of settings locally and nationally.</p><p>To prepare you for your clinical placements, you will build practical skills in our fully functioning demonstration pharmacy.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase The Bachelor of Pharmacy Program 2:01 <p>Learn about the program hearing first hand from current students studying the Bachelor of Pharmacy (Honours).</p> Meet Bryan 2:02 <p>Hear about Bryan’s experience studying the Bachelor of Pharmacy (Honours).</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/483800"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=12328">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-biomedical-science">Bachelor of Biomedical Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 70.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 48,650</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, PSB Singapore</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-nursing">Bachelor of Nursing<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 70.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 44,210</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-medical-radiation-science-honours-diagnostic-radiography">Bachelor of Medical Radiation Science (Honours) (Diagnostic Radiography)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 94.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 43,250</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 6 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <a href="/study/health-and-medicine">Explore study area</a> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://www.pharmacycouncil.org.au/"></a><p>This program is accredited by the Australian Pharmacy Council and approved by the Pharmacy Board of Australia.</p><a href="https://www.pharmacyboard.gov.au/"></a><p>Graduates of the program are eligible to apply for provisional registration with the Pharmacy Board of Australia in partnership with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA).</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>All University of Newcastle pharmacy students complete more than 420 hours of professional practice during their degree, starting in their first year. During your placement, you are mentored and supervised by qualified pharmacy educators.</p><p>You can undertake your placement in a variety of settings locally and nationally.</p><p>To prepare you for your clinical placements, you will build practical skills in our fully functioning demonstration pharmacy.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
