UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Physiotherapists work across many health settings and complex clinical problems. These involve musculoskeletal, neurological or cardiorespiratory systems.</p> <p>This program integrates the clinical and basic sciences, focusing on evidence-based physiotherapy practice. The program involves case-based learning with a strong inter-disciplinary focus. Gain hands-on experience through clinical placements and interactive teamwork activities. Learn exceptional communication and interpersonal skills needed to work one on one with patients.</p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Graduates work as physiotherapists in public and private practice, and hospital settings.</p> <p><strong>Professional outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>Registered Physiotherapist, specializations include; Cardiorespiratory, Continence and Women’s Health Rehabilitation/Injury Management, Gerontology, Hand Therapist, Musculoskeletal, Neurology, Occupational Health, Paediatrics, Sports</li><li>Health Promotion Officer</li><li>Rehabilitation Consultant</li><li>Research Scientist</li><li>University Lecturer/Academic</li></ul> <p>95.5% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduates Outcome Survey 2022-2024, undergraduate Rehabilitation</p> <p>91.5% of students rated learning resources positively.</p> <p>Student Experience Survey 2022-2024, undergraduate Rehabilitation</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Your physiotherapy studies will teach you theoretical knowledge in biomedical and behavioural sciences. You will also have plenty of opportunities to hone your skills through hands-on professional placements. You will study courses in areas such as:</p><ul><li>Advanced anatomy</li><li>Clinical physiotherapy</li><li>Community health</li><li>Health promotion</li><li>Physiology and pathophysiology</li><li>Statistics and research methodology</li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>HLSC1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC1000">Transition to Health Sciences Education and Practice</a></li><li><strong>HLSC4120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC4120">Research Methodology and Design</a></li><li><strong>HUBS1105</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1105">Musculoskeletal Anatomy</a></li><li><strong>HUBS1403</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1403">Biomedical Science Part 1</a></li><li><strong>HUBS1404</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1404">Biomedical Science Part 2</a></li><li><strong>HUBS2103</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS2103">Neural and Visceral Anatomy</a></li><li><strong>HUBS2503</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS2503">Clinical Exercise Physiology</a></li><li><strong>HUBS2505</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS2505">Human Pathophysiology</a></li><li><strong>INDH2490</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INDH2490">Foundations of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Health</a></li><li><strong>PHTY1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY1020">Physiotherapy II</a></li><li><strong>PHTY1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY1040">Introduction to Physiotherapy</a></li><li><strong>PHTY2020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY2020">Musculoskeletal Physiotherapy I</a></li><li><strong>PHTY2030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY2030">Neurological Physiotherapy I</a></li><li><strong>PHTY2040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY2040">Cardiopulmonary Physiotherapy I</a></li><li><strong>PHTY2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY2060">Physiotherapy Clinical Practice I</a></li><li><strong>PHTY3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY3020">Cardiopulmonary Physiotherapy II</a></li><li><strong>PHTY3070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY3070">Advanced Neurological Physiotherapy</a></li><li><strong>PHTY3080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY3080">Physiotherapy Through Life Stages</a></li><li><strong>PHTY3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY3090">Advanced Musculoskeletal Physiotherapy</a></li><li><strong>PHTY3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY3100">Critical Thinking in Musculoskeletal Physiotherapy</a></li><li><strong>PHTY4010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY4010">Clinical Practice in Physiotherapy II</a></li><li><strong>PHTY4090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY4090">Transition to Professional Practice</a></li><li><strong>PHTY4100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY4100">Clinical Practice in Physiotherapy III</a></li><li><strong>PUBH1080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PUBH1080">Studies in Population Health and Health Promotion</a></li><li><strong>STAT1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1070">Statistics for the Sciences</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12337">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Ungraded Honours</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following courses to fulfil the requirements of this option.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>PHTY4070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY4070">Advanced Concepts in Evidence-based Physiotherapy Practice</a></li><li><strong>PHTY4080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHTY4080">Advanced Concepts in Physiotherapy Practice</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Ungraded Honours"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12337">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Graded Honours</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following courses to fulfil the requirements of this option.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>HLSC4310A</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC4310A">Research Project A</a></li><li><strong>HLSC4310B</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC4310B">Research Project B</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Graded Honours"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12337">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12337">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12337">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Physiotherapy (Honours)</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=12337&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p>As a commencing student in this degree, you may be eligible for the new Tertiary Health Study Subsidy. You could secure up to $12,000 to support your health studies. To learn more and submit your application visit NSW Health.</p> <p><a href="https://www.health.nsw.gov.au/studysubsidies">NSW Health</a></p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Health Education and Research Building 2:48 <p>Take a quick tour of the Health Education and Research Building, a purpose-built facility that delivers modern teaching and learning for our nursing, midwifery and allied health students, here at our Callaghan campus.</p> Career-ready placements <p>All students complete professional placement during their degree. During your placement, you are mentored and supervised by qualified physiotherapy professionals.</p><p>You can undertake your placement in a variety of settings, both locally and nationally, including mandatory rural placements.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Celebrating 20 Years of Physiotherapy at the University of Newcastle 5:12 <p>We are proud of the achievements of our Physiotherapy students, graduates and staff who are making valuable contributions to the health and wellbeing of their local and global communities.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/483850">Apply via UAC</a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=12337">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-occupational-therapy-honours">Bachelor of Occupational Therapy (Honours)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 90.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 43,885</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 6 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-medical-radiation-science-honours-diagnostic-radiography">Bachelor of Medical Radiation Science (Honours) (Diagnostic Radiography)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 94.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 43,250</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 6 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-medical-science-doctor-of-medicine-joint-medical-program">Bachelor of Medical Science and Doctor of Medicine (Joint Medical Program)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> N/A (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 92,695</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 5 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 5 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <a href="/study/health-and-medicine">Explore study area</a> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://physiocouncil.com.au/"></a><p>This program is accredited by the Australian Physiotherapy Council.</p><a href="https://www.ahpra.gov.au/"></a><p>Graduates of this program are eligible to apply for registration with the Physiotherapy Board of Australia in partnership with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA).</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>All students complete professional placement during their degree. During your placement, you are mentored and supervised by qualified physiotherapy professionals.</p><p>You can undertake your placement in a variety of settings, both locally and nationally, including mandatory rural placements.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
