UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Help people stay mobile, independent, and pain‑free. </p><p>Enter a high-demand podiatry career identified as a national skills shortage, where industry-informed training and strong clinical networks ensure you graduate job-ready with the skills employers are actively seeking.</p> <p>The Bachelor of Podiatric Medicine is a four‑year degree designed to build strong clinical confidence through extensive, hands‑on experience. Guided by experienced podiatrists, you’ll develop practical, patient‑facing skills in diagnosing, treating, and preventing foot and lower limb conditions. You’ll also help prevent related issues such as back and joint pain caused by changes in posture, walking, and running. Specialist clinic areas include sports injuries, biomechanics, paediatrics, surgery, and more.</p><p>You’ll also have the opportunity to apply for the endorsed scheduled medicines pathway. This will prepare you for advanced clinical responsibilities, including administering medicines as part of patient care.</p><p>We offer a guaranteed entry pathway into this degree for those who have completed the <a href="https://training.gov.au/training/details/HLT43021/qualdetails">HLT43021 Certificate IV in Allied Health Assistance</a> course. For more information, visit <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/getting-in/entry-schemes/guaranteed-entry">Guaranteed Entry</a>.</p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>On completion of this degree, you’ll be able to work in a range of health environments, such as general or specialised podiatry practice (e.g sports podiatry), private and public practices, hospitals, rehabilitation and community health centres, sports clinics, research centres and consultancy.</p> <p>86.4% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcome Survey 2022-2024, undergraduate Health Services and Support</p> <p>89.7% of students rated learning resources positively.</p> <p>Student Experience Survey 2022-2024, undergraduate Health Services and Support</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>The Bachelor of Podiatric Medicine includes an option for scheduled medicines.</p><p>Students taking the option for scheduled medicine will take part in a special clinical program in year 4 designed to develop skills for registration with the Podiatry Board of Australia.</p><p><strong>As part of your studies you will:</strong></p><ul><li>Learn how to identify and analyse complex health problems within podiatry practice and develop solutions to these problems.</li><li>Learn to work within a multidisciplinary health team to best meet patients’ health needs.</li><li>Undertake rural and regional health placements at our podiatry clinics.</li><li>Develop critical research skills that will set you in good stead for life-long learning as a podiatrist.</li></ul><p>There is an option for high-achieving students to embed honours-level research courses over the final 1.5 years of the program. If this option is something you would be interested in, please discuss this with your academics/supervisors in the program. <a href="./?external-uuid=7bb6377a-1b5e-42db-a50c-cef0012c6257">For more information visit here</a>.</p> <p>Core</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>EXSS2020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS2020">Biomechanics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HLSC1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC1000">Transition to Health Sciences Education and Practice</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HLSC4120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC4120">Research Methodology and Design</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>HUBS1108</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1108">Fundamentals of Human Anatomy</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HUBS1403</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1403">Biomedical Science Part 1</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>HUBS1404</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1404">Biomedical Science Part 2</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>HUBS1420</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1420">Professional and Communication Skills in Biomedicine</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>HUBS2203</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS2203">Introductory Pharmacology</a> (Online, Singapore)</li><li><strong>HUBS2505</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS2505">Human Pathophysiology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>INDH2490</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INDH2490">Foundations of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Health</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>PDTY1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PDTY1003">Introduction to Podiatry</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PDTY2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PDTY2003">Musculoskeletal Disorders and Imaging</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>PDTY2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PDTY2005">Pathomechanics and Podiatric Medicine</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>PDTY2007</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PDTY2007">Podiatry Pre-Clinical</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>PDTY3023</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PDTY3023">Evidence in Professional Reasoning for Podiatric Medicine</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>PDTY3028</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PDTY3028">Podiatric Practice 1</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>PDTY3029</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PDTY3029">Podiatric Practice 2</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>PDTY3030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PDTY3030">Podiatric Surgery</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>PDTY3037</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PDTY3037">Pharmacology for Podiatrists</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>PDTY3052</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PDTY3052">Prescribing Theory and Application for Podiatrists</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>PDTY4021</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PDTY4021">The High Risk Foot</a> (Central Coast)</li><li><strong>PSYC2505</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2505">Foundations of Psychology and Sociology for Health Professionals</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>PUBH1080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PUBH1080">Studies in Population Health and Health Promotion</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><em>5 additional courses are part of "Core Courses" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50021">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50021">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Clinical Block Option</a></p><p><strong>Students may complete either PDTY4016 Podiatry Clinical Block or PDTY4036 Podiatry Clinical Block with Endorsed Prescribers to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><p>2 courses are part of "Clinical Block Option" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50021">handbook</a>.</p><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Clinical Block Option"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50021">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 20 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50021">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50021">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Podiatric Medicine</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=50021&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p>As a commencing student in this degree, you may be eligible for the new Tertiary Health Study Subsidy. You could secure up to $12,000 to support your health studies. To learn more and submit your application visit NSW Health.</p> <p><a href="https://www.health.nsw.gov.au/studysubsidies">NSW Health</a></p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Career-ready placements <p>Students complete more than 1,000 hours of practical experience during their second, third and fourth year of studies which will help them to become ‘life ready graduates’. The program strongly supports students with multidisciplinary experiences that will help the transition into the workforce. Work alongside experienced podiatrists in the University of Newcastle Student Podiatry Clinic''s located at Wyong Hospital and Newcastle Community Health Service (Hunter Street). Students also partake in external placements in rural and regional areas. Our graduates are highly sought-after with the experience and knowledge they gain during their studies.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Find out more</a> </p> Our industry partners Studying at Central Coast campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/central-coast/living-on-the-central-coast"> Living on the Central Coast <p>The Central Coast offers a relaxed and convenient lifestyle with access to beautiful beaches and national parks. Our campuses have industry-leading facilities all within beautiful bushland.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2025/blake-withers"> <p>Student</p> A passion to keep people moving drove Blake to study podiatry <p>Blake Withers passion to keep people moving drove him to study Podiatry at the University of Newcastle and forge his career in the industry.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2025/kristen-stone"> <p>Student</p> From Classroom to Clinic: Kristen''s Journey from Education to Podiatry <p>From classroom to clinic: hear from podiatry graduate, Kristen Stone, and her unique journey from education to podiatry.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2024/hazel-chua"> <p>Student</p> Transforming a passion for healthcare into a career in podiatry <p>Working at a public hospital in Singapore as a professional podiatrist, alumna Hazel Chua believes that the University of Newcastle equipped her with the tools, knowledge and experience needed to thrive in her profession.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <p>Video</p> A heart-saving check-up 2:02 <p>Peter reckons his chance visit to our Podiatry Teaching Clinic at Gosford Hospital was like winning the “medical lottery”. After hearing about the clinic on ABC radio, Peter made an appointment with Victoria Bennett, now a podiatrist practising in Canberra but then a student in the final weeks of her degree. What Victoria found would result in Peter undergoing a life-saving quadruple heart bypass.</p> <p>Video</p> Meet Angus 2:31 <p>Hear about Angus’ experience studying the Bachelor of Podiatric Medicine at the University of Newcastle.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/483905"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=50021">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-exercise-and-sport-science">Bachelor of Exercise and Sport Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 72.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 44,000</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-oral-health-therapy">Bachelor of Oral Health Therapy<p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <a href="undergraduate">View combined degrees</a> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Students complete more than 1,000 hours of practical experience during their second, third and fourth year of studies which will help them to become ‘life ready graduates’. The program strongly supports students with multidisciplinary experiences that will help the transition into the workforce. Work alongside experienced podiatrists in the University of Newcastle Student Podiatry Clinic''s located at Wyong Hospital and Newcastle Community Health Service (Hunter Street). Students also partake in external placements in rural and regional areas. Our graduates are highly sought-after with the experience and knowledge they gain during their studies.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Find out more</a> </p>',
