UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Using science to understand how people think, feel and behave</p><p>This program is for those interested in understanding people through science. Build new knowledge and explore how psychology applies to real-world situations using a range of scientific methods.</p> <p>You’ll cover areas such as mental health, brain function, development, memory and decision making, building a broad foundation in psychology.</p><p>Undertake pre-professional courses each year, with opportunities to engage in problem-based learning and hear from practising psychologists, helping you develop a well-rounded understanding of the field.</p><p>This evolving field can lead to a wide range of career opportunities where you can apply your skills to make a positive impact.</p><p><strong>Concurrent Enrolment</strong></p><p>Psychological Science students are encouraged to consider concurrent enrolment in the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-applied-data-science">Bachelor of Applied Data Science program.</a></p><p>Psychological Science explores the complexities of human thought, emotion, and behaviour. By pairing it with a Bachelor of Applied Data Science, students gain the ability to analyse behavioural data using advanced statistical and computational tools, design smarter research studies with robust data collection, and visualise and communicate insights more confidently.</p><p>Complete both programs in only one extra year of study and graduate with two degrees, increasing your in-demand skills and employability in areas such as health and clinical analytics, UX and human-centred design, organisational psychology and social research.</p> <p> <strong> World top 250 ? </strong> for Psychology </p> <p> <strong> APAC ? </strong> accredited degree </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>This degree can be applied in a broad range of industry sectors, enabling you to choose the career path that’s right for you.</p><p>Psychology graduates work in research, human resources and leadership, management, intelligence agencies, advertising, marketing and sales, public health, community services, project management, counselling, law and correctional services.</p> <p>Postgraduate pathways available for graduates who also complete the Bachelor of Psychological Science (Honours) degree include the research and Clinical PhD, Master of Clinical Psychology, Master of Professional Psychology, Master of Business Psychology, Master of Workplace Mental Health and Wellbeing and other psychology-related programs.</p><p>To practice as a psychologist, you must complete additional accredited postgraduate studies.</p><p><strong>Professional outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>careers counsellor</li><li>caseworker</li><li>juvenile justice officer</li><li>market researcher</li><li>mediator</li><li>practising psychologist (with further study)</li></ul> <p>87.6% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Psychology</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>This degree covers all the requirements of an APAC accredited undergraduate degree in Psychology, including a wide range of subject areas. Throughout your psychology degree you will learn about:</p><ul><li>psychological research methodology</li><li>statistics</li><li>cognition and information processing</li><li>social psychology and personality</li><li>clinical and abnormal behaviour</li><li>neuroscience</li><li>psychopharmacology</li><li>perceptual processes</li><li>learning theory</li><li>developmental psychology</li></ul><p>Combine your Psychology program with another degree to extend your learning and career pathway opportunities. Combined degree options include:</p><ul><li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-psychological-science-business">Bachelor of Psychological Science / Bachelor of Business</a></li><li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-psychological-science-laws-honours">Bachelor of Psychological Science / Bachelor of Laws (Honours)</a></li><li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-psychological-science-media-and-communication">Bachelor of Psychological Science / Bachelor of Media and Communication</a></li><li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-psychological-science-social-science">Bachelor of Psychological Science / Bachelor of Social Science</a></li><li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-criminology-psychological-science">Bachelor of Criminology / Bachelor of Psychological Science</a></li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>PSYC1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1000">Introductory Research Methods in Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1010">Psychology Introduction 1</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1020">Psychology Introduction 2</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1200">Foundations of Psychological Practice</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2200">Evidence-based Mental Health Interventions</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2300">Cognitive Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2400">Biological Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC2500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2500">Introduction to Mental Health and Mental Disorders</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC2900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2900">Social Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3000">Advanced Research Methods and Statistics in Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3002">Work Integrated Learning in Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3006">Individual Differences and Assessment</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC3200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3200">Foundations of Applied Psychological Science</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC3301</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3301">Advanced Perception and Learning in Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC3700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3700">Advanced Developmental Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>STAT1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1070">Statistics for the Sciences</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40099">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Science Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 20 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BIOL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1001">Molecules, Cells and Organisms</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1002">Organisms to Ecosystems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1003">Professional Skills for Biological Sciences 1</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1010">Introductory Chemistry I</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>CHEM1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1020">Introductory Chemistry II</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CRIM2020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM2020">Criminal Psychology</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>ENVS1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1001">Environmental Science Concepts and Methods</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1003">Environmental Values and Ethics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1004">Social Development and the Environment</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2004">Ecology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2008">The Sustainable Society</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>ENVS3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3005">Animal Behaviour</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EXSS1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS1050">Fundamentals of Exercise and Sport Science Practice</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>EXSS2030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/EXSS2030">Sport, Exercise and Performance Psychology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>FSHN1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN1030">Introduction to the Nutritional, Physical and Psychological Aspects of Wellness</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>FSHN2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FSHN2060">Food Marketing and Consumer Behaviour</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOG1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1030">Global Poverty and Development</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOG2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2080">Cities and Regions</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2130">Geographies of Development</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS1040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS1040">Earth: Our Dynamic Planet</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>GEOS1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOS1050">Earth: Natural Hazards</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MARI1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MARI1000">Our Oceans</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>MATH1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1001">Preparatory Studies in Mathematics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1002">Foundational Studies in Mathematics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1110">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 1</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1120">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 2</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1510</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1510">Discrete Mathematics</a> (Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>PHYS1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHYS1200">Introductory Physics for the Life Sciences</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PHYS1210</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHYS1210">Advanced Physics I</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PHYS2100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PHYS2100">Introduction to Astronomy</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC1800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1800">Sex, Drugs and Serial Killers</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC2505</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2505">Foundations of Psychology and Sociology for Health Professionals</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC2800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2800">Special Topics in Psychology</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SCIE1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE1002">Multidisciplinary Laboratories</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCIE2019</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE2019">Astrobiology: Life Beyond our Planet</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>STAT2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2000">Applied Statistics and Research Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Science Course List" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40099">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Science Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40099">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Psychology Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 20 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>PSYC3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3300">Advanced Cognitive Psychology: Theory and Applications</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3500">Advanced Health Psychology</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC3800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3800">Advanced Special Topics in Psychology 2</a> (Online)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Psychology Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40099">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 40 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40099">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40099">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Psychological Science</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=40099&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p>As a commencing student in this degree, you may be eligible for the new Tertiary Health Study Subsidy. You could secure up to $12,000 to support your health studies. To learn more and submit your application visit NSW Health.</p> <p><a href="https://www.health.nsw.gov.au/studysubsidies">NSW Health</a></p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Real-world experience in psychological science 2:32 <p>Hear from Psychological Science students, Joel and Emma about their experiences completing career-ready placements at the University of Newcastle.</p> Career-ready placements <p>Career-ready placement opportunities can be sought with Research labs, the University of Newcastle Psychology Community Clinic, external agencies, and with Industry Partners. </p><p>Students will access psychology labs and equipment. They will undertake pre-professional courses each year, preparing for professional practice with guest lectures and problem-based workshops.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Our industry partners <p>TAFE NSW Registered Training Organisation: 90003</p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Studying at Central Coast campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/central-coast/living-on-the-central-coast"> Living on the Central Coast <p>The Central Coast offers a relaxed and convenient lifestyle with access to beautiful beaches and national parks. Our campuses have industry-leading facilities all within beautiful bushland.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Meet Laiton, a Bachelor of Psychological Science (Honours) student 1:48 <p>When you study a Bachelor of Psychology (Honours) at the University of Newcastle, you will cover a broad range of areas within psychology such as memory, decision-making, and developmental studies.</p> Meet Huiqi Hau-Yong Ng, Bachelor of Psychological Science student from Malaysia 3:02 <p>Huiqi talks about her experience studying a Bachelor of Psychological Science at the University of Newcastle.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/483970"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=40099">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-arts">Bachelor of Arts<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 36,450</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Online</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-psychological-science-social-science">Bachelor of Psychological Science / Bachelor of Social Science<p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-social-science">Bachelor of Social Science<p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/science-and-the-environment">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://apac.au/"></a><p>The Bachelor of Psychological Science (Callaghan, Ourimbah) is accredited by the Australian Psychology Accreditation Council (APAC) as a LEVEL 1 APAC accredited degree.</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Career-ready placement opportunities can be sought with Research labs, the University of Newcastle Psychology Community Clinic, external agencies, and with Industry Partners. </p><p>Students will access psychology labs and equipment. They will undertake pre-professional courses each year, preparing for professional practice with guest lectures and problem-based workshops.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
