UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Develop your understanding of human nature and communication</p><p>Media and Communication is the cornerstone to psychology. Studying the combined Bachelor of Psychological Science/Bachelor of Media and Communication will prepare you with foundational knowledge in both areas and provide you with a broad skillset to be used in a variety of fields.</p> <p>This program is for those who are interested in using science to understand people while also learning how to effectively communicate information across multiple mediums.</p><p>With a range of course options, you’ll learn to push your individual creative boundaries, while examining the changing nature of today’s complex social landscapes.</p> <p> <strong> World top 250 ? </strong> for Psychology </p> <p> <strong> APAC ? </strong> accredited degree </p> <p> <strong> Cutting-edge facilities ? </strong> so you graduate work-ready <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/school/humanities-creative-industries-social-sciences/study-with-hciss/facilities">Find out more</a> </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>This combined program can be applied in a broad range of industry sectors, enabling you to choose the career path that’s right for you. You might work in media and communications, for a multi-national business or with the law, police, or correctional services.</p> <p><strong>Careers opportunities may include:</strong></p><ul><li>Case Worker</li><li>Careers Counsellor</li><li>Foreign Correspondent</li><li>Feature Writer</li><li>Film/Television Production</li><li>Behavioural Interventionalist</li><li>Victims Advocate</li><li>Project and Research Manager</li><li>Public Relations Manager</li><li>Strategic Planner</li></ul><p>A registered psychologist role (including clinical psychologist) requires additional accredited postgraduate study (an Honours plus relevant Masters degree).</p> <p>93.5% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Communications</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Students will complete a total of 320 units, comprised of the following:</p><ul><li>220 units of Core Courses</li><li>10 units of Psychology Directed Courses</li><li>10 units of WIL Directed Courses</li><li>80 unit Major chosen from the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50003">Bachelor of Media and Communication program handbook</a></li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARTS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS1004">Creative Collaborations</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1100">Media, Culture and Narrative</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1234</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1234">Media and Communication Concepts</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2000">Digital Media Engagement</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2510</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2510">Global Media Industries</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2600">Audience Participation and Interaction</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3310">Communication and Creativity</a></li><li><strong>PSYC1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1000">Introductory Research Methods in Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1010">Psychology Introduction 1</a></li><li><strong>PSYC1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1020">Psychology Introduction 2</a></li><li><strong>PSYC1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1200">Foundations of Psychological Practice</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2200">Evidence-based Mental Health Interventions</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2300">Cognitive Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2400">Biological Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2500">Introduction to Mental Health and Mental Disorders</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2900">Social Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3000">Advanced Research Methods and Statistics in Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3006">Individual Differences and Assessment</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3200">Foundations of Applied Psychological Science</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3301</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3301">Advanced Perception and Learning in Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3700">Advanced Developmental Psychology</a></li><li><strong>STAT1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1070">Statistics for the Sciences</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50007">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Psychology Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>PSYC3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3300">Advanced Cognitive Psychology: Theory and Applications</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3500">Advanced Health Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3800">Advanced Special Topics in Psychology 2</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Psychology Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50007">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready Placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARTS3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS3020">Professional Career Ready Studio</a></li><li><strong>HASS3010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3010">Professional Career Ready Placement</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3002">Work Integrated Learning in Psychology</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready Placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50007">handbook</a>.</p>Media and Communication Major<p><a href="#">Media Production</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following 20 units of compulsory courses</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 60 units from the following directed course list; 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2016</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2016">Interactive Storytelling</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2035</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2035">Cinematography</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2130">Sound Production</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2180</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2180">Screenwriting</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2700">Create Your Own Business</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2900">Documentary Filmmaking</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3440</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3440">Short Film Production</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3801">Media Production Project</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3999</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3999">Advanced Media Production</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Media Production" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50007">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Media Production"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50007">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">News Media</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following 20 units of compulsory courses</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 60 units from the following directed course list; 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2280</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2280">Feature Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2320</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2320">News Media</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2470</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2470">Data Storytelling</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3150</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3150">Podcasting</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3333</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3333">Multiplatform Journalism</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3666</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3666">Contemporary Journalism</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3802</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3802">Public Relations and News Media Project</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"News Media"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50007">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Public Relations</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following 20 units of compulsory courses</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 60 units from the following directed course list; 20 units at 2000 level and 40 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2140</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2140">Principles of Public Relations</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2212</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2212">Activism and Social Change</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2530</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2530">Organisational Communication</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3520</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3520">Political Communication</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3540</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3540">Public Relations Campaigns</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3737</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3737">Social Media Listening and Monitoring</a></li><li><strong>CMNS3802</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS3802">Public Relations and News Media Project</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Public Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50007">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/50007">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Psychological Science / Bachelor of Media and Communication</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=50007&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Behind the scenes of a university ad 2:38 <p>See behind the scenes of ''The Courier'' advertisement concept created entirely by staff and students within Creative Industries at the University of Newcastle. Students studying Media Production conceptualised, coordinated and filmed the recruitment ad as a Work Integrated Learning project.</p> Q Building Virtual Campus Tour 2:07 <p>Located in Honeysuckle, Q Building is part of our city precinct providing state-of-the-art facilities for the School of Humanities, Creative Industries and Social Sciences (HCISS) and the Integrated Innovation Network (I2N) Hub.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/483972"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=50007">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-social-science">Bachelor of Social Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 37,200</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-media-and-communication">Bachelor of Media and Communication<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 38,815</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-criminology">Bachelor of Criminology<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 35,130</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/creative-industries-and-communication">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://apac.au/"></a><p>The Bachelor of Psychological Science/Bachelor of Media and Communication (Callaghan, Ourimbah) is accredited by the Australian Psychology Accreditation Council (APAC) as a LEVEL 1 APAC accredited degree.</p>',
