UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Study human behaviour and help shape solutions to social challenges</p><p>The combined Bachelor of Psychological Science/Bachelor of Social Science will empower you to think differently, to analyse human nature, behaviours, social relationships and structures. You will use this understanding to make a positive impact on the lives of others.</p> <p>Use science to understand people. Be inspired to build new knowledge and discover new things using a variety of scientific methods. Cover a broad range of areas such as mental illness, interventions, the biology of the brain, memory, and decision making.</p><p>You will also explore the exciting complexities of the human social experience and learn to apply research methodologies of social science to the societies in which we exist.</p> <p> <strong> World top 250 ? </strong> for Psychology </p> <p> <strong> World top 300 ? </strong> for Social Sciences </p> <p> <strong> APAC ? </strong> accredited degree </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Careers stemming from this combined program are broad and varied. Common areas of employment for graduates include social research, management and policy work for government and non-government agencies, in addition to work in the private sector.</p> <p><strong>Some typical roles include:</strong></p><ul><li>Case worker</li><li>Community development worker</li><li>Counsellor</li><li>Health promotion officer</li><li>Historian</li><li>Juvenile justice officer</li><li>Mediator</li><li>Social scientist</li></ul><p>A registered psychologist role (including clinical psychologist) requires additional accredited postgraduate study (an Honours plus relevant Masters degree).</p> <p>87.6% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Psychology</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Students will complete 320 units, comprised of the following:</p><ul><li>220 units of Core Courses</li><li>10 unit Psychology Directed Course</li><li>10 unit WIL Directed Course</li><li>80 unit Major chosen from the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-social-science/handbook">Bachelor of Social Science program handbook</a></li></ul>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-psychological-science">Bachelor of Psychological Science</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-social-science">Bachelor of Social Science</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>PSYC1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1000">Introductory Research Methods in Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1010">Psychology Introduction 1</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1020">Psychology Introduction 2</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1200">Foundations of Psychological Practice</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2200">Evidence-based Mental Health Interventions</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2300">Cognitive Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2400">Biological Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC2500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2500">Introduction to Mental Health and Mental Disorders</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC2900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2900">Social Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3000">Advanced Research Methods and Statistics in Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3006">Individual Differences and Assessment</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC3200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3200">Foundations of Applied Psychological Science</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC3301</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3301">Advanced Perception and Learning in Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC3700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3700">Advanced Developmental Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1010">Society and Culture: an Introduction to Sociology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>SOCS1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS1100">Professional Skills and Key Debates in Social Sciences</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SOCS2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2200">Social Analysis: Theorising Social Problems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>SOCS2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2300">Ethics for the Social Sciences</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SOCS3100</strong> <a href="https://ha