eady Studio</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>HASS3010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3010">Professional Career Ready Placement</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3002">Work Integrated Learning in Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready Placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40291">handbook</a>.</p>Social Science Major<p><a href="#">Criminology</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Students must complete all courses to fulfill the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>CRIM1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM1010">Introduction to Criminology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CRIM1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM1020">Victimology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CRIM2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM2001">Criminal Justice in Practice</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CRIM2030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM2030">Criminology in the Legal Context</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CRIM3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM3020">Crime, Power and the State</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CRIM3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM3040">Forensic Evidence</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 20 units at the 3000 level from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>CRIM3051</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM3051">Cybercrime: Tools, Tactics and Traps</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SO