://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2004">Diplomacy, Trade and Politics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3001">Public Diplomacy and Social Media</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3002">Global Data Governance for Just and Sustainable Futures</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3003">International Relations in a Changing World Order</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>IREL3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3004">Indigenising International Politics, Policy and the Economy</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40291">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Linguistics</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory</strong></p><ul><li><strong>LING1111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING1111">How Languages Work: Linguistics and the Structure of Language</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>LING2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING2001">Indigenous languages of Australia and the Pacific</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>LING3310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3310">Language and Meaning</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 50 units with a max of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>LING1112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING1112">Languages in the World</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>LING2501</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING2501">Cross-cultural Communication