UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Understand the world around us and how it works</p><p>Science is about exploring the natural world, seeking to understand its mysteries, and developing solutions to challenges we face in society. It underpins a broad spectrum of fields, including technology, environmental management, business, research, and health. By studying science, you will complement and enhance your knowledge while developing critical business and communication skills.</p> <p>Tailor your degree to your interests with 10 diverse majors and flexible study pathways, allowing you to focus on areas that inspire you. Options such as double majors, or honours pathways enable you to deepen your expertise and broaden your career opportunities.</p><p>As you study, you’ll build the professional skills and networks essential for a successful career. With authentic opportunities to work in industry and research during your studies, you''ll gain the practical experience and connections needed to tackle the complex science challenges of our time.</p><p><strong>Concurrent Enrolment</strong></p><p>Bachelor of Science students are encouraged to consider concurrent enrolment in the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-applied-data-science">Bachelor of Applied Data Science program.</a> <br/><br/>A career in science is increasingly data-driven. From climate modelling to biomedical research, the ability to manage, interpret, and visualise data is essential. By combining a science major with the Bachelor of Applied Data Science, students gain advanced data analysis and visualisation skills, confidence in programming and database management, and tools for evidence-based decision-making.</p><p>Complete both programs in only one extra year of study and graduate with two degrees, increasing your in-demand skills and employability in broad and varied areas such as environmental and climate science, pharmaceuticals and biomedical research, geoscience, physics and engineering, and science communication and policy.</p> <p> <strong> World top 200 ? </strong> for Environmental Sciences </p> <p> <strong> 88.4% of students ? </strong> were happy with facilities and resources </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Most of the critical issues that face our society today require science to help find the right solutions for our current and future generations. Because this degree emphasises problem-solving, teamwork and critical thinking, graduates are sought after across a range of sectors.</p> <p>Use this degree as a steppingstone into the health and science fields to achieve your career goals.</p><p><strong>Professional outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>Wildlife or plant biologist</li><li>Chemist</li><li>Conservationist/ecologist</li><li>Data scientist or financial analyst</li><li>Geologist</li><li>Government or defence professional</li><li>Mathematician</li><li>Medical physicist</li><li>Meteorologist</li><li>Neuroscientist</li><li>Oceanographer</li><li>Research physicist</li><li>Statistician</li></ul> <p>88.5% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Science &amp; Mathematics</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Using the latest scientific developments and advancements, you''ll learn first-hand from our actively involved researchers how to deliver innovative solutions for real-world problems. You''ll also develop highly sought after and transferable skills in problem solving, communication and independent thinking.</p><p>Tailor your degree to your interests with 10 diverse majors and flexible <br/>study pathways, allowing you to focus on areas that inspire you.</p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>INFT1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INFT1004">Introduction to Programming</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCIE1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE1002">Multidisciplinary Laboratories</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCIE3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCIE3002">WIL for the Sciences</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40165">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Mathematics Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list. Which course you should complete will depend on your previous mathematical background, please refer to each course Handbook for more information. Please note that some disciplines require a minimum level of mathematical knowledge. MATH1002 or higher is required for a Chemistry Major. MATH1110 is required for Physics or Mathematics Majors.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>MATH1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1001">Preparatory Studies in Mathematics</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1002">Foundational Studies in Mathematics</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>MATH1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/MATH1110">Mathematics for Engineering, Science and Technology 1</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Mathematics Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40165">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Statistics Course List</a></p><p><strong>Complete 10 units from the following course list. The course you choose should align with your prior knowledge of statistics and mathematics. For detailed information about each course, please refer to the course handbook. If you are pursuing a major in Physics or Mathematics, it is recommended to complete STAT1300.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>STAT1070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1070">Statistics for the Sciences</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>STAT1300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1300">Fundamentals of Statistics</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Statistics Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40165">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Science Course List (for students who complete single major only)</a></p><p><strong>Complete either a second major, or 80 units from the Science course list (all major courses + SCIE), or 50 units if you are doing a Physics major. Students must complete at least 20 units from 2000 level courses and at least 20 units from 3000 level courses.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>BIOL1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1001">Molecules, Cells and Organisms</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL1002">Organisms to Ecosystems</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2001">Molecular Laboratory Skills for Biological Sciences</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2002">Laboratory Skills in Biological Systems</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL2090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2090">Microbial Biology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL2220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL2220">Plant Adaptation to Climate Change</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL3001">Advanced Laboratory Skills in Biological Sciences</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL3020">Animal Physiology, Reproduction and Development</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL3090">Molecular Biology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>BIOL3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/BIOL3100">Microbiology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1010">Introductory Chemistry I</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Singapore)</li><li><strong>CHEM1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM1020">Introductory Chemistry II</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM2110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM2110">Applied Analytical Chemistry</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM2210</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM2210">Materials Chemistry</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM2310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM2310">Organic Chemistry</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM2410</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM2410">Physical Chemistry</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM3110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM3110">Instrumental Chemical Analysis</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM3210</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM3210">Functional Materials</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>CHEM3310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHEM3310">Molecular Organic Synthesis</a> (Newc