castle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3310">Language and Meaning</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 50 units with a max of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>LING1112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING1112">Languages in the World</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>LING2501</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING2501">Cross-cultural Communication</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>LING2502</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING2502">Issues of Bilingualism and Bilingual Education</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>LING3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3008">Introduction to Phonology and Morphology</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>LING3110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3110">Language and Cognition</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>LING3350</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3350">Structure of English</a> (Online)</li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Linguistics" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10716">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Linguistics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10716">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Psychology Studies</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>PSYC1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1010">Psychology Introduction 1</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1020">Psychology Introduction 2</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC2500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2500">Introduction to Mental Health and Mental Disorders</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3500">Advanced Health Psychology</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC3700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3700">Advanced Developmental Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 30 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 20 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>PSYC2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2300">Cognitive Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2400">Biological Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC2505</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2505">Foundations of Psychology and Sociology for Health Professionals</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC2800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2800">Special Topics in Psychology</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC2900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2900">Social Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3000">Advanced Research Methods and Statistics in Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3006">Individual Differences and Assessment</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>PSYC3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3300">Advanced Cognitive Psychology: Theory and Applications</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC3301</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3301">Advanced Perception and Learning in Psychology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle)</li><li><strong>PSYC3800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3800">Advanced Special Topics in Psychology 2</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>STAT2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2000">Applied Statistics and Research Methods</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Psychology Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10716">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Sociology and Anthropology</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>SOCA1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1020">What is Anthropology</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2400">Future Societies: Beyond Capitalist Globalisation</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA3780</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3780">Leading Social Change: Applying Critical Theories in Critical Times</a> (Newcastle, Online)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 50 units with a maximum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>GEOG1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1030">Global Poverty and Development</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>SCRN2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN2200">Popular Culture and Society</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1050">Youth, Gender and Crime</a> (Central Coast, Newcastle, Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1200">Sociology of Health and Illness</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA2065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2065">Environment and Society</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA2700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2700">Gender, Religion and Power</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA3178</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3178">Health, ''Wellness'' and Power: The Social Contexts of Expert Knowledge</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3220">Youth Culture and Risk</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA3666</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3666">Consumption, Technology and Everyday Life</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA3790</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3790">Mobilities, Migration and the Environment</a> (Online)</li><li><strong>SOCA3850</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3850">Rage Against the Machine: Indigenous Activism, Ways of Life and the Future</a> (Online)</li><li><em>8 additional courses are part of "Sociology and Anthropology" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10716">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Sociology and Anthropology"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10716">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Tourism, Society and Sustainability</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following courses to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>THHE1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE1001">Introduction to Global Tourism</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>THHE1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE1002">Sustainable Tourism Systems</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>THHE2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE2002">Tourism and Intercultural Encounters</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>THHE3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE3001">Managing and Marketing Destinations</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the following Course List with a minimum of 20 units at the 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>THHE1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE1003">Event Management Principles</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>THHE2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE2001">Experience Design and Management</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>THHE2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE2003">Service Management in Tourism and Hospitality</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>THHE3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE3002">Strategy for Tourism Futures and Innovation</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>THHE3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE3003">Leadership for Tourism, Hospitality and Events</a> (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>THHE3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE3004">Digital Transformation in Tourism, Hospitality and Events</a> (Newcastle)</li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Tourism, Society and Sustainability"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10716">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 40 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10716">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/10716">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Social Science</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=10716&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Creating meaningful opportunities for students 0:44 <p>At the University of Newcastle, we embed practical, hands-on learning in all our degrees. Check out just some of the opportunities our students have had to build their experience.</p> Career-ready placements <p>You will gain practical social science skills in analysis and communication, policy, and research. You will complete a minimum 140-hour placement within the later stages of your studies. There will be a variety of opportunities available to acquire a placement in your desired career field. This includes local, state and commonwealth public service, non-government organisations, higher education, cultural and environmental organisations, and community and family services.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Studying at Central Coast campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/central-coast/living-on-the-central-coast"> Living on the Central Coast <p>The Central Coast offers a relaxed and convenient lifestyle with access to beautiful beaches and national parks. Our campuses have industry-leading facilities all within beautiful bushland.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Where can a Bachelor of Social Science take you? 1:24 <p>Meet current Bachelor of Social Science students Jade and Jesse and hear first-hand why they chose to study social science at the University of Newcastle.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/484050"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=10716">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="diploma-in-social-and-human-services">Diploma in Social and Human Services<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 50.00 (Gosford)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> undefined</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 1 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 4 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-social-work-honours">Bachelor of Social Work (Honours)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 67.00 (Gosford)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,415</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-psychological-science">Bachelor of Psychological Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 67.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 45,070</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/humanities-and-social-sciences">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>You will gain practical social science skills in analysis and communication, policy, and research. You will complete a minimum 140-hour placement within the later stages of your studies. There will be a variety of opportunities available to acquire a placement in your desired career field. This includes local, state and commonwealth public service, non-government organisations, higher education, cultural and environmental organisations, and community and family services.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
