UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Understand our world – then make an impact</p><p>Develop a deep understanding of the complex systems that define our world. Graduate with strong legal expertise that elevates your potential across a wide range of sectors.</p> <p>Through core and elective courses, you will learn to analyse, challenge and gain insight into globally significant research. Explore gender, class, race, crime, illness and health, social justice and more.</p><p>Pursue a traditional career in the legal field, or make your mark across government, NGOs, business, and community organisations – there are opportunities in almost every sector.</p> <p> <strong> World top 250 ? </strong> for Sociology </p> <p> <strong> World top 300 ? </strong> for Law </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Career opportunities span a wide range of industries and sectors, including:</p><ul><li>Legal Sector</li><li>Local, State and Federal Public Service</li><li>Non-Government Organisations</li><li>Global Health</li><li>Human Services</li><li>Higher Education.</li></ul> <p>90.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Undergraduate Law and Paralegal Studies</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>Within this combined degree program, you will study a combination of Social Science and Law courses over a period of five years full-time.</p><p>Learn and develop skills by studying courses in various aspects of law including:</p><ul><li>criminal law and procedure</li><li>evidence</li><li>equity and trusts</li><li>administrative law</li><li>property law</li><li>contract law.</li></ul>This is a combined degree<p>For additional information about this degree you can refer to the pages for the corresponding single degrees: <a href="bachelor-of-social-science">Bachelor of Social Science</a>, and <a href="bachelor-of-laws-honours">Bachelor of Laws (Honours) Combined</a></p> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>LAWS1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1010">Legal System and Method I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1011">Legal System and Method II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1020">Torts I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS1021</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS1021">Torts II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS2030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS2030">Criminal Law and Procedure</a></li><li><strong>LAWS3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS3040">Contracts I</a></li><li><strong>LAWS3041</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS3041">Contracts II</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4001">Constitutional Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4002">Administrative Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4003">Civil Dispute Resolution</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4004">Evidence</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4005">Company Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4007</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4007">Professional Conduct</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4010">Equity and Trusts</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4011">Property</a></li><li><strong>LAWS4012</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS4012">Public International Law</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1010">Society and Culture: an Introduction to Sociology</a></li><li><strong>SOCS1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS1100">Professional Skills and Key Debates in Social Sciences</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2200">Social Analysis: Theorising Social Problems</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2300">Ethics for the Social Sciences</a></li><li><strong>SOCS2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS2400">Surveying the Social: Applied Quantitative Research</a></li><li><strong>SOCS3100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS3100">Policy Development, Program Management and Evaluation</a></li><li><strong>SOCS3200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCS3200">Qualitative Social Inquiry: Applied Research Project</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Students choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARTS3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS3020">Professional Career Ready Studio</a></li><li><strong>HASS3010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3010">Professional Career Ready Placement</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Law Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 80 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>LAWS5036</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS5036">International Clinical Legal Externship</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6016</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6016">Taxation Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6017</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6017">Family Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6020">Environmental Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6021</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6021">Advanced Criminal Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6024">Employment Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6038</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6038">Law and Economics of Climate Change</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6043</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6043">Advanced Legal Research Project</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6087</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6087">Internet Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6090">Health Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6091</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6091">Special Interest Topic</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6094</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6094">Indigenous Peoples, Issues and the Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6096</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6096">Child Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6097</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6097">Competitive Mooting</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6099</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6099">Sport and the Law</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6102">Alternative Dispute Resolution</a></li><li><strong>LAWS6151</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LAWS6151">Gender and the Law</a></li><li><em>35 additional courses are part of "Law Course List" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Law Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</p>Social Science Majors<p><a href="#">Criminology</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Students must complete all courses to fulfill the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>CRIM1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM1010">Introduction to Criminology</a></li><li><strong>CRIM1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM1020">Victimology</a></li><li><strong>CRIM2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM2001">Criminal Justice in Practice</a></li><li><strong>CRIM2030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM2030">Criminology in the Legal Context</a></li><li><strong>CRIM3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM3020">Crime, Power and the State</a></li><li><strong>CRIM3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM3040">Forensic Evidence</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 20 units at the 3000 level from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>CRIM3051</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM3051">Cybercrime: Tools, Tactics and Traps</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3220">Youth Culture and Risk</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Criminology" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Criminology"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Global Indigenous Studies</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1110">Blak Australia</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2244</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2244">Sovereignty and Reconciliation</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3251</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3251">Global Indigenous Comparative Studies</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3380</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3380">Global Indigenous Human Rights</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units with maximum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 20 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1370</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1370">Community Engagement: Respect and Reciprocity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1390</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1390">Blak Rights and the Fight for Justice</a></li><li><strong>ABOR1420</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1420">Yarning, Media and Futures</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2243</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2243">Indigenous People and Sustainable Environments</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2245</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2245">Aboriginal People and Law</a></li><li><strong>ABOR2330</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR2330">Aboriginal Knowledge Systems</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3024</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3024">Blak Advocacy: Empowerment and Solidarity</a></li><li><strong>ABOR3080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR3080">Indigenous Research</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Global Indigenous Studies" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Global Indigenous Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">History</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 80 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 40 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>AHIS1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS1000">Ancient Greece</a></li><li><strong>AHIS2110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS2110">Sparta</a></li><li><strong>AHIS3510</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS3510">Greek Society</a></li><li><strong>AHIS3663</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/AHIS3663">Folklore and Fairy Tale in Antiquity</a></li><li><strong>HIST1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1001">Europe and the World</a></li><li><strong>HIST1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1002">The United States from Civil War to Superpower</a></li><li><strong>HIST1051</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1051">The Australian Experience</a></li><li><strong>HIST1052</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST1052">Origin of Controversies</a></li><li><strong>HIST2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2002">Fact or Fiction Reading the Past</a></li><li><strong>HIST2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2006">Australian Underworlds: Histories of Crime in Australia</a></li><li><strong>HIST2253</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2253">Bodies and Brains: Histories of Illness, Disability and Disease</a></li><li><strong>HIST2611</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2611">The Russian Revolution: From the Tsars to Putin</a></li><li><strong>HIST2650</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST2650">War and Trauma</a></li><li><strong>HIST3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3008">Global Perspectives on the First World War</a></li><li><strong>HIST3152</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3152">The History of Racism</a></li><li><strong>HIST3201</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3201">Power in the Asia Pacific: Conflict and Alliances</a></li><li><strong>HIST3621</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3621">Maps and Dreams: Aboriginal-Colonial Relationships in Australian History</a></li><li><strong>HIST3641</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3641">The Rise of Fascism: From the March on Rome to Hitler s Seizure of Power</a></li><li><strong>HIST3642</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HIST3642">The Downfall of Fascism: The Third Reich, War and Genocide</a></li><li><em>18 additional courses are part of "History" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"History"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Geography and the Environment</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this minor.</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3006">Surviving the Anthropocene: Sustainability in the 21st Century</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1020">Introduction to Human Geography</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2080">Cities and Regions</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3090">Society and Space</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the list for a major (10 units at 1000 level, 10 units at 2000 level and 20 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>ENVS1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1003">Environmental Values and Ethics</a></li><li><strong>ENVS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS1004">Social Development and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2002">Environmental Legislation and Planning</a></li><li><strong>ENVS2008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS2008">The Sustainable Society</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3001">Integrated Impact Assessment</a></li><li><strong>ENVS3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ENVS3008">Work Integrated Learning in the Environmental and Development Sectors</a></li><li><strong>GEOG1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1030">Global Poverty and Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG2130</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG2130">Geographies of Development</a></li><li><strong>GEOG3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG3300">Rethinking Development</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2065">Environment and Society</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Geography and the Environment"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Resource Management</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>HRER2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2001">Managing Talent</a></li><li><strong>HRER2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2002">Introduction to Employment Relations</a></li><li><strong>HRER2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2003">Dynamics of People and Work in Organisations</a></li><li><strong>HRER2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER2004">HR Analytics</a></li><li><strong>HRER3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3001">Future of Work</a></li><li><strong>HRER3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3002">Negotiation and Conflict Management</a></li><li><strong>HRER3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3003">Strategic HR</a></li><li><strong>HRER3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HRER3004">Human Capital Development</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Resource Management"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Human Services</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory</strong></p><ul><li><strong>HUSE1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUSE1001">Introduction to Human Services</a></li><li><strong>HUSE2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUSE2001">Shaping Human Services: Social Policy and the Political Process</a></li><li><strong>HUSE3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUSE3001">Person-centered practice and casework skills</a></li><li><strong>HUSE3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUSE3008">Human Services from the user perspective</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units with a maximum of 20 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 20 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>ABOR1370</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ABOR1370">Community Engagement: Respect and Reciprocity</a></li><li><strong>CRIM2030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CRIM2030">Criminology in the Legal Context</a></li><li><strong>HUSE2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUSE2002">Child Protection Work</a></li><li><strong>HUSE2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUSE2005">Gendered Violence</a></li><li><strong>HUSE3005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUSE3005">Working with Groups and Communities</a></li><li><strong>HUSE3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUSE3006">Social Policy and Planning in Regional Contexts</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1050">Youth, Gender and Crime</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2400">Future Societies: Beyond Capitalist Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3220">Youth Culture and Risk</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Human Services" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Human Services"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">International Relations</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Complete 80 units from this course list to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>IREL2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2001">International Policy, Politics and the Economy</a></li><li><strong>IREL2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2002">Business and the Politics of Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>IREL2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2003">The International Politics of Climate Change and the Future World</a></li><li><strong>IREL2004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL2004">Diplomacy, Trade and Politics</a></li><li><strong>IREL3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3001">Public Diplomacy and Social Media</a></li><li><strong>IREL3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3002">Global Data Governance for Just and Sustainable Futures</a></li><li><strong>IREL3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3003">International Relations in a Changing World Order</a></li><li><strong>IREL3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/IREL3004">Indigenising International Politics, Policy and the Economy</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"International Relations"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Linguistics</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory</strong></p><ul><li><strong>LING1111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING1111">How Languages Work: Linguistics and the Structure of Language</a></li><li><strong>LING2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING2001">Indigenous languages of Australia and the Pacific</a></li><li><strong>LING3310</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3310">Language and Meaning</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 50 units with a max of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>LING1112</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING1112">Languages in the World</a></li><li><strong>LING2501</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING2501">Cross-cultural Communication</a></li><li><strong>LING2502</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING2502">Issues of Bilingualism and Bilingual Education</a></li><li><strong>LING3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3008">Introduction to Phonology and Morphology</a></li><li><strong>LING3110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3110">Language and Cognition</a></li><li><strong>LING3350</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3350">Structure of English</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Linguistics" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Linguistics"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Psychology Studies</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>PSYC1010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1010">Psychology Introduction 1</a></li><li><strong>PSYC1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1020">Psychology Introduction 2</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2500">Introduction to Mental Health and Mental Disorders</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3500">Advanced Health Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3700">Advanced Developmental Psychology</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 30 units from the list to fulfil the requirements for this major (a minimum of 20 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>PSYC2300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2300">Cognitive Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2400">Biological Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2505</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2505">Foundations of Psychology and Sociology for Health Professionals</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2800">Special Topics in Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2900">Social Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3000">Advanced Research Methods and Statistics in Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3006">Individual Differences and Assessment</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3300</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3300">Advanced Cognitive Psychology: Theory and Applications</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3301</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3301">Advanced Perception and Learning in Psychology</a></li><li><strong>PSYC3800</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC3800">Advanced Special Topics in Psychology 2</a></li><li><strong>STAT2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT2000">Applied Statistics and Research Methods</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Psychology Studies"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Sociology and Anthropology</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>SOCA1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1020">What is Anthropology</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2400</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2400">Future Societies: Beyond Capitalist Globalisation</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3780</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3780">Leading Social Change: Applying Critical Theories in Critical Times</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 50 units with a maximum of 10 units at 1000 level and a minimum of 30 units at 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>GEOG1030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/GEOG1030">Global Poverty and Development</a></li><li><strong>SCRN2200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SCRN2200">Popular Culture and Society</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1050</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1050">Youth, Gender and Crime</a></li><li><strong>SOCA1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA1200">Sociology of Health and Illness</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2065</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2065">Environment and Society</a></li><li><strong>SOCA2700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA2700">Gender, Religion and Power</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3178</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3178">Health, ''Wellness'' and Power: The Social Contexts of Expert Knowledge</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3220</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3220">Youth Culture and Risk</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3666</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3666">Consumption, Technology and Everyday Life</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3790</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3790">Mobilities, Migration and the Environment</a></li><li><strong>SOCA3850</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SOCA3850">Rage Against the Machine: Indigenous Activism, Ways of Life and the Future</a></li><li><em>8 additional courses are part of "Sociology and Anthropology" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Sociology and Anthropology"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Tourism, Society and Sustainability</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following courses to fulfil the requirements of this major.</p><ul><li><strong>THHE1001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE1001">Introduction to Global Tourism</a></li><li><strong>THHE1002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE1002">Sustainable Tourism Systems</a></li><li><strong>THHE2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE2002">Tourism and Intercultural Encounters</a></li><li><strong>THHE3001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE3001">Managing and Marketing Destinations</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the following Course List with a minimum of 20 units at the 3000 level.</p><ul><li><strong>THHE1003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE1003">Event Management Principles</a></li><li><strong>THHE2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE2001">Experience Design and Management</a></li><li><strong>THHE2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE2003">Service Management in Tourism and Hospitality</a></li><li><strong>THHE3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE3002">Strategy for Tourism Futures and Innovation</a></li><li><strong>THHE3003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE3003">Leadership for Tourism, Hospitality and Events</a></li><li><strong>THHE3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/THHE3004">Digital Transformation in Tourism, Hospitality and Events</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Tourism, Society and Sustainability"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12341">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Social Science / Bachelor of Laws (Honours)</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=12341&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=NCLE&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Creating meaningful opportunities for students 0:44 <p>At the University of Newcastle, we embed practical, hands-on learning in all our degrees. Check out just some of the opportunities our students have had to build their experience.</p> Career-ready placements <p>An important part of your learning is the opportunity to apply your knowledge and theory in an industry or ''real life'' setting. Work Integrated Learning includes clinical, professional work placements, practicums, internships, or industry-led projects.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle City campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Law on the Beach 1:50 <p>Law on the Beach is a free legal advice clinic for members of the local community, held in the relaxed setting of Merewether Surf Club each January and February. Allowing our students to work on real-world cases alongside their studies with Newcastle Legal Centre lawyers, the clinics make seeking legal advice more approachable, particularly for young people.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/483100"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=12341">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-social-work-honours">Bachelor of Social Work (Honours)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 67.00 (Gosford)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 40,415</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Gosford, Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-arts">Bachelor of Arts<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 36,450</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Online</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-criminology">Bachelor of Criminology<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle City)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 35,130</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle City</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <p> <a href="combined">View combined degrees</a> <a href="/study/law">Explore study area</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://lpab.nsw.gov.au/"></a><p>Our LLB (Hons) is accredited by the Legal Profession Admission Board (LPAB) of New South Wales. It provides you with all the academic study necessary to apply to practice as a lawyer in Australia, subject to completing an accredited practical legal training program (including the required number of hours of supervised legal work experience) and satisfying the LPAB’s ‘fit and proper person’ test. For more details see the LPAB’s ‘Guide for Applicants’, or for specific inquiries please contact the LPAB.If you would like to complete an accredited program of practical legal training and supervised legal work experience while you complete your academic legal studies under the LLB (Hons), then you may enrol in, from the fourth year of LLB (Hons) studies, our combined LLB (Hons)/ Diploma of Legal Practice.</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>An important part of your learning is the opportunity to apply your knowledge and theory in an industry or ''real life'' setting. Work Integrated Learning includes clinical, professional work placements, practicums, internships, or industry-led projects.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
