UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Secure your future with highly specialised training, exciting placements and flexible outcomes.</p><p>When you study a Bachelor of Speech Pathology (Honours), you are accessing the most comprehensive degree of its kind in Australia. Open up experiences and job opportunities like no other when you study this program.</p> <p>Speech pathologists assess and treat children and adults with communication and swallowing needs. This includes developmental and acquired speech and language disorders, cognitive communication disorders, voice disorders and stuttering.</p> <p> <strong> 20+ weeks ? </strong> of clinical experience </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Gain professionally accredited expertise in all areas of speech pathology. The strong experience-based nature of this degree, along with an internationally recognised professional accreditation, prepares University of Newcastle graduates for immediate professional employment.</p> <p><strong>Professional Outcomes:</strong></p><ul><li>Speech Pathologist</li><li>Health Promotion Officer</li><li>Research Scientist</li><li>University Lecturer/Academic (with relevant higher degree qualifications)</li></ul> <p>86.4% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcome Survey 2022-2024, Undergraduate Health Services and Support</p> <p>89.7% of students rated learning resources positively.</p> <p>Student Experience Survey 2022-2024, undergraduate Health Services and Support</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You will learn and develop the necessary skills to competently take on the full range of conditions that speech pathologists assess and treat including:</p><ul><li>Acquired and developmental communication disorders (e.g., speech and language, cognitive communication, fluency and voice).</li><li>Swallowing disorders</li></ul><p>Students will study a variety of foundation courses including,but not limited to:</p><ul><li>Linguistics</li><li>Psychology</li><li>Bioscience</li><li>Anatomy</li><li>Health sciences</li><li>Statistics</li></ul><p><strong>Honours Study Pathways in Speech Pathology:</strong><br/> As a requirement for the honours program in this degree, you have the option to select one of the study paths detailed in the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/bachelor-of-speech-pathology-honours/handbook#honours">Speech Pathology handbook.</a></p><p><strong>Language Diploma with Speech Pathology Degree:</strong><br/>As a student of Speech Pathology, you can concurrently pursue a <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/diploma-in-languages">Diploma in Languages</a>, which offers you the opportunity to learn a new language alongside your main degree! This additional qualification will offer you unique opportunities and career pathways in Australia and around the world.</p> <p>Core</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>HLSC1000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC1000">Transition to Health Sciences Education and Practice</a></li><li><strong>HLSC4120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC4120">Research Methodology and Design</a></li><li><strong>HUBS1107</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1107">Neuroscience and Head and Neck Anatomy</a></li><li><strong>HUBS1403</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1403">Biomedical Science Part 1</a></li><li><strong>HUBS1404</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUBS1404">Biomedical Science Part 2</a></li><li><strong>INDH2490</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INDH2490">Foundations of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Health</a></li><li><strong>LING1111</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING1111">How Languages Work: Linguistics and the Structure of Language</a></li><li><strong>LING3008</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3008">Introduction to Phonology and Morphology</a></li><li><strong>LING3350</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/LING3350">Structure of English</a></li><li><strong>PSYC1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC1020">Psychology Introduction 2</a></li><li><strong>PSYC2505</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/PSYC2505">Foundations of Psychology and Sociology for Health Professionals</a></li><li><strong>SPTH1080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH1080">Introduction to Speech Pathology</a></li><li><strong>SPTH2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH2001">Fluency Across the Lifespan</a></li><li><strong>SPTH2002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH2002">Language, Literacy and Hearing</a></li><li><strong>SPTH2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH2003">Complex Communication Needs</a></li><li><strong>SPTH2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH2080">Professional Practice</a></li><li><strong>SPTH2101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH2101">Child Speech</a></li><li><strong>SPTH2102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH2102">Child Language</a></li><li><strong>SPTH3002</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH3002">Swallowing Across the Lifespan</a></li><li><strong>SPTH3004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH3004">Voice across the lifespan</a></li><li><strong>SPTH3080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH3080">Professional Practice</a></li><li><strong>SPTH3101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH3101">Adult Speech</a></li><li><strong>SPTH3102</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH3102">Adult Language</a></li><li><strong>SPTH3103</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH3103">Holistic Practice Across the Lifespan</a></li><li><strong>SPTH4030</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH4030">Professional Issues 1</a></li><li><strong>SPTH4035</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH4035">Professional Issues 2</a></li><li><strong>SPTH4080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH4080">Professional Practice 1</a></li><li><strong>SPTH4090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/SPTH4090">Professional Practice 2</a></li><li><strong>STAT1020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/STAT1020">Statistical Reasoning and Literacy</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12318">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Graded Honours</a></p><p><strong>Choose 20 units from the following course list.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>HLSC4310A</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC4310A">Research Project A</a></li><li><strong>HLSC4310B</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HLSC4310B">Research Project B</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Graded Honours"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12318">handbook</a>.</p>Ungraded Honours<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 20 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12318">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/12318">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Speech Pathology (Honours)</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=12318&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p>As a commencing student in this degree, you may be eligible for the new Tertiary Health Study Subsidy. You could secure up to $12,000 to support your health studies. To learn more and submit your application visit NSW Health.</p> <p><a href="https://www.health.nsw.gov.au/studysubsidies">NSW Health</a></p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Creating meaningful opportunities for students 0:44 <p>At the University of Newcastle, we embed practical, hands-on learning in all our degrees. Check out just some of the opportunities our students have had to build their experience.</p> Career-ready placements <p>Students take part in more than 20 weeks of placements within NSW services or facilities, including NSW Health facilities. You will gain quality practical experiences through a range of clinical education placements during your studies developing your skills and knowledge to meet professional accreditation requirements.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Speech Pathology Virtual Reality Program (VOMA) <p>Students have access to a virtual reality (VR) app, VOMA, which allows them to learn the clinical skill of an oral musculature assessment, and experience what this looks like in a real-life clinic environment. </p> <p>Designed in collaboration with speech pathology discipline staff Rachael Unicomb and Joanne Walters and industry partner Start Beyond, the VR environment also allows students at any stage in their program to practice the skills they have learnt through their studies, preparing them to be career-ready when they graduate.</p> Enabling change with Speech Pathology 1:59 <p>The Bachelor of Speech Pathology (Honours) is a highly specialised degree that equips graduates with the knowledge, confidence and practical skills needed to pursue a career as a professional speech pathologist. At UON, we offer flexible opportunities, pathways, and a strong clinical program, as well as regional and international links.</p> The talking cure 3:28 <p>Speech pathology students are playing an important role in the establishment of a new community-centred program to improve outcomes for children in regional NSW. Learn how the Guyati, Garraka wa Witing program is giving a voice to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander children in Kempsey, NSW.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/484150">Apply via UAC</a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 7.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=12318">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-occupational-therapy-honours">Bachelor of Occupational Therapy (Honours)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 90.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 43,885</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 6 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-education-primary">Bachelor of Education (Primary)<p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-psychological-science">Bachelor of Psychological Science<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 67.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 45,070</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <a href="/study/health-and-medicine">Explore study area</a> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <a href="https://www.speechpathologyaustralia.org.au/"></a><p>This program is accredited by the Speech Pathology Association of Australia. Mutual recognition of credentials includes speech pathology associations in the United States, the United Kingdom, Canada, Ireland, and New Zealand. For more information about the Mutual Recognition of Professional Association Credentials Agreement, and what this means, please visit: speechpathologyaustralia.org.au</p><h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>Students take part in more than 20 weeks of placements within NSW services or facilities, including NSW Health facilities. You will gain quality practical experiences through a range of clinical education placements during your studies developing your skills and knowledge to meet professional accreditation requirements.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
