UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Become an accomplished creative with skills in graphic communication, animation, illustration and interaction design.</p><p>This program will develop your creative skills; with our state-of-the-art studios, labs, and maker spaces. Industry experts will guide you through practical, real-world tasks with a hands-on, future focus to ready you for an innovative career in the design industries. You will graduate with a portfolio reflecting your creative vision and diverse visual communication skills.</p> <p>This program will give you the tools to bring your ideas to life. You will foster creativity and promote adaptability in the rapid-changing world of design, art and media. By integrating visual and design learning, you''ll be well positioned to carve out a unique creative path or contribute to diverse organisations worldwide.</p><p><strong>Specialise in the following majors and minors:</strong></p><ul><li>graphic design, including interaction design and photography</li><li>animation and illustration.</li></ul> <p> <strong> Cutting-edge facilities ? </strong> so you graduate work-ready <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/school/humanities-creative-industries-social-sciences/study-with-hciss/facilities">Find out more</a> </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>You will find employment in a variety of roles in many different types of organisations. The list below provides typical job titles for Visual Communication Design graduates.</p> <p>Professional outcomes for animation and illustration major and minor:</p><ul><li>2D animator</li><li>Commercial illustrator</li><li>Concept artist</li><li>Storyboard artist</li><li>Stopmotion animator</li><li>Interactive media artist</li><li>Motion graphic designer</li><li>Virtual production creator</li><li>Digital media artist</li><li>Experimental/speculative designer.</li></ul><p><strong>Professional outcomes for graphic design major and minor:</strong></p><ul><li>Editorial and publication designer</li><li>Data visualisation designer</li><li>Art director</li><li>Typographer</li><li>Infographic designer</li><li>Graphic novel/sequential art/comic/picture book designer</li><li>Branding designer</li><li>Product and packaging designer</li><li>UX and interface designer</li><li>Physical experience designer</li><li>Campaign designer</li><li>Exhibition and event designer</li><li>Social media designer.</li></ul> <p>93.5% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 Undergraduate Communications</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>You’ll learn to create visual material across a variety of visual formats and channels including broadcast, web, film, television, advertising, publishing, and industry.</p><p>This program allows you to specialise in one or two majors. Depending on your chosen major, examples of what you will study include:</p><ul><li>graphic design</li><li>web design</li><li>advertising</li><li>publishing</li><li>illustration</li><li>animation</li><li>transmedia</li><li>multi-media</li><li>creative arts</li><li>motion graphics</li><li>interaction design</li><li>game art and design typography</li><li>3D design</li><li>extended reality</li></ul> <p>Core</p><p>Majors</p><p>Minors</p><p>Electives</p> <p><a href="#">Core Courses</a></p><p><strong>Complete the following core courses to fulfil the requirements of this program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARTS1004</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS1004">Creative Collaborations</a></li><li><strong>DESN1011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1011">Visual Culture</a></li><li><strong>DESN1021</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1021">Studio: Motion and Interactive</a></li><li><strong>DESN1500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1500">Image Making</a></li><li><strong>DESN2003</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2003">Visual Process</a></li><li><strong>DESN2005</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2005">Prototyping</a></li><li><strong>DESN2006</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2006">Studio: Global</a></li><li><strong>DESN2211</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2211">Visual Narrative</a></li><li><strong>DESN3411</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3411">Studio: Professional Portfolio</a></li><li><em>1 additional courses are part of "Core Courses" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40208">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Core Courses"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40208">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Career-ready placement Course List</a></p><p><strong>Students Choose 10 units from the following course list to fulfil the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>ARTS3020</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/ARTS3020">Professional Career Ready Studio</a></li><li><strong>HASS3010</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HASS3010">Professional Career Ready Placement</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Career-ready placement Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40208">handbook</a>.</p>Visual Communication Design major<p><a href="#">Graphic Design</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses.</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1031</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1031">Visual Abstraction</a></li><li><strong>DESN3900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3900">Major Project</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 50 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 1000 level, 10 units at 2000 level and 20 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1101">Typography</a></li><li><strong>DESN1600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1600">Interaction Design (IxD) Fundamentals</a></li><li><strong>DESN1700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1700">Digital Photography</a></li><li><strong>DESN2011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2011">Design Futures</a></li><li><strong>DESN2221</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2221">Graphic Brand Identities and Spaces</a></li><li><strong>DESN2610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2610">User Interface (UI) Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN2700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2700">Commercial Studio Photography</a></li><li><strong>DESN2804</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2804">Motion Graphic Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3321</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3321">Publication Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3600">Physical Experience (PxD) Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3730</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3730">Transmedia Product and Campaign Design</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Graphic Design" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40208">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Graphic Design"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40208">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Animation and Illustration</a></p><p><strong>Compulsory </strong>Complete the following compulsory courses.</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1031</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1031">Visual Abstraction</a></li><li><strong>DESN3900</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3900">Major Project</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 50 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 1000 level, 10 units at 2000 level and 20 units at 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1200">Drawing Foundations</a></li><li><strong>DESN1331</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1331">Character Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN1601</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1601">Materials and Making</a></li><li><strong>DESN1801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1801">Animation Thinking</a></li><li><strong>DESN2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2060">Scientific Illustration</a></li><li><strong>DESN2801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2801">Animation Process</a></li><li><strong>DESN2804</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2804">Motion Graphic Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3040">Commercial Illustration</a></li><li><strong>DESN3801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3801">Production Studio</a></li><li><strong>DESN3802</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3802">Environment Design</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Animation and Illustration" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40208">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Animation and Illustration"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40208">handbook</a>.</p>Visual Communication Design Minor<p><a href="#">Graphic Design</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 1000 level and at least 20 units at 2000 or 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1101</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1101">Typography</a></li><li><strong>DESN1600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1600">Interaction Design (IxD) Fundamentals</a></li><li><strong>DESN1700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1700">Digital Photography</a></li><li><strong>DESN2011</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2011">Design Futures</a></li><li><strong>DESN2221</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2221">Graphic Brand Identities and Spaces</a></li><li><strong>DESN2610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2610">User Interface (UI) Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN2700</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2700">Commercial Studio Photography</a></li><li><strong>DESN2804</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2804">Motion Graphic Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3321</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3321">Publication Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3600">Physical Experience (PxD) Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3730</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3730">Transmedia Product and Campaign Design</a></li><li><em>2 additional courses are part of "Graphic Design" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40208">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Graphic Design"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40208">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Animation and Illustration</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>Choose 40 units from the following course list (with a minimum of 10 units at the 1000 level and at least 20 units at 2000 or 3000 level).</p><ul><li><strong>DESN1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1200">Drawing Foundations</a></li><li><strong>DESN1331</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1331">Character Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN1601</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1601">Materials and Making</a></li><li><strong>DESN1801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN1801">Animation Thinking</a></li><li><strong>DESN2060</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2060">Scientific Illustration</a></li><li><strong>DESN2801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2801">Animation Process</a></li><li><strong>DESN2804</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN2804">Motion Graphic Design</a></li><li><strong>DESN3040</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3040">Commercial Illustration</a></li><li><strong>DESN3801</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3801">Production Studio</a></li><li><strong>DESN3802</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/DESN3802">Environment Design</a></li><li><em>3 additional courses are part of "Animation and Illustration" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40208">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Animation and Illustration"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40208">handbook</a>.</p><p><a href="#">Communication</a></p><p><strong>Course List </strong>1000 Level Directed Courses - Complete 20 units from the following directed courses.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS1090</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1090">Introduction to Professional Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1100">Media, Culture and Narrative</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1234</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1234">Media and Communication Concepts</a></li><li><strong>CMNS1240</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS1240">Introduction to Media Production</a></li></ul><p><strong>Course List </strong>2000 Level Directed Courses - Complete 20 units from the following directed courses.</p><ul><li><strong>CMNS2000</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2000">Digital Media Engagement</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2140</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2140">Principles of Public Relations</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2212</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2212">Activism and Social Change</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2280</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2280">Feature Writing</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2320</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2320">News Media</a></li><li><strong>CMNS2470</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CMNS2470">Data Storytelling</a></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Communication"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40208">handbook</a>.</p>Electives<p><a href="#">Electives</a></p><p><strong>Complete 50 units of electives to fulfil the requirements of the program. Electives can be used to extend and complement your core studies with more courses in the same field of study, or from areas that might be of interest to you. Electives can be chosen from all courses available at the University that do not have any other conditions (such as a course requisite) applied to them.</strong></p><p>For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40208">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/40208">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Bachelor of Visual Communication Design</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=40208&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=NCLE&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience Reid McManus working with BMG artists Dune Rats and Hockey Dad 2:17 <p>Hear how Bachelor of Visual Communication Design (Honours) student Reid McManus gained real-world experience working with BMG artists Dune Rats and Hockey Dad.</p> Career-ready placements <p>You will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within your third year of study that will enable you to apply knowledge developed throughout your studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support your career readiness. You will undertake workplace experience in your desired career field, including advertising, marketing, and visual communications. You will showcase your skills through work placement, outcome-orientated projects and study experience options overseas.</p> <p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p> Studying at Newcastle City campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase Q Building Virtual Campus Tour 2:07 <p>Located in Honeysuckle, Q Building is part of our city precinct providing state-of-the-art facilities for the School of Humanities, Creative Industries and Social Sciences (HCISS) and the Integrated Innovation Network (I2N) Hub.</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://uac.edu.au/course-search/search/undergraduate/course/484650"><strong>Apply via UAC</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=40208">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="bachelor-of-arts">Bachelor of Arts<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 36,450</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Online</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-design-architecture">Bachelor of Design (Architecture)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 72.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 39,250</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-communication">Bachelor of Communication (Singapore)<p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <a href="/study/creative-industries-and-communication">Explore study area</a> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p> <h4>Career-ready placements</h4><p>You will complete 140 hours of supervised placement within your third year of study that will enable you to apply knowledge developed throughout your studies and acquire new knowledge and professional networks to support your career readiness. You will undertake workplace experience in your desired career field, including advertising, marketing, and visual communications. You will showcase your skills through work placement, outcome-orientated projects and study experience options overseas.</p><p> <a href="/current-students/career-ready-placements">Learn more</a> </p>',
