UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Explore a world of diversity. Study languages.</p><p>Proficiency in other languages will develop in-demand skills, opening many doors to diverse careers involving travel, overseas postings and teaching, as well as opportunities in sectors that have foreign language clients, markets and stakeholders. As part of this diploma, you will be able to study a range of languages including:</p><ul><li>Australian Sign Language</li><li>Chinese</li><li>French</li><li>Indonesian</li><li>Japanese</li></ul> <p>Either alongside your undergraduate degree or as a sole enrolment, you will learn how to speak, read, and write the language of your choice, while learning more about the relevant culture.</p><p>Graduates often report significant personal satisfaction as one of the many rewards of learning a language. By gaining a deeper appreciation of cultural differences, you can open your mind – and your future – to exciting opportunities in Australia and overseas.</p> <p> <strong> World top 250 ? </strong> for Sociology </p> <p> <strong> Top 150 ? </strong> in the world for Education </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Graduates enjoy diverse career opportunities, with their added qualification and language skills opening doors in Australia and around the world. Students who enrol in the diploma concurrently will only be adding one year of study to their undergraduate degree but graduating with two qualifications - a bachelor''s degree and a diploma.</p><p>Career pathways using your Diploma in Languages include roles in:</p><ul><li>Commercial Industries</li><li>Diplomacy and Government</li><li>Education</li><li>Journalism</li><li>Professional and Literary Translation</li><li>Law and Policy Development</li></ul> <p>Dual qualifications give an added boost to your employment chances in almost any job or industry.</p> <h4>Course overview</h4><p>This diploma offers courses that develop a range of language competencies across formal and informal contexts, including speaking, listening, reading and writing.</p><p>Students will have the opportunity to learn about the cultural foundations and business environment of the countries where the language is spoken. Explore a world of diversity by studying languages. They may focus on a single language for the 80 units (in the case of French, or Japanese) or choose to study multiple languages.</p><p>Out of the required 80 units, up to 40 units can come from credit transfers of language courses. – refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11718">handbook</a> for more info.</p> <p>Core</p> <p><a href="#">Course List</a></p><p><strong>Choose 80 units from the following list of course list to fulfill the requirements of the program.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHIN1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHIN1110">Chinese Language and culture Beginners 1 (A0 to A1.1) for students with other language backgrounds</a></li><li><strong>CHIN1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHIN1120">Chinese Language and Culture Beginners 2 (A1.1 to A1.2) for students with other language backgrounds</a></li><li><strong>CHIN2301</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHIN2301">Chinese Language and Culture Elementary 1 (A1.2 to A2.1)</a></li><li><strong>CHIN2302</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHIN2302">Chinese Language and Culture Elementary 2 (A2.1 to A2.2)</a></li><li><strong>CHIN2500</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHIN2500">Business English and Chinese</a></li><li><strong>CHIN2600</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/CHIN2600">Chinese-English Translation</a></li><li><strong>FREN1100</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN1100">French Language and Culture Beginners 1 (A0 to A1.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN1200</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN1200">French Language and Culture Beginners 2 (A1.1 to A1.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN2610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2610">French Language and Culture Elementary 1 (A1.2 to A2.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN2620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN2620">French Language and Culture Elementary 2 (A2.1 to A2.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3610</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3610">French Language and Culture Intermediate 1 (A2.2 to B1.1)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3620</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3620">French Language and Culture Intermediate 2 (B1.1 to B1.2)</a></li><li><strong>FREN3702</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/FREN3702">Extended French through Translation</a></li><li><strong>HUMA2001</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUMA2001">Global Experiences</a></li><li><strong>HUMA2070</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUMA2070">Auslan Language and Culture Beginners 1</a></li><li><strong>HUMA2080</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/HUMA2080">Auslan Language and Culture Beginners 2</a></li><li><strong>INDO1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INDO1110">Indonesian Language and Culture Beginners 1 (A0 to A1.1)</a></li><li><strong>INDO1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/INDO1120">Indonesian Language and Culture Beginners 2 (A1.1 to A1.2)</a></li><li><strong>JAPN1110</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/JAPN1110">Japanese Language and Culture Beginners 1 (A0 to A1.1)</a></li><li><strong>JAPN1120</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/JAPN1120">Japanese Language and Culture Beginners 2 (A1.1 to A1.2)</a></li><li><strong>JAPN2501</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/JAPN2501">Japanese In Context 1 (A1.2 to A2.1)</a></li><li><strong>JAPN2502</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/JAPN2502">Japanese in Context 2 (A2.1 to A2.2)</a></li><li><strong>JAPN3501</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/JAPN3501">Japanese in Context 3 (A2.2 to B1.1)</a></li><li><strong>JAPN3502</strong> <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/course/2026/JAPN3502">Japanese in Context 4 (B1.1 to B1.2)</a></li><li><em>9 additional courses are part of "Course List" but not offered in the current academic year, please review the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11718">handbook</a>.</em></li></ul><p>These are courses currently available in <em>"Course List"</em>, there may be additional courses available in future terms. For full requirements and course availability always refer to the <a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11718">handbook</a>.</p> 2026 Program Handbook <p>The courses shown above are a guide, and don''t reflect the exact year-by-year structure of the program, you should always refer to the program handbook for details of the complete program structure, course requirements and availability.</p> <p><a href="https://handbook.newcastle.edu.au/program/2026/11718">View program handbook</a></p> My Degree Planner <p>Use our degree planner to see what your study journey through the <strong>Diploma in Languages</strong> might look like.</p> <p> <a href="https://degreeplanner.newcastle.edu.au/students/r/pathways?program=11718&amp;region_status=domestic&amp;campus=CALLA&amp;academic_level=UGRD">Prospective student planner</a> <a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2438">Current student planner</a> </p> <p> <a href="#student-experience">Student experience</a> <a href="#student-showcase">Student showcase</a><a href="#how-to-apply">How to apply</a> </p> Student experience <p> Study a Diploma in Languages 1:41 </p> Learn a language, open up opportunities. <p>Hear from students, Madeleine and Georgia about their experience studying the Diploma in Languages at the University of Newcastle. Discover the many opportunities learning a language can open up for you.</p> Studying at Newcastle campus <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/newcastle/living-in-newcastle"> Living in Newcastle <p>Nestled on Australia''s spectacular east coast and surrounded by some of the state''s most popular destinations, Newcastle is an all-round wonderful choice as a safe and friendly place to live.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Studying online <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life"> Campus Life <p>Our campuses are welcoming, inspiring, and collaborative places for students, staff, and the community. Explore our beautiful campuses and discover what it’s like to study at the University of Newcastle.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/scholarships"> Scholarships <p>Our scholarships recognise achievement and support enthusiastic and dedicated students. If you are a current student, or planning to study with us, we encourage you to apply for all scholarships you meet the criteria for.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/campus-life/accommodation"> Accommodation <p>Living on campus is an experience unlike any other. Whether you''re from across Australia or around the globe, your home on campus is where you''ll form lifelong friendships and harness your potential in a supportive and diverse community.</p> <p>Read more</p> </a> Student showcase <a href="/media/viewer?media=969341"></a><a href="/media/viewer?media=969340"></a><a href="/media/viewer?media=969339"></a> <p>Student presenting to peers</p> <p>Students in the Library</p> <p>Student on Laptop</p> How to apply <p>Domestic</p> <p>International</p> Apply as a domestic student <p><strong>You are a domestic student if you are:</strong></p> <ul> <li>An Australian or New Zealand citizen (including dual citizens)</li> <li>A permanent resident of Australia</li> <li>A holder of a permanent Australian visa.</li> </ul> <p><a href="#apply-now">Apply now</a><p><a href="https://newcastle.uac.edu.au/apply"><strong>Apply Direct</strong></a></p><p><a href="https://askuon.newcastle.edu.au/app/answers/detail/a_id/2168"><strong>How to apply</strong></a></p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/undergraduate/admissions-and-entry">How to get into uni</a></p> Apply as an international student Entry requirements — Senior secondary school qualification <p>Admission to our undergraduate degree programs usually requires successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification similar to the <a href="//www.boardofstudies.nsw.edu.au/hsc/">Higher School Certificate (HSC)</a>, the highest educational award in New South Wales schools.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/study-with-us/what-can-i-study">More about entrance marks</a></li> </ul> English proficiency requirements <p>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement. Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at the <a href="https://policies.newcastle.edu.au/document/view-current.php?id=165">English Language Proficiency for Admission Policy</a>.</p> <ul> <li><strong>IELTS overall minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><strong>IELTS section minimum</strong> - 6.0</li> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/pathways/english-language-pathways">About English Language Pathways</a></li> </ul> Apply to the University via our online application portal. <p>In the application portal, you can enter the program you wish to study and upload relevant documents needed as part of your application. It is recommended you submit your application a minimum of 12 weeks before your intended semester of trimester start date.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/how-to-apply/what-you-will-need">What information you will need</a></li> </ul> <p>If you are applying through an education agent, they can also apply through the application portal. Ensure your agent is contracted to the University to avoid delays with your application.</p> <ul> <li><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/the-university-in-your-country">Find an education agent in your country</a></li> </ul> <p>Once you have started your application you will be provided with a reference number. You or your education agent will be able to track your application as it progresses.</p> <p><a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/international/admissions?ctx_prg=11718">Apply online</a></p> Similar degrees <a href="undergraduate-certificate-in-languages">Undergraduate Certificate in Languages<p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-education-secondary">Bachelor of Education (Secondary)<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 65.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 41,150</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 4 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 10 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Gosford</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <a href="bachelor-of-arts">Bachelor of Arts<ul><li><strong>Selection Rank:</strong> 63.00 (Newcastle)</li><li><strong>Indicative Fee1:</strong> AUD 36,450</li><li><strong>Full-time duration:</strong> 3 years</li><li><strong>Part-time duration:</strong> up to 8 years</li><li><strong>Locations:</strong> Newcastle, Online</li></ul><p>Learn more</p></a> <p>1 Indicative annual fees are based on a full year full time load (80 units). <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships/types-of-tuition-fees">Learn more.</a></p> <a href="/study/humanities-and-social-sciences">Explore study area</a> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://askuon.custhelp.com/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call 1300 275 866 </p> <p> <a href="tel:1300275866">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected">Sign up now</a> </p> Looking for more information? <p> Ask a question </p> <p> <a href="https://apply.newcastle.edu.au/international-enquirySPApp/">Find your answer</a> </p> <p> Call +61 2 4913 8300 </p> <p> <a href="tel:61249138300">Call us now</a> </p> <p> Sign up for updates </p> <p> <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/study/stay-connected#international">Sign up now</a> </p>',
