    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Learn basic research skills and the fundamental principles of clinical epidemiology.</p><p>This program is an introduction to clinical epidemiology. You will learn how to apply the principles of epidemiology and biostatistics. This program will improve your clinical decision making and develop your skills. You will graduate with an understanding of clinical and population based health problems.</p> <p>Your studies will count towards your continuing professional development points as a Clinician. This program is flexible with both full-time and part-time study options available. You can study online allowing you to juggle your work-life balance.</p><p>Graduates are eligible to apply for the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-clinical-epidemiology"> Master of Clinical Epidemiology</a>. You will also be eligible for prioritised entry to a research higher degree.</p> <p> <strong> Ranked 9 ? </strong> in Australia for Medicine </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>You will graduate with basic research skills and an understanding of epidemiological concepts.</p> <p>On completion of this degree, you will be able to work in roles such as:</p><ul><li>Epidemiology research</li><li>Academia</li><li>Policy Advisor</li><li>Health related industries.</li></ul> <p>93% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>(Graduate Outcomes Survey 2021-2023, postgraduate Health Services)</p> <p>$1,938 median weekly income before tax.</p> <p>(Labourmarketinsights.gov.au)</p>',
