    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Position yourself as an educational leader.</p><p>If you’re a practicing teacher or educator looking to deepen your understanding of broader education issues, the Graduate Certificate in Education is for you.</p> <p>You’ll enhance your current skills and connect with the latest industry developments and research. You’ll move beyond the classroom to examine system-level challenges and issues. By improving your professional knowledge, you can fast-track your career and increase your employability.</p><p>Our flexible study options and international recognition will enable you to pursue global career opportunities.</p> <p> <strong> Top 150 ? </strong> in the world for Education </p> <p> <strong> $107,800 ? </strong> teacher median salary </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p><strong>Possible career paths may include:</strong></p><ul><li>Higher education teacher within TAFEs and university sectors</li><li>Education consultant within TAFEs, universities or schools</li><li>Leadership, coordination, specialist or professional development positions in school systems.</li></ul><p>This program provides an entry pathway into the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-education">Master of Education</a>. You will receive credit for the courses you have already completed.</p> <p>97.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>(Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Postgraduate Education)</p>',
