UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Graduate Certificate in Human Resource Management</p><p>This program equips graduates with the essential knowledge and skills to launch or advance a career in human resource management. With HR skills continuing to rank among the most critical areas of skill shortage for Australian businesses, now is the ideal time to build your expertise in this high-demand field and take the next step in your career.</p> <p>Enjoy flexible study options: Fully online, face-to-face at NuSpace in Newcastle CBD, or a blended combination of both. Once completed, you will have the option to apply for advanced entry into the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-human-resource-management">Master of Human Resource Management.</a></p> <p> <strong> 19,300 extra ? </strong> Human Resources Managers needed by 2026 </p> <p> <strong> 12.4% projected growth ? </strong> for Human Resource Managers by 2030 </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>If you are pursuing a career in HRM, our Graduate Certificate in HRM gives you the competitive edge you need.</p><p>The program builds essential skills for managing people effectively while equipping you to navigate emerging workplace challenges and complexities.</p> <p>This qualification positions you for a variety of entry-level and professional roles, including:</p><ul><li>Human Resources Officer/Advisor</li><li>Union Official or Employer Association Advisor</li><li>Change Management Consultant</li><li>Graduate Recruitment Consultant.</li></ul> <p>94.7% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>(Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024) - Postgraduate Business and Management</p>',
