UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Make a difference in a changing world</p><p>The frequency and intensity of disasters and other crises around the world are increasing. The need for professionals with expertise in disaster risk and resilience has never been greater. Learn the essential skills and knowledge to excel in the field of disaster risk reduction and management.</p> <p>With flexible study options, this is an ideal choice for professionals seeking to advance their careers in disaster management, policy development, community resilience, and related fields.</p><p>Students will have the opportunity to progress into the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-of-disaster-risk-and-resilience">Master of Disaster Risk and Resilience</a> with credits earned from this program.</p> <p> <strong> Top 1% ? </strong> university in the world <!-- no link --> </p> <p> <strong> Top 30 ? </strong> in the world for impact </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>We have a strategic relationship with <a href="http://www.unitar.org">UNITAR</a> and UNDRR and through that connection hosts <a href="https://unitar.org/about/offices-training-centres-around-world/cifal-newcastle">CIFAL Newcastle</a>, an international training centre with a special focus on Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR). As a result of this partnership, graduates of this program will be well positioned to move into organisations that require experts specialised in and have knowledge of DRR.</p> <p>This qualification has wide relevance and appeal, and is suitable for those pursuing a career where they are responsible for human safety and business continuity such as a:</p><ul><li>Compliance Officer</li><li>Response and Recovery Outreach Worker</li><li>Policy Officer</li><li>Strategic Planner</li><li>Emergency Management Officer</li><li>Disaster Resilience Officer</li><li>Bureau of Meteorology Hazard Prediction Team Member</li><li>Disaster Risk Management role in humanitarian and international aid agencies.</li></ul> <p>11.9% projected employment growth by 2029.</p> <p>Jobs and Skills Australia 2024, Policy and Planning Managers.</p>',
