    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>A pathway to our Master of Social Work (Qualifying)</p><p>This program is designed for students interested in becoming qualified social workers with a bachelor''s degree in an unrelated field.</p><p>Students who have completed four (4) social and behavioural sciences courses in their undergraduate degree are eligible for admission to the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-of-social-work-qualifying">Master of Social Work (Qualifying)</a> in the following semester, upon completion of the Graduate Certificate in Human and Social Services.</p> <p> <strong> World top 250 ? </strong> for Sociology </p> <p> <strong> 88.2% employed ? </strong> found employment after graduating </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Social work offers many fields of practice that lead to diverse career pathways.</p><p>Upon completion of the Master in Social Work (Qualifying), possible careers include:</p><ul><li>Social Worker</li><li>Case manager (Child Protection, Out of Home Care, Housing, Addiction, Disability)</li><li>Community Development Officer</li><li>Policy Adviser</li><li>Counsellor</li><li>Mental Health Clinician.</li></ul>',
