UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Start your journey to becoming an expert in laboratory medicine.</p><p>The program will introduce you to laboratory medicine, with an emphasis on practical laboratory skills that will transfer to a modern pathology laboratory.</p><p>Laboratory Medicine is designed for graduates of biology, biotechnology, biomedical science, or related degrees. If you are interested in a career in diagnostic pathology, this is the program for you.</p> <p>You will gain practical experience of the latest advances in diagnostic medicine and undertake 10 days of industry placement as part of your program. You will develop the knowledge and skills to generate diagnostic laboratory reports.</p><p>Students will graduate career-ready with the skills and knowledge to work in a diagnostic pathology laboratory.</p><p>This program also provides an entry pathway into the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-of-laboratory-medicine">Master of Laboratory Medicine</a>. You will receive credit for the courses you have already completed.</p> <p> <strong> Clinical placement </strong> throughout program </p> <p> <strong> Top 1% ? </strong> university in the world <!-- no link --> </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>The skills and knowledge you will gain in this program allow you to expand your capabilities and work to a new level of expertise.</p><p>Upon graduation, you may find yourself working in positions in fields such as:</p><ul><li>Medical/diagnostic pathology laboratories – technical positions</li><li>Hospital laboratories</li><li>Pharmaceutical companies</li><li>Biomedical &amp; Biotechnology industries.</li></ul>',
