UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Enhance your strategic capabilities in the marketing field</p><p>Marketing is a dynamic, challenging and fast paced business function. Professionals must be prepared to meet these challenges and adapt with the changing nature of the industry. This programs equips you with essential skills for today’s evolving business sectors, blending marketing principles with advanced digital strategies. This program provides a foundation in marketing theory, covering the principles of strategy, consumer psychology and behaviour, and digital marketing strategy.</p> <p>This program offers a pathway to the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-of-marketing-and-digital-strategy">Master of Marketing and Digital Strategy</a> for students wanting to deepen their expertise and enhance their strategic capabilities in the marketing field.</p> <p> <strong> AACSB &amp; EQUIS ? </strong> accredited business school <!-- no link --> </p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>This program will provide you with invaluable knowledge and simultaneously build your skills in analysing situations and developing and managing a marketing strategy. These outcomes will facilitate you in meeting employment challenges with confidence and conviction.</p> <p>If you are looking to further expand your career opportunities or a career change, this program will give you the edge you need. It will enable you to differentiate yourself from other marketers in that you will possess a range of marketing skills and develop an understanding of how these skills interrelate with other organisational functions. These insights will enable you to contribute widely to the management of organisational offerings, customer-perceived value, strategic positioning and competitive advantage, in both local and global contexts. The relevant knowledge and skills underlie many senior roles including:</p><ul><li>Marketing Coordinator</li><li>Market Research Officer</li><li>Media Analyst</li><li>Marketing Manager</li><li>Brand Manager.</li></ul> <p>94.7% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey (2022-2024) - Postgraduate Business &amp; Management</p>',
