UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Dive into the world of IT.</p><p>Enhance your career opportunities within the IT industry. Develop analytical skills that are essential to organisations adopting new technologies or processes. Explore your interest in information systems, software engineering, multimedia, or telecommunications. Develop a solid foundation in relevant technologies and theoretical concepts.</p> <p>We offer different levels of entry based on your previous experience. If you have limited IT experience, you''ll gain foundational IT skills. If you''re an experienced IT professional, you can further enhance your skills. You can then apply these skills within emerging technology-driven growth areas. These areas include IT, communications, business, and entrepreneurship.</p><p>This program offers pathways to future study. On completion, you will be eligible for direct entry into programs such as <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-information-technology">Master of Information Technology</a> and <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-cyber-security">Master of Cyber Security</a>.</p> <p> <strong> Top 1% ? </strong> university in the world <!-- no link --> </p> <p> <strong> 86.1% of students ? </strong> were happy with facilities and resources </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>You''ll have the option to tailor the program to best suit your career development needs. Be equipped to hit the ground running with your newly attained specialist expertise.</p> <p>Your career opportunities are quite diverse with possible entry level career paths as a:</p><ul><li>Business Analyst</li><li>Database Developer</li><li>Systems Analyst</li><li>Software Developer.</li></ul> <p>14.3% projected employment growth by 2029.</p> <p>Jobs and Skills Australia 2024, ICT Professionals.</p>',
