UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Positively impact social change and development</p><p>This graduate certificate is designed to equip you with the foundational knowledge to work in social change and development. If you have the desire to work in the professional service of others this program is for you. Throughout your studies you will:</p><ul><li>Learn about the key areas of social change, studying both theoretical and practical coursework.</li><li>Develop an understanding of the implications of social and political changes at a global level.</li><li>Be prepared to meet the challenges of development work in a rapidly changing global environment.</li><li>Critically explore the legacies of development and reimagine pathways for change.</li></ul> <p>This program is recognised nationally and internationally, allowing you to apply your knowledge in roles across the globe. Both full-time and part-time study modes available; online or face-to-face.</p><p>This program provides a pathway into the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-social-change-development">Master of Social Change and Development.</a> You will receive credit for the courses you have completed.</p> <p> <strong> World top 250 ? </strong> for Sociology </p> <p> <strong> World top 300 ? </strong> for Social Sciences </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Australia is increasingly engaging with developing countries. This creates a need for qualified professionals in social change and development. Demand is increasing for professionals in the community development and policy analysis of development projects and aid organisations.</p> <p>You will graduate with the theoretical and practical knowledge to take on roles within:</p><ul><li>Government agencies</li><li>Non-government organisations</li><li>Private firms</li><li>Community groups</li><li>Social justice advocacy networks.</li></ul><p><strong>You may find yourself working in roles including:</strong></p><ul><li>Administrator</li><li>Field Officer</li><li>Development Planner</li><li>Overseas Aid</li><li>Community Development</li><li>Ministry of finance in developing countries.</li></ul> <p>90% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>(Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024)</p> <p>$81,500 median starting salary.</p> <p>(Graduate Outcomes Survey 2021-2023 – Humanities, Culture and Social Sciences)</p>',
