UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>An alternative pathway into psychology</p><p>Designed for graduates from any discipline, this program provides a flexible pathway into the field of psychology without requiring a prior background in the discipline. With the ability to study full-time, you can complete the program in as little as one year.</p> <p>Whether you’re looking to change careers, build psychological knowledge to support your current role, or pursue further study in psychology, this program will help you develop foundational skills in key areas such as cognitive, biological, developmental and social psychology.</p><p>With the option to study 100% online, you can balance study alongside work and personal commitments while progressing towards your goals.</p><p>Successful completion of the program can support progression into further psychology study, including Honours and Master’s programs, for those wishing to continue their pathway into the profession.</p> <p> <strong> APAC ? </strong> accredited degree </p> <p> <strong> World top 250 ? </strong> for Psychology </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Graduates develop a wide range of knowledge and skills valued across industries. You may continue to progress in your current career into management levels. Alternatively, you could specialise in human service organisations, employment agencies, counselling services. Roles in personnel management, market research, health and community services are also potential career paths.</p> <p>Depending on your career goals, you can further your education in Psychology by applying for entry to our Honours or Master’s programs. This opportunity allows you to develop your professional and clinical skills further.</p><p>Graduates of this program may qualify for the following roles within the industry:</p><ul><li>Behavioural Support Practitioner</li><li>Research assistant</li><li>Case manager</li><li>Mental health or disability support worker</li><li>Roles in health promotion, policy development, or other allied health or community service settings.</li></ul> <p>96.8% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024, Postgraduate Psychology.</p>',
