UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Design your path in architecture</p><p>Our program is grounded and future-focused, preparing you for professional practice and the next step towards becoming a registered architect.</p> <p>The program is shaped by a commitment to Caring for Country and a focus on social and ecological responsibility. You’ll develop your own approach to architecture through design-led studio learning that engages with real-world challenges and the communities you design for.</p><p>You’ll spend more time in the studio than any other NSW program. Working in a hands-on environment that supports exploration, collaboration and critical thinking. As part of a close-knit cohort, you’ll be supported by a strong design community and access to purpose-built facilities, including:</p><ul><li>24-hour access Architectural Design Studio</li><li>Workshop &amp; Advanced Prototyping Facility</li><li>Makerspace and emerging technology PixelSpace Lab</li><li>On-Country site experiences</li></ul><p>The program reflects the diverse and evolving nature of architectural practice. Through a mix of guided and self-directed projects, including the option to complete a year-long final project of your own conception, you’ll define your own architectural voice and the kind of practice you want to pursue.</p> <p> <strong> World top 200 ? </strong> for Architecture and the Built Environment </p> <p> <strong> Ranked 1 ? </strong> in Australia for full-time employment </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>This program prepares you for professional practice and a range of roles across the built environment.</p> <p>You’ll graduate with advanced design capability and a strong understanding of how architecture operates in real-world contexts, from concept through to delivery.</p><p><strong>Graduates pursue careers across areas including:</strong></p><ul><li>Architectural practice</li><li>Government and policy</li><li>Advocacy and community-led projects</li><li>Research</li><li>Construction and project delivery</li><li>Property and infrastructure development</li><li>International and humanitarian projects.</li></ul><p><strong>Career pathways may include roles such as:</strong></p><ul><li>Architect (following registration)</li><li>Project Manager</li><li>Infrastructure Planner</li><li>Construction Manager</li><li>Roles in private and commercial practice</li><li>Overseas aid and humanitarian work.</li></ul><p>Graduates from the program are recognised by industry, with students receiving major awards, including <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/highlights/student/2026/thomas-jagger">three NSW Architects Medallions</a> in the past five years.</p> <p>98.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024, Postgraduate Architecture and Building.</p> <p>10.5% projected employment growth by 2029.</p> <p>Jobs and Skills Australia 2024, Architects and Landscape Architects.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 104,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 86290,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td>Successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification or bachelor degree at the required level.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement.</li><li>Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at theEnglish Language Proficiency for Admission Policy.</li><li>IELTS overall minimum- 6.5</li><li>IELTS section minimum- 6.0</li><li>About English Language Pathways</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-architecture',
