UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Study a combined Masters program and lead an organisation''s most important asset - its people.</p><p>This combined degree program allows you to undertake studies in general business disciplines to complement your Master of Human Resources Management qualification.</p><p>If you’re looking to advance your career in human resources and business management, this program is for you. You will develop skills and strategies to manage people, workforces, workplace conflict, and other organisational challenges.</p> <p>Combine this with a range of analytic, strategic and leadership skills through concurrent study of the MBA. Study fundamental business areas such as accounting, finance, and marketing for a comprehensive understanding of resourcing and operations.</p><p>Learn to apply your knowledge within complex organisational environments to develop and lead high-performing teams, business strategies and processes.</p> <p> <strong> 19,300 extra ? </strong> Human Resources Managers needed by 2026 </p> <p> <strong> 12.4% projected growth ? </strong> for Human Resource Managers by 2030 </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>At the completion of this program, you will be positioned as a leader in the field and will have the credentials to show you have the distinct HR competencies that many companies need. You will be able to apply relevant, rigorous human resource management and employee relations theory to a variety of workforce situations. You will be ready to develop and implement evidence-based strategies to address complex individual, group and organisational challenges.</p><p>Our graduates go on to great careers in local, national, and multinational organisations.</p> <p>You will graduate with skills suited to diverse professional roles, including:</p><ul><li>Human Resource Advisor or Manager</li><li>Learning and Development / Training and Development Advisor or Manager</li><li>Employment Relations or Industrial Relations Manager</li><li>Senior Union Official or Senior Employer Association Advisor</li><li>Policy Advisor to government organisations</li><li>Change Manager.</li></ul> <p>94.7% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>(Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-20224 - Business and Management)</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 104,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 91950,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td>Successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification or bachelor degree at the required level.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement.</li><li>Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at theEnglish Language Proficiency for Admission Policy.</li><li>IELTS overall minimum- 6.5</li><li>IELTS section minimum- 6.0</li><li>About English Language Pathways</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
