UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Secure a future in cyber security</p><p>Cyberspace has transformed the way we live and do business. We are increasingly relying on networked applications for assessing information and making critical business decisions. It is crucial for individuals, enterprises, and governments to be able to secure cyberspace from attacks, to effectively conduct their business.</p> <p>This program provides an open path to cyber security for individuals from diverse backgrounds. You will develop a holistic understanding of security measures, encompassing network, system, and foundational theories. Gain insights into cyber systems and infrastructures, and their applications. Explore the human and legal aspects of cyber security. Learn the skills needed to address global skill shortages.</p><p>Access our advanced, industry-leading cyber security labs. You''ll help run cyber hackathons and develop real-world applications in a controlled environment. You will also have the choice between two specialisations to suit your career aspirations.</p><p>A <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/graduate-certificate-cyber-security">Graduate Certificate in Cyber Security </a>is also available to study and can be used as a pathway into the masters program.</p> <p> <strong> 86.1% of students ? </strong> were happy with facilities and resources </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Upon graduation, this program will allow you to harness your expertise in cyber security to work in a variety of industry sectors.</p> <p><strong>Career options may include:</strong></p><ul><li>Security System Manager</li><li>Security Consultant</li><li>Cryptographer</li><li>Cyber Security Architect</li><li>Security system developer</li><li>Cyber Security Analyst.</li></ul> <p>24.7% projected employment growth by 2034.</p> <p>Jobs and Skills Australia 2024, Database and Systems Administrations &amp; ICT Security Specialists.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 104,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 96300,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td>Successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification or bachelor degree at the required level.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement.</li><li>Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at theEnglish Language Proficiency for Admission Policy.</li><li>IELTS overall minimum- 6.5</li><li>IELTS section minimum- 6.0</li><li>About English Language Pathways</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-cyber-security',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '0100135';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Improve the lives and learning of children.</p><p>If you’re a practicing educator looking to retrain in an additional teaching area or advance your professional skills, our Master of Education program is for you.</p><p>You’ll deepen your understanding of educational theory and practice, stay updated with industry trends and research, and apply a proven teaching framework supported by strong evidence.</p> <p>Our Master of Education program empowers you to deepen your curriculum knowledge in specialised areas, enhancing your teaching effectiveness, accelerating your career growth, and improving your job prospects.</p><p>Our flexible study options and international recognition will enable you to pursue career opportunities worldwide. A <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/graduate-certificate-education">Graduate Certificate in Education</a> is also available to study and can be used as a pathway into the masters program.</p> <p> <strong> Top 150 ? </strong> in the world for Education </p> <p> <strong> Professional placement </strong> and practical opportunities </p> <p> <strong> $107,800 ? </strong> teacher median salary </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>This program prepares you with the skills and knowledge to build on your current teaching experience and further your career in education. You will graduate with an advanced understanding of the values and ethical principles that underlie the broad field of education and the conduct of various research traditions in complex settings in an ethical, collaborative, professional and accountable manner. You will enter the professional workforce with the ability to articulate an educational perspective in regards to the broader community issues of ethical conduct, equity and social justice.</p> <p>You''ll graduate with a qualification in an additional teaching area, in either Maths, Physics or TESOL.</p><p><strong>Possible career paths may include:</strong></p><ul><li>Specialist Teacher in areas such as TESOL, secondary maths and secondary physics</li><li>Higher Education Teacher within TAFEs and university sectors</li><li>Education Consultant or Advisor within TAFEs universities or schools</li><li>Leadership, Coordination, Specialist or Professional Development positions in school systems.</li></ul> <p>97.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>(Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024 - Postgraduate Education)</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 52,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 41175,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td>Successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification or bachelor degree at the required level.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement.</li><li>Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at theEnglish Language Proficiency for Admission Policy.</li><li>IELTS overall minimum- 6.5</li><li>IELTS section minimum- 6.0</li><li>About English Language Pathways</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/master-education',
    updated_at = NOW()
