UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Learn to strategically manage a workforce</p><p>This program provides you with skills and knowledge to manage people and efficient work practises within an organisation. Learn to apply your knowledge within complex organisational environments to develop and lead high-performing teams and workforces.</p> <p>If you’re looking to advance your career in human resource management (HRM), employment relations (ER) or consulting, this program is for you. You will develop a deep nuanced understanding of strategic human resource management and organisational psychology, while gaining practical skills to resolve effectively workplace conflicts, manage interpersonal relationships, and address a wide range of other organisational challenges.</p><p>With HR competencies consistently ranking among the most important areas of skill shortage for Australian businesses, now is the ideal time to build or refresh your expertise and propel your career forward. A <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/graduate-certificate-human-resource-management">Graduate Certificate in Human Resource Management</a> is also available, offering a flexible entry point and clear pathway into the full masters program.</p> <p> <strong> 19,300 extra ? </strong> Human Resources Managers needed by 2026 </p> <p> <strong> 12.4% projected growth ? </strong> for Human Resource Managers by 2030 </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Graduating with a Master of Human Resource Management positions you as a strategic leader in the profession, with the advanced competencies and credentials that top employers value.</p><p>You will master the application of contemporary HR and employee relations theories to real-world workforce scenarios and be ready to design and lead evidence-based strategies that resolve sophisticated individual, team and organisational challenges.</p><p>Our alumni advance to influential roles in organisations of all-scales – local, national and global.</p> <p>You will be well-prepared for high-impact positions, such as:</p><ul><li>Human Resource Advisor or Manager</li><li>Learning and Development Manager</li><li>Organisational Development Manager</li><li>Employment Industrial Relations Manager</li><li>Senior Union Official or Senior Employer Association Advisor</li><li>Government Policy Advisor (HR related)</li></ul> <p>94.7% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey (2022-2024) - Postgraduate Business &amp; Management</p>',
