UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Join the next generation of material scientists and engineers.</p><p>This program offers you the opportunity to participate in both coursework and research. You will have the opportunity to use state-of-the-art infrastructure. This is available at the world-renowned Global Innovative Centre for Advanced Nanomaterials (GICAN). You will undertake research related to the design and discovery of new materials, such as:</p><ul><li>Advanced materials</li><li>Nanomaterials</li><li>Functional materials</li><li>Drug carriers</li><li>Photovoltaics</li><li>Soft materials</li><li>Useful metal alloys.</li></ul> <p>This program will develop and train the next generation of material scientists and engineers.</p><p>You will gain an understanding of how the processing of a material influences its structure, properties and performance. You will learn to apply this knowledge to address challenging issues in a variety of fields, including:</p><ul><li>Applied Chemistry</li><li>Batter technology</li><li>Biosensors</li><li>Nanomedicine</li><li>Pharmacy</li><li>Instrumentation</li><li>Steel</li><li>Electronics</li><li>Nanotechnology</li><li>Energy and environmental technologies</li><li>Forensic engineering</li><li>Metallurgy and mining.</li></ul> <p> <strong> World top 250 ? </strong> for Engineering </p> <p> <strong> Industry sponsored </strong> projects at the GICAN centre </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Materials science and engineering expertise is in high demand across a range of industries and job roles.</p><ul><li>Defence</li><li>Medical technology</li><li>Environmental services</li><li>Catalysis</li><li>Petrochemical</li><li>Adsorption and separation.</li></ul> <p>94.1% of students rated learning resources positively.</p> <p>Student Experience Survey 2023-2024, Postgraduate Engineering.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 104,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 102040,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td>Successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification or bachelor degree at the required level.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement.</li><li>Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at theEnglish Language Proficiency for Admission Policy.</li><li>IELTS overall minimum- 6.5</li><li>IELTS section minimum- 6.0</li><li>About English Language Pathways</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
