UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Advance faster into senior nursing roles.</p><p>The Master of Nursing is designed to help registered nurses progress sooner into senior, specialist, leadership positions, educator roles, or researcher without stepping away from work, family, or community.</p> <p>You’ll build advanced knowledge and confidence to lead teams, manage complex care situations, and deliver evidence-based care across diverse healthcare settings. Whether you’re seeking clinical specialisation, leadership or education roles, or greater long-term career flexibility, a master’s qualification helps you stand out in a competitive job market and access opportunities that are often promoted from within.</p><p>The program is purpose-built for working nurses, supporting sustainable study alongside professional practice. Flexible learning options, supportive academic staff and pathways that recognise your existing experience allow you to balance study with the realities of shift work and professional demands.</p><p>As a nationally recognised leader in nursing education, the University of Newcastle works closely with the NSW health workforce to prepare graduates for the real-world challenges facing today’s healthcare system. Expand your impact in healthcare and build a more flexible, resilient and higher‑earning nursing career.</p> <p> <strong> World top 100 ? </strong> for Nursing </p> <p> <strong> $104,000 ? </strong> median starting salary </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Master of Nursing graduates will have the expertise to offer advanced clinical knowledge and advice in various healthcare settings.</p> <p><strong>Possible career paths may include:</strong></p><ul><li>Clinical Nurse Specialist</li><li>Clinical Research Nurse</li><li>Clinical Nurse Consultant</li><li>Clinical Nurse Educator</li><li>Clinical Facilitator</li><li>Nurse Unit Manager</li><li>Academic.</li></ul> <p>95% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>(Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024, postgraduate Nursing &amp; Midwifery)</p> <p>$1937 median weekly income before tax.</p> <p>(Labourmarketinsights.gov.au)</p>',
