UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Shape the future of the built environment</p><p>Advance your career in construction management and build the skills to lead complex projects across the built environment. With strong demand for professionals who can manage delivery, cost and risk, this program is designed to support progression into project management and leadership roles, with entry that recognises your prior qualifications and industry experience.</p> <p>Develop practical expertise in project management, cost estimation, scheduling and construction law, with a focus on real-world application. You’ll learn how to manage projects from planning through to completion, applying your knowledge to the challenges faced across the construction industry.</p><p>Guided by industry-experienced academics, you’ll build the confidence to lead teams and deliver projects effectively. Graduate ready to step into roles such as construction manager, project manager, estimator or quantity surveyor, with the skills to make an immediate impact.</p> <p> <strong> World top 200 ? </strong> for Architecture and the Built Environment </p> <p> <strong> Ranked 1 ? </strong> in Australia for full-time employment </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Demand for skilled construction professionals in Australia continues to grow. Building and construction employment is expected to increase from around <a href="https://www.amca.com.au/common/Uploaded%20files/MemberOnlyResources/ACIF%20Construction%20Market%20Report/ACIF%20November%202025%20ACMR%20FA.pdf">1.32 million jobs in 2024-25 to almost 1.5 million by 2029-30</a>, driven by rising infrastructure and development activity.</p><p>This program will prepare you for positions as a construction professional. You will gain skills in project management, cost estimation, scheduling, and construction.</p> <p>Additionally, you''ll have a strong foundation in legal and regulatory issues that are specific to the industry. This will help you to navigate the complexities and ensure compliance with relevant laws and regulations.</p><p><strong>After graduating, you’ll be able to work in roles such as:</strong></p><ul><li>Construction Manager</li><li>Estimator</li><li>Quantity Surveyor</li><li>Project Manager.</li></ul> <p>98.2% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024, Postgraduate Architecture and Building.</p>',
