UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Future-proof your career with essential data science skills for an AI-driven future</p><p>In today''s data-driven world and with AI transforming industries, this program puts you at the forefront of this dynamic field. Whether you want to enhance your current career or switch to a new path, this program prepares you for success.</p> <p>Merge essential data science principles with advanced AI techniques to interpret complex data and develop intelligent systems. Delve into areas such as data processing, visualisation, and predictive modelling. Develop the skills needed to solve real-world problems and lead in an AI-driven future.</p><p>Choose from two specialisations to further develop skills in your chosen field:</p><ul><li>Computational Intelligence</li><li>Health Data Analysis.</li></ul><p>This program is designed for both experienced professionals and those new to the field. Learn from industry-leading experts and engage with coursework that reflects the latest industry advancements. You''ll gain skills in high demand across a range of industries. These industries include healthcare, finance, technology, and government.</p> <p> <strong> 86.1% of students ? </strong> were happy with facilities and resources </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>This program will provide you with the skills needed to thrive in the rapidly expanding fields of data science and AI. There are broad job opportunities across various sectors.</p> <p>Graduates may qualify for the following roles within the industry:</p><ul><li>Machine Learning and Big Data Expert</li><li>Business Intelligence Specialist</li><li>Data Analyst and Scientist</li><li>Information Security Analyst</li><li>Data Manager.</li></ul><p>Future-proof your career. <a href="https://ia.acs.org.au/article/2026/ai-jobs-are-the-fastest-growing-in-australia.html">AI jobs are the fastest growing in Australia</a>, with AI literacy being one of the most sought-after skills by employers. This program equips you with the skills to step into these high-demand roles.</p> <p>14.3% projected employment growth by 2029.</p> <p>Jobs and Skills Australia 2024, ICT Professionals</p>',
