UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Shape the future of food.</p><p>Food is more than sustenance. Food is the cornerstone of culture, global health, and innovation. As the world population continues to expand, we face evolving challenges in food production, sustainability, and nutrition. The demand for forward-thinking professionals in the field of food science has never been greater.</p> <p>The Master of Food Science and Technology program at the University of Newcastle will provide you with the advanced knowledge, skills and opportunities to work in various areas in the food industry.</p><p>Our flexible program structure empowers you with the necessary skills, knowledge, and professional industry experience to thrive in this exciting area of work. You could pursue diverse roles across the food industry sector or continue into food science research, including product development and quality assurance.</p> <p> <strong> 96.4% employed ? </strong> within four months of graduating </p> <p> <strong> Real world experience </strong> through our modern food innovation centre and sensory laboratory </p> <p> <strong> 400 hours ? </strong> of career ready placement </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Graduates of Food Science programs are in high demand. The industry is rapidly growing as society becomes savvier and the thirst for healthier, more convenient and sustainable food alternatives grows.</p> <p>The Central Coast serves as a pivotal hub for national food production and manufacturing, boasting a vibrant community of over 50 small, medium and large food companies situated near the Ourimbah campus of the University of Newcastle.</p><p>On completion of this degree, you will possess the high level of knowledge, skills and experience necessary to address challenges related to food quality, safety, and sustainability, and to excel in the food industry.</p><p><strong>After graduation, you may take on roles such as:</strong></p><ul><li>Food scientist, technologist or chemist</li><li>Food product development</li><li>Food biotechnologist</li><li>Quality control/quality assurance</li><li>Flavourist</li><li>Food safety specialist</li><li>Product and packaging technologist</li><li>Nutrition education &amp; nutrition research</li><li>Sensory and analytical scientist</li><li>Community health promotion</li><li>Teaching and academic research.</li></ul> <p>$1,828 median starting salary.</p> <p><strong>for Chemists, and Food and Wine Scientists</strong><br/>(Jobs and Skills Australia - jobsandskills.gov.au)</p> <p>$2,090 median starting salary.</p> <p><strong>for Nutrition Professionals</strong><br/>(Jobs and Skills Australia - jobsandskills.gov.au)</p>',
