    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Study a combined Masters program and become a leader in the health sector</p><p>This combined masters program allows you to undertake studies in general business disciplines to complement your specialist knowledge in health management and policy.</p><p>Effective leadership skills and a thorough understanding of policy are crucial to navigating the complex challenges present in healthcare. This program prepares graduates to meet the growing demand for expertise in healthcare leadership and management roles.</p> <p>You will also study a range of analytic, strategic, and leadership skills through concurrent study of the MBA. Study fundamental business areas such as accounting, finance, economics and operations, for a comprehensive understanding of organisations.</p><p>Choose our fully flexible online learning options to study at the time and pace that works for you. Or, make use of our city precinct facilities through studying face-to-face at NuSpace in Newcastle CBD. Graduate a competitive candidate in two years, confident in your skills to respond to complex issues the sector faces.</p> <p> <strong> AACSB &amp; EQUIS ? </strong> accredited business school <!-- no link --> </p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Career opportunities in healthcare span the globe. Work in health, policy or research.</p> <p>The skills and knowledge you will gain in this program underpin many senior roles including:</p><ul><li>Chief Health Policy Officer</li><li>Health Strategy Consultant and Regulator</li><li>Healthcare Finance Manager</li><li>Health Program and Services Manager/Director</li><li>Health Policy/Services Researcher</li><li>Public Health Policy Advisor</li><li>Health economist</li></ul>',
