UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Shape the future of diagnostic medicine in a high‑demand profession.</p><p>Designed to meet Australia’s growing demand for skilled laboratory professionals, the Master of Laboratory Medicine prepares job-ready graduates with advanced expertise in diagnostic pathology and medical research, real clinical laboratory experience, and strong career pathways into hospital, pathology and regional laboratories.</p> <p>This degree is ideal for graduates of biomedical science, biology, biotechnology or closely related disciplines, as well as current laboratory or health professionals looking to upskill. If you’re seeking a career in diagnostic pathology, medical research or laboratory medicine, this degree equips you with the knowledge, skills and experience employers are actively looking for.</p><p>You’ll gain first-hand experience with the latest advances in diagnostic medicine. You''ll learn in real diagnostic environments and use current technologies and industry‑standard processes.</p><p>Integrated clinical placements ensure you graduate with hands‑on experience aligned to industry expectations, so you are prepared for employment in modern pathology facilities and laboratories. You’ll develop advanced laboratory capabilities that support innovation, research and evidence‑based medical decision‑making.</p><p>Laboratory medicine underpins more than 70% of medical decisions, placing graduates at the centre of patient diagnosis, disease monitoring and life‑saving healthcare. With strong national demand across pathology and diagnostic testing, graduates benefit from high job security, faster career progression and opportunities across metropolitan, regional and specialised laboratories.</p><p>You can also start with the <a href="https://www.newcastle.edu.au/degrees/graduate-certificate-in-laboratory-medicine">Graduate Certificate in Laboratory Medicine</a>, which provides a pathway into the master’s degree while building advanced, job‑ready laboratory skills.</p> <p> <strong> Clinical placement </strong> throughout program </p> <p> <strong> Top 1% ? </strong> university in the world <!-- no link --> </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>The skills and knowledge you will gain in this program allow you to expand your capabilities and work to a new level of expertise.</p> <p>Upon graduation you may find yourself working in positions in fields such as;</p><ul><li>Medical/diagnostic pathology laboratories – scientist positions</li><li>Leadership positions in laboratory medicine</li><li>Hospital laboratories</li><li>Pharmaceutical companies</li><li>Biomedical &amp; Biotechnology industries</li><li>Research &amp; education.</li></ul>',
    course_duration_per_week = 104,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 106530,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td>Successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification or bachelor degree at the required level.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement.</li><li>Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at theEnglish Language Proficiency for Admission Policy.</li><li>IELTS overall minimum- 6.5</li><li>IELTS section minimum- 6.0</li><li>About English Language Pathways</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
