UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Address complex global health challenges and lead changes across public health and healthcare systems.</p><p>The Master of Public Health / Master of Health Management and Policy is a two-year dual degree combining population health with leadership, policy, and management. It prepares public health practitioners, managers, and policy makers to advance their impact across health services, government, NGOs, and health systems.</p> <p>This interdisciplinary degree prepares you to address health challenges through evidence-based decision making and leadership. You will develop skills in public health practice, health management, policy, and governance.</p><p>Teaching is delivered by experienced public health practitioners, health management professionals, epidemiologists, biostatisticians, and active researchers. This ensures strong academic and industry relevance.</p><p>The curriculum covers public health, policy, governance, economics, data analytics, and communication, with opportunities to apply learning in real-world contexts.</p> <p> <strong> World top 150 ? </strong> for Public Health </p> <p> <strong> World top 175 ? </strong> for business and economics </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Graduates are prepared for a wide range of roles within the national and international health sector. You will have the potential for career advancement into mid-high level positions within complex health and organisational environments.</p> <p><strong>Potential career paths include:</strong></p><ul><li>Health Policy Analyst / Advisor</li><li>Health Services Manager / Health Services Administrator</li><li>Hospital / Health Network Administrator</li><li>Population Health Manager</li><li>Program and Project Management Lead (Health Systems &amp; Policy)</li><li>Quality Improvement Manager / Clinical Governance Lead</li></ul><p>Graduates also develop advanced skills applicable to research and professional practice, including:</p><ul><li>Population health practice and evaluation</li><li>Health promotion and health services management</li><li>Research design and methodology</li><li>Epidemiology and Medical statistics.</li></ul> <p>94% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>(Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024, postgraduate Health Services and Support)</p> <p>$1,938 median weekly income before tax.</p> <p>(Labourmarketinsights.gov.au)</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 104,
