UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Be empowered to address complex public health challenges through informed social change and development.</p><p>The Master of Public Health / Master of Social Change and Development is an interdisciplinary dual degree combining population health with social change and policy. Designed for professionals working across health, community development, and social policy, the program responds to growing demand for graduates who can influence health outcomes in complex social, economic, and political contexts.</p> <p>The program builds on your prior learning to develop advanced skills in public health practice, research, and policy analysis. You will complete a structured mix of public health and social change and development courses, with a strong focus on practical, critical and research-informed learning. You will learn how global and local factors shape health and how social change can improve population health and equity.</p><p>Teaching is delivered by experienced public health practitioners and leading academics in health promotion, epidemiology, biostatistics, social change, and development studies. The curriculum focuses on applied, practice-informed learning, helping you translate theory into real-world impact.</p> <p> <strong> World top 150 ? </strong> for Public Health </p> <p> <strong> World top 250 ? </strong> for Sociology </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>The program’s focus on population health, social change, and development prepares graduates for mid- to senior-level roles in complex organisations and global settings.</p> <p><strong>Graduates may pursue careers in roles and areas such as:</strong></p><ul><li>Public Health Advisor</li><li>Population Health Manager</li><li>Policy Analyst / Health Policy Analyst</li><li>Program Evaluator</li><li>Program Coordinator / Program Manager (Health, Social Services, Development)</li></ul><p>Depending on elective choices, graduates develop advanced skills that can be applied to research and professional practice, including:</p><ul><li>Population health practice and evaluation</li><li>Health promotion and community engagement</li><li>Health and development management</li><li>Research design and methodology</li><li>Epidemiology and medical statistics</li></ul> <p>94% employed within four months of graduating.</p> <p>(Graduate Outcomes Survey 2022-2024, postgraduate Health Services and Support)</p> <p>$1,938 median weekly income before tax.</p> <p>(Labourmarketinsights.gov.au)</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 104,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 81200,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td>Successful completion of a senior secondary school qualification or bachelor degree at the required level.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>Applicants who do not speak English as a first language must demonstrate that they meet the University''s English proficiency requirement.</li><li>Further information regarding English language proficiency requirements can be found at theEnglish Language Proficiency for Admission Policy.</li><li>IELTS overall minimum- 6.5</li><li>IELTS section minimum- 6.0</li><li>About English Language Pathways</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
