    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Specialise your engineering skills for global career opportunities</p><p>If you are an electrical engineer looking to advance your career, this program is designed for you.</p><p>Develop management expertise, specialise, and deepen your technical skills to lead projects and move into senior roles. You will build on your prior knowledge and develop core technical competencies. Deepen your technical knowledge in your area of specialisation and learn about engineering practice in the Australian context.</p> <p><strong>Focus on key emerging technologies such as:</strong></p><ul><li>Intelligent electricity networks</li><li>Renewable energy integration</li><li>Wireless energy transfer</li><li>Autonomous transportation</li><li>Telecommunication security</li><li>The Internet of Things (IoT).</li></ul><p>Engage with industry through projects, guest lectures, and mentorship opportunities. Enhance skills in project management, complex problem-solving, innovation, and communication through our professional leadership courses. Graduate with the technical and professional attributes needed to provide innovative solutions to society’s needs now and in the future.</p> <p> <strong> Ranked 2 ? </strong> in Australia and 18 in the world for Automation and Control </p> <p> <strong> 12 weeks </strong> of Industrial Experience </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Engineers work on a wide range of tasks in many different environments – industries like electronics, energy, food, manufacturing, pharmaceuticals, construction, environmental health and transportation. Engineering continues to be one of the most in-demand qualifications in the world, with many countries desperate to fill a shortage of professional skills in this field.</p> <p>This program will open up even more varied career opportunities, empowering you to take on a leadership role, start your own business or manage major engineering projects.</p> <p>94.1% of students rated 