UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Degree overview</h4><p>Specialise in geospatial engineering for senior roles on a global landscape</p><p>Are you looking to launch or advance your career in the field of surveying and spatial information? This program will help you develop management expertise, specialise and deepen your technical skills. Become equipped to lead projects and move into more senior roles.</p> <p>You may choose to deepen your competence in the discipline, including advanced surveying, geodesy and geopositioning, GPS/GNSS technology, spatial data systems, information technology and geospatial analysis. Alternatively, choose to broaden your technical skills in another discipline, such as disaster management, environmental management, sustainability or water engineering.</p><p>Engage with industry through projects, guest lectures, and mentorship opportunities. Enhance skills in project management, complex problem-solving, innovation, and communication through our professional leadership courses. Graduate with the technical and professional skills needed to provide innovative solutions to society’s needs now and in the future.</p> <p> <strong> 12 weeks </strong> of Industrial Experience </p> <p> <strong> World top 250 ? </strong> for Engineering </p> <h4>Career opportunities</h4><p>Surveyors and geospatial engineers work on a huge range of tasks in many different environments.</p><p><strong>Industries include:</strong></p><ul><li>Land surveying</li><li>Mining surveying</li><li>Remote sensing</li><li>Geodesy and space research</li><li>Construction</li><li>Environmental management</li><li>Transportation.</li></ul> <p>Surveying and geospatial engineering continues to be one of the most in-demand qualifications in the world, with many countries desperate to fill a shortage of professional skills in this field.</p><p>This program will open up even more varied career opportunities than you already have. You may take on a leadership role, start your own business or manage major surveying and engineering projects. As a qualified engineer you can travel the world and work almost anywhere you choose.</p> <p>94.1% of students rated learning resources positively.</p> <p>Student Experience Survey 2023-2024, Postgraduate Engineering.</p>',
